{"parentUuid":"1b5c75bf-0d35-49b9-9567-73604d528a0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDLvVLk7j8im21pygunq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017urgLSgEYKqsEAtLY8hYc8","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp","offset":220,"limit":70},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2850,"cache_read_input_tokens":51766,"output_tokens":324,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2850,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":51766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2850},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDLvUDmktHejeY8r1qQ7","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c6dff85-0094-4086-bb04-8f717a1c322f","timestamp":"2026-07-20T12:54:58.900Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"4c6dff85-0094-4086-bb04-8f717a1c322f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"db6277c7-d019-4524-aa8f-1e758800b456","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017urgLSgEYKqsEAtLY8hYc8","type":"tool_result","content":"220\t        register_module(norm);\n221\t        register_module(wQ); register_module(wK); register_module(wV);\n222\t        register_module(wO);\n223\t        register_parameter(q_gamma);\n224\t        register_parameter(k_gamma);\n225\t\n226\t        // ---- Context-parallel attention layer ----\n227\t        // ring   => HeadTail load-balance (matches shard_sequence_pre_embed's perm);\n228\t        // ulysses=> contiguous shard;\n229\t        // hybrid => Ulysses-inner (ulysses_pg) nested in Ring-outer (cp_pg==ring pg),\n230\t        //           HeadTail on the ring axis. RoPE/QK-norm/GQA applied INSIDE CP.\n231\t        const float attn_scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt(static_cast<float>(c.head_dim));\n232\t        const bool  lb = (c.ring_mode || c.hybrid_mode);\n233\t        cp_ = std::make_shared<ContextParallel>(\n234\t            mesh, cp_pg, attn_scale, /*is_causal=*/true, c.rotator,\n235\t            /*load_balance=*/lb);\n236\t        if (c.hybrid_mode) {\n237\t            cp_->enable_hybrid(ulysses_pg, c.ulysses_size, cos_sin_cache,\n238\t                               q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps);\n239\t        } else if (c.ring_mode) {\n240\t            cp_->enable_rope(cos_sin_cache, q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps);\n241\t        } else {\n242\t            cp_->enable_ulysses_fused(cos_sin_cache, q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps,\n243\t                                      c.rope_interleaved);\n244\t        }\n245\t    }\n246\t\n247\t    // x: LOCAL sequence shard [B, T_local, d_model]\n248\t    Tensor forward(const Tensor& x) override {\n249\t        const int64_t B  = x.shape().dims[0];\n250\t        const int64_t Tl = x.shape().dims[1];\n251\t\n252\t        Tensor h = norm.forward(x);\n253\t        Tensor q = wQ.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nq*hd]\n254\t        Tensor k = wK.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nkv*hd]\n255\t        Tensor v = wV.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nkv*hd]\n256\t\n257\t        // -> head-major [B, heads, T_local, hd]\n258\t        q = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(q, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.q_heads,  cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n259\t        k = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(k, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.kv_heads, cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n260\t        v = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(v, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.kv_heads, cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n261\t\n262\t        // CP fused attention: RoPE + QK-norm + causal GQA inside the ring/ulysses\n263\t        // path. pre_sharded=true (q/k/v are already the local shard); unshard=false\n264\t        // (output stays [B, Nq, T_local, hd], no all-gather).\n265\t        Tensor attn = cp_->forward_cp(q, k, v, /*unshard=*/false, /*pre_sharded=*/true);\n266\t\n267\t        Tensor merged = autograd::reshape(autograd::transpose(attn, 1, 2),\n268\t                                          Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.q_heads * cfg.head_dim}});\n269\t        Tensor proj = wO.forward(merged);\n270\t        return autograd::add(x, proj);                   // residual\n271\t    }\n272\t};\n273\t\n274\t// =============================================================================\n275\t// SwiGLU feed-forward (unchanged from bluscript.cpp; operates on the local shard)\n276\t// =============================================================================\n277\tclass SwiGLUMLP : public nn::Module {\n278\tpublic:\n279\t    nn::RMSNorm norm;\n280\t    nn::Linear  gate_up;\n281\t    nn::Linear  down;\n282\t\n283\t    SwiGLUMLP(const ModelConfig& c, DeviceIndex dev, InitRng& rng)\n284\t        : norm(c.d_model, c.rms_eps),\n285\t          gate_up(c.d_model, 2 * c.ffn_hidden, /*bias=*/false),\n286\t          down(c.ffn_hidden, c.d_model,        /*bias=*/false)\n287\t    {\n288\t        const float resid_scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt(2.0f * static_cast<float>(c.n_layers));\n289\t        init_linear(gate_up, 0.02f, rng);"}]},"uuid":"2f6cbe42-419c-4724-917d-161fc0d57986","timestamp":"2026-07-20T12:54:58.908Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp","content":"        register_module(norm);\n        register_module(wQ); register_module(wK); register_module(wV);\n        register_module(wO);\n        register_parameter(q_gamma);\n        register_parameter(k_gamma);\n\n        // ---- Context-parallel attention layer ----\n        // ring   => HeadTail load-balance (matches shard_sequence_pre_embed's perm);\n        // ulysses=> contiguous shard;\n        // hybrid => Ulysses-inner (ulysses_pg) nested in Ring-outer (cp_pg==ring pg),\n        //           HeadTail on the ring axis. RoPE/QK-norm/GQA applied INSIDE CP.\n        const float attn_scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt(static_cast<float>(c.head_dim));\n        const bool  lb = (c.ring_mode || c.hybrid_mode);\n        cp_ = std::make_shared<ContextParallel>(\n            mesh, cp_pg, attn_scale, /*is_causal=*/true, c.rotator,\n            /*load_balance=*/lb);\n        if (c.hybrid_mode) {\n            cp_->enable_hybrid(ulysses_pg, c.ulysses_size, cos_sin_cache,\n                               q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps);\n        } else if (c.ring_mode) {\n            cp_->enable_rope(cos_sin_cache, q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps);\n        } else {\n            cp_->enable_ulysses_fused(cos_sin_cache, q_gamma, k_gamma, c.qk_eps,\n                                      c.rope_interleaved);\n        }\n    }\n\n    // x: LOCAL sequence shard [B, T_local, d_model]\n    Tensor forward(const Tensor& x) override {\n        const int64_t B  = x.shape().dims[0];\n        const int64_t Tl = x.shape().dims[1];\n\n        Tensor h = norm.forward(x);\n        Tensor q = wQ.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nq*hd]\n        Tensor k = wK.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nkv*hd]\n        Tensor v = wV.forward(h);                        // [B, Tl, Nkv*hd]\n\n        // -> head-major [B, heads, T_local, hd]\n        q = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(q, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.q_heads,  cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n        k = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(k, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.kv_heads, cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n        v = autograd::transpose(autograd::reshape(v, Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.kv_heads, cfg.head_dim}}), 1, 2);\n\n        // CP fused attention: RoPE + QK-norm + causal GQA inside the ring/ulysses\n        // path. pre_sharded=true (q/k/v are already the local shard); unshard=false\n        // (output stays [B, Nq, T_local, hd], no all-gather).\n        Tensor attn = cp_->forward_cp(q, k, v, /*unshard=*/false, /*pre_sharded=*/true);\n\n        Tensor merged = autograd::reshape(autograd::transpose(attn, 1, 2),\n                                          Shape{{B, Tl, cfg.q_heads * cfg.head_dim}});\n        Tensor proj = wO.forward(merged);\n        return autograd::add(x, proj);                   // residual\n    }\n};\n\n// =============================================================================\n// SwiGLU feed-forward (unchanged from bluscript.cpp; operates on the local shard)\n// =============================================================================\nclass SwiGLUMLP : public nn::Module {\npublic:\n    nn::RMSNorm norm;\n    nn::Linear  gate_up;\n    nn::Linear  down;\n\n    SwiGLUMLP(const ModelConfig& c, DeviceIndex dev, InitRng& rng)\n        : norm(c.d_model, c.rms_eps),\n          gate_up(c.d_model, 2 * c.ffn_hidden, /*bias=*/false),\n          down(c.ffn_hidden, c.d_model,        /*bias=*/false)\n    {\n        const float resid_scale = 1.0f / std::sqrt(2.0f * static_cast<float>(c.n_layers));\n        init_linear(gate_up, 0.02f, rng);","numLines":70,"startLine":220,"totalLines":1289}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6f75c842-31b6-45d8-bf81-f743f35b7942","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"2f6cbe42-419c-4724-917d-161fc0d57986","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDLw1naB3ftNzLu6nbrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_read_input_tokens":54616,"output_tokens":1162,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":54616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDLvvreyBYQ1LrwGjtVi","type":"assistant","uuid":"a79aec00-a7ea-4e26-ad66-07e2a2cf4baa","timestamp":"2026-07-20T12:55:05.160Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"a79aec00-a7ea-4e26-ad66-07e2a2cf4baa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDLw1naB3ftNzLu6nbrY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short answer: **no — there are no explicit absolute position indices assigned in the data loader** in this script. RoPE positions are implicit, derived from the RoPE cache plus the shard geometry, and applied inside the CP kernel.\n\nHere is the actual flow:\n\n**1. The cache is built for positions `0 .. context_length-1`** — this is the only place \"positions\" materialize, in the model constructor at [bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L337-L338):\n\n```cpp\ncos_sin_cache(autograd::build_rope_cache(c.context_length, c.head_dim,\n                                         static_cast<float>(c.rope_theta), dev))\n```\n\nThe cache row `t` *is* absolute position `t`. Note the hard guard at [bluscriptCP.cpp:552](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L552) — `T != context_length` dies, because the cache is indexed directly by position.\n\n**2. The data loader only produces token ids** — `idx [B, T]`, no position column. See `forward(const Tensor& idx)` at [bluscriptCP.cpp:369](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L369). The loader/sharder (`shard_sequence_pre_embed` / hybrid variant, [bluscriptCP.cpp:377-383](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L377-L383)) splits the sequence and, for ring/hybrid, applies the **HeadTail load-balance permutation** — but it moves *tokens*, it never emits a positions tensor.\n\n**3. RoPE is applied inside `ContextParallel`, not here.** The cache is handed to the CP layer via `enable_rope` / `enable_hybrid` / `enable_ulysses_fused` ([bluscriptCP.cpp:237-243](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L237-L243)), and the fused kernel reconstructs each local token's absolute position from `(ring_rank, ulysses_rank, local_slot)` + the load-balance layout to index the correct cache row. That is why the HeadTail permutation the sharder uses must exactly match what the kernel assumes ([bluscriptCP.cpp:227](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L227)).\n\nSo the \"absolute position index that RoPE alters\" is never stored as data — it's the cache row number, and the mapping from a sharded local token back to its absolute position lives in the CP kernel's shard-geometry math, seeded by the `build_rope_cache` call in the constructor.\n\nIf you want, I can open `RoPEOps.h` / `ContextParallel.h` to show exactly where the local-slot → absolute-position index is computed inside the kernel."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_read_input_tokens":54616,"output_tokens":1162,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2006,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1162,"cache_read_input_tokens":54616,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2006,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2006},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDLvvreyBYQ1LrwGjtVi","type":"assistant","uuid":"aca76385-5b06-4b46-a792-c30c02260c93","timestamp":"2026-07-20T12:55:19.426Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"aca76385-5b06-4b46-a792-c30c02260c93","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"6df1d2f5-3590-49ba-9f90-aafc90bc406c","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"db6277c7-d019-4524-aa8f-1e758800b456\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Short answer: **no — there are no explicit absolute position indices assigned in the data loader** in this script. RoPE positions are implicit, derived from the RoPE cache plus the shard geometry, and applied inside the CP kernel.\\n\\nHere is the actual flow:\\n\\n**1. The cache is built for positions `0 .. context_length-1`** — this is the only place \\\"positions\\\" materialize, in the model constructor at [bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L337-L338):\\n\\n```cpp\\ncos_sin_cache(autograd::build_rope_cache(c.context_length, c.head_dim,\\n                                         static_cast<float>(c.rope_theta), dev))\\n```\\n\\nThe cache row `t` *is* absolute position `t`. Note the hard guard at [bluscriptCP.cpp:552](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L552) — `T != context_length` dies, because the cache is indexed directly by position.\\n\\n**2. The data loader only produces token ids** — `idx [B, T]`, no position column. See `forward(const Tensor& idx)` at [bluscriptCP.cpp:369](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L369). The loader/sharder (`shard_sequence_pre_embed` / hybrid variant, [bluscriptCP.cpp:377-383](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L377-L383)) splits the sequence and, for ring/hybrid, applies the **HeadTail load-balance permutation** — but it moves *tokens*, it never emits a positions tensor.\\n\\n**3. RoPE is applied inside `ContextParallel`, not here.** The cache is handed to the CP layer via `enable_rope` / `enable_hybrid` / `enable_ulysses_fused` ([bluscriptCP.cpp:237-243](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L237-L243)), and the fused kernel reconstructs each local token's absolute position from `(ring_rank, ulysses_rank, local_slot)` + the load-balance layout to index the correct cache row. That is why the HeadTail permutation the sharder uses must exactly match what the kernel assumes ([bluscriptCP.cpp:227](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L227)).\\n\\nSo the \\\"absolute position index that RoPE alters\\\" is never stored as data — it's the cache row number, and the mapping from a sharded local token back to its absolute position lives in the CP kernel's shard-geometry math, seeded by the `build_rope_cache` call in the constructor.\\n\\nIf you want, I can open `RoPEOps.h` / `ContextParallel.h` to show exactly where the local-slot → absolute-position index is computed inside the kernel.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":37},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1ac54bf-0380-47a7-8831-6d1877c04c3d","timestamp":"2026-07-20T12:55:19.558Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main"}
