{"parentUuid":"9c08c80c-9fd0-48a8-839d-6ce1a955cd06","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5f5c15a1-f104-4841-968c-d1e3de6d4476","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XMgpSiFTMBJPS9teMa4ro7","type":"tool_result","content":"147:2026-07-09 - Implemented canonical (HF/Qwen3) YaRN in build_rope_cache: NTK-by-parts freq blend via find_correction_dim dim-index ramp + attention temperature m=0.1*ln(s)+1 baked into cos/sin (m^2 logit temp, no kernel change); env-overridable YARN_SCALE/ORIG_MAXPOS/BETA_FAST/BETA_SLOW (scale=1 => bit-identical std RoPE); build-on-CPU-then-.to(device) bypasses uniform-freq CUDA kernel; robustness guards (R2 scale/seqlen warn, R3 init log, R5 bad-range throw). YARNOps.o symbol wins link over libtensor RopeOps. 2x3060 verified: standin parity 100% PASS cos=1.0 both no-env and YARN_SCALE=8, m=1.2079 matches, hd=128 low=11/high=36; ulysses fails only in pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug (identical at scale=1) - CP / context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp2026-07-09 - CORRECTION to 2026-07-09 YaRN entry (\"pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug\"): this was WRONG, not a kernel bug. Root-caused via precision-injection test: took the G=1 (MHA, no GQA at all) case, bf16-round-tripped K on the ref_sdpa side only (no kernel change), and dQ cos collapsed to 0.108 - identical magnitude to the \"GQA bug\" signature seen for 1<Nkv<Nq. Proves dQ is simply sensitive to bf16-vs-fp32 K precision mismatch between the fused/normal GQA kernels (bf16-internal) and the fp32 ref_sdpa reference; nothing GQA-specific. Kernel is correct. Retracting all prior \"fused/normal GQA backward dQ/dq_gamma bug\" claims (2026-07-02, 2026-07-07 entries) - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\n148:2026-07-16 - bluscriptCP re-warmup anchor fix + long-context PPL eval: (1) LR re-warmup was anchored at start_step (current resume step) so every resume of a context-extension run restarted the warmup ramp; added CP_REWARMUP_ANCHOR=<step> to pin the ramp to a fixed absolute step (default -1 = old start_step behavior), so resuming mid/post-ramp continues the same schedule; log now prints anchor+resume+phase (mid-ramp/past-ramp). (2) Added CP_EVAL_PPL forward-only eval mode: NP=1/CP_SIZE=1 (T_local==T, no cross-rank gather), loads ckpt via CP_CKPT_RESUME, teacher-forces CP_EVAL_WINDOWS windows on held-out val split, per-position NLL=logsumexp-logit[tgt] -> pos,count,mean_nll,ppl CSV (CP_EVAL_OUT); skips training + log/config writes (/dev/null). Base-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=1 (naive extrapolation) vs extended-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=4 curves show blow-up-vs-flat past orig ctx. (3) Notebook cell in graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb plots the CSVs + before/after-ctx PPL ratio verdict. Compile-verified (mpic++ -c, exit 0); server build/run pending - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb\n153:2026-07-10 - Process-group UNIFICATION (prereq for DataParallel+ContextParallel coexisting in bluscriptCP): made BluTrain dist/communication ProcessGroupNCCL the single canonical PG for CP+DP. (A) Extended BluTrain PG (additive) with the CP ring-overlap surface ported to run on its own comm_: cpRingStream() + cp_ring_stream_, sendrecv_async_stream, all_gather_async_stream, alltoallv_async, alltoallv_async_stream; + comm-adopting ctor (world_size,rank,ncclComm_t,...) + get_comm(). (B) Rewrote CP process_group/device_mesh.cpp to build sub-groups via ncclCommSplit(world_comm,color=other-coords,key=axis-coord) instead of MPI_Comm_split+WORLD id-bcast -> NCCL-native sub-groups, fixes the 2D-mesh wrong-id bug (world PG still 1x MPI_Bcast); device_mesh.h now includes canonical PG + holds world_pg_. (C) Repointed 8 CP files' #include process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> \"ProcessGroupNCCL.h\" (canonical). Collision: device_mesh.h's quote-include resolved CP's same-dir header first -> RENAMED (not deleted, per user) process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> ProcessGroupNCCL_cplegacy.h (dormant). (D) Makefile: +INCLUDES -IBluTrain/dist/communication/include -IBluTrain/dist/Data-Parallel/include; +BLUTRAIN_PG_SRC (processGroupNccl.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/Error_logs.cpp); CPP_EXCLUDE += process_group/processGroupNCCL.cpp. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED: builds clean (one ProcessGroupNCCL/Work/NCCLCHECK, no dup symbols); cp-rope-standin 12/12 PASS cos=1.0000000 (ring fwd+bwd+dgamma + ported overlap methods + ncclCommSplit 1D world identical to old CP PG); cp-ulysses 72 PASS, only the pre-existing bf16-ref-precision dQ/dq_gamma FAILs (unchanged by migration). Follow-ups: 2-D ncclCommSplit per-axis all-reduce test (needs 4 ranks), then bluscriptCP resume (wire DataParallel.cpp) - CP / BluTrain/dist/communication/{include/ProcessGroupNCCL.h,src/processGroupNccl.cpp}, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, context_parallel/*.h, Makefile2026-07-10 - bluscriptCP RESUME (CP Llama training on the unified PG): DataParallel + ContextParallel now coexist. Included DataParallel.hpp DIRECTLY (not the dist/distributed.h umbrella, which pulls the TP stack incl. a different class DeviceMesh -> collision); init_process_group comes from the canonical PG. Fixed double-init crash (\"process group instance already created\"): the DeviceMesh builds the world PG once (ncclCommSplit parent) and bluscriptCP now reuses it via new DeviceMesh::world_pg() for DataParallel instead of a 2nd init_process_group. Makefile: bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp targets; DataParallel.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/profiler.cpp scoped to this target only. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED (CP_FUSED_ROPE=1, tiny cfg L2/d256/hd64/GQA kv2/T256, edufineweb data in ~/Downloads via CP_DATA_ROOT): builds clean; world=1 trains loss 10.89->10.23 decreasing, finite grad-norm, fused-RoPE CP ring ran (first real training integration of the new kernels); ws=2 CP_SIZE=2 ring trains AND loss-parity vs world=1 (step0 10.884 vs 10.890, step4 10.2269 vs 10.2280) -> CP sequence-sharding + RoPE positions + ring correct end-to-end, and overlap-ON matching the serial reference proves the ring overlap is race-free (plan concern d). FOLLOW-UP: CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 diagnostic path crashes (\"convert_type_cuda: invalid resource handle\" — stream-handle issue under the unified PG; default overlap path unaffected + verified). Also pending: 2-D DPxCP run (dp>1), Ulysses-mode bluscriptCP (CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses), full-scale config - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, Makefile\n155:2026-07-10 - Documented bluscriptCP in README.md: new \"Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\" section (Ring vs Ulysses build+run commands, CP_FUSED_ROPE=1-to-both-build-and-run + checkpoint-resume gotchas, full env-var reference incl. topology CP_SIZE/CP_ATTN_MODE/CP_ROTATOR, model/data CP_N_EMBD/LAYER/HEAD/KVHEAD/T/B/GLOBAL_BATCH/MAX_STEPS/WARMUP/DATA_ROOT, YaRN YARN_*, diagnostics CP_NO_OVERLAP*/RING_BLOCKING/SYNC_RING/NO_GPUS_PER_NODE, build flags CP_FUSED_ROPE/CP_ROPE_DEBUG, full-scale example), + bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp make targets, intro + repo-layout mentions - CP / README.md\n157:2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: added 2-stage re-warmup for YaRN context-extension resume + checkpoint-visibility prints. get_lr gained a warmup_start anchor (ramp [warmup_start, warmup_start+warmup) then cosine-decay; warmup_start=0 reproduces old schedule exactly) since the base schedule's warmup is absolute-from-0 and cannot re-ramp on resume. New env: CP_REWARMUP=<steps> (0=off, only when start_step>0) re-anchors a fresh warmup at the resume step, CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=<frac of max_lr, default 1.0> for a reduced long-context peak; prints \"[re-warmup] anchored at step S ...\". Also added checkpointing/ckpt_freq/dir to the boxed Configuration block and a \"Checkpointing: ON -> <dir>/<prefix>_step_<N>.ckpt (every F steps, keep K)\" line at run start (user noticed these weren't shown; root of an earlier \"not checkpointing\" confusion was just the default ckpt_freq=250 -> first save at step 250). Context: discussed that context extension causes a perplexity spike so stop base run DECAYED (not at peak) then re-warmup to a reduced peak (~0.3x). IMPLEMENTED, NOT YET BUILT/VERIFIED (user had a run on the box) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\n158:2026-07-11 - Documented the above in README.md (bluscriptCP section): new \"Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup\" env table (CP_CKPT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME + CP_REWARMUP/CP_REWARMUP_PEAK, run-numbered ckpt/log naming, first-save-at-step-N note) and a \"2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup)\" subsection (base stage decay -> long-context resume with reduced-peak re-warmup, seq-len/world-size-independent checkpoint load, CP_MAX_STEPS/CP_CKPT_RESUME resumability gate) + a YaRN scale=1-means-off / CP_T==scale*orig_maxpos note - CP / README.md\n161:2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP output cleanup pt2: the remaining x4-duplicated init banners ([YaRN] build_rope_cache, [CP ring P2P/A2A/AllGather], [CP sdpa fwd], [CP bwd] overlap) were fprintf(stderr) (NOT std::cout) so the cout redirect could not touch them. Added context_parallel/CPLog.h with cp::log_rank() (reads OMPI_COMM_WORLD_RANK, fallback PMI_RANK, unknown-launcher -> true so never silently lost) and gated all 6 one-time stderr notices on global rank 0 at source (RingRotator.h x3, ContextParallelBackward.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, YARNOps.cpp x2) - real stderr errors from other ranks stay visible (vs a blanket stderr redirect). All main-repo context_parallel/ files (sync to server, no submodule). NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}\n162:2026-07-11 - FIX build break from the above: CPLog.h used a GLOBAL 'namespace cp', but the CP stack already has OwnTensor::cp (cp::ulysses_combine/head_repeat_interleave/...) -> two 'cp' in scope made EVERY cp:: reference ambiguous (server error: \"reference to 'cp' is ambiguous\", cascaded across ContextParallel/Ulysses/RingRotator). Renamed namespace cp -> cplog (unique, global) + updated all 6 call sites to cplog::log_rank(); existing cp::ulysses_* now resolve cleanly again. Verified by grep (no cp::log_rank left, 6 cplog sites, 1 def). NOT BUILT locally (avoid contending with user's run) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4958cc0-4248-4836-87a3-3b9f40d39dd5","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:00:35.342Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"147:2026-07-09 - Implemented canonical (HF/Qwen3) YaRN in build_rope_cache: NTK-by-parts freq blend via find_correction_dim dim-index ramp + attention temperature m=0.1*ln(s)+1 baked into cos/sin (m^2 logit temp, no kernel change); env-overridable YARN_SCALE/ORIG_MAXPOS/BETA_FAST/BETA_SLOW (scale=1 => bit-identical std RoPE); build-on-CPU-then-.to(device) bypasses uniform-freq CUDA kernel; robustness guards (R2 scale/seqlen warn, R3 init log, R5 bad-range throw). YARNOps.o symbol wins link over libtensor RopeOps. 2x3060 verified: standin parity 100% PASS cos=1.0 both no-env and YARN_SCALE=8, m=1.2079 matches, hd=128 low=11/high=36; ulysses fails only in pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug (identical at scale=1) - CP / context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp2026-07-09 - CORRECTION to 2026-07-09 YaRN entry (\"pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug\"): this was WRONG, not a kernel bug. Root-caused via precision-injection test: took the G=1 (MHA, no GQA at all) case, bf16-round-tripped K on the ref_sdpa side only (no kernel change), and dQ cos collapsed to 0.108 - identical magnitude to the \"GQA bug\" signature seen for 1<Nkv<Nq. Proves dQ is simply sensitive to bf16-vs-fp32 K precision mismatch between the fused/normal GQA kernels (bf16-internal) and the fp32 ref_sdpa reference; nothing GQA-specific. Kernel is correct. Retracting all prior \"fused/normal GQA backward dQ/dq_gamma bug\" claims (2026-07-02, 2026-07-07 entries) - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\n148:2026-07-16 - bluscriptCP re-warmup anchor fix + long-context PPL eval: (1) LR re-warmup was anchored at start_step (current resume step) s