e), and dQ cos collapsed to 0.108 - identical magnitude to the \\\"GQA bug\\\" signature seen for 1<Nkv<Nq. Proves dQ is simply sensitive to bf16-vs-fp32 K precision mismatch between the fused/normal GQA kernels (bf16-internal) and the fp32 ref_sdpa reference; nothing GQA-specific. Kernel is correct. Retracting all prior \\\"fused/normal GQA backward dQ/dq_gamma bug\\\" claims (2026-07-02, 2026-07-07 entries) - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n148:2026-07-16 - bluscriptCP re-warmup anchor fix + long-context PPL eval: (1) LR re-warmup was anchored at start_step (current resume step) so every resume of a context-extension run restarted the warmup ramp; added CP_REWARMUP_ANCHOR=<step> to pin the ramp to a fixed absolute step (default -1 = old start_step behavior), so resuming mid/post-ramp continues the same schedule; log now prints anchor+resume+phase (mid-ramp/past-ramp). (2) Added CP_EVAL_PPL forward-only eval mode: NP=1/CP_SIZE=1 (T_local==T, no cross-rank gather), loads ckpt via CP_CKPT_RESUME, teacher-forces CP_EVAL_WINDOWS windows on held-out val split, per-position NLL=logsumexp-logit[tgt] -> pos,count,mean_nll,ppl CSV (CP_EVAL_OUT); skips training + log/config writes (/dev/null). Base-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=1 (naive extrapolation) vs extended-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=4 curves show blow-up-vs-flat past orig ctx. (3) Notebook cell in graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb plots the CSVs + before/after-ctx PPL ratio verdict. Compile-verified (mpic++ -c, exit 0); server build/run pending - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb\\n153:2026-07-10 - Process-group UNIFICATION (prereq for DataParallel+ContextParallel coexisting in bluscriptCP): made BluTrain dist/communication ProcessGroupNCCL the single canonical PG for CP+DP. (A) Extended BluTrain PG (additive) with the CP ring-overlap surface ported to run on its own comm_: cpRingStream() + cp_ring_stream_, sendrecv_async_stream, all_gather_async_stream, alltoallv_async, alltoallv_async_stream; + comm-adopting ctor (wo