{"parentUuid":"3ad303f6-fdb2-4c20-a831-3241b3b49a9a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDMWXRhqZ5d2VoG8bKmN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019h6ECaooA17bnv17bFqwQA","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://github.com/bigai-nlco/CREAM","prompt":"List the repository's files and directories. What is the default branch? Is there a train.py? What does the README say CREAM does — specifically how it constructs randomized/manipulated position ids for context window extension? Summarize the method."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":67680,"output_tokens":213,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":213,"cache_read_input_tokens":67680,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDMWTjx1h8Gz5ttQHqXj","type":"assistant","uuid":"a7604696-f389-41f2-8218-314a3eba9d70","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:02:39.590Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a7604696-f389-41f2-8218-314a3eba9d70","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5f5c15a1-f104-4841-968c-d1e3de6d4476","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019h6ECaooA17bnv17bFqwQA","type":"tool_result","content":"# CREAM Repository Overview\n\n## Files and Directories\nThe repository contains:\n- `img/` - Images for documentation\n- `lm-evaluation-harness/lm_eval/` - Evaluation framework\n- `scripts/` - Training and evaluation scripts\n- `src/` - Source code\n- `README.md`, `requirements.txt`, `run_eval.sh`\n\n**Default branch:** master\n\n**train.py:** Not explicitly listed in the file tree shown.\n\n## What CREAM Does\n\nAccording to the README, \"CREAM\" stands for **Continuity-Relativity indexing with gaussian Middle**. The method works by:\n\n1. **Position Index Manipulation:** It \"interpolates positional encodings by manipulating position indices\" rather than modifying the encodings directly.\n\n2. **Gaussian-Focused Sampling:** During fine-tuning, the approach introduces \"a truncated Gaussian to encourage sampling from the middle part of the context,\" targeting the \"Lost-in-the-Middle\" problem.\n\n3. **Efficient Extension:** The technique \"only requires fine-tuning at the pre-trained context window\" (e.g., 4K tokens) while extending models to much longer sequences (e.g., 256K tokens).\n\nIn essence, CREAM extends LLM context windows by strategically sampling middle-context positions during training, using position index interpolation rather than traditional positional encoding modifications."}]},"uuid":"19c4da49-51bd-495a-b712-5ba51c516163","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:02:52.085Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":286642,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# CREAM Repository Overview\n\n## Files and Directories\nThe repository contains:\n- `img/` - Images for documentation\n- `lm-evaluation-harness/lm_eval/` - Evaluation framework\n- `scripts/` - Training and evaluation scripts\n- `src/` - Source code\n- `README.md`, `requirements.txt`, `run_eval.sh`\n\n**Default branch:** master\n\n**train.py:** Not explicitly listed in the file tree shown.\n\n## What CREAM Does\n\nAccording to the README, \"CREAM\" stands for **Continuity-Relativity indexing with gaussian Middle**. The method works by:\n\n1. **Position Index Manipulation:** It \"interpolates positional encodings by manipulating position indices\" rather than modifying the encodings directly.\n\n2. **Gaussian-Focused Sampling:** During fine-tuning, the approach introduces \"a truncated Gaussian to encourage sampling from the middle part of the context,\" targeting the \"Lost-in-the-Middle\" problem.\n\n3. **Efficient Extension:** The technique \"only requires fine-tuning at the pre-trained context window\" (e.g., 4K tokens) while extending models to much longer sequences (e.g., 256K tokens).\n\nIn essence, CREAM extends LLM context windows by strategically sampling middle-context positions during training, using position index interpolation rather than traditional positional encoding modifications.","durationMs":7604,"url":"https://github.com/bigai-nlco/CREAM"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba7cefce-73ea-4ce5-9512-1fdb190fc540","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
