{"parentUuid":"1fa3e53c-184d-4abf-a913-8aa82056d145","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDMbyWEyE92bBC5tzFoy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X8gWN2zuK3kAXVf3cUGpiR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Trace sharder and causal-mask position deps","prompt":"I am assessing whether a context-parallel training script can adopt \"CREAM\", which assigns each token a custom RoPE position label (non-contiguous: a head block, a gaussian-sampled middle block, and a tail block) while keeping a short physical sequence. I need to understand how sequence sharding and causal masking currently depend on tokens having contiguous positions 0..T-1.\n\nFocus ONLY on these files/dirs (do not wander broadly):\n- /home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp  (the forward() path, the sharding calls: shard_sequence_pre_embed and the hybrid variant, around lines 360-400)\n- /home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/  (the sequence sharder implementation — search for \"shard_sequence_pre_embed\", \"HeadTail\", \"load_balance\", \"load-balance\", \"permut\")\n- causal masking logic in the ring/ulysses attention (search for \"causal\", \"is_causal\", \"mask\", \"block_causal\")\n\nAnswer:\n1. Where is shard_sequence_pre_embed (and the hybrid version) defined? Show its signature and what it returns (does it return an idx_local plus any permutation/index info?). Show how it permutes tokens for the HeadTail load-balance scheme.\n2. Does the sharder produce or track any per-token index that maps a local shard slot back to its global sequence position? Or is that mapping implicit/recomputed elsewhere?\n3. How does the causal mask in the ring attention assume monotonic contiguous positions? Where exactly (file/function/lines)? Would non-contiguous CREAM position labels (still monotonic across head<middle<tail) break the causal correctness assumptions?\n4. In bluscriptCP.cpp forward(), trace how idx [B,T] flows: sharding -> embedding (wte) -> blocks -> CP attention. Confirm there is NO position_ids tensor currently threaded through.\n\nReport exact file paths, function names, line numbers, short code excerpts. Do not propose changes; just map the current mechanism.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_read_input_tokens":71197,"output_tokens":2732,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1434,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2732,"cache_read_input_tokens":71197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1434,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1434},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDMbvqkJjbt1smcwSDoa","type":"assistant","uuid":"07b7f0b5-f099-4db8-8080-375ff0a75db5","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:04:29.493Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
