  if (use_rope_ && q_gamma_.is_valid() && k_gamma_.is_valid()) {\\n1501:  // rank holds the full contiguous sequence -> pos_offset = 0.\\n1572:    const int cache_seq_len = static_cast<int>(cos_sin_cache_f_.shape().dims[0]);\\n1575:        packed.data<bfloat16_t>(), cos_sin_cache_f_.data<float>(),\\n1581:        cache_seq_len, /*pos_offset=*/0, eps_f_, interleaved_f_, /*is_causal=*/true);\\n1609:          packed, out_bf, lse, q_rstd, k_rstd, cos_sin_cache_f_, q_gamma_f_,\\n1611:          pre_sharded, B, nq_local, kv_local, hd, cache_seq_len, eps_f_,\\n1650:  // Set via enable_rope(). When false, none of these are read.\\n1651:  bool use_rope_ = false;\\n1652:  Tensor cos_sin_cache_;   // [cache_len, hd] cos/sin cache (resident, no grad)\\n1665:  Tensor cos_sin_cache_f_; // [cache_len, hd] fp32 cos/sin (resident, no grad)\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01WNQjGiFxmmjdH6S3P5Wei8\",\"duration_ms\":7}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:bash:pr-created\" \"scripts/hooks/post-bash-pr-created.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":38},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8ec50d20-f9f8-4386-a8b4-2db97067096a","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:06:06.564Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"8ec50d20-f9f8-4386-a8b4-2db97067096a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2738f77b3d044f59</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01X8gWN2zuK3kAXVf3cUGpiR</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2/tasks/a2738f77b3d044f59.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Trace sharder and causal-mask position deps\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I now have the complete mechanism mapped. Here are my findings.\n\n## 1. `shard_sequence_pre_embed` and the hybrid variant\n\n**File:** `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`\n\n**Return struct** (lines 81-85):\n```cpp\nstruct ShardedInputs {\n  Tensor idx_local;  // [B, T/n] int64\n  Tensor pos_local;  // [1, T/n] int64\n  Tensor y_local;    // [B, T/n] int64 (invalid Tensor if y_full was invalid)\n};\n```\n\n**`shard_sequence_pre_embed`** signature (lines 87-95):\n```cpp\ninline ShardedInputs shard_sequence_pre_embed(\n    const Tensor &amp;idx_full, const Tensor &amp;y_full, int64_t T_full,\n    int world_size, int rank, bool load_balance, DeviceIndex device)\n```\n\nIt builds a per-rank `perm_local` vector of global positions, then returns `idx_local` (gathered tokens), `pos_local` (those global positions), and `y_local`.\n\n**HeadTail permutation** (lines 126-137) — chunk-level PyTorch round-robin parity. Sequence is split into `2*world_size` chunks of `chunk_sz = T_full/(2*N)`; rank `r` owns chunks `(r, 2N-1-r)` laid out `[head_chunk | tail_chunk]`:\n```cpp\nint64_t chunk_sz = T_full / (2 * world_size);\nint64_t head_chunk = rank;\nint64_t tail_chunk = 2 * world_size - 1 - rank;\nfor (int64_t i = 0; i &lt; chunk_sz; ++i) {\n  perm_local[i]            = head_chunk * chunk_sz + i;\n  perm_local[chunk_sz + i] = tail_chunk * chunk_sz + i;\n}\n```\nContiguous (non-LB) branch (lines 123-125): `perm_local[i] = rank*T_local + i`. Tokens are then materialized either via `make_shards_inplace_axis` (contiguous, lines 150-161) or `OwnTensor::gather(idx_full, dim=1, gather_idx)` (HeadTail, lines 163-176).\n\n**`shard_sequence_pre_embed_hybrid`** signature (lines 194-202), composes ring-HeadTail (outer) with a contiguous Ulysses sub-slice (inner). It builds `perm_ring` (HeadTail for the ring block, lines 219-224) then takes a contiguous `perm_local` sub-slice for the ulysses rank (lines 226-230), and gathers identically.\n\n## 2. Per-token local→global mapping\n\nYes — `pos_local` **is** exactly that mapping (`[1, T_local]` holding each local slot's global position; built from `perm_local` at lines 139-148 and 230-235). **However it is dead metadata: it is produced but never consumed anywhere.** `grep` for `pos_local` across `context_parallel/` and the training script shows it is only ever assigned (`out.pos_local = ...`), never read. The training `forward()` uses only `sh.idx_local` and `sh.y_local` (the latter in the loss).\n\nInstead, global positions are **implicitly recomputed** inside the attention path via arithmetic on rank/step, in `compute_deltas` at `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h` (lines 58-89). It reconstructs each side's base offset from `rank`, ring step `i`, `world_size`, `T_local` (e.g. `head_base(x)=x*cs`, `tail_base(x)=(2N-1-x)*cs`), and RoPE indexes the cache as `global_pos(j) = j + (j&gt;=len/2 ? d1 : d0)` (line 48). This assumes each half is a **contiguous** ascending run of global positions.\n\n## 3. Causal mask assumption of contiguous monotonic positions\n\n**File:** `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`, in `forward_cp`.\n\nTwo coupled mechanisms:\n\n- **Ring-step causal decision** (lines 634-654): with load balance, `i==0` is `use_causal=true`, all other steps `use_causal=false`; without LB, future source ranks are skipped (`source_rank &gt; rank_` → `skip_step`), past ranks get full attention. This \"which ring step is diagonal/past/future\" logic is purely a function of `rank_`/`i`/`world_size_`, i.e. it assumes each rank's shard occupies a known contiguous global position band.\n\n- **Cross-chunk offsets** (lines 723-731): non-LB path sets `q_off = rank_*T_local`, `k_off = source_rank*T_local` — contiguous-position arithmetic fed to the kernel for masking.\n\n- **Sub-chunk slicing + LOCAL-index masking contract** (lines 748-770, the `&gt;&gt;&gt; CONTRACT` comment): the fused kernel (`GQA_fused_*_sm103_cp.cu`) \"does causal masking on LOCAL indices only.\" This is stated to be correct *only because* the Full / KHeadHalf / QTailHalf slicing \"keeps each ring step's tensor **LOCALLY MONOTONIC (local order == relative global order)**.\" The mask is `q_local_idx &gt;= k_local_idx` and relies on that local order equalling relative global order.\n\n**Would CREAM break this?** The causal-correctness assumption is not \"positions are 0..T-1 contiguous\" but \"local order equals relative global order,\" i.e. **monotonicity**. Since CREAM keeps labels monotonic across head&lt;middle&lt;tail, the boolean causal mask (`q&gt;=k`) would remain correct *as long as the sub-chunk slicing still yields locally-monotonic tensors*. What CREAM **does** break is the position-value reconstruction in `compute_deltas`/`rope_global_pos` (RopeDeltas.h): those compute positions as `base + j` (dense contiguous), so non-contiguous CREAM labels would be indexed into the RoPE cache incorrectly. Note the contract comment explicitly says \"The 4 deltas below drive RoPE cache indexing ONLY, never masking\" — so RoPE (delta) path is where non-contiguity bites, not the mask itself.\n\n## 4. Flow of `idx [B,T]` through `forward()` — no position_ids\n\n**File:** `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`\n\n- `forward(const Tensor&amp; idx)` at line 369.\n- Sharding (lines 375-384): `shard_sequence_pre_embed_hybrid(...)` or `shard_sequence_pre_embed(idx, empty_y, cfg.T, cp_size_, cp_rank_, load_balance=cfg.ring_mode, ...)` → `ShardedInputs sh`. Only `sh.idx_local` is used downstream; `sh.pos_local` is discarded.\n- Embedding (line 386): `Tensor x = wte.forward(sh.idx_local);` — comment explicitly notes \"NO wpe\" (no positional embedding table).\n- Blocks (lines 387-390): loop `x = attn[i]-&gt;forward(x); x = mlp[i]-&gt;forward(x);`.\n- CP attention: `CausalGQA::forward(const Tensor&amp; x)` (line 248) takes only `x`, computes q/k/v, and calls `cp_-&gt;forward_cp(q, k, v, /*unshard=*/false, /*pre_sharded=*/true)` (line 264). **No position tensor is passed.** RoPE positions are reconstructed internally by `compute_deltas` from rank/step.\n\n**Confirmed: there is NO `position_ids` tensor threaded through the forward path.** Positions exist only as (a) the unused `pos_local` from the sharder, and (b) values re-derived arithmetically inside `RopeDeltas.h::compute_deltas`, which assumes dense contiguous global positions per shard half.\n\n### Summary of what CREAM would touch\n- `pos_local` already carries the correct per-token global label but is currently ignored — nothing threads it into `wte`/blocks/`forward_cp`.\n- RoPE indexing (`compute_deltas` / `rope_global_pos` in `RopeDeltas.h`) assumes `base + local_j` contiguous positions — this is the core contiguity dependency that non-contiguous CREAM labels would violate.\n- The boolean causal mask depends on local monotonicity (order), not on contiguity, so monotonic CREAM labels (head&lt;middle&lt;tail) would keep the mask logically correct, but the ring-step skip/diagonal decisions and the delta arithmetic are all derived from rank/step contiguous-band assumptions rather than from actual position labels.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>47755</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>11</tool_uses><duration_ms>94113</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:06:03.614Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"32212af1-8e5d-4eae-9022-3d1a4d4ad40c","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:06:03.614Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
