{"parentUuid":"534ddb31-c85c-4eb4-8689-bb66b242eb17","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDNK15di6rbSEqwZmRdj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is verified. Confirmed the decisive fact: the wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from `cos_sin_cache.shape().dims[0]` ([FusedRoPESDPA.h:114](context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h#L114)), and at CP_SIZE=1 all deltas collapse to zero so `pos = local_idx`. This means single-GPU CREAM can be done by **gathering the cos/sin cache rows** — no CUDA kernel edits at all. Let me write the plan."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_read_input_tokens":108327,"output_tokens":5099,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5099,"cache_read_input_tokens":108327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDNJwycANvgifZVPYzkv","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1a3d090-318d-45ef-bd26-76147391420c","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:13:25.443Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"f1a3d090-318d-45ef-bd26-76147391420c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDNK15di6rbSEqwZmRdj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LyBvt5j4c25wL9DrM9RDbA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","content":"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n\n## Context\n\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\nchanges for single GPU.\n\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \"which variant\nhelps context extension\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\n\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\n\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\n\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\n\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\n\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\n\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n## Verification (end-to-end)\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\n\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_read_input_tokens":108327,"output_tokens":5099,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5099,"cache_read_input_tokens":108327,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDNJwycANvgifZVPYzkv","type":"assistant","uuid":"4e71455d-689d-465d-ba78-9ed0c8153141","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:14:17.431Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"4e71455d-689d-465d-ba78-9ed0c8153141","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5f5c15a1-f104-4841-968c-d1e3de6d4476","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LyBvt5j4c25wL9DrM9RDbA","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"63bc8877-742d-40e5-85dc-e41222430208","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:14:18.492Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","content":"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n\n## Context\n\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\nchanges for single GPU.\n\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \"which variant\nhelps context extension\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\n\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\n\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\n\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\n\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\n\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\n\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n## Verification (end-to-end)\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\n\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"06ebb248-cf3f-46ea-ab9a-c96649a9e319","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"63bc8877-742d-40e5-85dc-e41222430208","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDNQWwt6dz2Mje8hxDXb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5158,"cache_read_input_tokens":109784,"output_tokens":856,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5158,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":856,"cache_read_input_tokens":109784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5158},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDNQQpHEnpjz7fMHYJG7","type":"assistant","uuid":"a248858d-39fd-4fa5-94f9-eb057821060e","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:14:23.034Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a248858d-39fd-4fa5-94f9-eb057821060e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDNQWwt6dz2Mje8hxDXb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan is written. Here's the direct answer to your question, then I'll present the plan for approval.\n\n**Can bluscriptCP implement CREAM? Yes** — and more cleanly than you'd expect, because of how your RoPE works:\n\n- Your positions are never stored as data. The fused kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and looks up `cos_sin_cache[pos]` ([GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97](context_parallel/GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu#L94-L97)).\n- At **CP_SIZE=1** all deltas are zero, so `pos == local_idx`, and the wrapper reads `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's shape ([FusedRoPESDPA.h:114](context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h#L114)).\n- So CREAM = **gather the cache rows**: build the full scaled cache, generate CREAM labels `L[0..T)`, feed `cream_cache = gather(full_cache, 0, L)`. The unmodified kernel then rotates every token at its CREAM position. **No CUDA edits for single GPU.**\n\nOn your return-question — *which variant helps context extension?* All three do. **PoSE** is the seminal skip-wise method; **CREAM** improves on it with the truncated-Gaussian middle sampling to fix \"lost-in-the-middle\"; **RandPos** is a weaker random baseline. CREAM is the paper's contribution and the strongest, so the plan implements CREAM as primary behind a tiny generator interface that makes PoSE/RandPos ~10-line additions.\n\nThe files that change (single-GPU phase): a new `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h` (label generator), a one-line cache setter in `context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`, integration + env vars in `Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp` (build scaled cache, relax the `T != context_length` guard, install the gathered cache per step, wire the eval path), two tests, and README. Multi-GPU CP is deferred (needs an explicit per-token position array in the kernel, feeding the already-existing-but-unused `pos_local`)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5158,"cache_read_input_tokens":109784,"output_tokens":856,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5158,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":856,"cache_read_input_tokens":109784,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5158,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5158},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDNQQpHEnpjz7fMHYJG7","type":"assistant","uuid":"8767f2da-55e0-4dd3-b4de-fcba311abd51","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:14:33.679Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
