{"parentUuid":"edcb5c66-0044-41c7-a5e1-47f240f2d129","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDPGmfYmuWWZ7dZ8gTJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The source diff is decisive and confirms the reviewer's instinct on every point. Key findings from `/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223` + the call site (line 256, `fn_kwargs`):\n\n1. **Both head/tail branches are real** — `random.randint(0,1)` picks between `model_max//3` (big) and `4*factor` (small; = 32 when factor=8, i.e. the paper's `k=32`). My prose was faithful, but the generator must implement *both* with the random toggle.\n2. **`model_max` == the physical sequence length**, not a config pretrain constant (line 133 truncates the actual chunk to `model_max`). So in the reference `T == model_max` always, which is *why* `2*model_max/3 < T` never degenerates. The fix is to **bind the generator's `model_max := cfg.T`**.\n3. **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked**: line 256 `scaled_max = model_max * rope_scaling_factor`, and that same value is set as YaRN's `max_position_embeddings`/`original_max_position_embeddings`. So `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` must **not** be an independent env — it must be *derived* as `factor * T` with `factor = YARN_SCALE`. That directly resolves the \"two values that must agree\" hazard.\n\nLet me fold all of this into the plan."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4063,"cache_read_input_tokens":120249,"output_tokens":4175,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4063,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4175,"cache_read_input_tokens":120249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4063},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPGjAym4DaUPo7GKRhQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6082a48-7498-4160-8132-b12e9d0d5a14","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:22.725Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a6082a48-7498-4160-8132-b12e9d0d5a14","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDPGmfYmuWWZ7dZ8gTJk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","old_string":"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.","new_string":"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\n\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\n\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\n  \"1365+1365 > T\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\n  forbid.\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\n  one.\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4063,"cache_read_input_tokens":120249,"output_tokens":4175,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4063,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4175,"cache_read_input_tokens":120249,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4063},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPGjAym4DaUPo7GKRhQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc9665f8-eff9-43d6-9408-b76dca639745","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:37.464Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"cc9665f8-eff9-43d6-9408-b76dca639745","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"43e8493d-0495-4836-8c79-7da7628d5ae9","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:38.514Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.","newString":"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\n\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\n\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\n  \"1365+1365 > T\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\n  forbid.\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\n  one.\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.","originalFile":"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n\n## Context\n\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\nchanges for single GPU.\n\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \"which variant\nhelps context extension\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\n\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\n\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\n\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\n\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\n\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\n\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n## Verification (end-to-end)\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\n\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":45,"oldLines":6,"newStart":45,"newLines":34,"lines":[" (standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's"," optional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement."," ","+## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)","+","+These override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:","+","+- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to","+  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's","+  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that","+  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the","+  \"1365+1365 > T\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we","+  forbid.","+- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:","+  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the","+  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to","+  one.","+- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =","+  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's","+  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE","+  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO","+  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples","+  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.","+- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`","+  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq","+  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`","+  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).","+- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert","+  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a","+  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.","+"," ## Files to change"," "," 1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning)."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7cfed437-26e6-4807-bd55-4c3c6d908dc3","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"43e8493d-0495-4836-8c79-7da7628d5ae9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"new_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"newString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":45,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":45,\"newLines\":34,\"lines\":[\" (standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\",\" optional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\" \",\"+## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\",\"+\",\"+These override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\",\"+\",\"+- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\",\"+  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\",\"+  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\",\"+  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\",\"+  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\",\"+  forbid.\",\"+- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\",\"+  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\",\"+  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\",\"+  one.\",\"+- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\",\"+  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\",\"+  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\",\"+  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\",\"+  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\",\"+  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\",\"+- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\",\"+  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\",\"+  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\",\"+  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\",\"+- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\",\"+  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\",\"+  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"+\",\" ## Files to change\",\" \",\" 1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":23},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7536990f-0bef-44da-8132-053e77b64a65","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:37.535Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"7536990f-0bef-44da-8132-053e77b64a65","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"new_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"newString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":45,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":45,\"newLines\":34,\"lines\":[\" (standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\",\" optional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\" \",\"+## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\",\"+\",\"+These override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\",\"+\",\"+- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\",\"+  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\",\"+  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\",\"+  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\",\"+  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\",\"+  forbid.\",\"+- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\",\"+  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\",\"+  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\",\"+  one.\",\"+- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\",\"+  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\",\"+  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\",\"+  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\",\"+  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\",\"+  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\",\"+- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\",\"+  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\",\"+  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\",\"+  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\",\"+- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\",\"+  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\",\"+  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"+\",\" ## Files to change\",\" \",\" 1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":37},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e38724cd-488b-497a-99d8-33ced5f97aed","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:37.549Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"e38724cd-488b-497a-99d8-33ced5f97aed","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"new_string\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\"newString\":\"**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":45,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":45,\"newLines\":34,\"lines\":[\" (standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\",\" optional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\",\" \",\"+## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\",\"+\",\"+These override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\",\"+\",\"+- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\",\"+  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\",\"+  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\",\"+  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\",\"+  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\",\"+  forbid.\",\"+- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\",\"+  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\",\"+  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\",\"+  one.\",\"+- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\",\"+  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\",\"+  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\",\"+  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\",\"+  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\",\"+  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\",\"+- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\",\"+  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\",\"+  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\",\"+  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\",\"+- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\",\"+  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\",\"+  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\",\"+\",\" ## Files to change\",\" \",\" 1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_019mob4mk9H6z8ETnxtP1Pxq\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":39},"type":"attachment","uuid":"370e28a5-8557-437a-a0bf-9e2acb7ac671","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:37.551Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
