{"parentUuid":"8444a18a-e0d2-4375-b832-f19e685a895f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDPM4o3hdy4gzRDgcLGG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VDpUdxCUHHeSjTf3X8DEyv","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","old_string":"1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.","new_string":"1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4261,"cache_read_input_tokens":124312,"output_tokens":1350,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4261,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1350,"cache_read_input_tokens":124312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4261,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4261},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPLxiRou3WUaQHg7hqt","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f4aafdb-c338-4146-8fdc-38bc43f28c27","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:57.574Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"2f4aafdb-c338-4146-8fdc-38bc43f28c27","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VDpUdxCUHHeSjTf3X8DEyv","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"7625def8-f5f3-4bf1-9884-a14acc15dc2b","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:26:58.620Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).\n   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.","newString":"1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":76,"oldLines":9,"newStart":76,"newLines":23,"lines":[" ## Files to change"," "," 1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).","-   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int scaled_max, int model_max, float sigma, uint64_t seed, ...)` — C++ port of `CREAM()`: head block `[0,head_len)`, Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle via truncated-normal inverse-CDF (`std::erf`), tail block `[scaled_max-tail_len, scaled_max)`. `head_len=tail_len=model_max/3` or `4*factor` (random branch), `factor = scaled_max/model_max`.","-   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature (mirror `PoSE`/`RandPos` in `src/train.py`).","-   - Deterministic: takes an explicit seed (no `Date.now`-style hidden state), so runs are reproducible and testable.","+   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`","+     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`","+     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:","+     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.","+     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.","+     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,","+       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`","+       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),","+       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.","+     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).","+     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a","+       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.","+   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature","+     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).","+   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.","+   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a","+     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector."," "," 2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:","    - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8fe04e98-925d-420d-9cc2-1beba4a3287a"