960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.","new_string":"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1436,"cache_read_input_tokens":128573,"output_tokens":2091,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1436,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2091,"cache_read_input_tokens":128573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1436,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1436},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPNSWnZwfcs8MgSNmHh","type":"assistant","uuid":"d0a18c6a-91a9-4acb-aa88-27ea32a73a12","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:23.133Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"d0a18c6a-91a9-4acb-aa88-27ea32a73a12","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015LTx26th4QwtSsGAuy7g8X","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"59e5c6ac-1a60-4240-bed5-a2b3d257fe29","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:24.183Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.","newString":"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":95,"oldLines":14,"newStart":95,"newLines":15,"lines":["      clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector."," "," 2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:","-   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.","+   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack)."," "," 3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:","-   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).","-   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.","-   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.","-   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).","-   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.","+   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).","+   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.","+   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.","+   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.","+   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.","+   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's."," "," 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:","    - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"856cbd4c-834f-4c80-b8c0-754c4501b806","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
