*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\",\"new_string\":\"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\",\"newString\":\"2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\\n   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: assert that feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse harness from `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`). This is the core correctness proof of the no-CUDA trick.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":95,\"oldLines\":14,\"newStart\":95,\"newLines\":15,\"lines\":[\"      clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\",\" \",\" 2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\",\"-   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched.\",\"+   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\",\" \",\" 3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\",\"-   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` (target extended length; also usable as `scaled_max` = `YARN_SCALE * orig`), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA`, optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\",\"-   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` instead of `context_length` (extend the `build_rope_cache` call at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\",\"-   - **Guard:** relax `T != context_length` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) so that under CREAM the cache length (`scaled_max`) is legitimately decoupled from physical `T`.\",\"-   - **Per-step install:** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(...)`; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd — cache carries no grad); then loop layers and call `blk.attn.cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` before the block loop. Expose the layer's `cp_` (add a small accessor on `CausalGQA`/the block, or a `set_rope_cache` fan-out on the model).\",\"-   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), allow the same install so PPL-vs-position can be measured under CREAM/extended labels (a fixed labeling, not resampled) vs the naive-extrapolation baseline already supported.\",\"+   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\",\"+   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\",\"+   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\",\"+   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\",\"+   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"+   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\" \",\" 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\",\"    - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` (monotonic head<middle<tail, correct block lengths, middle within `[head_len, scaled_max-tail_len)`, boundary/`factor` edge cases, PoSE/RandPos shapes). Follows the existing `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp` style.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_015LTx26th4QwtSsGAuy7g8X\",\"duration_ms\":3}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":24},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c22c6f8a-cb58-476d-8b9e-3715e4294fc5","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:23.204Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
