the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \"no NaN\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \"focus the middle\" property — this is the check that catches it.\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":120,"oldLines":9,"newStart":120,"newLines":11,"lines":[" - Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`)."," "," ## Verification (end-to-end)","-1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).","-2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).","-3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.","+1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).","+2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.","+3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).","+4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \"no NaN\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \"focus the middle\" property — this is the check that catches it.","+5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell."," "," ## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)"," Multi-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6275bc0-60c7-457b-b556-4c280feac11e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b8fba5c6-60c8-4063-89d0-33657af477a0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"new_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"newString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` — (a) monotonic head<middle<tail; (b) exact block lengths for BOTH branches (`T/3` and `4*factor`); (c) middle within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; (d) total length == `T`; (e) generator guards throw on `factor<2`/`head+tail>=T`; (f) **diff a few seeded draws against values hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`** (mu, cdf, end_id bounds) so a silent formula drift fails here. PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":120,\"oldLines\":9,\"newStart\":120,\"newLines\":11,\"lines\":[\" - Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\",\" \",\" ## Verification (end-to-end)\",\"-1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\",\"-2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\",\"-3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"+1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\",\"+2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\",\"+3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\",\"+4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\",\"+5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\" \",\" ## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\",\" Multi-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":24},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4de0d28c-0fde-409e-ad8a-30e68c6ef65c","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:52.033Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"4de0d28c-0fde-409e-ad8a-30e68c6ef65c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"new_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"newString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` — (a) monotonic head<middle<tail; (b) exact block lengths for BOTH branches (`T/3` and `4*factor`); (c) middle within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; (d) total length == `T`; (e) generator guards throw on `factor<2`/`head+tail>=T`; (f) **diff a few seeded draws against values hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`** (mu, cdf, end_id bounds) so a silent formula drift fails here. PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":120,\"oldLines\":9,\"newStart\":120,\"newLines\":11,\"lines\":[\" - Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\",\" \",\" ## Verification (end-to-end)\",\"-1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\",\"-2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\",\"-3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"+1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\",\"+2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\",\"+3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\",\"+4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\",\"+5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\" \",\" ## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\",\" Multi-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":32},"type":"attachment","uuid":"921ac4d9-ac25-4aaa-8a1f-67005b1c1d9c","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:52.041Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"921ac4d9-ac25-4aaa-8a1f-67005b1c1d9c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"b6e0f4bb-988e-4012-8207-4018bb36f343\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"new_string\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"newString\":\"## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` — (a) monotonic head<middle<tail; (b) exact block lengths for BOTH branches (`T/3` and `4*factor`); (c) middle within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; (d) total length == `T`; (e) generator guards throw on `factor<2`/`head+tail>=T`; (f) **diff a few seeded draws against values hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`** (mu, cdf, end_id bounds) so a silent formula drift fails here. PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\\n3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":120,\"oldLines\":9,\"newStart\":120,\"newLines\":11,\"lines\":[\" - Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\",\" \",\" ## Verification (end-to-end)\",\"-1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path).\",\"-2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX=<N*T> YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs; confirm `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit (regression guard).\",\"-3. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt evaluated at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\"+1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\",\"+2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\",\"+3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\",\"+4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\",\"+5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\",\" \",\" ## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\",\" Multi-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Vjb5NLNPgHBBBf4BtCWJKx\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":33},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b8d7a084-5962-473c-a55b-91d516a444da","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:27:52.042Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b8d7a084-5962-473c-a55b-91d516a444da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDPSbPSqgkdLxZwV5z2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plan now incorporates every point from the review, grounded in the actual source diff. Summary of what changed:\n\n- **Head/tail regime (the main catch):** confirmed both branches (`T/3` and `4*factor`=paper's `k=32`) are real and randomly toggled — port both faithfully. The degenerate-middle fear is resolved by binding the generator's `model_max := cfg.T` (as the reference does), so `head+tail = 2T/3 < T` by construction; a `head+tail < T` guard is still added for the `4*factor` branch at tiny `T`.\n- **Locked scale:** dropped the independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env — `factor = YARN_SCALE`, `scaled_max = factor*T` are derived, with startup asserts (`YARN_SCALE>1`, `factor>=2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`). This kills the two-values-must-agree hazard.\n- **YaRN composition made explicit** + a cache spot-check test that the gathered rows are YaRN-interpolated, not plain-extrapolated.\n- **Guard replacement** (not deletion) for `T != context_length`.\n- **Distributional check** on the middle-block start histogram added to verification, since \"loss decreases\" can't catch a wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF.\n- **Off-mode bit-for-bit regression applied to the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path too**, not just training.\n- Smaller items: `set_rope_cache` asserted gradient-free; gather-once-fan-out-to-all-layers made explicit with a comment; unit test diffs seeded draws against the mirrored source lines.\n\nThe structural design (cache-row gather exploiting delta-collapse-to-zero, decoupled from causal masking, deferring per-token position arrays to CP>1) is unchanged — the review affirmed it."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":133238,"output_tokens":654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":133238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPSWo8E65sPHQQFrVqn","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b02efc6-0394-43df-bffe-14b2b6340604","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:28:05.506Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"5b02efc6-0394-43df-bffe-14b2b6340604","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDPSbPSqgkdLxZwV5z2c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019jfGkYY5Z9tynUTXHGoYv9","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n\n## Context\n\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\nchanges for single GPU.\n\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \"which variant\nhelps context extension\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\n\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\n\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\n\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\n\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\n\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\n\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\n  \"1365+1365 > T\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\n  forbid.\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\n  one.\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, testable, immutable/value-returning).\n   - `std::vector<int64_t> generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, float sigma, uint64_t seed)`\n     — a **line-by-line** C++ port of `CREAM()` (`/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`), with `model_max := T`\n     and `scaled_max := factor * T`:\n     - `rand_num = randint(0,1)`; branch 0 -> `head=tail=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head=tail=4*factor`.\n     - `len_chunk = T - head - tail`; `pos_ids_1 = [0,head)`; `pos_ids_3 = [factor*T - tail, factor*T)`.\n     - Middle: `mu = 1+factor`, `sigma` (default 3.0, from env); build `x = linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`,\n       `cdf = 0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`; draw `u ~ U(0,1)`, `rand_factor = round(interp(u, cdf, x))`\n       clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`; `end_id = randint(head + (len_chunk-1)*(rand_factor/2),\n       (rand_factor/2)*T - tail - 1)`; `pos_ids_2 = [end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`.\n     - Return `pos_ids_1 ++ pos_ids_2 ++ pos_ids_3` (length exactly `T`).\n     - **Do NOT** re-derive constants from memory — match the mirrored source; the unit test diffs a\n       few seeded draws against hand-computed values from those exact lines.\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` and `generate_randpos_positions(...)` sharing the signature\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\n   - Deterministic: explicit `seed` (no hidden global state), so runs are reproducible and testable.\n   - Guards inside the generator: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a\n     clear message rather than emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) label vector.\n\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — add a per-step cache setter:\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` (updates the resident cache used by both `forward_cp` and, via stored state, the backward). Cheap value swap; `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape. No delta/mask logic touched. The stored tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — build it with `with_req_grad(false)` and assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter (same shared-buffer discipline used elsewhere in this stack).\n\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\n   - **Cache build:** when CREAM is on, build the full cache at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (reuse `build_rope_cache` at `bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`); keep the base-cache path untouched when off.\n   - **Guard replacement:** the `T != context_length` check (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) is relaxed under CREAM but REPLACED by the narrower invariants above (`scaled_max = factor*T`), not merely deleted.\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\n\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: unit-test `generate_cream_positions` — (a) monotonic head<middle<tail; (b) exact block lengths for BOTH branches (`T/3` and `4*factor`); (c) middle within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; (d) total length == `T`; (e) generator guards throw on `factor<2`/`head+tail>=T`; (f) **diff a few seeded draws against values hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`** (mu, cdf, end_id bounds) so a silent formula drift fails here. PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\n\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\n\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n## Verification (end-to-end)\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \"no NaN\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \"focus the middle\" property — this is the check that catches it.\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\n\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\n","planFilePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_read_input_tokens":133238,"output_tokens":654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":133238,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1173},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDPSWo8E65sPHQQFrVqn","type":"assistant","uuid":"04d45218-fded-49d0-ba48-00cd4a3c351a","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:28:05.507Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
