{"parentUuid":"2afe3814-8d7e-43ff-b247-77d26e7f0595","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"2dc3d4e1-864e-4e28-83d1-0ae1e9a7bef8","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:36:13.161Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.","newString":"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":127,"oldLines":7,"newStart":127,"newLines":7,"lines":["    - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.","    - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.","    - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.","-   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.","+   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.","    - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's."," "," 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1fdac049-f2c2-4dd3-9931-2613a85ab39a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"2dc3d4e1-864e-4e28-83d1-0ae1e9a7bef8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"newString\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Non-destructive / additive invariant (hard requirement)\\n\\nEvery change is **purely additive and gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`**. No existing line's default\\nbehavior is altered or removed. With `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` (the default) the program must be\\n**bit-for-bit identical to today** — same cache built the same way, same guard, same forward, same\\neval. New behavior lives in new files, new members, new methods, and `if (cream_on) { ... } else\\n{ <existing code verbatim> }` branches. This mirrors the established additive-gating discipline\\nalready used in the CP stack (e.g. `-DCP_FUSED_ROPE` in `FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and the\\n`use_rope_==false` default path in `ContextParallel.h:749`). Nothing existing is erased.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, immutable/value-returning). Split into\\n   THREE layers so every cross-language hazard is isolated and unit-testable independent of RNG parity\\n   (a **line-by-line** port of `CREAM()` `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`, with `model_max := T`,\\n   `scaled_max := factor * T`):\\n\\n   - **(a) Pure math layer** — `std::vector<int64_t> cream_labels_from_draws(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor, int64_t end_id)`: given fully-resolved draws, assemble labels.\\n     `head=tail = (branch==0 ? T/3 : 4*factor)`; `len_chunk = T - head - tail`;\\n     `pos_ids_1=[0,head)`; `pos_ids_2=[end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`; `pos_ids_3=[factor*T-tail, factor*T)`;\\n     return the concat (length exactly `T`). No randomness — this is the deterministic transform.\\n   - **(b) Range/CDF layer** — the two spots where language semantics bite:\\n     - `int rand_factor_from_u(double u, int factor, double sigma)`: `mu=1+factor`;\\n       `x=linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`; `cdf=0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`;\\n       `rand_factor = round(np_interp(u, /*xp=*/cdf, /*fp=*/x))` clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`.\\n       **`np_interp` argument order MUST be `(query=u, xp=cdf, fp=x)`** — look `u` up against the CDF\\n       domain, return the `x` value (matches `np.interp(u, cdf, x)`); a swapped `xp/fp` silently\\n       samples the wrong distribution. Use a dedicated `np_interp` helper, not a generic one whose\\n       arg convention might differ.\\n     - `std::pair<int64_t,int64_t> end_id_range(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor)`:\\n       `lo = head + (len_chunk-1) * (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0)`,\\n       `hi = (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0) * T - tail - 1`, each floored to int.\\n       **`rand_factor/2` MUST be true division** (`rand_factor` is odd ~half the time; integer\\n       floor-division here biases `end_id` for half of all draws) — cast to `double` at BOTH sites.\\n   - **(c) Sampling wrapper** — `generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, double sigma, uint64_t seed)`:\\n     draws `branch = randint(0,1)`, `u = U[0,1)`, then `[lo,hi]=end_id_range(...)`,\\n     `end_id = randint(lo,hi)`, and returns `cream_labels_from_draws(...)`. Use\\n     **`std::uniform_int_distribution<int64_t>(a,b)`** for every `randint` (inclusive on BOTH ends,\\n     matching Python's `random.randint`) — never a hand-rolled `a + rng()%(b-a)` (excludes `b`).\\n     Explicit `seed` (no hidden global state). No claim of RNG-stream parity with Python — that is\\n     deliberately NOT relied on (see test 4).\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` / `generate_randpos_positions(...)` factored the same way\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Guards: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a clear message rather than\\n     emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — ADD a per-step cache setter (new method only; no existing member/method changed):\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` — points the resident cache at the caller's tensor. This is called ONLY when CREAM is on; when off it is never invoked and `cos_sin_cache_` keeps exactly the value `enable_rope()` gave it (existing behavior untouched). `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape, so no other code changes. No delta/mask logic touched. The passed tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — built with `with_req_grad(false)`; assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\\n   - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: because RNG streams are NOT bit-identical across Python and C++,\\n     the golden test targets the DETERMINISTIC layers with **injected draws** (not \\\"same seed\\\"):\\n     - **Golden math** — feed `(branch, rand_factor, end_id)` tuples *captured by running the actual\\n       Python reference once* into `cream_labels_from_draws(...)` and assert the exact label vector.\\n       Capture-and-commit those tuples as fixtures (a tiny script noted in the test header).\\n     - **Range/CDF** — assert `rand_factor_from_u(u,...)` and `end_id_range(...)` against values\\n       hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:209-219`; specifically include an ODD `rand_factor`\\n       case to catch integer-vs-true division, and an `interp` case that would differ if `xp/fp` were\\n       swapped.\\n     - **Structural** — monotonic head<middle<tail; exact block lengths for BOTH branches; middle\\n       within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; total length == `T`; guards throw on `factor<2` / `head+tail>=T`.\\n     - **randint convention** — a direct assert that the wrapper's `randint(a,b)` can return `b`\\n       (inclusive upper bound).\\n     - PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":127,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":127,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\",\"    - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\",\"    - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\",\"-   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"+   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"    - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\" \",\" 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF\",\"duration_ms\":5}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":24},"type":"attachment","uuid":"236da6f5-0e09-4843-87d6-3a4631b06f37","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:36:12.182Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"236da6f5-0e09-4843-87d6-3a4631b06f37","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"newString\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Non-destructive / additive invariant (hard requirement)\\n\\nEvery change is **purely additive and gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`**. No existing line's default\\nbehavior is altered or removed. With `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` (the default) the program must be\\n**bit-for-bit identical to today** — same cache built the same way, same guard, same forward, same\\neval. New behavior lives in new files, new members, new methods, and `if (cream_on) { ... } else\\n{ <existing code verbatim> }` branches. This mirrors the established additive-gating discipline\\nalready used in the CP stack (e.g. `-DCP_FUSED_ROPE` in `FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and the\\n`use_rope_==false` default path in `ContextParallel.h:749`). Nothing existing is erased.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, immutable/value-returning). Split into\\n   THREE layers so every cross-language hazard is isolated and unit-testable independent of RNG parity\\n   (a **line-by-line** port of `CREAM()` `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`, with `model_max := T`,\\n   `scaled_max := factor * T`):\\n\\n   - **(a) Pure math layer** — `std::vector<int64_t> cream_labels_from_draws(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor, int64_t end_id)`: given fully-resolved draws, assemble labels.\\n     `head=tail = (branch==0 ? T/3 : 4*factor)`; `len_chunk = T - head - tail`;\\n     `pos_ids_1=[0,head)`; `pos_ids_2=[end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`; `pos_ids_3=[factor*T-tail, factor*T)`;\\n     return the concat (length exactly `T`). No randomness — this is the deterministic transform.\\n   - **(b) Range/CDF layer** — the two spots where language semantics bite:\\n     - `int rand_factor_from_u(double u, int factor, double sigma)`: `mu=1+factor`;\\n       `x=linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`; `cdf=0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`;\\n       `rand_factor = round(np_interp(u, /*xp=*/cdf, /*fp=*/x))` clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`.\\n       **`np_interp` argument order MUST be `(query=u, xp=cdf, fp=x)`** — look `u` up against the CDF\\n       domain, return the `x` value (matches `np.interp(u, cdf, x)`); a swapped `xp/fp` silently\\n       samples the wrong distribution. Use a dedicated `np_interp` helper, not a generic one whose\\n       arg convention might differ.\\n     - `std::pair<int64_t,int64_t> end_id_range(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor)`:\\n       `lo = head + (len_chunk-1) * (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0)`,\\n       `hi = (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0) * T - tail - 1`, each floored to int.\\n       **`rand_factor/2` MUST be true division** (`rand_factor` is odd ~half the time; integer\\n       floor-division here biases `end_id` for half of all draws) — cast to `double` at BOTH sites.\\n   - **(c) Sampling wrapper** — `generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, double sigma, uint64_t seed)`:\\n     draws `branch = randint(0,1)`, `u = U[0,1)`, then `[lo,hi]=end_id_range(...)`,\\n     `end_id = randint(lo,hi)`, and returns `cream_labels_from_draws(...)`. Use\\n     **`std::uniform_int_distribution<int64_t>(a,b)`** for every `randint` (inclusive on BOTH ends,\\n     matching Python's `random.randint`) — never a hand-rolled `a + rng()%(b-a)` (excludes `b`).\\n     Explicit `seed` (no hidden global state). No claim of RNG-stream parity with Python — that is\\n     deliberately NOT relied on (see test 4).\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` / `generate_randpos_positions(...)` factored the same way\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Guards: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a clear message rather than\\n     emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — ADD a per-step cache setter (new method only; no existing member/method changed):\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` — points the resident cache at the caller's tensor. This is called ONLY when CREAM is on; when off it is never invoked and `cos_sin_cache_` keeps exactly the value `enable_rope()` gave it (existing behavior untouched). `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape, so no other code changes. No delta/mask logic touched. The passed tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — built with `with_req_grad(false)`; assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\\n   - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: because RNG streams are NOT bit-identical across Python and C++,\\n     the golden test targets the DETERMINISTIC layers with **injected draws** (not \\\"same seed\\\"):\\n     - **Golden math** — feed `(branch, rand_factor, end_id)` tuples *captured by running the actual\\n       Python reference once* into `cream_labels_from_draws(...)` and assert the exact label vector.\\n       Capture-and-commit those tuples as fixtures (a tiny script noted in the test header).\\n     - **Range/CDF** — assert `rand_factor_from_u(u,...)` and `end_id_range(...)` against values\\n       hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:209-219`; specifically include an ODD `rand_factor`\\n       case to catch integer-vs-true division, and an `interp` case that would differ if `xp/fp` were\\n       swapped.\\n     - **Structural** — monotonic head<middle<tail; exact block lengths for BOTH branches; middle\\n       within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; total length == `T`; guards throw on `factor<2` / `head+tail>=T`.\\n     - **randint convention** — a direct assert that the wrapper's `randint(a,b)` can return `b`\\n       (inclusive upper bound).\\n     - PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":127,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":127,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\",\"    - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\",\"    - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\",\"-   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"+   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"    - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\" \",\" 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF\",\"duration_ms\":5}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":40},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cfb00ec8-c5de-4a88-b00c-14e0dd254e90","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:36:12.198Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"cfb00ec8-c5de-4a88-b00c-14e0dd254e90","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"newString\":\"   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \\\"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\\\") extends a\\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that\\nrow (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\\n**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so\\n`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count\\n(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin\\nfor CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA\\nchanges for single GPU.\\n\\n**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to\\nserve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \\\"which variant\\nhelps context extension\\\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM\\nadds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random\\nbaseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos\\nbecome ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.\\n\\n## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather\\n\\nPer step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing\\n`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather\\n`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer\\nbefore running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks\\n`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the\\nsub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of\\nRoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are\\nmonotonic (head < middle < tail).\\n\\n**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so\\none CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample\\nfresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the\\nkernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk\\n(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's\\noptional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.\\n\\n## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)\\n\\nThese override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:\\n\\n- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to\\n  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's\\n  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that\\n  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the\\n  \\\"1365+1365 > T\\\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we\\n  forbid.\\n- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:\\n  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the\\n  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to\\n  one.\\n- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =\\n  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's\\n  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE\\n  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO\\n  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples\\n  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.\\n- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`\\n  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq\\n  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`\\n  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).\\n- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert\\n  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a\\n  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.\\n\\n## Non-destructive / additive invariant (hard requirement)\\n\\nEvery change is **purely additive and gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`**. No existing line's default\\nbehavior is altered or removed. With `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` (the default) the program must be\\n**bit-for-bit identical to today** — same cache built the same way, same guard, same forward, same\\neval. New behavior lives in new files, new members, new methods, and `if (cream_on) { ... } else\\n{ <existing code verbatim> }` branches. This mirrors the established additive-gating discipline\\nalready used in the CP stack (e.g. `-DCP_FUSED_ROPE` in `FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and the\\n`use_rope_==false` default path in `ContextParallel.h:749`). Nothing existing is erased.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, immutable/value-returning). Split into\\n   THREE layers so every cross-language hazard is isolated and unit-testable independent of RNG parity\\n   (a **line-by-line** port of `CREAM()` `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`, with `model_max := T`,\\n   `scaled_max := factor * T`):\\n\\n   - **(a) Pure math layer** — `std::vector<int64_t> cream_labels_from_draws(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor, int64_t end_id)`: given fully-resolved draws, assemble labels.\\n     `head=tail = (branch==0 ? T/3 : 4*factor)`; `len_chunk = T - head - tail`;\\n     `pos_ids_1=[0,head)`; `pos_ids_2=[end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`; `pos_ids_3=[factor*T-tail, factor*T)`;\\n     return the concat (length exactly `T`). No randomness — this is the deterministic transform.\\n   - **(b) Range/CDF layer** — the two spots where language semantics bite:\\n     - `int rand_factor_from_u(double u, int factor, double sigma)`: `mu=1+factor`;\\n       `x=linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`; `cdf=0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`;\\n       `rand_factor = round(np_interp(u, /*xp=*/cdf, /*fp=*/x))` clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`.\\n       **`np_interp` argument order MUST be `(query=u, xp=cdf, fp=x)`** — look `u` up against the CDF\\n       domain, return the `x` value (matches `np.interp(u, cdf, x)`); a swapped `xp/fp` silently\\n       samples the wrong distribution. Use a dedicated `np_interp` helper, not a generic one whose\\n       arg convention might differ.\\n     - `std::pair<int64_t,int64_t> end_id_range(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor)`:\\n       `lo = head + (len_chunk-1) * (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0)`,\\n       `hi = (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0) * T - tail - 1`, each floored to int.\\n       **`rand_factor/2` MUST be true division** (`rand_factor` is odd ~half the time; integer\\n       floor-division here biases `end_id` for half of all draws) — cast to `double` at BOTH sites.\\n   - **(c) Sampling wrapper** — `generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, double sigma, uint64_t seed)`:\\n     draws `branch = randint(0,1)`, `u = U[0,1)`, then `[lo,hi]=end_id_range(...)`,\\n     `end_id = randint(lo,hi)`, and returns `cream_labels_from_draws(...)`. Use\\n     **`std::uniform_int_distribution<int64_t>(a,b)`** for every `randint` (inclusive on BOTH ends,\\n     matching Python's `random.randint`) — never a hand-rolled `a + rng()%(b-a)` (excludes `b`).\\n     Explicit `seed` (no hidden global state). No claim of RNG-stream parity with Python — that is\\n     deliberately NOT relied on (see test 4).\\n   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` / `generate_randpos_positions(...)` factored the same way\\n     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).\\n   - Guards: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a clear message rather than\\n     emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) vector.\\n\\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — ADD a per-step cache setter (new method only; no existing member/method changed):\\n   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` — points the resident cache at the caller's tensor. This is called ONLY when CREAM is on; when off it is never invoked and `cos_sin_cache_` keeps exactly the value `enable_rope()` gave it (existing behavior untouched). `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape, so no other code changes. No delta/mask logic touched. The passed tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — built with `with_req_grad(false)`; assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter.\\n\\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:\\n   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).\\n   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\\n   - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\\n   - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\\n   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\\n   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\\n\\n4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\\n   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: because RNG streams are NOT bit-identical across Python and C++,\\n     the golden test targets the DETERMINISTIC layers with **injected draws** (not \\\"same seed\\\"):\\n     - **Golden math** — feed `(branch, rand_factor, end_id)` tuples *captured by running the actual\\n       Python reference once* into `cream_labels_from_draws(...)` and assert the exact label vector.\\n       Capture-and-commit those tuples as fixtures (a tiny script noted in the test header).\\n     - **Range/CDF** — assert `rand_factor_from_u(u,...)` and `end_id_range(...)` against values\\n       hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:209-219`; specifically include an ODD `rand_factor`\\n       case to catch integer-vs-true division, and an `interp` case that would differ if `xp/fp` were\\n       swapped.\\n     - **Structural** — monotonic head<middle<tail; exact block lengths for BOTH branches; middle\\n       within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; total length == `T`; guards throw on `factor<2` / `head+tail>=T`.\\n     - **randint convention** — a direct assert that the wrapper's `randint(a,b)` can return `b`\\n       (inclusive upper bound).\\n     - PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.\\n   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.\\n   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.\\n\\n5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.\\n\\n## Reuse (do not hand-roll)\\n- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.\\n- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.\\n- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.\\n- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.\\n- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\\n\\n## Verification (end-to-end)\\n1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).\\n2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.\\n3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).\\n4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \\\"no NaN\\\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \\\"focus the middle\\\" property — this is the check that catches it.\\n5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.\\n\\n## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)\\nMulti-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel\\n(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`\\noverriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused\\n`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail\\nshard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,\\n`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":127,\"oldLines\":7,\"newStart\":127,\"newLines\":7,\"lines\":[\"    - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.\",\"    - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.\",\"    - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.\",\"-   - **Per-step install (gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), when CREAM on: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)`; assert `head+tail < T` already enforced in the generator; `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(full_cache, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute this ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — with an explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for no benefit). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out.\",\"+   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.\",\"    - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.\",\" \",\" 4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01McmX2WqhhhJkVHL6YNgJPF\",\"duration_ms\":5}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":44},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8b6a5d9b-a5aa-49ee-9bdd-a159f8da72b4","timestamp":"2026-07-20T13:36:12.202Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
