{"parentUuid":"ef45add0-16c7-4523-bee2-5b7a0aa54754","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDSdk9hYZBqczWDR3KVN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018HwmCwFxCYZCvXA6J7ejyK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/blu-bridge25/CP; grep -n \"YARN\\|YaRN\\|re-warmup\\|CP_REWARMUP\\|context extension\\|bluscriptCP\\|CP_EVAL_PPL\" README.md | head -30","description":"Find README bluscriptCP/YaRN section anchors"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_read_input_tokens":248712,"output_tokens":183,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":183,"cache_read_input_tokens":248712,"cache_creation_input_tokens":342,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":342},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDSdhYw4z8NTS6Ak71w9","type":"assistant","uuid":"21c2f3fe-fb2b-4120-bcc8-6bf075f17bdc","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:09:50.457Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"21c2f3fe-fb2b-4120-bcc8-6bf075f17bdc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018HwmCwFxCYZCvXA6J7ejyK","type":"tool_result","content":"12:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) (fused QK-norm + RoPE + GQA,\n14:DataParallel — see [Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)](#context-parallel-llama-training-bluscriptcp).\n23:| `Scripts/BluTrain/` | `gpt2_cp_test.cpp` (GPT-2 CP trainer) + `bluscriptCP.cpp` (Llama-style CP trainer: Ring/Ulysses, fused RoPE+QK-norm+GQA) |\n153:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp        Build the Llama CP trainer (build/bluscriptCP_exec)\n154:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp [NP=2]  mpirun bluscriptCP on NP ranks (ring; drop the flag + CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses for Ulysses)\n163:## Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\n165:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) is a second, **Llama-style**\n244:### Environment variables (bluscriptCP)\n272:**Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup** — checkpoints go to `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run<N>_step_<S>.ckpt`; the run number `N` ties the CSV log (`CP_Training_logs/CP_Training_log<N>.csv`) and the checkpoint prefix, and is echoed at startup (`Checkpointing: ON -> …`).\n280:| `CP_REWARMUP` | 0 | **Resume-only** (`start_step > 0`): re-anchor a fresh LR warmup of this many steps at the resume step. `0` keeps the continuous schedule (the base warmup is absolute from step 0 and cannot re-ramp). |\n281:| `CP_REWARMUP_PEAK` | 1.0 | Peak of the re-warmup as a fraction of the run's `max_lr` (6e-4). E.g. `0.3` for a reduced long-context peak. |\n283:**RoPE / YaRN context extension** (the shared `build_rope_cache`; `YARN_SCALE=1.0` ⇒ plain RoPE)\n287:| `YARN_SCALE` | 1.0 | Context-extension factor; set to `target_ctx / orig_ctx`. |\n288:| `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` | 1024 | Original pretrain context length. |\n289:| `YARN_BETA_FAST` / `YARN_BETA_SLOW` | 32 / 1 | NTK-by-parts correction bounds. |\n291:`build_rope_cache` prints `[YaRN] … scale=<s>` at model init — `scale=1.000` means YaRN is **off**. Keep `CP_T == YARN_SCALE · YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` or it warns that the cache is sized for a different context than it is scaled for.\n293:**2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup).** To extend a model from `orig_ctx` to a longer context, run two stages rather than changing `CP_T` at peak LR (which meets the context-shift perplexity spike with full-strength updates):\n296:2. **Long-context stage** — resume with the extended `CP_T`, YaRN on, and a fresh **re-warmup to a reduced peak** so the spike is met with a gentle, rising LR:\n299:   CP_T=4096 YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=1024 \\\n301:   CP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\n305:   Model params are sequence-length- and world-size-independent (RoPE positions are computed, not learned), so the extended `CP_T` — and even a different world size — loads the same checkpoint; the RoPE cache is rebuilt from the YaRN env. Keep the architecture (`d_model` / heads / kv / layers / vocab) identical. Set `CP_MAX_STEPS` above the base-stage step (or pass `CP_CKPT_RESUME`) so the run is treated as incomplete — otherwise a completed run starts fresh instead of resuming.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"ba79fcb6-5dac-4c98-86f2-bc3ea50acf98","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:09:50.538Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"12:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) (fused QK-norm + RoPE + GQA,\n14:DataParallel — see [Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)](#context-parallel-llama-training-bluscriptcp).\n23:| `Scripts/BluTrain/` | `gpt2_cp_test.cpp` (GPT-2 CP trainer) + `bluscriptCP.cpp` (Llama-style CP trainer: Ring/Ulysses, fused RoPE+QK-norm+GQA) |\n153:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp        Build the Llama CP trainer (build/bluscriptCP_exec)\n154:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp [NP=2]  mpirun bluscriptCP on NP ranks (ring; drop the flag + CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses for Ulysses)\n163:## Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\n165:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) is a second, **Llama-style**\n244:### Environment variables (bluscriptCP)\n272:**Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup** — checkpoints go to `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run<N>_step_<S>.ckpt`; the run number `N` ties the CSV log (`CP_Training_logs/CP_Training_log<N>.csv`) and the checkpoint prefix, and is echoed at startup (`Checkpointing: ON -> …`).\n280:| `CP_REWARMUP` | 0 | **Resume-only** (`start_step > 0`): re-anchor a fresh LR warmup of this many steps at the resume step. `0` keeps the continuous schedule (the base warmup is absolute from step 0 and cannot re-ramp). |\n281:| `CP_REWARMUP_PEAK` | 1.0 | Peak of the re-warmup as a fraction of the run's `max_lr` (6e-4). E.g. `0.3` for a reduced long-context peak. |\n283:**RoPE / YaRN context extension** (the shared `build_rope_cache`; `YARN_SCALE=1.0` ⇒ plain RoPE)\n287:| `YARN_SCALE` | 1.0 | Context-extension factor; set to `target_ctx / orig_ctx`. |\n288:| `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` | 1024 | Original pretrain context length. |\n289:| `YARN_BETA_FAST` / `YARN_BETA_SLOW` | 32 / 1 | NTK-by-parts correction bounds. |\n291:`build_rope_cache` prints `[YaRN] … scale=<s>` at model init — `scale=1.000` means YaRN is **off**. Keep `CP_T == YARN_SCALE · YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` or it warns that the cache is sized for a different context than it is scaled for.\n293:**2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup).** To extend a model from `orig_ctx` to a longer context, run two stages rather than changing `CP_T` at peak LR (which meets the context-shift perplexity spike with full-strength updates):\n296:2. **Long-context stage** — resume with the extended `CP_T`, YaRN on, and a fresh **re-warmup to a reduced peak** so the spike is met with a gentle, rising LR:\n299:   CP_T=4096 YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=1024 \\\n301:   CP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\n305:   Model params are sequence-length- and world-size-independent (RoPE positions are computed, not learned), so the extended `CP_T` — and even a different world size — loads the same checkpoint; the RoPE cache is rebuilt from the YaRN env. Keep the architecture (`d_model` / heads / kv / layers / vocab) identical. Set `CP_MAX_STEPS` above the base-stage step (or pass `CP_CKPT_RESUME`) so the run is treated as incomplete — otherwise a completed run starts fresh instead of resuming.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d29555a9-46c0-46a6-a7a6-002d7aaa4593","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ba79fcb6-5dac-4c98-86f2-bc3ea50acf98","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_018HwmCwFxCYZCvXA6J7ejyK","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"32dd5294-a51c-4b70-b70c-e83ded2aeae2\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"high\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Bash\",\"tool_input\":{\"command\":\"cd /home/blu-bridge25/CP; grep -n \\\"YARN\\\\|YaRN\\\\|re-warmup\\\\|CP_REWARMUP\\\\|context extension\\\\|bluscriptCP\\\\|CP_EVAL_PPL\\\" README.md | head -30\",\"description\":\"Find README bluscriptCP/YaRN section anchors\"},\"tool_response\":{\"stdout\":\"12:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) (fused QK-norm + RoPE + GQA,\\n14:DataParallel — see [Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)](#context-parallel-llama-training-bluscriptcp).\\n23:| `Scripts/BluTrain/` | `gpt2_cp_test.cpp` (GPT-2 CP trainer) + `bluscriptCP.cpp` (Llama-style CP trainer: Ring/Ulysses, fused RoPE+QK-norm+GQA) |\\n153:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp        Build the Llama CP trainer (build/bluscriptCP_exec)\\n154:make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp [NP=2]  mpirun bluscriptCP on NP ranks (ring; drop the flag + CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses for Ulysses)\\n163:## Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\\n165:[Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) is a second, **Llama-style**\\n244:### Environment variables (bluscriptCP)\\n272:**Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup** — checkpoints go to `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run<N>_step_<S>.ckpt`; the run number `N` ties the CSV log (`CP_Training_logs/CP_Training_log<N>.csv`) and the checkpoint prefix, and is echoed at startup (`Checkpointing: ON -> …`).\\n280:| `CP_REWARMUP` | 0 | **Resume-only** (`start_step > 0`): re-anchor a fresh LR warmup of this many steps at the resume step. `0` keeps the continuous schedule (the base warmup is absolute from step 0 and cannot re-ramp). |\\n281:| `CP_REWARMUP_PEAK` | 1.0 | Peak of the re-warmup as a fraction of the run's `max_lr` (6e-4). E.g. `0.3` for a reduced long-context peak. |\\n283:**RoPE / YaRN context extension** (the shared `build_rope_cache`; `YARN_SCALE=1.0` ⇒ plain RoPE)\\n287:| `YARN_SCALE` | 1.0 | Context-extension factor; set to `target_ctx / orig_ctx`. |\\n288:| `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` | 1024 | Original pretrain context length. |\\n289:| `YARN_BETA_FAST` / `YARN_BETA_SLOW` | 32 / 1 | NTK-by-parts correction bounds. |\\n291:`build_rope_cache` prints `[YaRN] … scale=<s>` at model init — `scale=1.000` means YaRN is **off**. Keep `CP_T == YARN_SCALE · YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` or it warns that the cache is sized for a different context than it is scaled for.\\n293:**2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup).** To extend a model from `orig_ctx` to a longer context, run two stages rather than changing `CP_T` at peak LR (which meets the context-shift perplexity spike with full-strength updates):\\n296:2. **Long-context stage** — resume with the extended `CP_T`, YaRN on, and a fresh **re-warmup to a reduced peak** so the spike is met with a gentle, rising LR:\\n299:   CP_T=4096 YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=1024 \\\\\\n301:   CP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\\\\n305:   Model params are sequence-length- and world-size-independent (RoPE positions are computed, not learned), so the extended `CP_T` — and even a different world size — loads the same checkpoint; the RoPE cache is rebuilt from the YaRN env. Keep the architecture (`d_model` / heads / kv / layers / vocab) identical. Set `CP_MAX_STEPS` above the base-stage step (or pass `CP_CKPT_RESUME`) so the run is treated as incomplete — otherwise a completed run starts fresh instead of resuming.\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_018HwmCwFxCYZCvXA6J7ejyK\",\"duration_ms\":7}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:bash:pr-created\" \"scripts/hooks/post-bash-pr-created.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":32},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4ed9db4b-f44d-4c66-81fa-ffecc0d6d327","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:09:50.537Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
