CP files' #include process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> \\\"ProcessGroupNCCL.h\\\" (canonical). Collision: device_mesh.h's quote-include resolved CP's same-dir header first -> RENAMED (not deleted, per user) process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> ProcessGroupNCCL_cplegacy.h (dormant). (D) Makefile: +INCLUDES -IBluTrain/dist/communication/include -IBluTrain/dist/Data-Parallel/include; +BLUTRAIN_PG_SRC (processGroupNccl.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/Error_logs.cpp); CPP_EXCLUDE += process_group/processGroupNCCL.cpp. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED: builds clean (one ProcessGroupNCCL/Work/NCCLCHECK, no dup symbols); cp-rope-standin 12/12 PASS cos=1.0000000 (ring fwd+bwd+dgamma + ported overlap methods + ncclCommSplit 1D world identical to old CP PG); cp-ulysses 72 PASS, only the pre-existing bf16-ref-precision dQ/dq_gamma FAILs (unchanged by migration). Follow-ups: 2-D ncclCommSplit per-axis all-reduce test (needs 4 ranks), then bluscriptCP resume (wire DataParallel.cpp) - CP / BluTrain/dist/communication/{include/ProcessGroupNCCL.h,src/processGroupNccl.cpp}, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, context_parallel/*.h, Makefile2026-07-10 - bluscriptCP RESUME (CP Llama training on the unified PG): DataParallel + ContextParallel now coexist. Included DataParallel.hpp DIRECTLY (not the dist/distributed.h umbrella, which pulls the TP stack incl. a different class DeviceMesh -> collision); init_process_group comes from the canonical PG. Fixed double-init crash (\\\"process group instance already created\\\"): the DeviceMesh builds the world PG once (ncclCommSplit parent) and bluscriptCP now reuses it via new DeviceMesh::world_pg() for DataParallel instead of a 2nd init_process_group. Makefile: bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp targets; DataParallel.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/profiler.cpp scoped to this target only. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED (CP_FUSED_ROPE=1, tiny cfg L2/d256/hd64/GQA kv2/T256, edufineweb data in ~/Downloads via CP_DATA_ROOT): builds clean; world=1 trains loss 10.89->10.23 decreasing, finite grad-norm, fused-RoPE CP ring ran (first real training integration of the new kernels); ws=2 CP_SIZE=2 ring trains AND loss-parity vs world=1 (step0 10.884 vs 10.890, step4 10.2269 vs 10.2280) -> CP sequence-sharding + RoPE positions + ring correct end-to-end, and overlap-ON matching the serial reference proves the ring overlap is race-free (plan concern d). FOLLOW-UP: CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 diagnostic path crashes (\\\"convert_type_cuda: invalid resource handle\\\" — stream-handle issue under the unified PG; default overlap path unaffected + verified). Also pending: 2-D DPxCP run (dp>1), Ulysses-mode bluscriptCP (CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses), full-scale config - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, Makefile\\n2026-07-10 - bluscriptCP follow-ups #1/#3/#4 + ROOT-CAUSED a real sub-group-PG device bug. #1 CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 crash (\\\"convert_type/NCCL enqueue: invalid resource handle\\\") AND #3 Ulysses crash (\\\"Sync failed line 484 / Cuda 400 invalid resource handle\\\") had the SAME root cause introduced by the ncclCommSplit migration: BluTrain PG derived its CUDA device from rank_%gpus_per_node, and DeviceMesh passed the SUB-GROUP rank (my_group_rank); a size-1 DP axis has my_group_rank=0 -> its adopt-ctor set device 0, so the NEXT axis (CP) created its comm_stream while device=0 while its ncclCommSplit comm_ lived on device 1 -> stream/comm device mismatch (blocking collectives on communication_stream_ failed; overlap ring escaped it because cpRingStream is created lazily at ring-time on the correct device). FIX: adopt-ctor now cudaGetDevice(&local_rank_) (adopt caller's global physical device, don't derive from sub-group rank); DeviceMesh re-asserts cudaSetDevice(global_device) at the start of each axis iteration before ncclCommSplit/stream create. 2x3060 VERIFIED: cp-rope-standin 12/12 still PASS (1D regression); ws=2 ring no-overlap now trains + A/B matches overlap (step0 identical 10.884422, step4 diff 2e-5 => overlap race-free, plan concern d); #3 Ulysses ws=2 trains loss 10.890->10.228 with step0 parity vs world=1 (10.889622 vs 10.889627); #4 full-scale d768/L12/q12-kv4/T4096 114M params, CP_SIZE=2 (T_local=2048/rank), trains loss 11.02->10.21 no OOM/NaN on 2x3060. (#2 2D DPxCP deferred: needs 4 ranks.) - CP / BluTrain/dist/communication/src/processGroupNccl.cpp, process_group/device_mesh.cpp\\n2026-07-10 - Documented bluscriptCP in README.md: new \\\"Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\\\" section (Ring vs Ulysses build+run commands, CP_FUSED_ROPE=1-to-both-build-and-run + checkpoint-resume gotchas, full env-var reference incl. topology CP_SIZE/CP_ATTN_MODE/CP_ROTATOR, model/data CP_N_EMBD/LAYER/HEAD/KVHEAD/T/B/GLOBAL_BATCH/MAX_STEPS/WARMUP/DATA_ROOT, YaRN YARN_*, diagnostics CP_NO_OVERLAP*/RING_BLOCKING/SYNC_RING/NO_GPUS_PER_NODE, build flags CP_FUSED_ROPE/CP_ROPE_DEBUG, full-scale example), + bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp make targets, intro + repo-layout mentions - CP / README.md\\n2026-07-10 - Aligned bluscriptCP logging/terminal prints with gpt2_cp_test.cpp: added banner, ULYSSES attn-mode note, gpt2-style params block (Parameters/per-GPU/max_steps/warmup), per-step line (step|loss|lr|norm|dt|tok/sec|mem|Time Left) + [TIMING] breakdown via ported CudaTimer (event-based data/fwd/loss/bwd/clip/optim), validation-loss print, and the RUN-NUMBERED logging system (CP_Training_logs/CP_Training_log{N}.csv + _config.txt with GPU mem, run_number tied to ckpt prefix blumodelcp_run{N}, MPI_Bcast, CP_CKPT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME env, auto-resume-latest/complete->new-run scan of checkpoints_bluscriptcp). Kept the boxed Configuration block as-is per user. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED (world=1 tiny cfg): builds clean, all 4 log paths correct (fresh run1, complete->new run2, resume run2 from step3, CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN->run3), CSV/config.txt written, checkpoints run-numbered - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: added 2-stage re-warmup for YaRN context-extension resume + checkpoint-visibility prints. get_lr gained a warmup_start anchor (ramp [warmup_start, warmup_start+warmup) then cosine-decay; warmup_start=0 reproduces old schedule exactly) since the base schedule's warmup is absolute-from-0 and cannot re-ramp on resume. New env: CP_REWARMUP=<steps> (0=off, only when start_step>0) re-anchors a fresh warmup at the resume step, CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=<frac of max_lr, default 1.0> for a reduced long-context peak; prints \\\"[re-warmup] anchored at step S ...\\\". Also added checkpointing/ckpt_freq/dir to the boxed Configuration block and a \\\"Checkpointing: ON -> <dir>/<prefix>_step_<N>.ckpt (every F steps, keep K)\\\" line at run start (user noticed these weren't shown; root of an earlier \\\"not checkpointing\\\" confusion was just the default ckpt_freq=250 -> first save at step 250). Context: discussed that context extension causes a perplexity spike so stop base run DECAYED (not at peak) then re-warmup to a reduced peak (~0.3x). IMPLEMENTED, NOT YET BUILT/VERIFIED (user had a run on the box) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - Documented the above in README.md (bluscriptCP section): new \\\"Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup\\\" env table (CP_CKPT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME + CP_REWARMUP/CP_REWARMUP_PEAK, run-numbered ckpt/log naming, first-save-at-step-N note) and a \\\"2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup)\\\" subsection (base stage decay -> long-context resume with reduced-peak re-warmup, seq-len/world-size-independent checkpoint load, CP_MAX_STEPS/CP_CKPT_RESUME resumability gate) + a YaRN scale=1-means-off / CP_T==scale*orig_maxpos note - CP / README.md\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: silenced the DataLoader per-shard \\\"Current shard:\\\"/max_tokens debug spam during the RESUME replay (fired once per shard crossing x every rank). Added a NullBuf(std::streambuf) discard buffer; redirect std::cout->NullBuf around train_loader.skip_batches (all ranks) then restore, replaced with a single rank-0 line \\\"[resume] fast-forwarded data loader N batches (start_step*global_batch tokens)\\\". Change kept in bluscriptCP.cpp (main repo, syncs to server) rather than the Tensor-Implementations submodule DataLoader.h advance_shard() prints (sync friction). Residual: training-time shard crossings still print (submodule source). IMPLEMENTED, NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: rank-gated ALL stdout to rank 0 (standard MPI idiom) to stop world_size-times-duplicated library chatter ([CheckpointManager] Auto-loading latest, [CP ring A2A] OVERLAP, [CP bwd] overlap=ON etc. were printing x4 on 4 ranks). Redirect std::cout->static NullBuf on every non-master rank right after computing is_master; std::cerr left intact so per-rank errors still surface. Subsumes/complements the skip_batches rank-0 redirect (rank 0's cout stays live). Kept in bluscriptCP.cpp (main repo). NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP output cleanup pt2: the remaining x4-duplicated init banners ([YaRN] build_rope_cache, [CP ring P2P/A2A/AllGather], [CP sdpa fwd], [CP bwd] overlap) were fprintf(stderr) (NOT std::cout) so the cout redirect could not touch them. Added context_parallel/CPLog.h with cp::log_rank() (reads OMPI_COMM_WORLD_RANK, fallback PMI_RANK, unknown-launcher -> true so never silently lost) and gated all 6 one-time stderr notices on global rank 0 at source (RingRotator.h x3, ContextParallelBackward.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, YARNOps.cpp x2) - real stderr errors from other ranks stay visible (vs a blanket stderr redirect). All main-repo context_parallel/ files (sync to server, no submodule). NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}\\n2026-07-11 - FIX build break from the above: CPLog.h used a GLOBAL 'namespace cp', but the CP stack already has OwnTensor::cp (cp::ulysses_combine/head_repeat_interleave/...) -> two 'cp' in scope made EVERY cp:: reference ambiguous (server error: \\\"reference to 'cp' is ambiguous\\\", cascaded across ContextParallel/Ulysses/RingRotator). Renamed namespace cp -> cplog (unique, global) + updated all 6 call sites to cplog::log_rank(); existing cp::ulysses_* now resolve cleanly again. Verified by grep (no cp::log_rank left, 6 cplog sites, 1 def). NOT BUILT locally (avoid contending with user's run) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}\\n\\n2026-07-13 - LlamaFactory v1 DeepSpeed+Ulysses from-scratch PT reference for 48M Qwen3 (to compare vs CP-Ulysses bluscriptCP): mapped that Ulysses SP lives ONLY in v1 (cp_mode/cp_size plugin, patches flash-attn fwd) while stage:pt+train_from_scratch live only in v0; built qwen3_48m/ config matching bluscriptCP.cpp cfg exactly (d384/L6/qh6/kvh2/hd64/ffn1024/vocab50304-gpt2/no-tie/rope5e5/rms1e-5 = 48.076M total), seeded random-init checkpoint, empty-prompt-alpaca pretrain data (full-seq LM loss), v1 deepspeed+ulysses cp_size2 YAML. Found v1 has NO true from-config random-init (meta path chunk-loads a checkpoint) -> materialize seeded random weights to disk then load. Validated no-CP fsdp2 run: loss 10.96 ~ ln(vocab), decreasing, from-scratch confirmed. flash-attn (req for Ulysses) compiling from source on cu130. Caveats logged: v1 constant-LR + AdamW wd0.01 only (no cosine/warmup/wd0.1 without custom plugin); chat-wrapper neutralized via custom_chat_template - LlamaFactory / qwen3_48m/{config.json,model.safetensors,pretrain_data.yaml,validate_nocp.yaml}, examples/v1/train_full/qwen3_48m_pt_ds_ulysses.yaml, data/pretrain_c4_demo.json\\n2026-07-13 - LlamaFactory Qwen3-48M from-scratch Ulysses run WORKING + launched (compare vs bluscriptCP). Key blocker: DeepSpeed+Ulysses is impossible in LF (hub.py:65 raises \\\"CP requires fsdp2\\\"); Ulysses CP is FSDP2-only -> switched backend to FSDP2 (ZeRO3-style, ships/tested). Also fixed model_engine.py from_c