rep=P/nkv only when nkv<P, grouped broadcast done LOCALLY (kv_local->nq_local) since CP SDPA is MHA-only, backward = two group-reduces (adjoint of local broadcast g_local, then of replication rep). Added head_repeat_interleave (narrow+cat) + head_group_reduce (narrow + raw Tensor operator+) to UlyssesAttention.h. Bug found+fixed during bringup: OwnTensor::reduce_sum over a middle axis of a 5D tensor gave wrong dK/dV (dQ passed since no reduce) -> reimplemented group-reduce as explicit narrow+add. RUNTIME PASS 2x3060 ws=2: cp_ulysses_parity forward+dQ/dK/dV cos=1.0000000 for GQA nkv=4,2 + MQA nkv=1 + MHA(unshard t/f); ring rope-standin regression still ALL PASS; gpt2_cp_test TU parses clean. ws=4 GQA configs (nq=16 nkv=4/1) pending 4-GPU box. GQA is CP-layer capability (parity test); gpt2 model stays MHA - CP / context_parallel/UlyssesGQAAttentionBackward.h, UlyssesAttention.h, ContextParallel.h, Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n2026-07-02 - CP Ulysses FUSED RoPE+QKnorm+GQA path (Llama-style, additive): new enable_ulysses_fused()+forward_ulysses_fused()+UlyssesFusedGQAAttentionBackward.h calling the team's bf16 gqa_fused_flash_attn_forward/backward (kernel is GQA-native so NO local head-broadcast; only nkv<P replication remains; pos_offset=0 since Ulysses gathers full contiguous seq). Mirrors production sdpa_gqa_fused pack (as_type bf16 + cat) / narrow_view split; gamma grads SUM-all-reduced over CP group (op_t::sum). Reused v2 head_repeat_interleave/head_group_reduce. Parity run_fused_mode (rms_norm+rope+GQA ref, bf16 tol). FOUND KERNEL BUG: fused GQA *backward* returns wrong dQ+dq_gamma for true GQA 1<Nkv<Nq (nkv=2 g=4: dQ cos0.12, dq_gamma cos0.27) while fwd/dK/dV/dk_gamma correct; reproduced at ws=1 (kernel called directly, no CP) -> it's GQA_fused_bwd_sm103.cu dQ path, NOT CP. MHA(nkv=8,G=1) + MQA(nkv=1,G=8) fused PASS all grads (cos>0.9999) ws=1&2; marked intermediate-GQA dQ/dq_gamma XFAIL. All other gates (v1 MHA, v2 plain-GQA/MQA incl nkv=2, fused MHA/MQA) + ring rope-standin regression PASS. gpt2 TU clean - CP / context_parallel/UlyssesFusedGQAAttentionBackward.h, ContextParallel.h, Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n2026-07-02 - Wrote EOD report (EOD.md first-person narrative style) covering the GQA-based Ulysses attention implementation - CP / .mdfiles/EOD_2026-07-02_gqa_ulysses.md\\n\\n2026-07-03 - Ada CP grad explosion localized to FORWARD compute/comm overlap race (CP_NO_OVERLAP_FWD=1 clean to 111 steps; full CP_NO_OVERLAP clean). Next probe CP_FWD_SYNC_RECV=1 to split recv-consume event ordering (next_buffer_streamordered work->streamWait) vs pack/allocator path. Interim stable config: CP_NO_OVERLAP_FWD=1 - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, RingRotator.h\\n2026-07-03 - CP fwd-overlap race fix: CP_DRAIN_AT=1 pinned the backward-save clone (saved_k_chunks[i]=curr_k.clone()) as the victim racing the concurrent ring exchange; hoisted Step3 skip/causal + the conditional clone ABOVE exchange_buffers (so pack_ev orders the clone before ring send/recv), moved skip-continue below exchange, preserved backward is_valid() skip detection - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h2026-07-06 - CP Ulysses fused-GQA bug: sharpened root cause via new run_fused_vs_seq_mode() isolator in cp_ulysses_parity.cpp - compares FUSED kernel directly vs the team's OWN plain (non-fused) GQA kernel (gqa_flash_attn_forward/backward), fed identical RoPE+QKnorm'd Q/K (no hand-rolled matmul/softmax ref). Non-causal (plain kernel has no causal support): dQ/dK/dV/dq_gamma/dk_gamma ALL match fused perfectly (cos>0.9999) for nkv=2, nkv=4(nq=12), and nkv=8(MHA) - so GQA group-indexing (hkv=hq/G) is NOT the bug. Combined with prior causal finding (dQ/dq_gamma wrong only for 1<nkv<nq when causal), isolates the defect to the fused backward's CAUSAL dQ path interacting with G>1 grouping specifically (dK/dV use a separate KV-tile-centric path, unaffected). Verified at ws=1 and ws=2, deterministic - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n2026-07-07 - CP Ulysses GQA bug MAJOR reframe: added 3rd leg to run_fused_vs_seq_mode() comparing the REAL plain (non-fused) GQA kernel (gqa_flash_attn_forward/backward, non-causal) directly against ref_sdpa - it does NOT match for true GQA (1<nkv<nq): dQ cos=0.09 (nkv=2) and cos=-0.07 (nkv=4, sign-flipped!), dq_gamma also fails; MHA (nkv=8) passes cos=0.99. Same failure signature as the fused kernel. This proves the bug is NOT fused-specific and NOT causal-specific - it's shared by BOTH plain and fused GQA backward dQ kernels for true GQA, non-causally too. Ruled out ref_sdpa/expansion methodology as the culprit since the identical construction matches a 3rd unrelated kernel (our own CP sm89 path via run_gqa_mode) at cos=1.0 for the same G values. dQ is per-query-head independent (no cross-head sum needed, unlike dK/dV which DO match) so there's no legitimate algorithmic reason for it to diverge - strong signature of a real, shared dQ-kernel defect (GQA_fused_bwd_sm103.cu documents itself as a \\\"sibling\\\" of GQA_bwd_sm103.cu, likely inherited bug) rather than a causal-masking or fusion-specific issue - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n2026-07-08 - MAX_LR sweep script (MultiStep sched) + MAX_LR env override - BluTrain / gpt2_fmha_ddp_sched.cpp, run_maxlr_sweep.sh\\n2026-07-08 - Fixed MAX_LR sweep env: rebuilt libdist (GLIBCXX mismatch), fixed MPI 4.1.2/5.0.9 mismatch in Makefile, local data_root + INIT_FROM_BIN; smoke-verified all 9 LRs - BluTrain / gpt2_fmha_ddp_sched.cpp, Makefile, run_maxlr_sweep.sh\\n2026-07-09 - MAX_LR sweep complete (9/9 runs, 6767 steps each); compared via compare_sched_fmha.py, best val loss at 1.5e-3 - BluTrain / compare_maxlr_*.png, maxlr_sweep_logs/\\n\\n2026-07-09 - Ported disk-state checkpointing (CheckpointManager save/resume) into CP training script, run-numbered filenames tied to log index, preserved across resume; env CP_CHECKPOINT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME; auto-resume latest incomplete run, new run on complete, targeted resume; rank-0-only save (shard_dir=false shared path); Makefile host std -> c++2a for Checkpointing.h C++20 API. 2x3060 verified all paths - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/gpt2_cp_test.cpp, Makefile\\n2026-07-09 - Implemented canonical (HF/Qwen3) YaRN in build_rope_cache: NTK-by-parts freq blend via find_correction_dim dim-index ramp + attention temperature m=0.1*ln(s)+1 baked into cos/sin (m^2 logit temp, no kernel change); env-overridable YARN_SCALE/ORIG_MAXPOS/BETA_FAST/BETA_SLOW (scale=1 => bit-identical std RoPE); build-on-CPU-then-.to(device) bypasses uniform-freq CUDA kernel; robustness guards (R2 scale/seqlen warn, R3 init log, R5 bad-range throw). YARNOps.o symbol wins link over libtensor RopeOps. 2x3060 verified: standin parity 100% PASS cos=1.0 both no-env and YARN_SCALE=8, m=1.2079 matches, hd=128 low=11/high=36; ulysses fails only in pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug (identical at scale=1) - CP / context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp2026-07-09 - CORRECTION to 2026-07-09 YaRN entry (\\\"pre-existing GQA-bwd dQ/dq_gamma bug\\\"): this was WRONG, not a kernel bug. Root-caused via precision-injection test: took the G=1 (MHA, no GQA at all) case, bf16-round-tripped K on the ref_sdpa side only (no kernel change), and dQ cos collapsed to 0.108 - identical magnitude to the \\\"GQA bug\\\" signature seen for 1<Nkv<Nq. Proves dQ is simply sensitive to bf16-vs-fp32 K precision mismatch between the fused/normal GQA kernels (bf16-internal) and the fp32 ref_sdpa reference; nothing GQA-specific. Kernel is correct. Retracting all prior \\\"fused/normal GQA backward dQ/dq_gamma bug\\\" claims (2026-07-02, 2026-07-07 entries) - CP / Tests/cp_ulysses_parity.cpp\\n2026-07-16 - bluscriptCP re-warmup anchor fix + long-context PPL eval: (1) LR re-warmup was anchored at start_step (current resume step) so every resume of a context-extension run restarted the warmup ramp; added CP_REWARMUP_ANCHOR=<step> to pin the ramp to a fixed absolute step (default -1 = old start_step behavior), so resuming mid/post-ramp continues the same schedule; log now prints anchor+resume+phase (mid-ramp/past-ramp). (2) Added CP_EVAL_PPL forward-only eval mode: NP=1/CP_SIZE=1 (T_local==T, no cross-rank gather), loads ckpt via CP_CKPT_RESUME, teacher-forces CP_EVAL_WINDOWS windows on held-out val split, per-position NLL=logsumexp-logit[tgt] -> pos,count,mean_nll,ppl CSV (CP_EVAL_OUT); skips training + log/config writes (/dev/null). Base-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=1 (naive extrapolation) vs extended-ckpt+YARN_SCALE=4 curves show blow-up-vs-flat past orig ctx. (3) Notebook cell in graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb plots the CSVs + before/after-ctx PPL ratio verdict. Compile-verified (mpic++ -c, exit 0); server build/run pending - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb\\n2026-07-10 - Cosine MAX_LR sweep complete (9/9) + compare_sched_fmha.py; best val 1.5e-3, cosine ~0.03 worse than multistep in basin - BluTrain / compare_maxlr_cosine_*.png, maxlr_cosine_sweep_logs/\\n2026-07-10 - CP fused-RoPE Phase 3: implemented 4-delta offset-parameterized fused GQA kernels (fwd+bwd) in GQA_fused_{fwd,bwd}_sm103_cp.cu -> cp::cuda::gqa_fused_rope_cp_{forward,backward}. Scalar pos_offset replaced by per-side head/tail deltas (pos=local+(local>=len/2?d1:d0), matches RopeDeltas.h) for HeadTail-LB non-contiguous [head|tail] shards; separate T_q/T_k + Q/K/V ptrs; bwd recomputes rstd->smem (drops saved q/k_rstd); causal UNCHANGED (local-monotonic sub-chunks; deltas index RoPE only). Whole TU gated #if CP_FUSED_ROPE (default=empty TU, no libtensor collision); FusedRoPESDPA.h decls+wrappers reconciled to bf16 (as_type casts); Makefile CP_FUSED_ROPE/CP_ROPE_DEBUG knobs; monotonicity-contract comment at ContextParallel.h call site. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED: default build unchanged (standin 12/12 PASS); CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 new Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity - fwd+dQ/dK/dV BIT-IDENTICAL to production kernel at deltas=0 (cos=1.0 maxdiff=0), dq/dk_gamma cos=1.0 maxdiff~3e-7, HeadTail seam case (deltas 0,32) cos=0.99999 + seam rows exact, OOR counter zero. Makefile hardened so NO make clean is ever needed: (1) flag-stamp $(OBJDIR)/.cp_rope_flags (rewritten only on change, prereq of all obj rules) makes CP_FUSED_ROPE/CP_ROPE_DEBUG a real build dep; (2) added -MMD -MP + -include *.d for automatic header-dependency tracking (was absent). Verified: same-flags=0 rebuilds, flag-flip auto-rebuilds 13 TUs, touching FusedRoPESDPA.h selectively rebuilds only its 1 includer. GOTCHA: pass the flags to the RUN target too (make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-cp-rope-fused), else run-only re-evaluates flag-off and rebuilds to the empty default -> throws - CP / context_parallel/GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu, GQA_fused_bwd_sm103_cp.cu, FusedRoPESDPA.h, ContextParallel.h, Makefile, Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp\\n\\n2026-07-10 - Fixed AdamW::load_state segfault on resume-from-step-0 checkpoint (m_/v_ empty vectors + initialized_=true left step() indexing OOB); count==0 now stays uninitialized so lazy-init runs normally. Same latent bug also present in gpt2_fmha_ddp.cpp (shared library) - CP / BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/src/nn/optimizer/Optim.cpp\\n2026-07-10 - Process-group UNIFICATION (prereq for DataParallel+ContextParallel coexisting in bluscriptCP): made BluTrain dist/communication ProcessGroupNCCL the single canonical PG for CP+DP. (A) Extended BluTrain PG (additive) with the CP ring-overlap surface ported to run on its own comm_: cpRingStream() + cp_ring_stream_, sendrecv_async_stream, all_gather_async_stream, alltoallv_async, alltoallv_async_stream; + comm-adopting ctor (world_size,rank,ncclComm_t,...) + get_comm(). (B) Rewrote CP process_group/device_mesh.cpp to build sub-groups via ncclCommSplit(world_comm,color=other-coords,key=axis-coord) instead of MPI_Comm_split+WORLD id-bcast -> NCCL-native sub-groups, fixes the 2D-mesh wrong-id bug (world PG still 1x MPI_Bcast); device_mesh.h now includes canonical PG + holds world_pg_. (C) Repointed 8 CP files' #include process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> \\\"ProcessGroupNCCL.h\\\" (canonical). Collision: device_mesh.h's quote-include resolved CP's same-dir header first -> RENAMED (not deleted, per user) process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.h -> ProcessGroupNCCL_cplegacy.h (dormant). (D) Makefile: +INCLUDES -IBluTrain/dist/communication/include -IBluTrain/dist/Data-Parallel/include; +BLUTRAIN_PG_SRC (processGroupNccl.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/Error_logs.cpp); CPP_EXCLUDE += process_group/processGroupNCCL.cpp. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED: builds clean (one ProcessGroupNCCL/Work/NCCLCHECK, no dup symbols); cp-rope-standin 12/12 PASS cos=1.0000000 (ring fwd+bwd+dgamma + ported overlap methods + ncclCommSplit 1D world identical to old CP PG); cp-ulysses 72 PASS, only the pre-existing bf16-ref-precision dQ/dq_gamma FAILs (unchanged by migration). Follow-ups: 2-D ncclCommSplit per-axis all-reduce test (needs 4 ranks), then bluscriptCP resume (wire DataParallel.cpp) - CP / BluTrain/dist/communication/{include/ProcessGroupNCCL.h,src/processGroupNccl.cpp}, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, context_parallel/*.h, Makefile2026-07-10 - bluscriptCP RESUME (CP Llama training on the unified PG): DataParallel + ContextParallel now coexist. Included DataParallel.hpp DIRECTLY (not the dist/distributed.h umbrella, which pulls the TP stack incl. a different class DeviceMesh -> collision); init_process_group comes from the canonical PG. Fixed double-init crash (\\\"process group instance already created\\\"): the DeviceMesh builds the world PG once (ncclCommSplit parent) and bluscriptCP now reuses it via new DeviceMesh::world_pg() for DataParallel instead of a 2nd init_process_group. Makefile: bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp targets; DataParallel.cpp + Data-Parallel/src/profiler.cpp scoped to this target only. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED (CP_FUSED_ROPE=1, tiny cfg L2/d256/hd64/GQA kv2/T256, edufineweb data in ~/Downloads via CP_DATA_ROOT): builds clean; world=1 trains loss 10.89->10.23 decreasing, finite grad-norm, fused-RoPE CP ring ran (first real training integration of the new kernels); ws=2 CP_SIZE=2 ring trains AND loss-parity vs world=1 (step0 10.884 vs 10.890, step4 10.2269 vs 10.2280) -> CP sequence-sharding + RoPE positions + ring correct end-to-end, and overlap-ON matching the serial reference proves the ring overlap is race-free (plan concern d). FOLLOW-UP: CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 diagnostic path crashes (\\\"convert_type_cuda: invalid resource handle\\\" — stream-handle issue under the unified PG; default overlap path unaffected + verified). Also pending: 2-D DPxCP run (dp>1), Ulysses-mode bluscriptCP (CP_ATTN_MODE=ulysses), full-scale config - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, process_group/device_mesh.{h,cpp}, Makefile\\n2026-07-10 - bluscriptCP follow-ups #1/#3/#4 + ROOT-CAUSED a real sub-group-PG device bug. #1 CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 crash (\\\"convert_type/NCCL enqueue: invalid resource handle\\\") AND #3 Ulysses crash (\\\"Sync failed line 484 / Cuda 400 invalid resource handle\\\") had the SAME root cause introduced by the ncclCommSplit migration: BluTrain PG derived its CUDA device from rank_%gpus_per_node, and DeviceMesh passed the SUB-GROUP rank (my_group_rank); a size-1 DP axis has my_group_rank=0 -> its adopt-ctor set device 0, so the NEXT axis (CP) created its comm_stream while device=0 while its ncclCommSplit comm_ lived on device 1 -> stream/comm device mismatch (blocking collectives on communication_stream_ failed; overlap ring escaped it because cpRingStream is created lazily at ring-time on the correct device). FIX: adopt-ctor now cudaGetDevice(&local_rank_) (adopt caller's global physical device, don't derive from sub-group rank); DeviceMesh re-asserts cudaSetDevice(global_device) at the start of each axis iteration before ncclCommSplit/stream create. 2x3060 VERIFIED: cp-rope-standin 12/12 still PASS (1D regression); ws=2 ring no-overlap now trains + A/B matches overlap (step0 identical 10.884422, step4 diff 2e-5 => overlap race-free, plan concern d); #3 Ulysses ws=2 trains loss 10.890->10.228 with step0 parity vs world=1 (10.889622 vs 10.889627); #4 full-scale d768/L12/q12-kv4/T4096 114M params, CP_SIZE=2 (T_local=2048/rank), trains loss 11.02->10.21 no OOM/NaN on 2x3060. (#2 2D DPxCP deferred: needs 4 ranks.) - CP / BluTrain/dist/communication/src/processGroupNccl.cpp, process_group/device_mesh.cpp\\n2026-07-10 - Documented bluscriptCP in README.md: new \\\"Context-parallel Llama training (bluscriptCP)\\\" section (Ring vs Ulysses build+run commands, CP_FUSED_ROPE=1-to-both-build-and-run + checkpoint-resume gotchas, full env-var reference incl. topology CP_SIZE/CP_ATTN_MODE/CP_ROTATOR, model/data CP_N_EMBD/LAYER/HEAD/KVHEAD/T/B/GLOBAL_BATCH/MAX_STEPS/WARMUP/DATA_ROOT, YaRN YARN_*, diagnostics CP_NO_OVERLAP*/RING_BLOCKING/SYNC_RING/NO_GPUS_PER_NODE, build flags CP_FUSED_ROPE/CP_ROPE_DEBUG, full-scale example), + bluscript-cp/run-bluscript-cp make targets, intro + repo-layout mentions - CP / README.md\\n2026-07-10 - Aligned bluscriptCP logging/terminal prints with gpt2_cp_test.cpp: added banner, ULYSSES attn-mode note, gpt2-style params block (Parameters/per-GPU/max_steps/warmup), per-step line (step|loss|lr|norm|dt|tok/sec|mem|Time Left) + [TIMING] breakdown via ported CudaTimer (event-based data/fwd/loss/bwd/clip/optim), validation-loss print, and the RUN-NUMBERED logging system (CP_Training_logs/CP_Training_log{N}.csv + _config.txt with GPU mem, run_number tied to ckpt prefix blumodelcp_run{N}, MPI_Bcast, CP_CKPT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME env, auto-resume-latest/complete->new-run scan of checkpoints_bluscriptcp). Kept the boxed Configuration block as-is per user. 2x3060 sm86 VERIFIED (world=1 tiny cfg): builds clean, all 4 log paths correct (fresh run1, complete->new run2, resume run2 from step3, CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN->run3), CSV/config.txt written, checkpoints run-numbered - CP / Scripts/BluTrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: added 2-stage re-warmup for YaRN context-extension resume + checkpoint-visibility prints. get_lr gained a warmup_start anchor (ramp [warmup_start, warmup_start+warmup) then cosine-decay; warmup_start=0 reproduces old schedule exactly) since the base schedule's warmup is absolute-from-0 and cannot re-ramp on resume. New env: CP_REWARMUP=<steps> (0=off, only when start_step>0) re-anchors a fresh warmup at the resume step, CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=<frac of max_lr, default 1.0> for a reduced long-context peak; prints \\\"[re-warmup] anchored at step S ...\\\". Also added checkpointing/ckpt_freq/dir to the boxed Configuration block and a \\\"Checkpointing: ON -> <dir>/<prefix>_step_<N>.ckpt (every F steps, keep K)\\\" line at run start (user noticed these weren't shown; root of an earlier \\\"not checkpointing\\\" confusion was just the default ckpt_freq=250 -> first save at step 250). Context: discussed that context extension causes a perplexity spike so stop base run DECAYED (not at peak) then re-warmup to a reduced peak (~0.3x). IMPLEMENTED, NOT YET BUILT/VERIFIED (user had a run on the box) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - Documented the above in README.md (bluscriptCP section): new \\\"Checkpointing / resume / LR re-warmup\\\" env table (CP_CKPT/CP_CKPT_FREQ/CP_CKPT_NEW_RUN/CP_CKPT_RESUME + CP_REWARMUP/CP_REWARMUP_PEAK, run-numbered ckpt/log naming, first-save-at-step-N note) and a \\\"2-stage context extension (YaRN + re-warmup)\\\" subsection (base stage decay -> long-context resume with reduced-peak re-warmup, seq-len/world-size-independent checkpoint load, CP_MAX_STEPS/CP_CKPT_RESUME resumability gate) + a YaRN scale=1-means-off / CP_T==scale*orig_maxpos note - CP / README.md\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: silenced the DataLoader per-shard \\\"Current shard:\\\"/max_tokens debug spam during the RESUME replay (fired once per shard crossing x every rank). Added a NullBuf(std::streambuf) discard buffer; redirect std::cout->NullBuf around train_loader.skip_batches (all ranks) then restore, replaced with a single rank-0 line \\\"[resume] fast-forwarded data loader N batches (start_step*global_batch tokens)\\\". Change kept in bluscriptCP.cpp (main repo, syncs to server) rather than the Tensor-Implementations submodule DataLoader.h advance_shard() prints (sync friction). Residual: training-time shard crossings still print (submodule source). IMPLEMENTED, NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP: rank-gated ALL stdout to rank 0 (standard MPI idiom) to stop world_size-times-duplicated library chatter ([CheckpointManager] Auto-loading latest, [CP ring A2A] OVERLAP, [CP bwd] overlap=ON etc. were printing x4 on 4 ranks). Redirect std::cout->static NullBuf on every non-master rank right after computing is_master; std::cerr left intact so per-rank errors still surface. Subsumes/complements the skip_batches rank-0 redirect (rank 0's cout stays live). Kept in bluscriptCP.cpp (main repo). NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp\\n2026-07-11 - bluscriptCP output cleanup pt2: the remaining x4-duplicated init banners ([YaRN] build_rope_cache, [CP ring P2P/A2A/AllGather], [CP sdpa fwd], [CP bwd] overlap) were fprintf(stderr) (NOT std::cout) so the cout redirect could not touch them. Added context_parallel/CPLog.h with cp::log_rank() (reads OMPI_COMM_WORLD_RANK, fallback PMI_RANK, unknown-launcher -> true so never silently lost) and gated all 6 one-time stderr notices on global rank 0 at source (RingRotator.h x3, ContextParallelBackward.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, YARNOps.cpp x2) - real stderr errors from other ranks stay visible (vs a blanket stderr redirect). All main-repo context_parallel/ files (sync to server, no submodule). NOT BUILT (box busy) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}\\n2026-07-11 - FIX build break from the above: CPLog.h used a GLOBAL 'namespace cp', but the CP stack already has OwnTensor::cp (cp::ulysses_combine/head_repeat_interleave/...) -> two 'cp' in scope made EVERY cp:: reference ambiguous (server error: \\\"reference to 'cp' is ambiguous\\\", cascaded across ContextParallel/Ulysses/RingRotator). Renamed namespace cp -> cplog (unique, global) + updated all 6 call sites to cplog::log_rank(); existing cp::ulysses_* now resolve cleanly again. Verified by grep (no cp::log_rank left, 6 cplog sites, 1 def). NOT BUILT locally (avoid contending with user's run) - CP / context_parallel/{CPLog.h,RingRotator.h,ContextParallelBackward.h,FusedSDPAOp.h,YARNOps.cpp}\\n\\n2026-07-13 - LlamaFactory v1 DeepSpeed+Ulysses from-scratch PT reference for 48M Qwen3 (to compare vs CP-Ulysses bluscriptCP): mapped that Ulysses SP lives ONLY in v1 (cp_mode/cp_size plugin, patches flash-attn fwd) while stage:pt+train_from_scratch live only in v0; built qwen3_48m/ config matching bluscriptCP.cpp cfg exactly (d384/L6/qh6/kvh2/hd64/ffn1024/vocab50304-gpt2/no-tie/rope5e5/rms1e-5 = 48.076M total), seeded random-init checkpoint, empty-prompt-alpaca pretrain data (full-seq LM loss), v1 deepspeed+ulysses cp_size2 YAML. Found v1 has NO true from-config random-init (meta path chunk-loads a checkpoint) -> materialize seeded random weights to disk then load. Validated no-CP fsdp2 run: loss 10.96 ~ ln(vocab), decreasing, from-scratch confirmed. flash-attn (req for Ulysses) compiling from source on cu130. Caveats logged: v1 constant-LR + AdamW wd0.01 only (no cosine/warmup/wd0.1 without custom plugin); chat-wrapper neutralized via custom_chat_template - LlamaFactory / qwen3_48m/{config.json,model.safetensors,pretrain_data.yaml,validate_nocp.yaml}, examples/v1/train_full/qwen3_48m_pt_ds_ulysses.yaml, data/pretrain_c4_demo.json\\n2026-07-13 - LlamaFactory Qwen3-48M from-scratch Ulysses run WORKING + launched (compare vs bluscriptCP). Key blocker: DeepSpeed+Ulysses is impossible in LF (hub.py:65 raises \\\"CP requires fsdp2\\\"); Ulysses CP is FSDP2-only -> switched backend to FSDP2 (ZeRO3-style, ships/tested). Also fixed model_engine.py from_config to pass attn_implementation (meta/from-scratch path left _attn_implementation default -> SP flash-attn check failed). Matched bluscriptCP.cpp exactly: head_dim=32 (46.896M), GPT-2 scaled init (o/down_proj std 0.02/sqrt(2*6)), AdamW betas0.9/0.95 wd0.1 (cpp:562), cosine 6e-4->6e-5 warmup91 917steps B2 T4096 524288tok/step. Added CSVLoggingCallback (exact bluscriptCP CSV header + training_config.txt) + bluscriptCP-format terminal line + [TIMING] via CUDA events (loss fused into fwd; fsdp2 separates clip/optim). Smoke 5-step PASS: cp=2 SP engaged (flash fwd patched), loss 10.905->10.706. Full 917-step launched bg task bsc4vevqv, ETA ~2h, ~7s/step tok/sec~75k - LlamaFactory / examples/v1/train_full/qwen3_48m_pt_fsdp2_ulysses.yaml, qwen3_48m/*, src/llamafactory/v1/{core/model_engine.py,core/base_trainer.py,plugins/trainer_plugins/{optimizer,lr_scheduler}.py,utils/callbacks/csv_logging_callback.py}\\n2026-07-13 - Followup: switched LF Qwen3-48M Ulysses run from FSDP2-sharded to PURE CP (replicated params) to match bluscriptCP's dp*cp/replicated setup. Discovery: default FSDP2+Ulysses ALSO does ZeRO-3 sharding (model_device_mesh mp_shard=2) on top of CP -> extra all-gather/reduce-scatter not in bluscriptCP. Fix: dist_config mp_replicate_size=2/mp_shard_size=1 -> mesh (replicate=2,shard=1)+(dp=1,cp=2), params replicated, Ulysses cp=2 only. Smoke PASS (fwd dropped 2.3->1.5s = removed param all-gather; loss identical 10.905->10.706). Also found user's OWN suspended (STAT T) Qwen3-8B v0 deepspeed full-PT launcher PID1557605 (~3.75h, 0 GPU, would OOM 31GB RAM as predicted) - left untouched. Full 917-step pure-CP run relaunched bg task bmdq6tyj8 - LlamaFactory / examples/v1/train_full/qwen3_48m_pt_fsdp2_ulysses.yaml (dist_config mp_replicate_size/mp_shard_size)\\n2026-07-13 - Built GPT-2 ~44M from-scratch pure-CP Ulysses reference in LlamaFactory (matches gpt2_cp_test.cpp MODEL_44M: n_embd384/L3/H6/vocab50304/ctx1024/no-tie, GPT-2 scaled init c_proj std 0.02/sqrt(2*3)). Verified GPT2 supports flash_attention_2 in transformers 5.7. Hit CUDA device-assert: v1 SP path overflows GPT-2 wpe (learned pos-emb) by one when cutoff_len==n_positions (Qwen3 RoPE has no such table). Fix: n_positions=2048 headroom (unused rows, +0.39M) -> 44.744M. Smoke 5-step PASS cp=2 SP engaged loss 10.917->10.716, CSV+TIMING ok, dt~3.2s. Files: gpt2_44m/*, examples/v1/train_full/gpt2_44m_pt_fsdp2_ulysses.yaml - LlamaFactory\\n2026-07-13 - Option A exact token-packing for GPT-2 44M CP run (match gpt2_cp_test.cpp nanoGPT loader). Read edufineweb .bin (headerless raw uint16, EOT=50256, 100M tok/shard, CP/Data_Loader/Data), packed 60000 contiguous 1024-tok blocks -> data/edufineweb_packed_1024.parquet. Added v1 \\\"pretrain_packed\\\" converter (pass-through input_ids) + Renderer.process_samples branch (feeds input_ids verbatim, labels=input_ids full-seq LM loss, position_ids 0..T-1, full causal attention across block = cross-doc). Set global_batch_size=64 (65536 tok/step, grad_accum16). Also root-caused earlier gpt2 wpe OOB: rendering.py position_ids=range(1,len+1) starts at 1 -> idx 1024 at ctx1024 (n_positions=2048 absorbs). Smoke 5-step PASS: gbs64/micro4/16 accum, cp=2 SP, real-data loss 10.917->10.699, CSV+TIMING ok, EXIT0 - LlamaFactory / src/llamafactory/v1/{plugins/data_plugins/converter.py,core/rendering/rendering.py}, gpt2_44m/pretrain_packed.yaml, examples/v1/train_full/gpt2_44m_pt_fsdp2_ulysses.yaml\\n2026-07-16 - Mem-scaling sweep folder for bluscriptCP (production CP model) vs DeepSpeed-Ulysses Qwen3: ported CP_MEM_PROBE snapshot mode into bluscriptCP.cpp (env CP_MEM_PROBE/CP_MEM_PROBE_STEPS/CP_MODEL_LABEL, grad_accum->1, skip val/ckpt, cudaMemGetInfo+alloc-peak+nvidia-smi snapshot matching gpt2_cp_test format) + new Tests/bluscriptcp/{mem_scaling_sweep.sh,mem_scaling_table.py} driving deepspeed qwen3_ds_ulysses.py; portable across 2xRTX3060/Nx6000Ada via CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES; syntax-verified (mpic++ c++20 fsyntax rc=0, bash -n, py_compile) NOT run e