.91, separate ring issue); added CP_RING_OUTER mesh-order toggle ({ring,dp,ulysses}) so Ring crosses NUMA/nodes while Ulysses+DDP stay intra-domain; fused-tile CP_T guard - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Tests/cp_hybrid_parity.cpp, README.md\\n2026-07-15 - 3D hybrid CP {DDP,CP-Ring,CP-Ulysses}: Ulysses-inner all-to-all nested in Ring-outer via enable_hybrid/forward_hybrid + composed HeadTail-over-ring/contiguous-over-ulysses sharder + combine/partition autograd nodes; bluscriptCP CP_ATTN_MODE=hybrid 3D mesh wiring; cp-hybrid parity test (MHA bit-exact vs pure-ring) + hybrid_cp_smoke.sh; README - CP / context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, HybridUlyssesBackward.h, Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Makefile, Tests/cp_hybrid_parity.cpp, Tests/hybrid_cp_smoke.sh, README.md\\n2026-04-20 - CP-aware TF32 WMMA attention fwd/bwd: AttentionForward/Backward CP copies modified with T_q/T_k/q_offset/k_offset, exp11 bwd dQ/dK/dV atomicAdd for ring accumulation, namespace OwnTensor::cp - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/AttentionForward.cu, AttentionBackward.cu\\n2026-04-18 - Throughput fixes: remove cudaDeviceSynchronize (Fix1), zeros->empty bwd (Fix2), P2PRingRotator grouped sendrecv (Fix4) - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPAOp.h, RingRotator.h\\n2026-04-16 - SDPA LB fwd+bwd implemented but grad explosion unresolved; LB disabled for causal, TC backward re-enabled, backward deadlock fix (step_skipped), AlltoAllRingRotator rewritten to sparse alltoallv (PyTorch parity), alltoallv_async added to ProcessGroupNCCL - TensorParallelismBeta / RingRotator.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, FusedSDPABackwardKernel.cu, ProcessGroupNCCL.h, processGroupNCCL.cpp\\n2026-04-15 - Grad explosion fix: TC backward `if (false)` guard re-applied in launch_flash_attn_bwd_f32 - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPABackwardKernel.cu\\n2026-04-10 - CP throughput gap debug (55.5k vs 64k PyTorch) - TC kernel T_q/T_k/K_head_stride, LEFT_HALF/BOT_HALF TC dispatch, clone overhead identified - TensorParallelismBeta / AttentionKernels.cu, AttentionKernels.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-03-20 - Context Parallelism implementation (RingRotator, SDPA, Merger, Forward/Backward) - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/RingRotator.h, SDPAOp.h, SDPAMerger.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-03-20 - Context Parallel test file and Makefile target - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp, DTensor/Makefile\\n2026-03-21 - CP backward rotator fix, load_balance causal fix, gpt2_cp_test.cpp full rewrite with data loader/timing/logging/token-gen - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallelBackward.h, ContextParallel.h, gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-03-21 - gpt2_cp_test.cpp weight tying (NoGradGuard+transpose), global_batch/grad_accum/max_steps/warmup_steps from gpt2_tp_test pattern, grad_scale backward - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-03-21 - OOM fix: flatten_concat returns [1,N] not [N]; added .flatten() before narrow() in ContextParallel ring loop to prevent 1.15TB allocation - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h\\n2026-03-28 - Debug: wrong gradients in CP - root cause: saved_k_chunks[i] aliases recv_buffer_ (P2P/AlltoAll rotators), fix: clone before saving in ContextParallel.h:216-217 - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, RingRotator.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, SDPAOp.h\\n2026-03-28 - Debug: CP vs normal wpe gradient mismatch (10-17x smaller for positions 0..511) - root cause: Phase 3 sendrecv in ContextParallelBackward not delivering dK/dV from rank 1 back to rank 0 - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallelBackward.h, gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-03-28 - Fix: Phase 3 backward now dispatches on rotator_type_: AlltoAll uses alltoall_async (build send_buf per dest slot, sum recv slots), P2P keeps sendrecv - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-03-28 - New test: attn_block_grad_test.cpp - compares CP vs standard full attention block gradients (ln, c_attn, c_proj, x.grad) with exact same weights/config - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/attn_block_grad_test.cpp, DTensor/Makefile\\n2026-03-21 - CP correctness fixes (3 bugs: non-causal attention, backward grad shape, backward merger rescaling) + optimizations (GPU HeadTail, pre-alloc buffers, ring loop cleanup) - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, SDPAOp.h, RingRotator.h, gpt2_cp_test.cpp, tensor/dtensor.cpp\\n2026-03-23 - HeadTail permutation rewrite: replaced wrong stride permutation with correct head-tail CUDA kernel [0,T-1,1,T-2,...], backward clone fix, k/v edge fix - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/tensor/headtail_kernel.cu, headtail_kernel.cuh, dtensor.cpp, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-03-24 - CP backward Di correction debug & revert, added test_sdpa_backward.cpp - TensorParallelismBeta / SDPAOp.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, ContextParallel.h, tests/test_sdpa_backward.cpp\\n2026-03-26 - CP vs Normal loss divergence root cause analysis (rcp.approx.f32 P_local/LSE inconsistency) - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedKernels.cu, SDPAOp.h, SDPAMerger.h\\n2026-03-27 - Context Parallel contiguous() stride bug fix - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h\\n2026-03-30 16:19 - megatronCP.py rewrite using Megatron TEDotProductAttention + TE install - TensorParallelismBeta / megatronCP.py\\n2026-03-31 - Fused SDPA (FlashAttention tiled kernel) impl + test - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/FusedSDPAKernel.cu, FusedSDPAKernel.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, gpt2_cp_test/test_fused_sdpa.cpp, DTensor/Makefile\\n2026-03-31 - Fused SDPA (FlashAttention tiled kernel) + CP fair timing test vs MegatronLM - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/FusedSDPAKernel.cu, FusedSDPAKernel.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, gpt2_cp_test/test_fused_sdpa.cpp, gpt2_cp_test/cp_sdpa_compare_test.cpp, DTensor/Makefile\\n2026-03-31 - Wire fused SDPA into ContextParallel::forward_cp replacing unfused sdpa_forward; CP time 5.547ms->2.659ms (2.1x), gap vs Megatron 5.4x->2.6x - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, DTensor/Makefile\\n2026-04-01 - Component optimizations (FusedAdamW 7.86x, VectorizedLayerNorm 1.89x fwd/1.75x bwd, FusedLMHead TF32 1.62x fwd) + test files - TensorParallelismBeta / dnn/FusedAdamWKernel.cu, dnn/VectorizedLayerNormKernel.cu, dnn/FusedLMHeadKernel.cu, gpt2_cp_test/test_fused_adamw.cpp, test_vectorized_layernorm.cpp, test_lm_head_opt.cpp\\n2026-04-02 - Wire FusedLayerNorm into gpt2_cp_test (3 sites); revert FusedAdamW wiring (543MB regression); FusedLayerNorm confirmed no memory regression - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp, dnn/FusedLayerNormOp.h, dnn/FusedLayerNormOp.cpp\\n2026-04-04 - CP training norm explosion fix (TC backward kernel bug) - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPABackwardKernel.cu, FusedSDPAKernel.cu\\n2026-04-04 - PyTorch SDPA backward timing regression debug & fix - TensorParallelismBeta / pytorch_attn_bench.py\\n2026-04-04 - PyTorch SDPA backward timing regression debug & fix (2-step ring simulation) - TensorParallelismBeta / pytorch_attn_bench.py\\n2026-04-07 - CP backward graph fix (autograd::mul + autograd::contiguous) + generation shape fix (generation_mode_ in CPAttention) - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test.cpp, ContextParallel.h\\n2026-04-10 - TDD verification tests for CP Round-Robin + Tiling - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/test_roundrobin_verify.py\\n2026-04-10 - Debug: CP 56k vs PyTorch 64k gap root cause = scalar FP32 kernel (no TC), WMMA TC path disabled in FusedSDPAOp.h; cudaStreamSync fix was no-op, reverted - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPAOp.h, FusedSDPAKernel.cu, ContextParallel.h, AttentionKernels.cu\\n2026-04-10 - Wire TC forward kernel for CAUSAL+NONE ring steps (self+future), scalar fallback for LEFT_HALF/BOT_HALF; namespace fix OwnTensor::cuda:: - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPAOp.h\\n2026-04-14 - BOT_HALF TC forward/backward mismatch root cause analysis & fix - TensorParallelismBeta / FusedSDPAOp.h, FusedSDPABackwardKernel.cu\\n2026-04-27 - MultiTensorKernels scale/grad_norm rewritten to chunked+float4 (sm_86) - TensorParallelismBeta / MultiTensorKernels.cu\\n2026-04-27 - 124M scaling diagnosis: dual optim.step + cudaSync + clip kernels - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test.cpp, MultiTensorKernels.cu\\n2026-04-27 - 124M bottleneck rediagnosis: optim 0.06% of step, real cost is attn_cp+bwd compute - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-04-28 - CP attention forward+backward kernels updated to support strided Q/K/V/dO/O/LSE/dQ/dK/dV; dropped autograd::contiguous(q) in ContextParallel.h - TensorParallelismBeta / AttentionForward.cu, AttentionBackward.cu, AttentionForward.h, AttentionBackward.h, FusedSDPAOp.h, ContextParallel.h\\n2026-04-28 - Added strided KV pack kernel; CP forward ring rotator now sends from non-contig K/V; dropped autograd::contiguous on K and V in pre_sharded path - TensorParallelismBeta / KVPackKernel.cu, KVPackKernel.h, ContextParallel.h\\n2026-04-29 - CP causal LB enable: drop !is_causal_ guard on lb_active + gate inner loadbalance on !pre_sharded (Zigzag round-robin sub-chunking now active for causal training) - TensorParallelismBeta / ContextParallel.h\\n2026-04-29 - CP LB sub-chunking: drop .contiguous() on strided make_shards halves; rely on strided kernel dispatch (fixes silent data corruption on transposed Q with stride[1]<stride[2]) - TensorParallelismBeta / ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-04-30 - Reverted LB-causal enable: lb_active back to load_balance_ && !is_causal_; LB sub-chunking diverges/explodes norm at 44M correctness check. Skip-future path is the stable baseline. - TensorParallelismBeta / ContextParallel.h\\n2026-04-30 - LB-causal correctness harness scaffold (TDD RED): cp_lb_causal_correctness_test.cpp + force_lb_active knob in CP ctor + Makefile target - TensorParallelismBeta / cp_lb_causal_correctness_test.cpp, ContextParallel.h, Makefile\\n2026-05-07 - Step 2 forward activation parity debug - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_headtail_fp32.py, gpt2_cp_test.cpp, diff_act_checksums.py - Fixed token dump placement (C++ was pre-sharding, PT post-sharding), found embedding divergence starts with sharded tokens\\n2026-05-07 - Embedding divergence was missing LOAD_INIT_WEIGHTS env var; embedding parity confirmed bit-exact, real divergence at block_0_out (attention) - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test.cpp, gpt2_cp_headtail_fp32.py\\n2026-05-07 - CP backward dK/dV ring accumulation fix (memset wiping rotating accumulator) - TensorParallelismBeta / AttentionBackward.cu\\n2026-05-08 - CP attn kernel HD=64 + T_q!=T_k divergence diagnosed (not yet fixed) - TensorParallelismBeta / AttentionForward.cu\\n2026-05-08 - HD=64 TC kernel bypass + repro mismatch fix - TensorParallelismBeta / AttentionForward.cu, ContextParallel.h\\n2026-05-08 - Gradient checksum logging added to both PT and C++ (DUMP_GRADS=1) - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test.cpp, gpt2_cp_headtail_fp32.py\\n2026-05-09 - CatBackward autograd node + autograd::cat fix restoring wte/wpe gradient chain in shard_sequence - TensorParallelismBeta / CatBackward.h, CatBackward.cpp, ContextParallel.h\\n2026-05-13 - CP utility-based feature comparison table (Ours vs Megatron vs PyTorch) - TensorParallelismBeta / misc/comparison_table_prompt.md\\n2026-05-15 - Debug printing restored for all CP ranks at every step (all parameter/gradient values) - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_headtail_fp32.py\\n2026-05-15 - Pre-embedding sequence sharding (contiguous + HeadTail) for CP - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-05-16 - LB+causal gate untangled (external_balanced + sub_chunk_active) - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-05-16 - HeadTail kernel rewritten to chunk-level (PyTorch parity, Option 2) - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor/tensor/headtail_kernel.cu, headtail_kernel.cuh, dtensor.cpp, gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h\\n2026-05-18 - Re-introduced LOAD_INIT_WEIGHTS pipeline (PT writer + C++ reader) for true bit-parity init between PyTorch and C++ CP training - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor / Pytorch/gpt2_cp_headtail_fp32.py, gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-05-19 - CP backward switched from merged_out/merged_lse to per-step saved_out/saved_lse to fix LB partial-step gradient corruption - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-05-20 - CP-bwd isolated test built (PT+C++); localized LB-true training bug to exp11 SDPA backward kernel producing ~1.35x over-amplified dQ at head index >= 1 in chunk_3 tail region - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor / gpt2_cp_test/cp_bwd_isolated_test.cpp, Pytorch/cp_bwd_isolated_test.py, tensor_lib_partial_update_test.cpp, AttentionBackward.cu (suspect)\\n2026-05-20 - Isolated CP-bwd test LB-OFF run confirms kernel is innocent: all dQ/dK/dV match PT within ~1e-5 (TF32 noise) under non-LB; LB-ON has 100x errors localized to LB-specific accumulation paths (partial dQ on rank 0, head-half pad-then-add on rank 1). Tensor library ops verified correct in isolation. Bug is in LIVE invocation of CPB.h accumulation paths under LB - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor\\n2026-05-20 - SDPAMerger partial-merge narrow_view stride bug fix - TensorParallelismBeta / SDPAMerger.h, ContextParallel.h, cp_bwd_isolated_test.{py,cpp}, cp_bwd_diff_deep.py\\n2026-05-20 - EOD writeup on loss deviation / step-33 norm explosion debug (root cause: SDPAMerger partial-branch narrow_view fed to flat-fast-path elementwise op) - TensorParallelismBeta / SDPAMerger.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, cp_bwd_isolated_test\\n2026-05-23 - Link DTensor Makefile with BluBlas via WITH_BLUBLAS flag - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/Makefile\\n\\n2026-06-05 - CP step-0 grad parity: root-caused orthogonal grads to LOAD_INIT_WEIGHTS scrambling weights (C++ vs PT param-order mismatch); added name+transpose-aware LOAD_INIT_NAMED loader; forward parity confirmed (emb cos 1.0), residual TF32/GELU divergence left for next session - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test.cpp, Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py, Pytorch/compare_step0_grads.py, Pytorch/compare_fwd_parity.py\\n2026-06-05 - Backported TF32 round-to-nearest (round_tf32_wmma_frag, +0x1000u half-ULP) into CP attention kernels to remove biased truncation suspected of driving C++ grad-norm drift (->2 vs PT 0.8); 2 fwd + 7 bwd WMMA sites - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/AttentionForward.cu, AttentionBackward.cu\\n2026-06-05 - Verified TF32 round-to-nearest backport: NO effect (blk0 cos 0.9475 unchanged, grad cos unchanged) -> attention WMMA NOT the divergence source; suspect Linear-GEMM matmul precision / LayerNorm / structural pos-0 anomaly; next = intra-block bisect - TensorParallelismBeta / misc/compareoutputenwattnkernel.md, DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/Attention{Forward,Backward}.cu\\n2026-06-05 - Compared latest-of-latest TI attn kernels vs TxT/2: GPU is RTX 3060 (sm86) so sm89/Ada + 3xTF32 precision paths cannot run; on sm86 generic path TxT/2 is numerically equivalent to latest -> no port needed, attention RULED OUT as divergence source; suspect Linear-GEMM/LayerNorm/pos-0 - TensorParallelismBeta / misc/compareoutputenwattnkernel.md\\n2026-06-05 - Reran ws=1 parity with new latest-of-latest TI lib: ZERO change (blk0 cos 0.9475 identical); added PT_TF32 toggle, PT-in-TF32 also ZERO change -> precision RULED OUT, divergence is STRUCTURAL (prime suspect: causal position-0 edge, cos 0.17); grad magnitudes still match (1.0026) - TensorParallelismBeta / Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py, misc/compareoutputenwattnkernel.md\\n2026-06-05 - LOCALIZED the C++<->PT divergence to the ATTENTION sub-block via intra-block-0 bisect: emb cos 1.0 -> post-attn 0.941 (gap appears here) -> post-MLP 0.948 (MLP adds nothing); prime cause = C++ TF32-WMMA SDPA vs PT fp32 SDPA (PT_TF32 didnt fix bc allow_tf32 != SDPA backend); added ATTN_FP32=1 toggle to force scalar fp32 attn kernel to confirm - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/FusedSDPAOp.h, AttentionForward.h, Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py, compare_fwd_parity.py\\n2026-06-05 - ATTN_FP32 test: C++ scalar-fp32 vs TF32 attn give DIFFERENT bytes (md5 e7fe29 vs 2d3312) but BOTH cos 0.9408 vs PT -> attention gap is STRUCTURAL not precision (precision fully ruled out). Clue: per-token pos-0 cos 0.18 (attends only to self) -> causal-mask/first-row or CP-ring-vs-PT-SDPA algorithmic diff. NOTE grad mags match + training works (may be benign). Next: dump raw SDPA output pre-c_proj - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/FusedSDPAOp.h\\n2026-06-05 - ROOT CAUSE of entire CP grad-orthogonality saga: raw SDPA output matches PT exactly (cos 1.0 incl token0), divergence is 100% attn.c_proj. LOAD_INIT_NAMED loader transposed Linear weights by SHAPE-detection, which silently fails for the only SQUARE Linear (attn.c_proj 768x768) -> loaded W instead of W^T (proved: cos(c_proj_cpp, y@W)=1.0 vs y@W^T=0.003). Fixed loader to transpose by ROLE (explicit needs_transpose per param). Only attn.c_proj behavior changes. Rebuild+rerun pending - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-06-05 - CONFIRMED FIX: after attn.c_proj transpose correction, full ws=1 parity achieved - all forward checkpoints (emb/sdpa/blk0attn/blk0/lnf) cosine 1.000000, step-0 grads cosine 1.000000 (ln_f & c_attn, was 0.42/0.033), TOTAL ratio 0.9999. Entire CP grad-orthogonality investigation CLOSED: root cause was parity-harness square-Linear transpose bug, not model/CP/kernel - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp\\n2026-06-05 - FULL backward parity verified: extended step-0 grad dump to all 149 params per-element cosine (C++ raw blob, Linear weights transposed to PT layout). Result: cosine min=mean=1.000000, #(<0.999)=0, TOTAL ratio 0.9999. C++ CP forward AND backward now bit-faithful to PyTorch at matched init - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp, Pytorch/compare_step0_grads.py\\n2026-06-05 - ws=2 ring parity: C++ ws=2 grad == PT ws=1 (true single-pass full-batch grad) at cosine min 0.9998/mean 0.99998 -> C++ CP RING IS CORRECT. PT attnstyle ws=2 DEVIATES from its own ws=1 (wpe cos 0.80, early-MLP lower) -> PyTorch's load-balanced ring changes the gradient (position-routing fingerprint on wpe). So C++ ws=2 'mismatch' vs PT ws=2 is PT deviating, not C++. Likely root of original Q1 (attnstyle behaves differently) - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test + Pytorch attnstyle\\n2026-06-05 - DUG OUT Q1 ROOT CAUSE: PT attnstyle CP position-embedding bug. gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py:423 sets pos=arange(0,T_local) -> at ws=2 BOTH ranks use pos 0..511, so wpe[512:1024] gets ZERO grad (measured: same-pos cos=0.000 for p>=512, 0.10 for 256:512, 0.886 for 0:256) and rank1 tokens get wrong positional encoding. Should be GLOBAL positions per rank (LB-reorder-aware). C++ does this correctly (C++ ws=2 == PT ws=1 single-pass at cos 0.9998). This is why attnstyle loss differed/worsened. Fix = compute global pos per rank - TensorParallelismBeta / Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py:423\\n2026-06-05 - Q1 FIX CONFIRMED: sharded global pos through CP LB machinery (gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py:~413, pos_full added to _context_parallel_buffers). After fix: PT ws=2 vs PT ws=1 cosine min=mean=1.000000 (#<0.999=0), wpe[512:] now nonzero; PT ws=2(fixed) vs C++ ws=2 cosine 0.9998. The attnstyle CP pos-embedding bug (pos=arange(0,T_local)) was THE root of Q1. All now in full parity: ws=1 & ws=2, PT & C++, forward & backward - TensorParallelismBeta / Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py\\n2026-06-05 - Added PT MODEL_44M env flag mirroring ALL C++ fourtyfour changes (n_embd384/n_layer3/n_head6, global_batch65536, max_steps6768); SAVE_INIT_NAMED now writes config-tagged files. Generated init_weights_named_161M.bin (149 params, 652MB) and init_weights_named_44M.bin (41 params, 177MB), seed 1234, loadable via LOAD_INIT_NAMED with matching config - TensorParallelismBeta / Pytorch/gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py\\n2026-06-08 - ROOT CAUSE of C++ CP grad-norm explosion / loss saturation (161M, ~step 800+): param-gradient all-reduce across CP ranks was COMMENTED OUT in training loop -> divergent replicas (each rank steps on its own sequence-shard grad). Ring only sums attn dQ/dK/dV, not Linear/LN/embed weight grads. Fixed: enabled AVG all-reduce (not stale SUM; loss is NOT 1/ws-scaled, AVG verified == single-GPU grad cos 1.0 at step0) after micro-accum, before clip; CP_NO_GRAD_ALLREDUCE=1 to A/B. Independent of overlap work. - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/gpt2_cp_test.cpp:1278\\n2026-06-08 - REAL root cause of no compute/comm overlap: DeviceMesh creates the NCCL comm stream with cudaStreamCreate (DEFAULT/blocking flags) at tensor/device_mesh.cpp:190 and passes it to init_process_group -> else-branch uses it as-is. A default-flagged stream implicitly serializes with the legacy NULL stream (stream 0) where ALL compute runs (kernels launch with no stream arg; setCurrentStream never called) -> zero overlap. The cudaStreamNonBlocking edit in processGroupNCCL.cpp was DEAD CODE (stream==0 branch never taken from mesh, so its print never fired). FIX: cudaStreamCreateWithFlags(&comm_stream, cudaStreamNonBlocking) at device_mesh.cpp:190. Algorithm already matches PyTorch (post-exchange-before-compute, copy-to-send, streamWait consume); PyTorch overlaps same ncclDevKernel_SendRecv because its streams are non-blocking. P2P disabled on 2x3060 (canAccessPeer=0) but asyncEngineCount=2. - TensorParallelismBeta / tensor/device_mesh.cpp\\n2026-06-10 - Overlap run unstable AND CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 gave SAME unstable curve. Cause: comm stream was made non-blocking GLOBALLY+UNCONDITIONALLY in device_mesh.cpp -> removed the implicit stream0<->comm ordering the whole codebase relied on (e.g. K/V pack on stream0 then NCCL send on comm with NO explicit event in non-overlap path) -> both paths race -> identical instability. CP_NO_OVERLAP only gated ring scheduling, not the stream flag. FIX: gate comm-stream flag on CP_NO_OVERLAP in device_mesh.cpp (blocking when off=stable original; non-blocking when on). Overlap-ON path still has unmasked races to fix (validate via ws=2 step0 parity). Cleaner long-term: dedicated CP-ring stream, not global comm-stream flip. - TensorParallelismBeta / tensor/device_mesh.cpp\\n2026-06-10 - VERIFIED via nsys (ws=2, this 2x3060 box): dedicated-CP-ring-stream overlap WORKS and toggles correctly. CP_NO_OVERLAP=0 -> ring on dedicated non-blocking stream(18), 2324 NCCL-vs-compute(stream7) overlap pairs (~1966ms incl bwd-SDPA overlapping SendRecv). CP_NO_OVERLAP=1 -> dedicated stream never created, ring on shared blocking stream(14), 0 overlap pairs. Shared comm stream stays blocking (DP/TP safe). Step-0 grad parity ovl-vs-noovl cos 0.99998. Next: full multi-step =0 run to confirm training stability (global-flip destabilizer removed) + measure throughput. - TensorParallelismBeta / ProcessGroupNCCL, device_mesh.cpp, RingRotator.h2026-06-10 - CP ring-attention overlap race audit: CUDA stream ordering bugs in forward send_buf lifetime, bwd dkv_send lifetime, shared pack_event destroy-while-pending, and cross-step recv slot aliasing - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/RingRotator.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-06-10 - CP ring-attention overlap race audit: CUDA stream ordering bugs in forward send_buf lifetime, bwd dkv_send lifetime, shared pack_event destroy-while-pending, and cross-step recv slot aliasing - TensorParallelismBeta / DTensor/gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/RingRotator.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n\\n2026-06-10 - Fixed the ~step-145 overlap explosion: two races found by cpp-review. (1) pack_event was created+destroyed PER CALL and shared across ring iters -> at full pipeline depth cudaEventDestroy fired while the ring stream's pending cudaStreamWaitEvent still referenced it (UB) -> send stopped waiting for pack. (2) stack-local send_buf/dkv_send freed at function return while the FINAL slot's send still in flight (reuse guard never covers last slot). FIX: rotator now OWNS persistent per-slot pack events (pack_ev_[2], never per-call destroy); exchange_buffers takes pack_stream (compute stream) not an event; added post-loop streamWait drain of all pending sends before staging buffers free (fwd + bwd). Step-0 A/B overlap-vs-nooverlap now cos 1.000000. NEEDS multi-step (>145) run to confirm explosion gone. Added CP_NO_OVERLAP_FWD/BWD bisection gates. - TensorParallelismBeta / RingRotator.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-06-10 - Addressed all 4 overlap_fix.md review points: (1) comments recast event-destroy race as unconditional UB not 'deep pipeline'; (2) pack_ev_[2] invariant documented + rotator SELF-GUARDS (streamWait prior slot send before re-record); (3) audited drain coverage - in-loop guard + both-slot drain = complete; (4) drain tail-serialization ceiling documented w/ PyTorch upgrade path (recordStream/TensorShelf, verified from shipped ProcessGroupNCCL.hpp). FIXED sentinel bug: pack stream==NULL stream(0) made overlap silently degrade to blocking; exchange_buffers now takes explicit bool overlap. Verified: toggle flips fwd+bwd correctly, step-0 A/B cos 0.99998 - TensorParallelismBeta / RingRotator.h, ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h, misc/overlap_fix.md\\n2026-06-11 - PyTorch-parity fix: gave the CP ring its OWN NCCL communicator (cp_comm_) in ProcessGroupNCCL, separate from comm_ (loss/param all-reduces). Constructor inits cp_comm_ (2nd ncclGetUniqueId on rank0 + MPI_Bcast + ncclCommInitRank); sendrecv_async_stream/alltoallv_async_stream (the overlap-only ring methods) now use cp_comm_; launch_work_collectives takes work_comm; destructor frees cp_comm_+cp_ring_stream_. Zero plumbing through model/mesh (ring already used only the *_stream methods). Matches PyTorch (separate comm per parallelism dim) -> ring + all-reduces never share a comm. Also reconciled overlapfixplanfix.md review: its criticals (per-slot send-work streamWait guard exch_work/dkv_work; events absorbed into rotator as pack_ev_; .data<float>()+k_numel) were ALREADY in code. Verified: toggle ok, no deadlock, step-0 A/B cos 0.99999. PENDING: full >150-step run to confirm slow divergence fixed. - TensorParallelismBeta / process_group/ProcessGroupNCCL.{h,cpp}\\n2026-06-11 - Separate cp_comm_ did NOT fix the overlap explosion (still diverges ~step140) -> NOT the shared comm. Found the REAL bug: dkv_rotater is a LOCAL unique_ptr in ContextParallelBackward (line 142), destroyed at function return; grad_key/grad_value were returned to autograd as VIEWS into its recv buffer (final_flat.narrow().reshape()) -> dangling/use-after-free. No-overlap hides it (CPU-blocking + caching allocator delays reuse); overlap's async CPU-run-ahead lets the freed buffer be reused before downstream c_attn backward consumes grad_key -> rare corruption -> grad spikes at depth. Explains overlap-only + depth-dependent + spiky + survived-separate-comm. FIX: .clone() grad_key/grad_value at the LB final collect (ContextParallelBackward.h:543). Step-0 A/B cos 0.999999 (no regression). Running full 160-step confirmation. - TensorParallelismBeta / gpt2_cp_test/context_parallel/ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-06-11 - CP overlap divergence root-caused & fixed (cross-stream allocator-reuse race at ring tail; GPU-side drain -> CPU wait) - gpt2_cp_test / ContextParallel.h, ContextParallelBackward.h\\n2026-06-15 - CP overlap race-fix docs review (both false-positive); fixed misleading drain comment & AllGather sync - OldPush / ContextParallel.h, RingRotator.h\\n2026-06-16 - PyTorch 2.9.0+cu128 TF32-vs-FP32 precision research (Linear/SDPA/ring-attn/LayerNorm/GELU on RTX 3060 sm86); confirmed allow_tf32 default off + SDPA independent of allow_tf32 vs v2.9.0 source - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor (research only, no files modified)\\n2026-06-16 - Audited C++ vs PyTorch CP FP32/TF32 placement parity: MISMATCH at Linear GEMMs (C++ TF32 hardcoded vs PT FP32 default) and SDPA attention (C++ TF32-WMMA vs PT FP32 mem-efficient; PT_TF32 doesn't affect SDPA, ATTN_FP32 doesn't affect C++ Linear); MATCH on LayerNorm/GELU/softmax/CE/embeddings; full FP32 parity needs PT-default+ATTN_FP32=1+C++ GEMM code change, full TF32 impossible (PT SDPA has no TF32 path) - OldPush / gpt2_cp_test.cpp, gpt2_cp_attnstyle_fp32.py, GenMatmul.cu, AttentionForward.cu, AttentionBackward.cu, FusedSDPAOp.h\\n2026-06-16 - PyTorch 2.9.0 mem-efficient SDPA fp32-on-sm86 MMA-op source audit: confirmed DefaultGemmType<ArchTag,float,kMinComputeCapability>=80> uses OpClassTensorOp + cutlass::arch::OpMultiplyAddFastF32 (3xTF32 tensor cores), compile-time fixed, NOT gated by allow_tf32; both Q.K^T (MM0) and P.V (MM1) GEMMs use it - TensorParallelismBeta/DTensor (research only, no files modified)\\n2026-06-17 - CP TxT/2 kernel question: confirmed PyTorch 2.9 needs NO specialized TxT/2 kernel - zigzag LB produces 3 shapes (2cx2c causal diag, 2cxc + cx2c dense rectangular) all dispatched to the SAME SDPA op via tensor slicing in _templated_ring_attention; rectangular cases are dense (is_causal=False, no MFU waste); only requirement = one kernel handling Tq!=Tk - TensorParallelismBeta / torch _attention.py:442-466, AttentionForward.cu\\n\\n2026-06-18 - sm89 drop-in FusedSDPAOp variant: calls Ada PTX-MMA fwd/bwd kernels directly (no arch gate), t