r bluscriptCP (production CP model) vs DeepSpeed-Ulysses Qwen3: ported CP_MEM_PROBE snapshot mode into bluscriptCP.cpp (env CP_MEM_PROBE/CP_MEM_PROBE_STEPS/CP_MODEL_LABEL, grad_accum->1, skip val/ckpt, cudaMemGetInfo+alloc-peak+nvidia-smi snapshot matching gpt2_cp_test format) + new Tests/bluscriptcp/{mem_scaling_sweep.sh,mem_scaling_table.py} driving deepspeed qwen3_ds_ulysses.py; portable across 2xRTX3060/Nx6000Ada via CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES; syntax-verified (mpic++ c++20 fsyntax rc=0, bash -n, py_compile) NOT run end-to-end - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Tests/bluscriptcp/mem_scaling_sweep.sh, Tests/bluscriptcp/mem_scaling_table.py\",\" 2026-07-16 - bluscriptcp mem-scaling sweep: added CP_FFN + CP_WEIGHT_TYING env to bluscriptCP.cpp (ffn now recomputed 8/3*d_model after CP_N_EMBD override; tying env-settable) and expanded Tests/bluscriptcp/mem_scaling_sweep.sh to a 2-config matrix (48M d384/L6/6-2/ffn1024/untied + 114M d768/L12/12-4/ffn2048/tied) driving BOTH bluscriptCP and DS-Qwen3 with matching dims (DS head_dim forced 64 via --head_dim, --intermediate, --tie_weights); DS_MODEL=qwen3|gpt2|both toggle; per-config Ulysses head-split guard (48M->CP<=2, 114M->CP<=4). Verified mpic++ c++20 fsyntax rc=0, bash -n, py_compile - CP / Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Tests/bluscriptcp/mem_scaling_sweep.sh, Tests/bluscriptcp/mem_scaling_table.py\",\"+2026-07-20 - CREAM context-extension (single-GPU/CP_SIZE=1) in bluscriptCP, fully ADDITIVE (CP_CREAM_MODE=off => byte-identical): exploits that at CP_SIZE=1 the fused kernel indexes cos_sin_cache[local_idx] (deltas collapse to 0), so gathering cache rows for CREAM labels needs NO CUDA change. New header CreamPositions.h (3-layer: pure cream_labels_from_draws / rand_factor_from_u+end_id_range / RNG wrapper; faithful port of bigai-nlco CREAM src/train.py incl. .astype(int) truncation, true rand_factor/2 division, inclusive randint, np.interp(u,cdf,x) arg order) + PoSE/RandPos. ContextParallel.h: additive set_rope_cache setter (grad-free assert). bluscriptCP.cpp: CP_CREAM_MODE/SIGMA/SEED/LOG env, factor=YARN_SCALE & scaled_max=factor*T derived (no independent knob), startup asserts (YARN_SCALE>1, factor>=2, CP_SIZE=1), separate cream_full_cache_ built at scaled_max (base cache untouched), T!=context_length guard preserved verbatim on off-path/gated on cream, per-step gather-once-fan-out install (train resample per step, eval fixed seed). Tests: cream_positions_test (34 golden checks vs Python; odd-rf true-div guard) PASS; cream_cache_gather_parity (gather exact + kernel(cache=Gd,delta=0)==ref cos>0.999 + YaRN-active dir check) PASS. Built CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 clean; smoke tiny cfg T256 CP_SIZE=1: off-mode loss 10.87->10.27 (baseline unchanged), cream YARN_SCALE=8 scaled_max=2048 loss 10.87->10.29 no-NaN, middle_start dist varies. README CP_CREAM_* section. CP>1 deferred (needs per-token pos array in kernel) - CP / context_parallel/CreamPositions.h, context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp, Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp, Makefile, README.md\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MuofgskhLvgMXtnLJYS1Fz\",\"duration_ms\":6}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":72},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eed3d97f-1825-461f-9f71-9964b83a3c52","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:13:57.142Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"eed3d97f-1825-461f-9f71-9964b83a3c52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDSxJqy1tpNDQxZ8erJS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the session report:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_read_input_tokens":272598,"output_tokens":2431,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2431,"cache_read_input_tokens":272598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDSxGqv2BixUUqrjfypd","type":"assistant","uuid":"21088799-f02e-459e-b956-879b260b4d98","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:14:00.693Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"21088799-f02e-459e-b956-879b260b4d98","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDSxJqy1tpNDQxZ8erJS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0198SDZ2KZDJM6x93RxdaaZg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/Documents/obsidian Vaults/Adhitya's Vault/Claude Reports/ClaudeReport_session_2026-07-20_cream_context_extension.md","content":"# Claude Report — CREAM context extension in bluscriptCP\n\n- **Date - time:** 2026-07-20 19:43\n- **One line:** Implemented CREAM position-relabeling context extension (single-GPU / CP_SIZE=1) in the CP Llama trainer, fully additive, with a no-CUDA-change cache-gather trick.\n- **Workspace / files:** CP / context_parallel/CreamPositions.h, context_parallel/ContextParallel.h, Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp, Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp, Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp, Makefile, README.md\n\n---\n\n## Goal\n\nAssess whether `Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp` can implement the CREAM method\n(bigai-nlco/CREAM, NeurIPS 2024 — *Continuity-Relativity indexing with Gaussian Middle*)\nand, if so, implement it. CREAM extends the usable context window by fine-tuning at the\nphysical sequence length `T` while feeding manipulated RoPE position **labels** drawn from a\nlarger `scaled_max` range (head block + truncated-Gaussian middle + tail block), keeping the\nattention matrix `T x T`.\n\nUser constraints: single-GPU (`CP_SIZE=1`) first, CP later; serve both training and the\n`CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path; **every change must be additive** (no existing implementation erased;\n`CP_CREAM_MODE=off` byte-identical to before).\n\n## Key finding (why it is feasible with no CUDA change)\n\nRoPE positions in this stack are never stored as data. The fused kernel computes\n`pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes `cos_sin_cache[pos]`\n(`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At\n`CP_SIZE=1` all deltas collapse to 0, so `pos == local_idx`, and the wrapper derives\n`cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count (`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore feeding a\ncache whose row `j` holds the cos/sin for CREAM label `L[j]` makes the UNMODIFIED kernel rotate\neach token at its label. Implementation = gather cache rows per step; no kernel edits.\n\n## What was built (all additive, gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`)\n\n1. **`context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (new, header-only, std-only, unit-testable). Three\n   layers isolating cross-language port hazards: pure `cream_labels_from_draws`, the\n   `rand_factor_from_u` / `end_id_range` range-CDF layer, and an RNG sampling wrapper. Faithful\n   port of `src/train.py` including the four subtle details: `.astype(int)` **truncation** (not\n   round), **true** `rand_factor/2` division, inclusive `randint`\n   (`std::uniform_int_distribution`), and `np.interp(u, cdf, x)` argument order. Plus PoSE and\n   RandPos.\n2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — added `set_rope_cache()` (grad-free assert); only\n   called under CREAM, so the default path is untouched.\n3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — `CP_CREAM_MODE/SIGMA/SEED/LOG` env; `factor =\n   YARN_SCALE` and `scaled_max = factor*T` **derived** (no independent knob → cannot drift);\n   startup asserts (`YARN_SCALE>1`, `factor>=2`, `CP_SIZE=1`, `scaled_max % T == 0`); a separate\n   `cream_full_cache_` built at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (base cache left verbatim); the\n   `T != context_length` guard preserved verbatim on the off-path and gated for CREAM; per-step\n   install that gathers once and fans out to all layers (training resamples per step; eval uses a\n   fixed seed); optional middle-block-start distribution log.\n4. **Tests** — `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp` (golden values captured from the real Python\n   math; includes the odd-`rand_factor` true-division guard) and\n   `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp` (gather exactness, `kernel(cache=Gd, delta=0)` vs\n   de-fused reference, YaRN-active direction check). Both wired into the Makefile.\n5. **README.md** — CREAM env-var section with the batch-shared-labeling caveat and single-GPU\n   scope.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `make cream-positions` — 34/34 checks PASS (golden math, range/CDF, structural, guards, randint,\n  PoSE/RandPos).\n- `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cream-cache-parity` — PASS: gather rows exact (maxdiff 0), kernel vs ref\n  cos=0.9996, YaRN direction identical at pos 0 and diverges (cos 0.36) at high pos.\n- `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp` — clean build.\n- Smoke (tiny cfg, `CP_SIZE=1`, `T=256`): off-mode loss 10.87→10.27 (baseline unchanged);\n  `CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=8` (scaled_max=2048) loss 10.87→10.29, no NaN, finite grad-norm;\n  distribution log varies across the middle range.\n\n## Notes / deferred\n\n- v1 shares one labeling across the batch (resampled per step) and relabels the natural\n  contiguous token chunk — sufficient for extension; documented.\n- The pre-existing YaRN warn when the base cache (length `context_length`) is built with\n  `YARN_SCALE>1` is harmless under CREAM (that base cache is overridden by the gather); the\n  `cream_full_cache_` at `scaled_max` matches `factor*T` cleanly.\n- **Deferred (CP_SIZE>1):** needs an explicit per-token position array threaded into\n  `gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` (device `pos = q_pos[idx]`), fed from the sharder's\n  already-computed-but-unused `ShardedInputs::pos_local`. This also unlocks true per-row labels.\n\n## Plan file\n\n`/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md` (approved after three review rounds:\nsource-diff fidelity, cross-language port hazards, and the additive/non-destructive requirement).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_read_input_tokens":272598,"output_tokens":2431,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2431,"cache_read_input_tokens":272598,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1866,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1866},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDSxGqv2BixUUqrjfypd","type":"assistant","uuid":"210cc643-59d8-4d2b-b5e6-0a2b98537704","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:14:28.180Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
