{"parentUuid":"ba830a95-d7a7-49d0-9e74-864c96cfa729","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdDT1bwx9DGqLxNSLNHhU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. CREAM context extension is implemented, built, tested, and documented — single-GPU (`CP_SIZE=1`) as you scoped, fully additive.\n\n## What was delivered\n\n**The core insight that made it cheap:** at `CP_SIZE=1` the fused kernel's RoPE deltas collapse to zero, so `pos == local_idx`. Feeding a cache whose row `j` holds the cos/sin for CREAM label `L[j]` makes the *unmodified* kernel rotate every token at its label. So CREAM is a per-step **cache-row gather** — **no CUDA changes**.\n\n**Files (all changes gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`; `off` = byte-identical to before):**\n- [context_parallel/CreamPositions.h](context_parallel/CreamPositions.h) — new generator, faithful port of the paper's `train.py` with the four cross-language hazards pinned (`.astype(int)` truncation, true `rand_factor/2`, inclusive `randint`, `np.interp` arg order). CREAM + PoSE + RandPos.\n- [context_parallel/ContextParallel.h](context_parallel/ContextParallel.h) — additive `set_rope_cache()` (grad-free assert).\n- [Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp) — env, derived `factor=YARN_SCALE`/`scaled_max=factor·T` (no drift), startup asserts, separate `cream_full_cache_`, guard preserved-and-gated, gather-once/fan-out install for train + eval.\n- Two tests + Makefile targets, README section.\n\n**Verification (all green):**\n- Unit test: 34/34 (golden values from the real Python math, incl. the odd-`rand_factor` true-division trap).\n- Parity: gather exact, `kernel(cache=Gd, delta=0)` vs reference cos=0.9996, YaRN confirmed active.\n- Smoke on 2×3060: off-mode loss 10.87→10.27 (baseline intact); CREAM `YARN_SCALE=8` (scaled_max=2048) loss 10.87→10.29, no NaN; distribution log varies.\n\n**On which variant helps context extension:** all three do — PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method, CREAM adds the Gaussian middle (lost-in-the-middle), RandPos is a weaker baseline. CREAM is implemented as primary; PoSE/RandPos ride the same plumbing.\n\n**Deferred (as agreed):** multi-GPU CP needs an explicit per-token position array in the kernel (fed from the sharder's unused `pos_local`) — documented in the plan.\n\nWork logged to your Obsidian Logs.md and a session report written to Claude Reports/. Note I did not run any git commands, per your rules."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_read_input_tokens":276991,"output_tokens":966,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":276991,"cache_creation_input_tokens":751,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":751},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdDT1Ydma8ZBhZ5PDLWVp","type":"assistant","uuid":"577f8782-4214-4df2-a60d-60e087b7d6dd","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:14:58.094Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
