\\n- Unit test: 34/34 (golden values from the real Python math, incl. the odd-`rand_factor` true-division trap).\\n- Parity: gather exact, `kernel(cache=Gd, delta=0)` vs reference cos=0.9996, YaRN confirmed active.\\n- Smoke on 2×3060: off-mode loss 10.87→10.27 (baseline intact); CREAM `YARN_SCALE=8` (scaled_max=2048) loss 10.87→10.29, no NaN; distribution log varies.\\n\\n**On which variant helps context extension:** all three do — PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method, CREAM adds the Gaussian middle (lost-in-the-middle), RandPos is a weaker baseline. CREAM is implemented as primary; PoSE/RandPos ride the same plumbing.\\n\\n**Deferred (as agreed):** multi-GPU CP needs an explicit per-token position array in the kernel (fed from the sharder's unused `pos_local`) — documented in the plan.\\n\\nWork logged to your Obsidian Logs.md and a session report written to Claude Reports/. Note I did not run any git commands, per your rules.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":54},"type":"attachment","uuid":"68ace408-e39c-4711-94c4-a737bd6933b8","timestamp":"2026-07-20T14:14:58.188Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.212","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
