{"parentUuid":"50f0336e-dabb-4d9d-9ff3-be5d4ff5effd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEbDKwZCrZvJCozZoGjr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's not a correctness knob — it's a statistical-stability one. `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` is how many length-`T` sequences get teacher-forced and averaged into each position's NLL.\n\n**What determines it:** each position `t` in the curve gets `count = CP_EVAL_WINDOWS × CP_B` samples averaged (see the `cnt[t]` accumulation, [bluscriptCP.cpp:1097-1098](Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp#L1097-L1098)). PPL(t) = exp(mean NLL over those samples). So the window count sets the samples-per-position.\n\n**Rule of thumb:**\n- **Shape/sanity check:** `count ≈ 50–100` per position is enough to see whether the curve is flat vs. blows-up. With the default `CP_B=8`, that's `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS ≈ 8–16` (the default is 10).\n- **A clean/comparable A-vs-B curve:** aim for `count ≈ 300–500` per position — e.g. `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS ≈ 40–64` at `CP_B=8`. Long positions have higher NLL variance, so lean to the top of that range at 16k.\n\n**Two hard constraints:**\n1. **Don't exceed distinct held-out data.** Total tokens consumed = `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS × CP_B × T`. If that exceeds the val split, the loader wraps and you just re-average the same sequences — more windows then adds no statistical power (and silently biases toward whatever repeats). Size it to what the val shards actually hold in **≥T-token** documents.\n2. **Cost is linear in windows** — each window is a full `T×T` forward. At 16k on one GPU that's the expensive part, so use the *smallest* window count that gives a stable curve; validate the shape at small T first.\n\nKeep `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` **identical across models A/B/C** — the comparison is only valid if every curve is averaged over the same number of samples on the same eval data."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262837,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":1207,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262837,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1207,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":262837,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":262837},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdEbDHTEMf66SvV9xkt8P","type":"assistant","uuid":"f86d42ff-dfb8-4ac5-b9f0-fabf8e0603d4","timestamp":"2026-07-21T04:43:15.605Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
