{"parentUuid":"8e1e4ace-6a77-4825-9bbe-87eed0c94674","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEc1qQP2YqzTiZYGq1qz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_read_input_tokens":283724,"output_tokens":711,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":283724,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEc1o9CSDKftC58DSLAQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"baa30f5a-b58f-4e2c-b32e-2aded44c2013","timestamp":"2026-07-21T04:53:28.171Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"baa30f5a-b58f-4e2c-b32e-2aded44c2013","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEc1qQP2YqzTiZYGq1qz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — they're unrelated, and it's worth being clear because conflating them would bias your eval.\n\n| | `YARN_SCALE` | `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` |\n|---|---|---|\n| **What it is** | A **modeling** parameter — the context-extension factor `target_ctx / orig_ctx` (e.g. 4 for 4k→16k). | A **measurement** parameter — how many length-`T` sequences you average to estimate PPL. |\n| **What it changes** | The RoPE frequencies (NTK-by-parts interpolation) the model actually computes with. It changes the model's *output*. | Nothing about the model. Only the *statistical precision* of your PPL curve. |\n| **Set by** | The extension target you're evaluating. Must match how the model was trained. | The variance you'll tolerate / how much held-out data you have. |\n\nSo `YARN_SCALE` is part of *what* you're testing (the 16k extension); `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` is part of *how carefully* you measure it. Changing `YARN_SCALE` gives you a different model behavior; changing `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` just makes the same curve smoother or noisier.\n\nThe one thing they share: both must be held **fixed and identical** across models A/B/C, or the comparison isn't apples-to-apples — but for opposite reasons (`YARN_SCALE` because it defines the task, `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` because it defines the sample size)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_read_input_tokens":283724,"output_tokens":711,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":711,"cache_read_input_tokens":283724,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEc1o9CSDKftC58DSLAQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a12b55c5-0241-4d53-abce-62c3c0ef5fa8","timestamp":"2026-07-21T04:53:34.243Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a12b55c5-0241-4d53-abce-62c3c0ef5fa8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"37bc1370-ba3c-4703-a84a-5f3408a6b226","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"e4da3d24-7ccc-48c6-b090-7b90b1602e18\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"No — they're unrelated, and it's worth being clear because conflating them would bias your eval.\\n\\n| | `YARN_SCALE` | `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **What it is** | A **modeling** parameter — the context-extension factor `target_ctx / orig_ctx` (e.g. 4 for 4k→16k). | A **measurement** parameter — how many length-`T` sequences you average to estimate PPL. |\\n| **What it changes** | The RoPE frequencies (NTK-by-parts interpolation) the model actually computes with. It changes the model's *output*. | Nothing about the model. Only the *statistical precision* of your PPL curve. |\\n| **Set by** | The extension target you're evaluating. Must match how the model was trained. | The variance you'll tolerate / how much held-out data you have. |\\n\\nSo `YARN_SCALE` is part of *what* you're testing (the 16k extension); `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` is part of *how carefully* you measure it. Changing `YARN_SCALE` gives you a different model behavior; changing `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` just makes the same curve smoother or noisier.\\n\\nThe one thing they share: both must be held **fixed and identical** across models A/B/C, or the comparison isn't apples-to-apples — but for opposite reasons (`YARN_SCALE` because it defines the task, `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` because it defines the sample size).\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":52},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cb543735-da86-4475-8377-1033433078cc","timestamp":"2026-07-21T04:53:34.326Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
