{"parentUuid":"f6bf50ae-8ab1-4814-8b65-d1b55f10bac7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEcWr6rYHqz7rjiMLjTS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":284949,"output_tokens":1549,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1549,"cache_read_input_tokens":284949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEcWovPSVxTLtE4R74Ch","type":"assistant","uuid":"0b55cd62-3356-45cb-b235-626315a3be93","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:00:04.661Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"0b55cd62-3356-45cb-b235-626315a3be93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEcWr6rYHqz7rjiMLjTS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the concrete runbook.\n\n## 1. Build (once)\n```bash\ncd /home/blu-bridge25/CP\nmake CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp\n```\n\n## 2. Run CREAM fine-tuning\nCREAM is a fine-tune, so the normal flow is: base checkpoint at 4k → resume with CREAM on. But you can also just launch it directly to see it work.\n\n**Quick test (tiny, single GPU — the config I verified):**\n```bash\nCP_SIZE=1 CP_T=256 \\\nCP_N_EMBD=256 CP_N_LAYER=2 CP_N_HEAD=4 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 \\\nCP_B=2 CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=512 CP_MAX_STEPS=50 CP_WARMUP=5 CP_CKPT=0 \\\nCP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 CP_CREAM_LOG=cream_mid.csv \\\nYARN_SCALE=8 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=256 \\\nCP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\n**Real shape (4k physical, labels to 16k → `YARN_SCALE=4`):**\n```bash\nCP_SIZE=1 CP_T=4096 \\\nCP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\nYARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\nCP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<target> \\\nCP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\nCP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\n## The knobs that matter\n- `CP_CREAM_MODE=cream` — turns it on (`off` = normal training; also `pose`/`randpos`).\n- `YARN_SCALE` — **this is the extension factor**; `factor` and `scaled_max = factor·CP_T` are derived from it. Must be integer ≥ 2. `scaled_max` here = the \"16k interval\" your labels span.\n- `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=CP_T` — keeps YaRN sized to your physical length (avoids the mismatch warn).\n- `CP_SIZE=1` — required (single-GPU only for now).\n- `CP_CREAM_LOG=cream_mid.csv` — optional; logs `step,middle_start` so you can confirm the Gaussian sampling.\n\n## Sanity checks at startup\nYou should see **two** cache builds — the base (`seq_len=CP_T`) and the CREAM source (`seq_len=scaled_max`), both `scale=<factor>`:\n```\n[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=4096 hd=... scale=4.000 ...\n[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=16384 hd=... scale=4.000 ...\n```\nThen loss should decrease with finite grad-norm. If you set `CP_CREAM_MODE=off`, it's byte-identical to a normal run.\n\nWant the base→CREAM two-stage as a single script, or are you starting from an existing base checkpoint?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_read_input_tokens":284949,"output_tokens":1549,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1549,"cache_read_input_tokens":284949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":794,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":794},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEcWovPSVxTLtE4R74Ch","type":"assistant","uuid":"ccdd7bde-f398-4c99-b0ff-a0f902f6d907","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:00:17.999Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ccdd7bde-f398-4c99-b0ff-a0f902f6d907","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"4274a9f0-5c80-4329-a0e3-99f4b0080474","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"c320af6f-fba1-4dbe-93a7-f5643b5de2bc\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Here's the concrete runbook.\\n\\n## 1. Build (once)\\n```bash\\ncd /home/blu-bridge25/CP\\nmake CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp\\n```\\n\\n## 2. Run CREAM fine-tuning\\nCREAM is a fine-tune, so the normal flow is: base checkpoint at 4k → resume with CREAM on. But you can also just launch it directly to see it work.\\n\\n**Quick test (tiny, single GPU — the config I verified):**\\n```bash\\nCP_SIZE=1 CP_T=256 \\\\\\nCP_N_EMBD=256 CP_N_LAYER=2 CP_N_HEAD=4 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 \\\\\\nCP_B=2 CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=512 CP_MAX_STEPS=50 CP_WARMUP=5 CP_CKPT=0 \\\\\\nCP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 CP_CREAM_LOG=cream_mid.csv \\\\\\nYARN_SCALE=8 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=256 \\\\\\nCP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads \\\\\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\n\\n**Real shape (4k physical, labels to 16k → `YARN_SCALE=4`):**\\n```bash\\nCP_SIZE=1 CP_T=4096 \\\\\\nCP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\\\\nYARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\\\\nCP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<target> \\\\\\nCP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\\\\nCP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads \\\\\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\n\\n## The knobs that matter\\n- `CP_CREAM_MODE=cream` — turns it on (`off` = normal training; also `pose`/`randpos`).\\n- `YARN_SCALE` — **this is the extension factor**; `factor` and `scaled_max = factor·CP_T` are derived from it. Must be integer ≥ 2. `scaled_max` here = the \\\"16k interval\\\" your labels span.\\n- `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=CP_T` — keeps YaRN sized to your physical length (avoids the mismatch warn).\\n- `CP_SIZE=1` — required (single-GPU only for now).\\n- `CP_CREAM_LOG=cream_mid.csv` — optional; logs `step,middle_start` so you can confirm the Gaussian sampling.\\n\\n## Sanity checks at startup\\nYou should see **two** cache builds — the base (`seq_len=CP_T`) and the CREAM source (`seq_len=scaled_max`), both `scale=<factor>`:\\n```\\n[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=4096 hd=... scale=4.000 ...\\n[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=16384 hd=... scale=4.000 ...\\n```\\nThen loss should decrease with finite grad-norm. If you set `CP_CREAM_MODE=off`, it's byte-identical to a normal run.\\n\\nWant the base→CREAM two-stage as a single script, or are you starting from an existing base checkpoint?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":41},"type":"attachment","uuid":"83d0f510-c6c1-4090-88a2-38f7fc07aa4f","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:00:18.093Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
