{"parentUuid":"eefc1715-64e6-4500-9a3d-19380e2cbbd5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_15306","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[SessionEnd] Updated session file: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/sessions/2026-07-21-CP-session.tmp\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"386d8f14-ddb2-4ea1-b2d1-659a72f0d120","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:14:30.155Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"386d8f14-ddb2-4ea1-b2d1-659a72f0d120","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEddFDSm3XEiuZ7vQSwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":287312,"output_tokens":3386,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3386,"cache_read_input_tokens":287312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEddDAfKy7TSvametxES","type":"assistant","uuid":"9365e76c-2f60-48a8-b95a-8289aa3b877c","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:15:01.009Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9365e76c-2f60-48a8-b95a-8289aa3b877c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEddFDSm3XEiuZ7vQSwq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two good questions.\n\n## What `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` does\n\nIt's the width (std-dev) of the truncated Gaussian that places the **middle block** within the extended range — the \"Gaussian Middle\" in CREAM's name. In [CreamPositions.h](context_parallel/CreamPositions.h) it feeds `cdf = 0.5·(1+erf((x−μ)/(σ·√2)))` with `μ = 1+factor` over `x ∈ [2, 2·factor]`; the sampled `rand_factor` then sets where the middle block lands (small → near the start of the range, large → near `scaled_max`), centered at `μ` = the **middle** of the extended context.\n\n- **Small σ** → middle blocks cluster tightly at the center of the long context. Strongly trains middle positions (fights \"lost-in-the-middle\") but under-covers the extremes.\n- **Large σ** → approaches uniform coverage across the whole range (more PoSE-like), less middle emphasis.\n- **σ = 3.0** (default) = the paper's balance.\n\nSo it's the one knob that distinguishes CREAM from a plain uniform position-skip scheme.\n\n## You're right — the two commands weren't a matched pair\n\nThose were a *tiny smoke test* and a *real-shape example* at different scales, not the A-vs-B pair. For a valid comparison, **pin every model/optim/data/YaRN/eval config identically** across arms; only the training-position strategy and physical length differ.\n\n**Shared block (identical for A and B):**\n```bash\nSHARED=\"CP_SIZE=1 \\\n  CP_N_EMBD=768 CP_N_LAYER=12 CP_N_HEAD=12 CP_N_KVHEAD=4 \\\n  CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=524288 CP_MAX_STEPS=<N> CP_WARMUP=<W> \\\n  YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\n  CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads\"\n```\n\n**A — CREAM+YaRN (cheap, 4k physical):**\n```bash\nenv $SHARED CP_T=4096 CP_B=8 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\n**B — YaRN LCE (expensive, real 16k):**\n```bash\nenv $SHARED CP_T=16384 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=off \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=<needs CP for 16k attention>\n```\n\nTwo things **must** differ (and that's the point, not a config error):\n- **`CP_T`** — 4096 for A, 16384 for B. This is the whole experiment: A never allocates 16k attention.\n- **`grad_accum`** — it's *derived* as `CP_GLOBAL_BATCH / (CP_B·CP_T·dp)`, so it auto-adjusts. Keep **`CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` identical** (same tokens/step) and let grad_accum change. `CP_B` may also have to drop for B purely for memory (16k is 4× the activation of 4k) — that's fine *as long as `CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` stays equal*, because that's what fixes the optimization trajectory.\n\nEverything else — d_model/heads/layers/vocab, LR schedule, weight decay, seed, data split, and the **eval** (`CP_T=16384`, `CP_CREAM_MODE=off`, `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS`) — identical across A, B, and the naive-C baseline."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_read_input_tokens":287312,"output_tokens":3386,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3386,"cache_read_input_tokens":287312,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1659,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1659},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdEddDAfKy7TSvametxES","type":"assistant","uuid":"9353a755-1245-4985-bb9e-957ceb7e6a9a","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:15:15.852Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9353a755-1245-4985-bb9e-957ceb7e6a9a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"d097f268-ed5f-4be6-ade1-23353dfe66d2","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"4f7aefe4-e678-4cc8-a264-50489ab08058\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Two good questions.\\n\\n## What `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` does\\n\\nIt's the width (std-dev) of the truncated Gaussian that places the **middle block** within the extended range — the \\\"Gaussian Middle\\\" in CREAM's name. In [CreamPositions.h](context_parallel/CreamPositions.h) it feeds `cdf = 0.5·(1+erf((x−μ)/(σ·√2)))` with `μ = 1+factor` over `x ∈ [2, 2·factor]`; the sampled `rand_factor` then sets where the middle block lands (small → near the start of the range, large → near `scaled_max`), centered at `μ` = the **middle** of the extended context.\\n\\n- **Small σ** → middle blocks cluster tightly at the center of the long context. Strongly trains middle positions (fights \\\"lost-in-the-middle\\\") but under-covers the extremes.\\n- **Large σ** → approaches uniform coverage across the whole range (more PoSE-like), less middle emphasis.\\n- **σ = 3.0** (default) = the paper's balance.\\n\\nSo it's the one knob that distinguishes CREAM from a plain uniform position-skip scheme.\\n\\n## You're right — the two commands weren't a matched pair\\n\\nThose were a *tiny smoke test* and a *real-shape example* at different scales, not the A-vs-B pair. For a valid comparison, **pin every model/optim/data/YaRN/eval config identically** across arms; only the training-position strategy and physical length differ.\\n\\n**Shared block (identical for A and B):**\\n```bash\\nSHARED=\\\"CP_SIZE=1 \\\\\\n  CP_N_EMBD=768 CP_N_LAYER=12 CP_N_HEAD=12 CP_N_KVHEAD=4 \\\\\\n  CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=524288 CP_MAX_STEPS=<N> CP_WARMUP=<W> \\\\\\n  YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\\\\n  CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**A — CREAM+YaRN (cheap, 4k physical):**\\n```bash\\nenv $SHARED CP_T=4096 CP_B=8 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\\\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\n\\n**B — YaRN LCE (expensive, real 16k):**\\n```bash\\nenv $SHARED CP_T=16384 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=off \\\\\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=<needs CP for 16k attention>\\n```\\n\\nTwo things **must** differ (and that's the point, not a config error):\\n- **`CP_T`** — 4096 for A, 16384 for B. This is the whole experiment: A never allocates 16k attention.\\n- **`grad_accum`** — it's *derived* as `CP_GLOBAL_BATCH / (CP_B·CP_T·dp)`, so it auto-adjusts. Keep **`CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` identical** (same tokens/step) and let grad_accum change. `CP_B` may also have to drop for B purely for memory (16k is 4× the activation of 4k) — that's fine *as long as `CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` stays equal*, because that's what fixes the optimization trajectory.\\n\\nEverything else — d_model/heads/layers/vocab, LR schedule, weight decay, seed, data split, and the **eval** (`CP_T=16384`, `CP_CREAM_MODE=off`, `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS`) — identical across A, B, and the naive-C baseline.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c4a62372-0e86-4db2-93b0-c22f60e1558a","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:15:15.922Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
