{"parentUuid":"459507f8-68dd-4a3f-89c2-fad350f9dd1e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"4ec26f20-c968-4324-a7fc-e0d6f51300f2","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"0f976e19-cb9f-433c-b0c0-09edf096379a\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"No. `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` does **not** touch `T` or the extension length at all.\\n\\n- **What sets 16k:** `YARN_SCALE × CP_T`. That's it. `scaled_max = factor·CP_T` — the position range the labels can span. (e.g. `CP_T=4096`, `YARN_SCALE=4` → labels reach 16k.)\\n- **What σ does:** given that range is already fixed at [0, 16k), σ only controls *where inside it* the middle block tends to land — tightly clustered at the center (small σ) vs. spread toward the extremes (large σ). It reshapes the *sampling distribution*, not the range.\\n\\nAnalogy: `YARN_SCALE` sets how wide the dartboard is (up to 16k); σ sets how tightly your throws cluster around the bullseye (the middle). Changing σ never makes the board bigger.\\n\\nSo the physical sequence stays `CP_T` (4k of real attention), the reachable positions stay `factor·CP_T` (16k), regardless of σ. σ just tunes how much of the training emphasizes middle positions.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":51},"type":"attachment","uuid":"28382224-242a-4894-a409-1de91b85d86f","timestamp":"2026-07-21T05:17:49.404Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP