{"parentUuid":"e26eb15b-1a41-4fd5-83e1-b66022f37110","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_15933","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 123 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d859d79a-403e-4bbe-be19-f93980d1be79","timestamp":"2026-07-21T06:32:51.666Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"d859d79a-403e-4bbe-be19-f93980d1be79","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEjbq34sim1cSQZV2pwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274457,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":1865,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdEjbnTY8ZdKY91xqMALT","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8265d4e-eddb-463b-a53b-657b3616b6f6","timestamp":"2026-07-21T06:33:11.303Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a8265d4e-eddb-463b-a53b-657b3616b6f6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdEjbq34sim1cSQZV2pwx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both are fine-tunes on top of the **same base checkpoint** — CREAM is *not* trained from scratch. That's the entire premise of the method.\n\n**Why:** CREAM and YaRN-LCE are both **context-extension** techniques. They answer \"I have a model pretrained at 4k — how do I cheaply teach it 16k?\" Training from scratch wouldn't be \"extension,\" it'd be pretraining (vastly more expensive, and not what the paper does). CREAM's whole selling point is *short fine-tune, cheap attention* — which only makes sense starting from a competent base.\n\n**So the protocol is:**\n\n```\nBase model: pretrained at 4k, normal positions  ──┐  (one shared checkpoint)\n                                                   │\n        ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┤\n        ▼                                           ▼\nArm A: resume base, CREAM fine-tune (4k)   Arm B: resume base, YaRN fine-tune (16k)\n```\n\nBoth **`CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run>`** from identical weights, both a short fine-tune, ideally the **same step budget** — otherwise you're comparing training recipes *and* training length, and the eval isn't clean.\n\nConcretely, CREAM uses the exact same resume path you'd use for YaRN LCE:\n\n```bash\n# Arm A — CREAM, resumed from base:\nenv $SHARED CP_T=4096 CP_B=8 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<base_step + K> \\\n    CP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\nSame `CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run>` for arm B (just `CP_T=16384 CP_CREAM_MODE=off`). The re-warmup (`CP_REWARMUP`) matters for both — resuming for extension causes a perplexity spike, so you re-ramp LR to a reduced peak (the 2-stage flow already in the README).\n\nNote the checkpoint loads fine even though `CP_T` differs between base (4k) and the extension arms — RoPE positions are computed, not learned, so the same weights load at any sequence length and the cache is rebuilt from the YaRN/CREAM env (this was verified in earlier sessions). Keep the architecture (d_model/heads/kv/layers/vocab) identical or the load won't match.\n\nSo: **base once, then CREAM and YaRN both branch off it as fine-tunes** — never CREAM from scratch."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274457,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":1865,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274457,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1865,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274457},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdEjbnTY8ZdKY91xqMALT","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a9506ef-1cc4-42b6-8740-ddac8977c6fa","timestamp":"2026-07-21T06:33:22.870Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"8a9506ef-1cc4-42b6-8740-ddac8977c6fa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"20be279f-97f3-4cfe-b52b-d3818c0d7689","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"9a716507-2186-4087-8fdd-e0ea44a67ff6\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Both are fine-tunes on top of the **same base checkpoint** — CREAM is *not* trained from scratch. That's the entire premise of the method.\\n\\n**Why:** CREAM and YaRN-LCE are both **context-extension** techniques. They answer \\\"I have a model pretrained at 4k — how do I cheaply teach it 16k?\\\" Training from scratch wouldn't be \\\"extension,\\\" it'd be pretraining (vastly more expensive, and not what the paper does). CREAM's whole selling point is *short fine-tune, cheap attention* — which only makes sense starting from a competent base.\\n\\n**So the protocol is:**\\n\\n```\\nBase model: pretrained at 4k, normal positions  ──┐  (one shared checkpoint)\\n                                                   │\\n        ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n        ▼                                           ▼\\nArm A: resume base, CREAM fine-tune (4k)   Arm B: resume base, YaRN fine-tune (16k)\\n```\\n\\nBoth **`CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run>`** from identical weights, both a short fine-tune, ideally the **same step budget** — otherwise you're comparing training recipes *and* training length, and the eval isn't clean.\\n\\nConcretely, CREAM uses the exact same resume path you'd use for YaRN LCE:\\n\\n```bash\\n# Arm A — CREAM, resumed from base:\\nenv $SHARED CP_T=4096 CP_B=8 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\\\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<base_step + K> \\\\\\n    CP_REWARMUP=<W> CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\\\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\n\\nSame `CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base_run>` for arm B (just `CP_T=16384 CP_CREAM_MODE=off`). The re-warmup (`CP_REWARMUP`) matters for both — resuming for extension causes a perplexity spike, so you re-ramp LR to a reduced peak (the 2-stage flow already in the README).\\n\\nNote the checkpoint loads fine even though `CP_T` differs between base (4k) and the extension arms — RoPE positions are computed, not learned, so the same weights load at any sequence length and the cache is rebuilt from the YaRN/CREAM env (this was verified in earlier sessions). Keep the architecture (d_model/heads/kv/layers/vocab) identical or the load won't match.\\n\\nSo: **base once, then CREAM and YaRN both branch off it as fine-tunes** — never CREAM from scratch.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":44},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3d5ce544-e4df-4953-8bd6-171a95552bb8","timestamp":"2026-07-21T06:33:22.941Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
