{"parentUuid":"223d1b70-ff58-4458-9f7d-db15be9ec5f2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFFSoMMiQeA5T3b5Wwhs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two steps — and the notebook cell only does the **second** one. That `.mdfiles/pplevalipynb.md` is empty, and the plotting cell actually lives in [graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb](graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb). It does **not** run the model — it just plots CSVs. So you first generate the CSVs by running the binary in eval mode, then run the notebook cell to overlay them.\n\n## Step 1 — generate one CSV per model (this is the actual eval)\n\nEval mode (`CP_EVAL_PPL=1`) is forward-only, requires `CP_SIZE=1`/`NP=1`, loads a checkpoint via `CP_CKPT_RESUME`, writes `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` to `CP_EVAL_OUT`, and exits. Same eval config for all three; only the checkpoint (and CREAM being off) varies:\n\n```bash\nEVAL=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off \\\n  CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0 \\\n  CP_T=16384 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 \\\n  YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\n  CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads\"\n\n# C — naive baseline: base model, no long fine-tune, YaRN at inference\nenv $EVAL CP_CKPT_RESUME=$BASE CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_C_naive.csv \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n\n# A — CREAM+YaRN\nenv $EVAL CP_CKPT_RESUME=101 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_A_cream.csv \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n\n# B — YaRN LCE\nenv $EVAL CP_CKPT_RESUME=102 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_B_yarn.csv \\\n    make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\nKey points:\n- **`CP_CREAM_MODE=off` on all three** — CREAM is training-only; at eval every model sees natural positions `[0..16k)` on the YaRN cache. That's the fair test.\n- **Everything identical except `CP_CKPT_RESUME`** — same `CP_T=16384`, same `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32`, same YaRN. Only the weights differ.\n- It reads the **val** split; make sure your val data has documents ≥16k tokens or the far positions carry no signal.\n\n## Step 2 — plot/overlay in the notebook\n\nOpen [graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb](graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb) and run the PPL-vs-position cell, pointing it at the three CSVs (`ppl_A_cream.csv`, `ppl_B_yarn.csv`, `ppl_C_naive.csv`). You want: **A and B flat and overlapping, both well below C** past the 4k mark. If the cell is hardcoded to one filename, tell me and I'll give you a small overlay cell that loads all three and plots `ppl` vs `pos`.\n\n## Caveat (same as before)\nThe 16k eval is one 16k×16k forward on a single 3060 — even forward-only this may OOM at 12GB. If it does, prove the pipeline first at **8k** (`CP_T=8192 YARN_SCALE=2`, base was 4k), then scale up. The eval is where the 16k cost lands regardless of how the model was trained.\n\nWant me to write the 3-CSV overlay cell into the notebook so Step 2 is one run?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284371,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":2605,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":284371,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2605,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":284371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":284371},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdFFSmM4HuxtTBcKBBP5B","type":"assistant","uuid":"a4297557-00c7-4fcd-8ba1-59a1b0028026","timestamp":"2026-07-21T13:04:51.442Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
