{"parentUuid":"17d11567-1005-4b5f-a60d-b1df2ffc6d22","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFMgay4LyvfwcQw9jXoD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3325,"cache_read_input_tokens":328140,"output_tokens":1256,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1256,"cache_read_input_tokens":328140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3325},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFMgWqGfxQCZmcgTkAo6","type":"assistant","uuid":"1dec90ae-ec21-4094-894f-bf8e9406e3cd","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:26:13.090Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"1dec90ae-ec21-4094-894f-bf8e9406e3cd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFMgay4LyvfwcQw9jXoD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"Moves\" = **step to step, the same middle slots get relabeled to a different part of the 0–16k range.** The physical tokens don't move; only the *labels* assigned to the middle block get re-randomized each optimizer step.\n\nConcretely — the middle always occupies physical slots `1365..2730`, and head/tail labels are always fixed. Only the middle's label window slides:\n\n```\n                 head (fixed)      MIDDLE (re-sampled a)     tail (fixed)\nstep 0:  labels  0..1364     |     7000 .. 8365       |    15019..16383\nstep 1:  labels  0..1364     |     3000 .. 4365       |    15019..16383\nstep 2:  labels  0..1364     |    11000 ..12365       |    15019..16383\nstep 3:  labels  0..1364     |     6200 .. 7565       |    15019..16383\n```\n\nSame 4096 physical tokens every step. Same head labels, same tail labels. The **only** thing changing is the middle block's starting label `a` — a fresh draw each step.\n\nIn the code this is literally: each step calls `install_cream_positions(seed = cream_seed + step)`, which re-samples `a` (via the Gaussian) and rebuilds the label vector. You saw this in the smoke run's `CP_CREAM_LOG` — the `middle_start` column was different every row (727, 328, 1242, …); those are the successive `a` values.\n\n**Why it matters:** if `a` were fixed, the model would only ever practice one middle region and one set of gap sizes. By re-drawing `a` each step, over the course of training the middle block **sweeps across the whole interior** of the 0–16k range — so the model eventually sees every intermediate position and a wide range of head→middle and middle→tail gap distances. That coverage-over-time is the \"relativity\" part; the Gaussian just makes it linger near the center (the lost-in-the-middle weak spot) more than the edges.\n\nSo: within one step it's a fixed 3-block layout; across steps the middle block's label window keeps jumping to new locations. That's the \"movement.\""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3325,"cache_read_input_tokens":328140,"output_tokens":1256,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3325,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1256,"cache_read_input_tokens":328140,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3325,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3325},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFMgWqGfxQCZmcgTkAo6","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ba0fbf2-ad18-4859-ad0c-e8000e35ce25","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:26:22.824Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6ba0fbf2-ad18-4859-ad0c-e8000e35ce25","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"a0c761d8-a9fc-4023-b10a-44991ab17bc2","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"e0329bcb-4bfe-49fa-92da-6a358435d9f1\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"\\\"Moves\\\" = **step to step, the same middle slots get relabeled to a different part of the 0–16k range.** The physical tokens don't move; only the *labels* assigned to the middle block get re-randomized each optimizer step.\\n\\nConcretely — the middle always occupies physical slots `1365..2730`, and head/tail labels are always fixed. Only the middle's label window slides:\\n\\n```\\n                 head (fixed)      MIDDLE (re-sampled a)     tail (fixed)\\nstep 0:  labels  0..1364     |     7000 .. 8365       |    15019..16383\\nstep 1:  labels  0..1364     |     3000 .. 4365       |    15019..16383\\nstep 2:  labels  0..1364     |    11000 ..12365       |    15019..16383\\nstep 3:  labels  0..1364     |     6200 .. 7565       |    15019..16383\\n```\\n\\nSame 4096 physical tokens every step. Same head labels, same tail labels. The **only** thing changing is the middle block's starting label `a` — a fresh draw each step.\\n\\nIn the code this is literally: each step calls `install_cream_positions(seed = cream_seed + step)`, which re-samples `a` (via the Gaussian) and rebuilds the label vector. You saw this in the smoke run's `CP_CREAM_LOG` — the `middle_start` column was different every row (727, 328, 1242, …); those are the successive `a` values.\\n\\n**Why it matters:** if `a` were fixed, the model would only ever practice one middle region and one set of gap sizes. By re-drawing `a` each step, over the course of training the middle block **sweeps across the whole interior** of the 0–16k range — so the model eventually sees every intermediate position and a wide range of head→middle and middle→tail gap distances. That coverage-over-time is the \\\"relativity\\\" part; the Gaussian just makes it linger near the center (the lost-in-the-middle weak spot) more than the edges.\\n\\nSo: within one step it's a fixed 3-block layout; across steps the middle block's label window keeps jumping to new locations. That's the \\\"movement.\\\"\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":45},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ee3ef54f-d2f1-49ef-803a-7012f0d86e66","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:26:22.911Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
