{"parentUuid":"448bc3d1-37e4-4c0d-813e-f98ee88656f9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_54708","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 136 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"edd87802-d4f0-43e0-a0ed-4ed9c320b15e","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:27:54.694Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"edd87802-d4f0-43e0-a0ed-4ed9c320b15e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFMpxHSHKWNAcqwWDwoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":331465,"output_tokens":2334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2334,"cache_read_input_tokens":331465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFMpsGorFAmdTks9LRpR","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b8dc9e1-3f76-4d6b-9c2f-2aa6c47e2d56","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:28:13.921Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"5b8dc9e1-3f76-4d6b-9c2f-2aa6c47e2d56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFMpxHSHKWNAcqwWDwoU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes — `a` comes from an RNG, but it's a **two-stage** draw, not a flat uniform pick. The Gaussian enters in stage 1; a uniform jitter finishes it in stage 2. Here's the exact chain from [CreamPositions.h](context_parallel/CreamPositions.h) (`generate_cream_positions`):\n\n**Seed:** one `std::mt19937_64` seeded with `cream_seed + step` — deterministic per step, different every step. Three draws come off it:\n\n1. **`branch = randint(0,1)`** — picks the head/tail size regime (`T/3` vs `4·factor`).\n\n2. **`u = uniform_real(0,1)`** — a plain uniform draw. This is the *only* raw randomness for placement.\n\n3. **`rand_factor = rand_factor_from_u(u, factor, sigma)`** — this is where the Gaussian lives. `u` is pushed through the **inverse CDF of a truncated Gaussian** (`mu = 1+factor`, width `sigma`) over the range `[2, 2·factor]`:\n   ```\n   cdf = 0.5·(1 + erf((x − mu)/(sigma·√2))),  rand_factor = trunc(interp(u, cdf, x))\n   ```\n   So `rand_factor` is **Gaussian-distributed, centered at the middle** of `[2, 2·factor]`. It's the coarse \"how far out into the 16k range\" knob. With `factor=4`: `rand_factor ∈ [2,8]`, centered at 5.\n\n4. **`[lo,hi] = end_id_range(...)`** — `rand_factor` defines a window: roughly `hi ≈ (rand_factor/2)·T`. So `rand_factor=2` → window near `T` (≈4k), `rand_factor=8` → window near `4T` (≈16k), `rand_factor=5` → ≈`2.5T` (≈10k).\n\n5. **`end_id = randint(lo, hi)`** — a **uniform** draw *inside* that window (the fine jitter).\n\n6. **`a = end_id − (len_chunk − 1)`** — the middle-block start is derived from `end_id` (the block is `[a, end_id]`).\n\nSo the distribution of `a` is: **Gaussian-weighted across the extended range** (via `rand_factor`, step 3 — this is what concentrates it near the center), then **uniformly jittered within the selected band** (via `end_id`, step 5). It is *not* uniform over `[head, scaled_max−tail)` — that's the whole point; a uniform pick there would be RandPos/PoSE, and would under-sample the middle.\n\nQuick sanity map (`factor=4`, so the range is 16k):\n\n| `u` (uniform) | `rand_factor` (Gaussian) | middle lands near |\n|---|---|---|\n| ~0.05 | 2 | ~4k (low end of interior) |\n| ~0.5 | 5 (the peak) | ~10k (center-ish) |\n| ~0.95 | 8 | ~16k (far interior) |\n\nMost draws cluster around `rand_factor≈5` because that's the Gaussian peak — so the middle block spends most steps in the center region, occasionally venturing toward the ends. That's the \"importance-sample the middle\" behavior, implemented as: **uniform RNG → truncated-Gaussian inverse-CDF → band → uniform RNG jitter.**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_read_input_tokens":331465,"output_tokens":2334,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2334,"cache_read_input_tokens":331465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1273},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFMpsGorFAmdTks9LRpR","type":"assistant","uuid":"5870a31c-9ab7-4d45-8259-185c1f639a72","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:28:27.431Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"5870a31c-9ab7-4d45-8259-185c1f639a72","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"7370ab4f-64f1-4fc0-b743-7371f682f814","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"f7ad3f22-271b-451d-b400-39103e2c049f\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Yes — `a` comes from an RNG, but it's a **two-stage** draw, not a flat uniform pick. The Gaussian enters in stage 1; a uniform jitter finishes it in stage 2. Here's the exact chain from [CreamPositions.h](context_parallel/CreamPositions.h) (`generate_cream_positions`):\\n\\n**Seed:** one `std::mt19937_64` seeded with `cream_seed + step` — deterministic per step, different every step. Three draws come off it:\\n\\n1. **`branch = randint(0,1)`** — picks the head/tail size regime (`T/3` vs `4·factor`).\\n\\n2. **`u = uniform_real(0,1)`** — a plain uniform draw. This is the *only* raw randomness for placement.\\n\\n3. **`rand_factor = rand_factor_from_u(u, factor, sigma)`** — this is where the Gaussian lives. `u` is pushed through the **inverse CDF of a truncated Gaussian** (`mu = 1+factor`, width `sigma`) over the range `[2, 2·factor]`:\\n   ```\\n   cdf = 0.5·(1 + erf((x − mu)/(sigma·√2))),  rand_factor = trunc(interp(u, cdf, x))\\n   ```\\n   So `rand_factor` is **Gaussian-distributed, centered at the middle** of `[2, 2·factor]`. It's the coarse \\\"how far out into the 16k range\\\" knob. With `factor=4`: `rand_factor ∈ [2,8]`, centered at 5.\\n\\n4. **`[lo,hi] = end_id_range(...)`** — `rand_factor` defines a window: roughly `hi ≈ (rand_factor/2)·T`. So `rand_factor=2` → window near `T` (≈4k), `rand_factor=8` → window near `4T` (≈16k),