nter of the extended range is the mode; the tails (near the head end and near `scaled_max`) are rare because the fixed head/tail blocks already cover those, and the Gaussian deliberately doesn't waste middle-block draws there.\\n\\nIf you want to *see* the actual empirical distribution rather than reason about it: you already have `CP_CREAM_LOG` logging `middle_start` (that's essentially `a`) per step. Run a few thousand steps and histogram that column — you'll see the bell with the mild band structure. Want a quick cell to plot that histogram against an ideal Gaussian so you can confirm σ is doing what you expect?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":46},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e82b3be7-72c5-4240-a9ef-52de67e382ac","timestamp":"2026-07-21T14:32:07.558Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
