{"parentUuid":"7a45c5fb-578f-4246-b022-81ba22cd6291","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFQumQLAfpVLziENjHMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":340010,"output_tokens":2009,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":340010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFQuiCM8KPzb9L4GDAKW","type":"assistant","uuid":"80288fad-a566-434e-85b9-80286e757f30","timestamp":"2026-07-21T15:08:42.609Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"80288fad-a566-434e-85b9-80286e757f30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdFQumQLAfpVLziENjHMy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I want to be honest about the line between what I'm confident of and what I'd be guessing at.\n\n**What I'm reasonably confident about (qualitative):** CREAM (Wu et al., NeurIPS 2024, \"Never Miss A Beat…\", bigai-nlco) doesn't rely on PPL alone — its headline evaluations are the *retrieval / positional* ones, precisely because the Gaussian-middle is designed to attack \"lost in the middle\":\n\n- **Lost-in-the-Middle / multi-document QA** — this is CREAM's signature result. Baselines (PoSE, uniform/PI extension) show the classic U-shaped accuracy (good at the ends, sagging in the middle); CREAM's whole pitch is that its middle-focused sampling **flattens that curve** — more uniform accuracy across document positions. This is the eval where CREAM is claimed to *beat* the cheaper baselines, not just match full fine-tuning.\n- **Needle-in-a-Haystack** up to the target extended length — reported to retrieve well across positions including the middle band.\n- **Long-context benchmark suite(s)** (LongBench-style) and long-context **PPL** — reported competitive with/close to full-length fine-tuning while training only at the original window.\n\nSo the short version: **yes, the paper reports it does well beyond PPL, and specifically claims its advantage shows up most on the middle-position retrieval evals** — which is the point of the Gaussian, and directly relevant to my earlier caveat that PPL alone doesn't certify long-range retrieval.\n\n**What I won't fabricate:** exact numbers (which models, which lengths — I think Llama-2-7B extended to long windows — and the specific accuracy deltas vs PoSE). I don't have those pinned with confidence, and this is a factual claim about a specific paper, so I'd rather verify than guess.\n\nI have web access — want me to fetch the paper (and the repo's README/eval scripts) and pull the actual benchmark tables so you get the real numbers instead of my recollection? That also tells us exactly which evals to reproduce on your model to check that *your* CREAM run inherits the middle-retrieval benefit, not just the flat PPL."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_read_input_tokens":340010,"output_tokens":2009,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2009,"cache_read_input_tokens":340010,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2773,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2773},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdFQuiCM8KPzb9L4GDAKW","type":"assistant","uuid":"e8013cad-be0a-4fb6-a600-5114c319d5f0","timestamp":"2026-07-21T15:08:52.605Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
