t of the Gaussian, and directly relevant to my earlier caveat that PPL alone doesn't certify long-range retrieval.\\n\\n**What I won't fabricate:** exact numbers (which models, which lengths — I think Llama-2-7B extended to long windows — and the specific accuracy deltas vs PoSE). I don't have those pinned with confidence, and this is a factual claim about a specific paper, so I'd rather verify than guess.\\n\\nI have web access — want me to fetch the paper (and the repo's README/eval scripts) and pull the actual benchmark tables so you get the real numbers instead of my recollection? That also tells us exactly which evals to reproduce on your model to check that *your* CREAM run inherits the middle-retrieval benefit, not just the flat PPL.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1f632df7-2d91-4a32-b4ab-2a22ceeb467b","timestamp":"2026-07-21T15:08:52.680Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.215","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
