{"parentUuid":"87059456-7b00-43d0-b09e-a63e70d7d321","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHK7QWNFPFFhywEcR2f7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332637,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":3277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3277,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdHK7M31wGVk2ZbMaw64g","type":"assistant","uuid":"f1e00a34-4ede-4708-b792-c58b9fe3f43f","timestamp":"2026-07-22T15:14:08.724Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"f1e00a34-4ede-4708-b792-c58b9fe3f43f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHK7QWNFPFFhywEcR2f7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news: nothing is corrupted — you just didn't get an F=16 model, and run 33 is fine as your **F=8** model. Here's what actually happened and the fix.\n\n## What happened\nBecause `[16]=33` collided with `[8]=33`:\n- The F=16 step did `cp base → run33`, but run 33 already had the **F=8-trained** checkpoints at higher steps (e.g. step 1300).\n- `CP_CKPT_RESUME=33` loads the *latest* run-33 checkpoint → that's the F=8 model at its top step.\n- `start_step` already equalled `CP_MAX_STEPS`, so the loop ran zero steps → \"completed as it started.\" No training, and **no new checkpoint was saved**, so run 33 was not overwritten.\n\nNet state: **run 31 = F=2, run 32 = F=4, run 33 = F=8** (all intact). F=16 simply doesn't exist yet.\n\n## Fix — just do F=16 into a fresh number (34)\n\nFirst confirm the state and that 34 is free:\n```bash\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/ | grep -o 'run[0-9]*' | sort -u\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run33_*   # should show top step > base (the trained F=8)\n```\n\nThen branch base → 34 and train F=16 (single line):\n```bash\nBASE=<base_run>; R=34; (cd checkpoints_bluscriptcp && for f in blumodelcp_run${BASE}_*; do cp \"$f\" \"${f/run${BASE}/run${R}}\"; done); env $ARCH CP_T=4096 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 YARN_SCALE=16 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$R CP_MAX_STEPS=<base+K> CP_REWARMUP=100 CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n(Make sure `<base+K>` is above the base's top step, or this one will \"complete as it starts\" too.)\n\n## Two things to remember at eval time\n- **Run 33 is an F=8 model** — eval it with `YARN_SCALE=8 CP_T=32768`, regardless of what any config file says (the no-op F=16 attempt may have left a stray `YARN_SCALE=16` line in `CP_Training_log33_config.txt`; ignore it — the *weights* were trained at F=8).\n- Eval map becomes: run31→F2 (8k), run32→F4 (16k), run33→F8 (32k), run34→F16 (64k).\n\nThat's it — one clean F=16 run into 34 and your sweep is complete."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332637,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":3277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332637,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3277,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":332637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":332637},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdHK7M31wGVk2ZbMaw64g","type":"assistant","uuid":"c5a8c03c-4fa8-4289-9ae7-555d744020ff","timestamp":"2026-07-22T15:14:20.538Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c5a8c03c-4fa8-4289-9ae7-555d744020ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"08a96a59-07ea-4999-ba29-496abee6684a","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"f45a724d-36de-49ea-84ab-ec98c7ea51cc\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Good news: nothing is corrupted — you just didn't get an F=16 model, and run 33 is fine as your **F=8** model. Here's what actually happened and the fix.\\n\\n## What happened\\nBecause `[16]=33` collided with `[8]=33`:\\n- The F=16 step did `cp base → run33`, but run 33 already had the **F=8-trained** checkpoints at higher steps (e.g. step 1300).\\n- `CP_CKPT_RESUME=33` loads the *latest* run-33 checkpoint → that's the F=8 model at its top step.\\n- `start_step` already equalled `CP_MAX_STEPS`, so the loop ran zero steps → \\\"completed as it started.\\\" No training, and **no new checkpoint was saved**, so run 33 was not overwritten.\\n\\nNet state: **run 31 = F=2, run 32 = F=4, run 33 = F=8** (all intact). F=16 simply doesn't exist yet.\\n\\n## Fix — just do F=16 into a fresh number (34)\\n\\nFirst confirm the state and that 34 is free:\\n```bash\\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/ | grep -o 'run[0-9]*' | sort -u\\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run33_*   # should show top step > base (the trained F=8)\\n```\\n\\nThen branch base → 34 and train F=16 (single line):\\n```bash\\nBASE=<base_run>; R=34; (cd checkpoints_bluscriptcp && for f in blumodelcp_run${BASE}_*; do cp \\\"$f\\\" \\\"${f/run${BASE}/run${R}}\\\"; done); env $ARCH CP_T=4096 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 YARN_SCALE=16 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$R CP_MAX_STEPS=<base+K> CP_REWARMUP=100 CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\n(Make sure `<base+K>` is above the base's top step, or this one will \\\"complete as it starts\\\" too.)\\n\\n## Two things to remember at eval time\\n- **Run 33 is an F=8 model** — eval it with `YARN_SCALE=8 CP_T=32768`, regardless of what any config file says (the no-op F=16 attempt may have left a stray `YARN_SCALE=16` line in `CP_Training_log33_config.txt`; ignore it — the *weights* were trained at F=8).\\n- Eval map becomes: run31→F2 (8k), run32→F4 (16k), run33→F8 (32k), run34→F16 (64k).\\n\\nThat's it — one clean F=16 run into 34 and your sweep is complete.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":46},"type":"attachment","uuid":"85fe8037-76d6-4481-8d45-4ab30263fa3e","timestamp":"2026-07-22T15:14:20.639Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
