{"parentUuid":"99c586c2-5824-4bcb-acdd-688369a85219","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHKNBEaPUxeFYxKDPcAv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3695,"cache_read_input_tokens":353524,"output_tokens":3168,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3168,"cache_read_input_tokens":353524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHKN8PRgpMEgJiB4AT2k","type":"assistant","uuid":"b2d009c7-7bef-43bc-83f1-d1b1a1565503","timestamp":"2026-07-22T15:17:24.167Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b2d009c7-7bef-43bc-83f1-d1b1a1565503","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHKNBEaPUxeFYxKDPcAv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything checks out. Run 33 is a proper **F=8 model**: base clone at `step_917`, then CREAM fine-tuned `917 → 1222` (top step **1222**). And **34 is free** (your run list has no run34). So you're clear to do F=16 into 34.\n\nTwo quick confirmations first:\n\n**1. Find your BASE run** (the one you branched 31/32/33 from — it's the run whose top step is exactly 917):\n```bash\nfor r in $(ls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/ | grep -o 'run[0-9]*' | sort -u); do echo \"$r -> $(ls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_${r}_step_*.ckpt 2>/dev/null | grep -o 'step_[0-9]*' | sed 's/step_//' | sort -n | tail -1)\"; done\n```\nThe run that tops out at `917` (and isn't 31/32/33) is your base.\n\n**2. Match the fine-tune length.** Your F=8 arm ran `917 → 1222` (305 steps). Use the **same `CP_MAX_STEPS=1222`** for F=16 so all arms are comparable.\n\n## Run F=16 into run 34\n```bash\nBASE=<the run that tops at 917>; R=34; (cd checkpoints_bluscriptcp && for f in blumodelcp_run${BASE}_*; do cp \"$f\" \"${f/run${BASE}/run${R}}\"; done); env $ARCH CP_T=4096 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 YARN_SCALE=16 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=34 CP_MAX_STEPS=1222 CP_REWARMUP=100 CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n\nYou should see `[Resume] run 34 from step 917` and it should train to 1222 (not \"complete as it starts\"). After that your sweep is:\n\n| run | F | YARN_SCALE (train + eval) | target len |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 31 | 2 | 2 | 8k |\n| 32 | 4 | 4 | 16k |\n| 33 | 8 | 8 | 32k |\n| 34 | 16 | 16 | 64k |\n\nThen eval each with its matching `YARN_SCALE` and `CP_T = 4096·F`, `CP_CREAM_MODE=off`, `CP_B=1`. Reminder: the 32k/64k evals are the ones most likely to hit the single-GPU logits-memory ceiling — if run33/34 OOM at eval, that's the test-rig limit, not the model."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3695,"cache_read_input_tokens":353524,"output_tokens":3168,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3695,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3168,"cache_read_input_tokens":353524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3695,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3695},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHKN8PRgpMEgJiB4AT2k","type":"assistant","uuid":"a29c17fc-5f8c-4aeb-926b-e3ad70a2c7a1","timestamp":"2026-07-22T15:17:34.708Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
