{"parentUuid":"4a160b7b-ed50-4f7a-b91f-2954f3524b8e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHdJWk5Arwh11jwKekAs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339623,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":2249,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339623},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdHdJRkBzJnzrDcPnHPhd","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a867b7d-f112-44f0-9177-df6185359a49","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:12:19.518Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"3a867b7d-f112-44f0-9177-df6185359a49","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHdJWk5Arwh11jwKekAs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"After the four training runs finish, you move to the **eval phase**: generate one PPL-vs-position CSV per arm (plus a base floor), then overlay them and read off the extension limit.\n\n## 1. (Re-)set the shared vars in your shell\nIf this is a fresh login, re-declare them:\n```bash\nARCH=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0 CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=131072 CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads\"\nBASE=<run that tops at 917>\ndeclare -A RUN=( [2]=31 [4]=32 [8]=33 [16]=34 )\n```\n(Adjust `CP_DATA_ROOT` if the data lives elsewhere on this mount.)\n\n## 2. Eval each arm at its target length\n```bash\nfor F in 2 4 8 16; do R=${RUN[$F]}; T=$((4096*F)); env $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=$T CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=$F YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$R CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_cream_x${F}.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1; done\n```\nEach writes `ppl_cream_x{2,4,8,16}.csv` and exits. Note: `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` for all (CREAM is training-only), `YARN_SCALE=F` must match how that arm was trained.\n\n## 3. Add the 4k in-distribution floor (reference line)\n```bash\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=4096 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$BASE CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_base_4096.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\nThis is the PPL level you're trying not to exceed.\n\n## 4. Plot/overlay in the notebook\nIn [graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb](graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb), set:\n```python\nORIG_CTX = 4096\nCURVES = {\n    'x2  (8k)':   'ppl_cream_x2.csv',\n    'x4  (16k)':  'ppl_cream_x4.csv',\n    'x8  (32k)':  'ppl_cream_x8.csv',\n    'x16 (64k)':  'ppl_cream_x16.csv',\n    'base 4k floor': 'ppl_base_4096.csv',\n}\n```\nand run the cell.\n\n## 5. Read the answer\n- **Curve stays flat to the end** (tracks the 4k floor, no upward slope past 4096) → that factor extended cleanly.\n- **Curve starts climbing** past some position → that's where it breaks.\n- The **verdict table** (`ratio = PPL≥4096 / PPL<4096 ≈ 1`) quantifies it: the **largest F whose ratio stays ≈1 and whose absolute PPL stays near the floor** = how far 4k-physical CREAM+YaRN extends without PPL degradation.\n\n## Heads-up\n- The **32k (x8) and 64k (x16) evals are the risky ones** for single-GPU memory — the `[B,T,V]` logits dominate. If they OOM, that's the test-rig ceiling, not the model; drop to a shorter target or that's where multi-GPU eval (deferred CP path) would be needed.\n- Keep `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32` identical across all arms so the curves are equally smooth/comparable.\n- Flat PPL = tolerates the length. If you later care about *using* long range, follow up with a retrieval/needle eval at the winning F.\n\nWant me to drop steps 1–3 into a `cream_eval_sweep.sh` (with the `RUN` map and `BASE` at the top) so it's one command instead of a paste?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339623,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":2249,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2249,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":339623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":339623},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdHdJRkBzJnzrDcPnHPhd","type":"assistant","uuid":"1c545923-f8ad-4e56-8e89-beb3b9f550ac","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:12:36.030Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"