{"parentUuid":"14949f66-a0d7-4344-850e-a9685cc3f87e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHeR9c96ZzQjMNcpmeho","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2791,"cache_read_input_tokens":364491,"output_tokens":2139,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2139,"cache_read_input_tokens":364491,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHeR57X2dsymRMP2Cuz7","type":"assistant","uuid":"61d8649d-5f37-4653-9c66-558f03bfd555","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:27:03.202Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"61d8649d-5f37-4653-9c66-558f03bfd555","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHeR9c96ZzQjMNcpmeho","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That works — with two checks.\n\n**1. It'll correctly pin to physical GPU 3.** With `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3`, only that GPU is visible (as device 0), and the code's `cudaSetDevice(rank=0)` lands on physical GPU 3. It propagates through `make → mpirun` because OpenMPI forwards the launching environment to the rank — that's the same mechanism that got your `CP_*` vars to the executable, so it's reliable here.\n\n**2. You dropped `CP_DATA_ROOT` — eval still needs val data.** If you omit it, the loader falls back to the default `Data_Loader/Data`. On this `/mnt/volgrp03/...` box that's probably **not** where your shards are, and eval will fail to open the val split. So either keep it in `ARCH`:\n```bash\nARCH=\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3 CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0 CP_DATA_ROOT=<your data dir>\"\n```\nor pass `CP_DATA_ROOT=...` inside the eval loop. (Use the same data dir your training runs used.)\n\n`CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` correctly omitted — eval ignores it.\n\n**Verify before using:**\n```bash\necho \"$ARCH\"\n```\nConfirm every `NAME=value` is intact (no space inside `CP_GLOBAL`/`CP_FFN`/etc.) and `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3` is the first token.\n\nThen the eval loop is unchanged. One note: since `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` is now baked into `$ARCH`, don't also set a conflicting device elsewhere in the command."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2791,"cache_read_input_tokens":364491,"output_tokens":2139,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2791,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2139,"cache_read_input_tokens":364491,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2791},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHeR57X2dsymRMP2Cuz7","type":"assistant","uuid":"a4578a5a-4e0d-4838-8cb6-8a2d0a30f622","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:27:10.966Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a4578a5a-4e0d-4838-8cb6-8a2d0a30f622","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"05e2df2d-3989-459d-a3be-86867002b0b9","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"84e98fa3-4448-48ab-af2c-7e1dba475a70\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"That works — with two checks.\\n\\n**1. It'll correctly pin to physical GPU 3.** With `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3`, only that GPU is visible (as device 0), and the code's `cudaSetDevice(rank=0)` lands on physical GPU 3. It propagates through `make → mpirun` because OpenMPI forwards the launching environment to the rank — that's the same mechanism that got your `CP_*` vars to the executable, so it's reliable here.\\n\\n**2. You dropped `CP_DATA_ROOT` — eval still needs val data.** If you omit it, the loader falls back to the default `Data_Loader/Data`. On this `/mnt/volgrp03/...` box that's probably **not** where your shards are, and eval will fail to open the val split. So either keep it in `ARCH`:\\n```bash\\nARCH=\\\"CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3 CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0 CP_DATA_ROOT=<your data dir>\\\"\\n```\\nor pass `CP_DATA_ROOT=...` inside the eval loop. (Use the same data dir your training runs used.)\\n\\n`CP_GLOBAL_BATCH` correctly omitted — eval ignores it.\\n\\n**Verify before using:**\\n```bash\\necho \\\"$ARCH\\\"\\n```\\nConfirm every `NAME=value` is intact (no space inside `CP_GLOBAL`/`CP_FFN`/etc.) and `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3` is the first token.\\n\\nThen the eval loop is unchanged. One note: since `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` is now baked into `$ARCH`, don't also set a conflicting device elsewhere in the command.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"18b79ea2-69e6-4df7-b9da-559ba29237bf","timestamp":"2026-07-22T19:27:11.054Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
