{"parentUuid":"96b5dec4-aff1-416e-b970-a598b6ca9515","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_64220","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 150 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"7e2cf598-142b-4221-a224-f6cb60af0474","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:05:16.432Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"7e2cf598-142b-4221-a224-f6cb60af0474","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHhMx29TQpd9nyELkcZj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3091,"cache_read_input_tokens":367282,"output_tokens":2375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3091,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2375,"cache_read_input_tokens":367282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3091},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHhMtZnVwRJir4JCDgHG","type":"assistant","uuid":"7811bbb5-3c8f-43bc-8d88-627d4da390d2","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:05:43.327Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"7811bbb5-3c8f-43bc-8d88-627d4da390d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdHhMx29TQpd9nyELkcZj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a clean **success** — and it says CREAM+YaRN extends *at least* 8× on 4k-physical training without PPL degradation.\n\n## What the numbers say\nAll three ratios are ~1.0:\n\n| arm | target | PPL<4k | PPL≥4k | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| x2 | 8k | 126.6 | 127.3 | **1.01** |\n| x4 | 16k | 126.0 | 127.7 | **1.01** |\n| x8 | 32k | 134.2 | 136.5 | **1.02** |\n\n- **Ratio ≈ 1 everywhere → PPL is flat past the original 4k**, for every factor including 32k. No position-dependent blow-up. That's exactly the \"extended cleanly\" signal.\n- **The curves overlap in one band and stay flat to the very end** — the green x8 line holds its level all the way out to 32,768 with no upward drift. So at 8× you still haven't hit the wall.\n\n**Answer to your question:** on this 48M model, 4k-physical CREAM+YaRN extends to **32k (8×) with essentially zero PPL increase** (ratio 1.02), and the limit isn't reached yet — all three are flat.\n\n## The one thing to watch\nThe absolute floor is *starting* to creep: x2/x4 sit at ~126, x8 at ~134 (+6%). Ratio is still ~1, but that slow rise in the baseline level is the **leading edge** of eventual degradation. It tells you the breaking point is beyond 32k but approaching — which is exactly why the next arm matters.\n\n## Missing arm — run x16 (64k)\nThe plot and table only show 2x/4x/8x; **x16 (run 34) isn't here.** Either you haven't evaled it yet or it OOM'd at 64k. That's the arm that will actually *find the limit*: if x16 stays flat with a similar floor, you've shown ≥16×; if its curve finally slopes up (ratio > ~1.1) or the floor jumps, that's where 4k-physical extension breaks. Run:\n```bash\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=65536 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=16 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT_RESUME=34 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_cream_x16.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\nIf it OOMs, that's the single-GPU logits ceiling (`[1, 65536, 50304]` ≈ 13 GB fp32) — tells you nothing bad about the model, just that 64k eval needs a bigger GPU or chunked logits.\n\n## Honest caveat (same as before)\nFlat PPL means the model **tolerates** 32k positions — not that it **uses** long-range content. To claim real long-context capability at 8×, follow up with a needle/retrieval eval at 32k. But as a position-extension result, this is a textbook-clean CREAM demonstration: **8× context from 4k-only training, flat PPL.**\n\nEdge spikes at the end of each curve (~8.1k, ~16.3k, ~32.7k) are just the smoothing-window boundary artifact — ignore them."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3091,"cache_read_input_tokens":367282,"output_tokens":2375,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3091,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2375,"cache_read_input_tokens":367282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3091,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3091},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdHhMtZnVwRJir4JCDgHG","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad379a5d-323a-4bb3-b2a3-3c34b21a8d3c","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:05:57.236Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ad379a5d-323a-4bb3-b2a3-3c34b21a8d3c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"00ccc65a-f5b4-4acc-8d6b-f17631142e97","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"03c38118-65a1-44e8-b76e-4af655252051\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"This is a clean **success** — and it says CREAM+YaRN extends *at least* 8× on 4k-physical training without PPL degradation.\\n\\n## What the numbers say\\nAll three ratios are ~1.0:\\n\\n| arm | target | PPL<4k | PPL≥4k | ratio |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| x2 | 8k | 126.6 | 127.3 | **1.01** |\\n| x4 | 16k | 126.0 | 127.7 | **1.01** |\\n| x8 | 32k | 134.2 | 136.5 | **1.02** |\\n\\n- **Ratio ≈ 1 everywhere → PPL is flat past the original 4k**, for every factor including 32k. No position-dependent blow-up. That's exactly the \\\"extended cleanly\\\" signal.\\n- **The curves overlap in one band and stay flat to the very end** — the green x8 line holds its level all the way out to 32,768 with no upward drift. So at 8× you still haven't hit the wall.\\n\\n**Answer to your question:** on this 48M model, 4k-physical CREAM+YaRN extends to **32k (8×) with essentially zero PPL increase** (ratio 1.02), and the limit isn't reached yet — all three are flat.\\n\\n## The one thing to watch\\nThe absolute floor is *starting* to creep: x2/x4 sit at ~126, x8 at ~134 (+6%). Ratio is still ~1, but that slow rise in the baseline level is the **leading edge** of eventual degradation. It tells you the breaking point is beyond 32k but approaching — which is exactly why the next arm matters.\\n\\n## Missing arm — run x16 (64k)\\nThe plot and table only show 2x/4x/8x; **x16 (run 34) isn't here.** Either you haven't evaled it yet or it OOM'd at 64k. That's the arm that will actually *find the limit*: if x16 stays flat with a similar floor, you've shown ≥16×; if its curve finally slopes up (ratio > ~1.1) or the floor jumps, that's where 4k-physical extension breaks. Run:\\n```bash\\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=65536 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=16 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT_RESUME=34 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_cream_x16.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\\n```\\nIf it OOMs, that's the single-GPU logits ceiling (`[1, 65536, 50304]` ≈ 13 GB fp32) — tells you nothing bad about the model, just that 64k eval needs a bigger GPU or chunked logits.\\n\\n## Honest caveat (same as before)\\nFlat PPL means the model **tolerates** 32k positions — not that it **uses** long-range content. To claim real long-context capability at 8×, follow up with a needle/retrieval eval at 32k. But as a position-extension result, this is a textbook-clean CREAM demonstration: **8× context from 4k-only training, flat PPL.**\\n\\nEdge spikes at the end of each curve (~8.1k, ~16.3k, ~32.7k) are just the smoothing-window boundary artifact — ignore them.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1c5e01ca-6c2f-4098-b49c-8ac62457278a","timestamp":"2026-07-22T20:05:57.325Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
