{"parentUuid":"76c7f9f4-aaac-4291-ae87-c2536fa4d073","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_67787","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 151 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e70240d8-bb36-4110-816b-9fb477d40f2c","timestamp":"2026-07-23T05:05:38.436Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"e70240d8-bb36-4110-816b-9fb477d40f2c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJQZu4f3uLwLzXQaq2bW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351881,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":2724,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2724,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdJQZrKD275XZMtAQD9f1","type":"assistant","uuid":"6f956c0b-07af-41f6-8969-13329d830f81","timestamp":"2026-07-23T05:06:12.132Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6f956c0b-07af-41f6-8969-13329d830f81","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJQZu4f3uLwLzXQaq2bW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That `nan` is **expected, not an error** — and the `168.60` needs a caveat.\n\n## Why the nan\nYou evaluated the base floor at `CP_T=4096`, so its CSV only has positions **0–4095**. The verdict code computes `PPL≥4096` over positions ≥4096 — of which there are none → mean of an empty set = `nan`, and `after/before = nan`. Nothing wrong; the base-floor curve simply doesn't extend past 4k, so there's no \"after\" region. The meaningful number from that run is just the single value: **base 4k PPL = 168.6**.\n\n## The catch: 168.6 is *higher* than your extended arms (126–136) — and that's a red flag about the comparison, not a real result\nNormally the in-distribution 4k floor should be the *lowest* PPL. It's higher here because **the base is a less-trained checkpoint**: base stopped at **step 917**, while your CREAM arms were fine-tuned to **step 1222** (+305 steps). More training → lower PPL. So the CREAM arms beating the \"floor\" is just the extra 305 steps, **not** extension magic. Don't read `168.6 → 126` as \"extension improved the model.\"\n\n## What the valid floor actually is\nThe correct per-arm floor is each arm's **own `PPL<4096`** — which the ratio already uses as the denominator:\n- x2/x4: ~126, x8: ~134.\n\nThose are the honest reference levels, and the ratios (~1.0) say PPL stays flat past 4k relative to *that arm's own* short-context PPL. **That's your real result, and it stands** — the base-floor line is just a mismatched-training-length distraction.\n\n## If you want a clean absolute reference, pick one of these\n1. **Fairest floor:** eval one CREAM arm at its *native* 4k (`CP_T=4096 YARN_SCALE=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=31`). Same checkpoint, same training length — its 4k PPL is the true floor to compare the extended level against. (It'll be ~126, matching the `PPL<4096` you already have.)\n2. **Naive baseline (does extension even help?):** eval the **base** checkpoint at the *long* length with YaRN (`CP_T=32768 YARN_SCALE=8 CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base>`), CREAM off. That's the \"C\" arm — it shows what the un-fine-tuned model does at 32k. If *that* blows up while x8 stays flat, you've shown the fine-tune (not just YaRN) did the work.\n\nBottom line: drop the `168.6` line from your conclusion (or relabel it \"base @ step 917, fewer steps — not comparable\"). Your **ratios ≈ 1.0 across 8k/16k/32k are the result**, and they're clean."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351881,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"output_tokens":2724,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2724,"cache_read_input_tokens":20887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":351881,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":351881},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdJQZrKD275XZMtAQD9f1","type":"assistant","uuid":"18b82868-9549-45d1-abfc-af4d2c89c913","timestamp":"2026-07-23T05:06:25.554Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"18b82868-9549-45d1-abfc-af4d2c89c913","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"a1a17721-49fa-4e7e-a5bd-7f261689bf1a","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/7f89f0ac-da79-42e5-975f-b63bab3c65d2.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"e3cd6e8c-2d72-4d80-b535-06b4680e3618\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"That `nan` is **expected, not an error** — and the `168.60` needs a caveat.\\n\\n## Why the nan\\nYou evaluated the base floor at `CP_T=4096`, so its CSV only has positions **0–4095**. The verdict code computes `PPL≥4096` over positions ≥4096 — of which there are none → mean of an empty set = `nan`, and `after/before = nan`. Nothing wrong; the base-floor curve simply doesn't extend past 4k, so there's no \\\"after\\\" region. The meaningful number from that run is just the single value: **base 4k PPL = 168.6**.\\n\\n## The catch: 168.6 is *higher* than your extended arms (126–136) — and that's a red flag about the comparison, not a real result\\nNormally the in-distribution 4k floor should be the *lowest* PPL. It's higher here because **the base is a less-trained checkpoint**: base stopped at **step 917**, while your CREAM arms were fine-tuned to **step 1222** (+305 steps). More training → lower PPL. So the CREAM arms beating the \\\"floor\\\" is just the extra 305 steps, **not** extension magic. Don't read `168.6 → 126` as \\\"extension improved the model.\\\"\\n\\n## What the valid floor actually is\\nThe correct per-arm floor is each arm's **own `PPL<4096`** — which the ratio already uses as the denominator:\\n- x2/x4: ~126, x8: ~134.\\n\\nThose are the honest reference levels, and the ratios (~1.0) say PPL stays flat past 4k relative to *that arm's own* short-context PPL. **That's your real result, and it stands** — the base-floor line is just a mismatched-training-length distraction.\\n\\n## If you want a clean absolute reference, pick one of these\\n1. **Fairest floor:** eval one CREAM arm at its *native* 4k (`CP_T=4096 YARN_SCALE=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=31`). Same checkpoint, same training length — its 4k PPL is the true floor to compare the extended level against. (It'll be ~126, matching the `PPL<4096` you already have.)\\n2. **Naive baseline (does extension even help?):** eval the **base** checkpoint at the *long* length with YaRN (`CP_T=32768 YARN_SCALE=8 CP_CKPT_RESUME=<base>`), CREAM off. That's the \\\"C\\\" arm — it shows what the un-fine-tuned model does at 32k. If *that* blows up while x8 stays flat, you've shown the fine-tune (not just YaRN) did the work.\\n\\nBottom line: drop the `168.6` line from your conclusion (or relabel it \\\"base @ step 917, fewer steps — not comparable\\\"). Your **ratios ≈ 1.0 across 8k/16k/32k are the result**, and they're clean.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6a3c43ea-5fe6-482e-8a09-b5b7f44ee241","timestamp":"2026-07-23T05:06:25.632Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
