{"parentUuid":"179488ca-9b91-406f-9c56-3fc280a5b1ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJQxM9fa4qYUudjrRkLH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the naive baseline — base checkpoint stretched to 8k/16k/32k with YaRN, CREAM off. Make sure `$ARCH` (with `CP_DATA_ROOT` and `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=3`) and `BASE` are set first:\n\n```bash\nBASE=<run that tops at 917>\n```\n\n```bash\nfor F in 2 4 8; do T=$((4096*F)); env $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=$T CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=$F YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$BASE CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_naive_x${F}.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1; done\n```\n\nThis writes `ppl_naive_x2.csv` (8k), `ppl_naive_x4.csv` (16k), `ppl_naive_x8.csv` (32k).\n\nThen in the notebook add them alongside the CREAM curves:\n```python\nCURVES = {\n    'x2 CREAM (8k)':  'ppl_cream_x2.csv',\n    'x4 CREAM (16k)': 'ppl_cream_x4.csv',\n    'x8 CREAM (32k)': 'ppl_cream_x8.csv',\n    'x2 naive (8k)':  'ppl_naive_x2.csv',\n    'x4 naive (16k)': 'ppl_naive_x4.csv',\n    'x8 naive (32k)': 'ppl_naive_x8.csv',\n}\n```\n\nWhat to look for:\n- **naive curves climb past 4096** (or sit well above CREAM) → the fine-tune did real work; CREAM's flat curves win.\n- **naive curves also flat and close to CREAM** → YaRN-at-inference already extends this model, so CREAM's edge is smaller on PPL (and you'd look to a retrieval eval to separate them).\n\nRemember the label caveat when you read it: naive = base @ step 917 (305 fewer steps than the CREAM arms), so if there's a gap, run the matched-step control before attributing all of it to CREAM."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4627,"cache_read_input_tokens":375502,"output_tokens":932,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4