{"parentUuid":"2b3a74cd-e24c-4729-85ec-58d645854546","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJX7UKDiKsy6HLETcw2U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4933,"cache_read_input_tokens":389438,"output_tokens":2803,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4933,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2803,"cache_read_input_tokens":389438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4933},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJX7Pk8gerA29YSy174K","type":"assistant","uuid":"555ca28d-1316-47bc-acb9-9574402a07ab","timestamp":"2026-07-23T06:31:54.972Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"555ca28d-1316-47bc-acb9-9574402a07ab","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdJX7UKDiKsy6HLETcw2U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That plot and your CREAM sweep aren't contradictory — they used **two different definitions of \"naive,\" differing by one flag: `YARN_SCALE`.**\n\nThis 114M plot's blue curve is labeled **\"base @16384, *no YaRN*, naive extrapolation\"** → it was run with `YARN_SCALE=1`. That's **plain RoPE extrapolation** — no frequency interpolation at all. So past position 4096 the rotations alias and PPL climbs steadily (~40 → 300+). That's the classic blow-up.\n\nYour CREAM-sweep \"naive\" was run with **`YARN_SCALE=F` (YaRN ON)**, CREAM off. YaRN's frequency interpolation prevents the aliasing, so it stayed **flat** — just elevated (the train/eval mismatch penalty I described).\n\nSo the blue curve here blows up **only because YaRN was off**. Turn YaRN on (that's what the CREAM-sweep naive did, and what the orange curve here did) and the blow-up disappears.\n\n## The full three-regime picture\n\n| regime | YaRN? | fine-tuned on long pos? | curve |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **This plot's blue** | ❌ off (`SCALE=1`) | ❌ base | **blows up past 4k** |\n| **CREAM-sweep naive** | ✅ on (`SCALE=F`) | ❌ base | flat but **high** (~174) |\n| **This plot's orange / your CREAM arms** | ✅ on | ✅ (YaRN-LCE / CREAM) | flat and **low** |\n\nReading it top to bottom:\n1. **No YaRN** → aliasing → catastrophic blow-up (blue). This is what YaRN exists to fix.\n2. **YaRN, no adaptation** → no blow-up, but the model was never trained under YaRN's reparametrized frequencies+temperature, so PPL is uniformly elevated (your naive sweep).\n3. **YaRN + fine-tune** → flat *and* low (orange here, CREAM arms in your sweep).\n\nSo this plot is actually the **missing first row** of your CREAM story — it shows what happens when you remove YaRN entirely. It confirms everything:\n- YaRN is what kills the blow-up (blue→orange).\n- Fine-tuning is what lowers the flat level (your naive→CREAM).\n\nIf you re-ran your CREAM-sweep \"naive\" with `YARN_SCALE=1` instead of `F`, you'd reproduce this blue blow-up on the 48M model. The flatness you saw was YaRN doing its job — not the base being secretly good at long context.\n\n(Note this is the older 114M run, a different model than your 48M sweep — but the mechanism is identical and model-independent.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4933,"cache_read_input_tokens":389438,"output_tokens":2803,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4933,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2803,"cache_read_input_tokens":389438,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4933,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4933},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdJX7Pk8gerA29YSy174K","type":"assistant","uuid":"23cb43e7-ca6e-4b12-9755-cc946bab7c5a","timestamp":"2026-07-23T06:32:07.095Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.216","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
