{"parentUuid":"75fef74b-f461-4022-8732-fdbb31d3ba24","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"date_change","newDate":"2026-07-30"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"71ced5d4-4c3b-4713-94df-d66664f9144f","timestamp":"2026-07-30T04:02:35.735Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"71ced5d4-4c3b-4713-94df-d66664f9144f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdXaRVJu2wJpdjW7qFJwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378176,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"output_tokens":6560,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378176,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6560,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378176},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdXaRRrHUAYbktrnM76qX","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f46eedb-08fb-42b5-8824-6688d2dc2a57","timestamp":"2026-07-30T04:04:00.554Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"8f46eedb-08fb-42b5-8824-6688d2dc2a57","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdXaRVJu2wJpdjW7qFJwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\n\nGood direction — and you're better positioned than you think, because two of these are **already coded** in your `CreamPositions.h`. Here's the landscape, grouped by how much work each is *in your stack* (you have: `build_rope_cache`+YaRN, the CREAM position plumbing, a fused kernel that indexes the cache by position, and the single-GPU PPL-vs-pos rig).\n\nMy knowledge here runs to early 2026 and covers all of these; I'll flag where I'd verify specifics with a search before you implement.\n\n## Tier 0 — already implemented, just run them\n- **PoSE** (Positional Skip-wisE) and **RandPos** — both are in `CreamPositions.h` and wired to `CP_CREAM_MODE=pose|randpos`. Zero new code. Run them as extra arms in the exact sweep you just did → CREAM vs PoSE vs RandPos on identical rig. That's the most natural next experiment and a real comparison.\n\n## Tier 1 — RoPE frequency reparametrization (cache-only, like YaRN; hours)\nAll of these are changes to `build_rope_cache` only — no kernel/training-loop touch:\n- **Positional Interpolation (PI)** — Chen et al. 2023. Just scale positions `m → m/s`. The simplest baseline; YaRN should beat it. ~10 lines.\n- **NTK-aware scaling** — change the RoPE base `θ → θ·s^(d/(d−2))` instead of scaling positions. One-line cache variant.\n- **Dynamic NTK** — same, but scale the base as a function of the *actual* sequence length at inference (rebuild cache per length). Good for \"no fine-tune\" inference.\n- **ABF / RoPE-base scaling** — Llama-2-long / CodeLlama: just raise the base (you already use `rope_theta=500000`) and fine-tune. You could sweep base as its own extension method.\n- **LongRoPE** (Microsoft, 2024) — the strongest cache-only method: *non-uniform per-dimension* rescale factors found by evolutionary search, + progressive extension (extends to millions of tokens). More work (a search loop over per-dim factors) but directly comparable and high-impact.\n\n## Tier 2 — training-free attention/position remapping (medium; different axis)\nThese need no fine-tune — a great contrast to CREAM's \"train cheaply\" story:\n- **Self-Extend** (Jin et al. 2024) — training-**free**. Neighbor tokens use normal positions; distant tokens use `floor(pos/group)`. Implementable purely in the RoPE index computation at inference. Strong \"do you even need training?\" baseline.\n- **StreamingLLM / attention sinks** (Xiao et al.) — keep the first few \"sink\" tokens + a sliding window. Training-free, enables unbounded streaming — but note it *bounds* effective context (windowed), so it extends *streaming*, not true long-range use. Easy and illustrative.\n- **LM-Infinite** — Λ-shaped mask (sinks + local window) + a distance ceiling on positions. Close cousin of the above.\n- **Dual Chunk Attention (DCA)** — training-free; splits attention into intra-chunk + inter-chunk with remapped relative positions (Qwen uses it). More involved but powerful.\n\n## Tier 3 — architectural (large; new modules + training)\n- **Landmark Attention** — learnable landmark tokens summarizing blocks, retrieved over. \n- **Activation Beacon** — compress past activations into \"beacon\" tokens.\n- **Infini-attention** (Google) — compressive memory + local attention for effectively unbounded context.\nThese change the model, not just positions — bigger lifts, less directly comparable to your current PPL rig.\n\n## My recommendation\nFor a coherent, paper-shaped study on your existing rig, do this sequence:\n1. **Now (free):** add PoSE + RandPos arms → CREAM vs PoSE vs RandPos. Same sweep, same plots.\n2. **Cheap cache-only baselines:** PI + NTK-aware + YaRN-alone (no fine-tune) — these round out the \"frequency methods\" axis.\n3. **One training-free contender:** Self-Extend — tests whether fine-tuning is even needed.\n4. **Stretch:** LongRoPE — the current SOTA cache-only method; the one most likely to beat CREAM+YaRN and worth the search-loop effort.\n\nThat gives you two clean axes: *position-training methods* (CREAM/PoSE/RandPos) × *frequency methods* (PI/NTK/YaRN/LongRoPE), plus a *training-free* reference (Self-Extend) — all measurable on the PPL-vs-position rig you already built.\n\nWant me to (a) wire up the PoSE/RandPos comparison arms right now since the code exists, or (b) search for the latest 2025 methods + pull the specific paper/repo for whichever one you want to implement first (LongRoPE and Self-Extend have clean reference implementations I can find)?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378176,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"output_tokens":6560,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378176,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6560,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":378176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":378176},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdXaRRrHUAYbktrnM76qX","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f05ef41-a666-4fbc-a9c2-897c9f571d85","timestamp":"2026-07-31T09:39:11.183Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
