{"parentUuid":"9b4f14a8-f6d6-4c66-86d5-332b8cf14899","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"81657d94-892e-455b-ac3e-0e71c82221fa","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<ide_opened_file>The user opened the file /home/blu-bridge25/CP/graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb in the IDE. This may or may not be related to the current task.</ide_opened_file>"},{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/png","data":""}},{"type":"image","source":{"type":"base64","media_type":"image/png","data":""}},{"type":"text","text":"1. what is the difference bw the ppl graph that increases as position increases and the graph that doesnt seem to increase with position ?  the naive run must only have low ppl within pretraining pos range ryt? how is the second graph also having naive one less across all positions ?\n2. LongRoPE is done in the RoPE kernels or in the build sincos cache ? how does this search work ? and does it require trainig like YARN or does it not require like CREAM ?"}]},"uuid":"fb0937d0-cc55-482d-a308-76e96fd46119","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:02:54.452Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","origin":{"kind":"human"},"promptSource":"sdk","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
