{"parentUuid":"ec9c3d90-0fda-4971-8bff-232ad7b9f46c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_2954681","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[SessionEnd] Updated session file: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/sessions/2026-07-31-CP-session.tmp\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6656ba81-7333-4999-bb07-9b0920c6c790","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:19:33.508Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6656ba81-7333-4999-bb07-9b0920c6c790","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZxypmtUCv96G4xg9RYw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5377,"cache_read_input_tokens":417210,"output_tokens":3075,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5377,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3075,"cache_read_input_tokens":417210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5377},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZxybHXccaoe1KU3AMwf","type":"assistant","uuid":"c503d242-65ef-452a-91d1-3c13c7c91c0b","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:20:12.720Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c503d242-65ef-452a-91d1-3c13c7c91c0b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZxypmtUCv96G4xg9RYw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\n\nYou're right, and my earlier phrasing was too loose — let me correct it. **In practice all three involve a weight fine-tune / annealing stage.** YaRN in any real deployment is applied during that long-context annealing tail, exactly as you say. So \"requires training\" is the fair statement for how these are actually used.\n\nThe precise distinction isn't \"training vs no training\" — it's **two separate things** each method does, and whether each needs training:\n\n| | (1) determine the position scheme | (2) adapt the weights (anneal/FT) | inference-only possible? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **YaRN** | fixed **formula** — no training | **yes**, annealing FT | yes, but degraded |\n| **CREAM** | position **relabeling** — *is* the training | **yes**, mandatory FT | **no** (nothing to apply at inference) |\n| **LongRoPE** | evolutionary **search** — training-free search | **yes**, progressive FT | cache yes, but weights are FT'd |\n\nSo to your direct question: **yes, LongRoPE is the same — it fine-tunes the weights during the extension/annealing stage, just like YaRN and CREAM.** Its *only* extra wrinkle is that the way it *finds* the interpolation factors (the evolutionary search) needs no gradients — but that's about choosing the cache, not about adapting the model. The weight adaptation is still a training stage.\n\nThe one genuine asymmetry worth keeping straight:\n\n- **YaRN and LongRoPE only change the RoPE cache** (a non-learned lookup table), so they *can* be switched on at inference with no weight update and still function — that's literally your **naive-C arm** (YaRN inference-only, flat but elevated). Training just closes the adaptation gap.\n- **CREAM has no inference-time component at all** — it's purely training-time position sampling. At inference you use normal positions. So CREAM is training-*only* in a stronger sense: there's nothing to \"turn on\" without training.\n\nNet: all three are **applied during annealing/fine-tuning** — your framing is correct. What differs is *how the position change is decided* (formula / search / training-recipe) and *whether the change even has an inference-time form* (YaRN & LongRoPE: yes; CREAM: no). LongRoPE = YaRN-style trained annealing **plus** a training-free search for a better-than-formula cache."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5377,"cache_read_input_tokens":417210,"output_tokens":3075,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5377,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3075,"cache_read_input_tokens":417210,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5377,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5377},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZxybHXccaoe1KU3AMwf","type":"assistant","uuid":"fff62d85-4f4a-4931-970e-0f6e19edc811","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:20:22.583Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"fff62d85-4f4a-4931-970e-0f6e19edc811","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"5df7ca80-48ef-4df4-b766-95f06b771598","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"ab3e4c32-6daf-49e5-b996-28e2f90c45c7\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\n\\nYou're right, and my earlier phrasing was too loose — let me correct it. **In practice all three involve a weight fine-tune / annealing stage.** YaRN in any real deployment is applied during that long-context annealing tail, exactly as you say. So \\\"requires training\\\" is the fair statement for how these are actually used.\\n\\nThe precise distinction isn't \\\"training vs no training\\\" — it's **two separate things** each method does, and whether each needs training:\\n\\n| | (1) determine the position scheme | (2) adapt the weights (anneal/FT) | inference-only possible? |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **YaRN** | fixed **formula** — no training | **yes**, annealing FT | yes, but degraded |\\n| **CREAM** | position **relabeling** — *is* the training | **yes**, mandatory FT | **no** (nothing to apply at inference) |\\n| **LongRoPE** | evolutionary **search** — training-free search | **yes**, progressive FT | cache yes, but weights are FT'd |\\n\\nSo to your direct question: **yes, LongRoPE is the same — it fine-tunes the weights during the extension/annealing stage, just like YaRN and CREAM.** Its *only* extra wrinkle is that the way it *finds* the interpolation factors (the evolutionary search) needs no gradients — but that's about choosing the cache, not about adapting the model. The weight adaptation is still a training stage.\\n\\nThe one genuine asymmetry worth keeping straight:\\n\\n- **YaRN and LongRoPE only change the RoPE cache** (a non-learned lookup table), so they *can* be switched on at inference with no weight update and still function — that's literally your **naive-C arm** (YaRN inference-only, flat but elevated). Training just closes the adaptation gap.\\n- **CREAM has no inference-time component at all** — it's purely training-time position sampling. At inference you use normal positions. So CREAM is training-*only* in a stronger sense: there's nothing to \\\"turn on\\\" without training.\\n\\nNet: all three are **applied during annealing/fine-tuning** — your framing is correct. What differs is *how the position change is decided* (formula / search / training-recipe) and *whether the change even has an inference-time form* (YaRN & LongRoPE: yes; CREAM: no). LongRoPE = YaRN-style trained annealing **plus** a training-free search for a better-than-formula cache.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":50},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9447e4e8-dbf0-45f5-b099-2e68aefe830a","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:20:22.694Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
