{"parentUuid":"d46e7f66-ae0e-49d2-8d0a-e248b0ce43b9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_2992669","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 165 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"db892de0-5d9a-465e-93b5-d5779f7b368d","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:25:17.074Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"db892de0-5d9a-465e-93b5-d5779f7b368d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZyQzFqqEwaN55SuufDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3117,"cache_read_input_tokens":422587,"output_tokens":3405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3405,"cache_read_input_tokens":422587,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3117},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZyQv93MSL1gqWLKE7vJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"68763660-f53b-4472-ac98-0e911636668d","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:25:51.673Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"68763660-f53b-4472-ac98-0e911636668d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZyQzFqqEwaN55SuufDJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\n\nYou're right — and it's a good instinct. A **no-YaRN C** (`YARN_SCALE=1`) is the more illustrative baseline: base weights + plain RoPE at long `T` → **low PPL below 4096** (matches training) and **rising past 4096** (extrapolation aliasing). That's the canonical \"this is why we need extension at all\" curve — exactly your Plot 1 shape, which you'd reproduce on the 48M.\n\nThe reason I ran C *with* YaRN wasn't wrong, though — the two naive versions answer **different questions**, and a rigorous study wants both:\n\n| C variant | setting | shape | what it isolates |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **C0 — no-YaRN** | `YARN_SCALE=1` | low <4k, **rises** after | *Is any extension method needed?* (motivation) |\n| **C1 — YaRN inference-only** | `YARN_SCALE=F` | flat, **elevated** | *Does YaRN need fine-tuning?* (controlled baseline for A/B) |\n\nThe subtlety on fairness: arms **A (CREAM) and B (YaRN-LCE) both use YaRN at eval.** So:\n- **C1 (YaRN on)** differs from A/B in *one* way — no fine-tune — so the A/B-vs-C1 gap cleanly isolates **the fine-tuning contribution** (YaRN held constant).\n- **C0 (no YaRN)** differs in *two* ways — no fine-tune **and** no YaRN cache — so an A/B-vs-C0 gap mixes \"fine-tuning helped\" with \"YaRN helped.\"\n\nSo C0 is the better **motivation** curve (shows the raw failure), and C1 is the better **controlled** curve (isolates the fine-tune). Ideally your plot has both: C0 blowing up, C1 flat-but-high, and A/B flat-and-low — that reads as \"no method → explodes; YaRN alone → stops the explosion; +fine-tune → also lowers PPL.\"\n\nAdd the C0 curve for the 48M with one run (base ckpt, YaRN off, long T):\n```bash\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=off CP_T=16384 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=1 CP_CKPT_RESUME=$BASE CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_naive_noyarn_16k.csv make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 run-bluscript-cp NP=1\n```\n(`YARN_SCALE=1` = bit-identical plain RoPE, so this will give you the low-then-rising shape. `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` is irrelevant at scale 1.)\n\nThen in the notebook you'd have, at 16k: `noyarn` (C0, rising) + `naive` (C1, flat high) + `cream` (A) + `yarn_lce` (B). That's the complete picture — and you were right that the rising curve is the one that actually shows the extrapolation failure your C arm was meant to illustrate."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3117,"cache_read_input_tokens":422587,"output_tokens":3405,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3117,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3405,"cache_read_input_tokens":422587,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3117,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3117},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZyQv93MSL1gqWLKE7vJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"595a7e85-7529-4a5c-a968-0c3f6ca21ef9","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:26:04.656Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
