{"parentUuid":"2e465417-b7e4-4fc9-8c61-b59ff1f697a6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZzt79T2boBzba6z5Ntm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HuoKSfUGJjTd6iCZw5EhTr","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"LongRoPE evolutionary search mutation crossover algorithm per-dimension rescale factor lambda"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1311,"cache_read_input_tokens":439061,"output_tokens":344,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":344,"cache_read_input_tokens":439061,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZzt3zSk7HfgPALgFaxf","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e4dc23e-6942-4999-9896-1319e670e56b","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:44:35.718Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9e4dc23e-6942-4999-9896-1319e670e56b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b0dc195-6ba6-4645-97dc-202d605be840","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HuoKSfUGJjTd6iCZw5EhTr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"LongRoPE evolutionary search mutation crossover algorithm per-dimension rescale factor lambda\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"LongRoPE: Extending RoPE for LLMs\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/longrope\"},{\"title\":\"LongRoPE: Extending LLM Context Window Beyond 2 Million Tokens\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1\"},{\"title\":\"CIXL2: A Crossover Operator for Evolutionary Algorithms ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1109.2146\"},{\"title\":\"Rethinking RoPE Scaling in Quantized LLM: Theory, Outlier, and Channel-Band Analysis with Weight Rescaling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.00028\"},{\"title\":\"Cross-over Mutation - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/cross-over-mutation\"},{\"title\":\"Evolutionary System Prompt Learning for Reinforcement Learning in LLMs\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.14697\"},{\"title\":\"Constrained Discrete Black-Box Optimization using Mixed-Integer   Programming\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.09569\"},{\"title\":\"Large-Scale Multiobjective Evolutionary Algorithm Guided by Low-Dimensional Surrogates of Scalarization Functions | Evolutionary Computation | MIT Press\",\"url\":\"https://direct.mit.edu/evco/article/33/3/309/122628/Large-Scale-Multiobjective-Evolutionary-Algorithm\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about LongRoPE and its evolutionary search approach:\n\nThe optimal rescale factors {λᵢ} and start-token threshold n̂ are identified via evolutionary search, seeded with known baseline schemes (e.g., PI, NTK, YaRN) plus random perturbations, with a monotonicity constraint (λ₀ ≤ λ₁ ≤ ...).\n\nThe evolutionary search algorithm uses a population size of 40 (T=40) and selects the top-32 candidates for mutation and crossover in each iteration. Perplexity is calculated using validation set samples with a minimum length requirement of the target context length, and for windows over 512k, the population, mutation, and crossover sizes are halved.\n\nThe per-dimension rescale factor λᵢ is used in the RoPE extension formula, where for positions n ≥ n̂, the angle becomes nθᵢ/λᵢ. LongRoPE employs dimension-specific rescaling and preserves early-token information through a start-token threshold, optimized with evolutionary search to mitigate nonuniformities.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"98d3f63c-a02e-4b0e-9453-bd28aed4913b","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:44:46.813Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"LongRoPE evolutionary search mutation crossover algorithm per-dimension rescale factor lambda","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01BivWycsprz8G8uNy4mKX8S","content":[{"title":"LongRoPE: Extending RoPE for LLMs","url":"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/longrope"},{"title":"LongRoPE: Extending LLM Context Window Beyond 2 Million Tokens","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1"},{"title":"CIXL2: A Crossover Operator for Evolutionary Algorithms ...","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1109.2146"},{"title":"Rethinking RoPE Scaling in Quantized LLM: Theory, Outlier, and Channel-Band Analysis with Weight Rescaling","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2510.00028"},{"title":"Cross-over Mutation - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics","url":"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/cross-over-mutation"},{"title":"Evolutionary System Prompt Learning for Reinforcement Learning in LLMs","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.14697"},{"title":"Constrained Discrete Black-Box Optimization using Mixed-Integer   Programming","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2110.09569"},{"title":"Large-Scale Multiobjective Evolutionary Algorithm Guided by Low-Dimensional Surrogates of Scalarization Functions | Evolutionary Computation | MIT Press","url":"https://direct.mit.edu/evco/article/33/3/309/122628/Large-Scale-Multiobjective-Evolutionary-Algorithm"}]},"Based on the search results, I found relevant information about LongRoPE and its evolutionary search approach:\n\nThe optimal rescale factors {λᵢ} and start-token threshold n̂ are identified via evolutionary search, seeded with known baseline schemes (e.g., PI, NTK, YaRN) plus random perturbations, with a monotonicity constraint (λ₀ ≤ λ₁ ≤ ...).\n\nThe evolutionary search algorithm uses a population size of 40 (T=40) and selects the top-32 candidates for mutation and crossover in each iteration. Perplexity is calculated using validation set samples with a minimum length requirement of the target context length, and for windows over 512k, the population, mutation, and crossover sizes are halved.\n\nThe per-dimension rescale factor λᵢ is used in the RoPE extension formula, where for positions n ≥ n̂, the angle becomes nθᵢ/λᵢ. LongRoPE employs dimension-specific rescaling and preserves early-token information through a start-token threshold, optimized with evolutionary search to mitigate nonuniformities."],"durationSeconds":8.048799128000159,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5a6d57c0-7548-48c6-bb43-8004da06c7b5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
