{"parentUuid":"e5ac9873-2df4-4f6f-b680-a3bee0ec96d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZzuE1UiUH2jMoDHi4NN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01He2UrDP6AJncSnfpECYnvf","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1","prompt":"Find the \"Searching the non-uniform position interpolation\" / evolutionary search section and its Algorithm pseudocode. Extract exactly: (1) the search space and the RoPE rescale formula using per-dimension lambda_i and the start-token count n_hat (the formula for the rotation angle for positions >= n_hat vs < n_hat); (2) population size, number of evolution iterations, how many top candidates are selected (parents); (3) the initialization: which seeds (PI, NTK, YaRN, and how many mutated copies); (4) the mutation operator — exactly how lambda_i is changed and by how much, any probability, and whether magnitude is annealed; (5) the crossover operator; (6) the monotonicity constraint and how invalid candidates are handled; (7) the fitness = perplexity computation details; (8) the progressive extension steps (256k fine-tune then search to 2048k, and 8k readjust)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":492,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1374,"cache_read_input_tokens":440372,"output_tokens":501,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1374,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":492,"output_tokens":501,"cache_read_input_tokens":440372,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1374,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1374},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZzu9CFz3pjoKiPp6soV","type":"assistant","uuid":"65a43c6e-cc71-4074-8718-c645895c18b8","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:44:56.668Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"65a43c6e-cc71-4074-8718-c645895c18b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5b0dc195-6ba6-4645-97dc-202d605be840","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01He2UrDP6AJncSnfpECYnvf","type":"tool_result","content":"# LongRoPE: Evolutionary Search Details\n\n## (1) Search Space & RoPE Rescale Formula\n\n**Search Space (Table 4):**\n- λᵢ (per-dimension): (1.0, s×1.25, step 0.01) where s = extension ratio\n- n̂ (starting tokens): {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 64, 128, 256}\n\n**Rotation Angle Formula (Eq. 3):**\nFor position n and dimension i:\n```\nangle = 𝕀(λ̂ᵢ, n̂) × (n/βⁱ)\n\nwhere 𝕀(λ̂ᵢ, n̂) = {\n  1           if n < n̂\n  1/λᵢ        if n ≥ n̂\n}\n```\n\n## (2) Population & Selection Parameters\n\n- Population size (P): 64\n- Mutation size (N₁): 16\n- Crossover size (N₂): 16\n- Max iterations (𝒯): 40\n- **Top-k selected as parents: 32** per iteration\n\n## (3) Initialization Strategy\n\nThree seed solutions plus mutations:\n- \"PI, NTK, and YaRN\" added as initial individuals\n- Remaining P−3 candidates: \"randomly mutate the three rescale factors with a probability of p\"\n- Mutation probability (p): 0.3\n\n## (4) Mutation Operator\n\nThe document states mutation occurs \"with a probability of p [0.3]\" but provides **no explicit magnitude specification**. The constraint section indicates λᵢ values are sampled subject to monotonicity, but specific delta/annealing details are absent from the pseudocode.\n\n## (5) Crossover Operator\n\nAlgorithm 1 references `Crossover_with_mono_constraint` but the **exact mechanics are not detailed**—only that it produces N₂ new candidates while respecting monotonicity.\n\n## (6) Monotonicity Constraint\n\n**Constraint:** \"λᵢ ≤ λᵢ₊₁\" across RoPE dimensions (i = 0,…,63)\n\n**Invalid handling:** \"Only RoPE that satisfies this constraint is applied to LLM for perplexity evaluation, significantly reducing the search costs.\"\n\n## (7) Fitness (Perplexity) Computation\n\n- **Metric:** Validation perplexity on language modeling loss\n- **For ≤256k:** 5 random PG19 samples, minimum target context length\n- **For >512k:** 3 random Pile-Books3 samples\n- Computed via forward pass through LLM with current RoPE configuration\n\n## (8) Progressive Extension Strategy\n\n**Stage 1:** Search for 128k and 256k targets on pre-trained model\n  \n**Stage 2:** Fine-tune to 256k context (400 steps @128k, then 600 steps @256k)\n\n**Stage 3:** Secondary search on fine-tuned 256k model to reach 2048k without additional fine-tuning (\"an 8× extension in non-fine-tuning scenarios\")\n\n**Stage 4:** Readjust RoPE factors for 4k/8k recovery via dedicated search with \"reduced maximum allowed searched λ\""}]},"uuid":"95fcd24b-9702-4a70-b9be-b969050ce3c8","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:45:10.094Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":471715,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# LongRoPE: Evolutionary Search Details\n\n## (1) Search Space & RoPE Rescale Formula\n\n**Search Space (Table 4):**\n- λᵢ (per-dimension): (1.0, s×1.25, step 0.01) where s = extension ratio\n- n̂ (starting tokens): {0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 64, 128, 256}\n\n**Rotation Angle Formula (Eq. 3):**\nFor position n and dimension i:\n```\nangle = 𝕀(λ̂ᵢ, n̂) × (n/βⁱ)\n\nwhere 𝕀(λ̂ᵢ, n̂) = {\n  1           if n < n̂\n  1/λᵢ        if n ≥ n̂\n}\n```\n\n## (2) Population & Selection Parameters\n\n- Population size (P): 64\n- Mutation size (N₁): 16\n- Crossover size (N₂): 16\n- Max iterations (𝒯): 40\n- **Top-k selected as parents: 32** per iteration\n\n## (3) Initialization Strategy\n\nThree seed solutions plus mutations:\n- \"PI, NTK, and YaRN\" added as initial individuals\n- Remaining P−3 candidates: \"randomly mutate the three rescale factors with a probability of p\"\n- Mutation probability (p): 0.3\n\n## (4) Mutation Operator\n\nThe document states mutation occurs \"with a probability of p [0.3]\" but provides **no explicit magnitude specification**. The constraint section indicates λᵢ values are sampled subject to monotonicity, but specific delta/annealing details are absent from the pseudocode.\n\n## (5) Crossover Operator\n\nAlgorithm 1 references `Crossover_with_mono_constraint` but the **exact mechanics are not detailed**—only that it produces N₂ new candidates while respecting monotonicity.\n\n## (6) Monotonicity Constraint\n\n**Constraint:** \"λᵢ ≤ λᵢ₊₁\" across RoPE dimensions (i = 0,…,63)\n\n**Invalid handling:** \"Only RoPE that satisfies this constraint is applied to LLM for perplexity evaluation, significantly reducing the search costs.\"\n\n## (7) Fitness (Perplexity) Computation\n\n- **Metric:** Validation perplexity on language modeling loss\n- **For ≤256k:** 5 random PG19 samples, minimum target context length\n- **For >512k:** 3 random Pile-Books3 samples\n- Computed via forward pass through LLM with current RoPE configuration\n\n## (8) Progressive Extension Strategy\n\n**Stage 1:** Search for 128k and 256k targets on pre-trained model\n  \n**Stage 2:** Fine-tune to 256k context (400 steps @128k, then 600 steps @256k)\n\n**Stage 3:** Secondary search on fine-tuned 256k model to reach 2048k without additional fine-tuning (\"an 8× extension in non-fine-tuning scenarios\")\n\n**Stage 4:** Readjust RoPE factors for 4k/8k recovery via dedicated search with \"reduced maximum allowed searched λ\"","durationMs":10877,"url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4d22fad2-0876-4ea4-99ed-7f2cabd4639e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"95fcd24b-9702-4a70-b9be-b969050ce3c8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"todo_reminder","content":[{"content":"Create context_parallel/CreamPositions.h (3-layer: math, range/CDF, sampling wrapper) + PoSE/RandPos","status":"completed","activeForm":"Creating CreamPositions.h"},{"content":"Write Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp (golden math, range/CDF, structural, randint, PoSE/RandPos) and run RED->GREEN","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing cream_positions_test.cpp"},{"content":"Add set_rope_cache setter to context_parallel/ContextParallel.h (additive, grad-free assert)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Adding set_rope_cache setter"},{"content":"Integrate into Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp (config/env, asserts, cream_full_cache_, gated guard, per-step install, eval path)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Integrating CREAM into bluscriptCP.cpp"},{"content":"Write Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp (gather==direct RoPE + YaRN spot-check), wire Makefile","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp"},{"content":"Document CP_CREAM_* env vars in README.md","status":"completed","activeForm":"Documenting in README.md"},{"content":"Build bluscript-cp with CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 (compile-verify integration)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Building bluscript-cp"},{"content":"Verification: parity test, off-mode regression, CREAM smoke run, distribution check","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running verification"},{"content":"Log work to Obsidian Logs.md + write session report","status":"completed","activeForm":"Logging work"}],"itemCount":9},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d33d56f8-e10f-40ba-8fdd-4145a4448213","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:45:10.097Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"d33d56f8-e10f-40ba-8fdd-4145a4448213","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZzw1DLfMZT5C5eKBBjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2603,"cache_read_input_tokens":441746,"output_tokens":3968,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2603,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3968,"cache_read_input_tokens":441746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2603,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2603},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZzvrbvVhAnWysx13hPn","type":"assistant","uuid":"36e6e340-3cb6-4ac7-9f53-41a4b5d84253","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:45:45.440Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"36e6e340-3cb6-4ac7-9f53-41a4b5d84253","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdZzw1DLfMZT5C5eKBBjP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\n\nI pulled the paper — and it **corrects my earlier \"small multiplicative jitter\" description.** LongRoPE doesn't nudge `λ_i` by a small amount; it **resamples it from a discrete grid.** Here's exactly how, from the paper's Algorithm 1 and Table 4.\n\n## How `λ_i` is changed and \"by how much\" (the real answer)\n\nEach `λ_i` lives on a **discrete grid**, not a continuous value:\n- **Range:** `λ_i ∈ [1.0, s × 1.25]` where `s` = extension ratio.\n- **Step:** `0.01`.\n\n**Mutation operator:** take a parent's `λ` vector, and **for each dimension, with probability `p = 0.3`, replace `λ_i` with a fresh value drawn from that grid** (with prob 0.7, keep the parent's value). So it's **not** a tuned step size — each mutated dimension is a **full re-draw** from the whole allowed range `[1.0, s×1.25]`, bounded only by the range and the monotonicity constraint. There is **no magnitude parameter and no annealing** specified — the \"how much\" is \"anywhere in the legal grid,\" decided by a random draw, and selection does the rest (exactly the blind-variation + selective-retention principle from before).\n\n**Invalid candidates are discarded, not repaired:** if a mutated vector violates monotonicity, it's simply **not evaluated** — \"only RoPE that satisfies the constraint is applied for perplexity evaluation, significantly reducing search cost.\"\n\n## The exact search parameters (Table 4 / Alg. 1)\n\n| Parameter | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Population `P` | **64** |\n| Mutation size `N₁` | 16 |\n| Crossover size `N₂` | 16 |\n| Iterations `𝒯` | 40 |\n| Parents kept (top-k) | **32** per iteration |\n| Mutation prob `p` | **0.3** |\n| `λ_i` grid | `[1.0, s×1.25]`, step **0.01** |\n| `n̂` (start tokens) | `{0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}` |\n| Monotonicity | `λ₀ ≤ λ₁ ≤ … ≤ λ₆₃` (64 dims → head_dim 128) |\n\n**Genome = 64 `λ_i` values + `n̂`.** `n̂` is the \"keep initial tokens unscaled\" knob, also searched over its discrete set.\n\n**Initialization:** seed with **PI, NTK, and YaRN** (3 individuals) + the remaining 61 made by mutating those three at `p=0.3`. So it starts from known-good priors, not random noise.\n\n## The rescale formula it's optimizing (Eq. 3)\n\nFor position `n`, dimension `i`:\n```\nangle = n / (β^i)          if n < n̂      (initial tokens: original RoPE, no rescale)\nangle = n / (λ_i · β^i)    if n ≥ n̂      (rescaled: λ_i DIVIDES the frequency)\n```\nLarger `λ_i` ⇒ slower rotation ⇒ more interpolation for that dim. That's the per-dim, per-position non-uniformity fixed formulas can't express.\n\n## Fitness\n\nValidation perplexity, forward-only: **5 random PG19 samples** (≤256k target) or **3 Pile-Books3 samples** (>512k), each ≥ the target length. (For >512k, population/mutation/crossover sizes are halved to save cost.)\n\n## Progressive extension\n\n1. Search on the pretrained model for 128k/256k.\n2. **Fine-tune** to 256k (400 steps @128k, then 600 @256k).\n3. **Second search** on the fine-tuned 256k model → 2048k **with no further fine-tune** (the \"8× non-fine-tuning extension\").\n4. **Readjust** with a search at 4k/8k (reduced max `λ`) to recover short-context performance.\n\n## The corrected mental model for your GA driver\n\n- Genome: 64-long `λ` vector on a `0.01` grid in `[1, s·1.25]`, plus `n̂` from its set.\n- Each generation: from 32 parents, make 16 **mutants** (per-dim resample at p=0.3) + 16 **crossovers**, all forced monotonic (skip violators), evaluate PPL on ~5 long samples, keep the best 32. Repeat 40×.\n- Seed the first population with PI/NTK/YaRN so you're refining, not starting cold.\n- Your `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary is the fitness call; `build_rope_cache` needs to accept the explicit `(λ vector, n̂)` instead of the YaRN formula.\n\nSources:\n- [LongRoPE (arXiv HTML, Ding et al. 2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1)\n- [LongRoPE overview — EmergentMind](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/longrope)\n\nWant me to write this up into `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md` (the file you have open) as a clean implementation spec — the genome, the GA loop, the `build_rope_cache` signature change, and the search-driver skeleton wired to `CP_EVAL_PPL`?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2603,"cache_read_input_tokens":441746,"output_tokens":3968,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2603,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3968,"cache_read_input_tokens":441746,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2603,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2603},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdZzvrbvVhAnWysx13hPn","type":"assistant","uuid":"9e709347-6100-482d-ada8-431d127ead55","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:46:08.424Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9e709347-6100-482d-ada8-431d127ead55","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"16a92c57-1404-497a-a123-7e61080b6e33","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"5b0dc195-6ba6-4645-97dc-202d605be840\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\\n\\nI pulled the paper — and it **corrects my earlier \\\"small multiplicative jitter\\\" description.** LongRoPE doesn't nudge `λ_i` by a small amount; it **resamples it from a discrete grid.** Here's exactly how, from the paper's Algorithm 1 and Table 4.\\n\\n## How `λ_i` is changed and \\\"by how much\\\" (the real answer)\\n\\nEach `λ_i` lives on a **discrete grid**, not a continuous value:\\n- **Range:** `λ_i ∈ [1.0, s × 1.25]` where `s` = extension ratio.\\n- **Step:** `0.01`.\\n\\n**Mutation operator:** take a parent's `λ` vector, and **for each dimension, with probability `p = 0.3`, replace `λ_i` with a fresh value drawn from that grid** (with prob 0.7, keep the parent's value). So it's **not** a tuned step size — each mutated dimension is a **full re-draw** from the whole allowed range `[1.0, s×1.25]`, bounded only by the range and the monotonicity constraint. There is **no magnitude parameter and no annealing** specified — the \\\"how much\\\" is \\\"anywhere in the legal grid,\\\" decided by a random draw, and selection does the rest (exactly the blind-variation + selective-retention principle from before).\\n\\n**Invalid candidates are discarded, not repaired:** if a mutated vector violates monotonicity, it's simply **not evaluated** — \\\"only RoPE that satisfies the constraint is applied for perplexity evaluation, significantly reducing search cost.\\\"\\n\\n## The exact search parameters (Table 4 / Alg. 1)\\n\\n| Parameter | Value |\\n|---|---|\\n| Population `P` | **64** |\\n| Mutation size `N₁` | 16 |\\n| Crossover size `N₂` | 16 |\\n| Iterations `𝒯` | 40 |\\n| Parents kept (top-k) | **32** per iteration |\\n| Mutation prob `p` | **0.3** |\\n| `λ_i` grid | `[1.0, s×1.25]`, step **0.01** |\\n| `n̂` (start tokens) | `{0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}` |\\n| Monotonicity | `λ₀ ≤ λ₁ ≤ … ≤ λ₆₃` (64 dims → head_dim 128) |\\n\\n**Genome = 64 `λ_i` values + `n̂`.** `n̂` is the \\\"keep initial tokens unscaled\\\" knob, also searched over its discrete set.\\n\\n**Initialization:** seed with **PI, NTK, and YaRN** (3 individuals) + the remaining 61 made by mutating those three at `p=0.3`. So it starts from known-good priors, not random noise.\\n\\n## The rescale formula it's optimizing (Eq. 3)\\n\\nFor position `n`, dimension `i`:\\n```\\nangle = n / (β^i)          if n < n̂      (initial tokens: original RoPE, no rescale)\\nangle = n / (λ_i · β^i)    if n ≥ n̂      (rescaled: λ_i DIVIDES the frequency)\\n```\\nLarger `λ_i` ⇒ slower rotation ⇒ more interpolation for that dim. That's the per-dim, per-position non-uniformity fixed formulas can't express.\\n\\n## Fitness\\n\\nValidation perplexity, forward-only: **5 random PG19 samples** (≤256k target) or **3 Pile-Books3 samples** (>512k), each ≥ the target length. (For >512k, population/mutation/crossover sizes are halved to save cost.)\\n\\n## Progressive extension\\n\\n1. Search on the pretrained model for 128k/256k.\\n2. **Fine-tune** to 256k (400 steps @128k, then 600 @256k).\\n3. **Second search** on the fine-tuned 256k model → 2048k **with no further fine-tune** (the \\\"8× non-fine-tuning extension\\\").\\n4. **Readjust** with a search at 4k/8k (reduced max `λ`) to recover short-context performance.\\n\\n## The corrected mental model for your GA driver\\n\\n- Genome: 64-long `λ` vector on a `0.01` grid in `[1, s·1.25]`, plus `n̂` from its set.\\n- Each generation: from 32 parents, make 16 **mutants** (per-dim resample at p=0.3) + 16 **crossovers**, all forced monotonic (skip violators), evaluate PPL on ~5 long samples, keep the best 32. Repeat 40×.\\n- Seed the first population with PI/NTK/YaRN so you're refining, not starting cold.\\n- Your `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary is the fitness call; `build_rope_cache` needs to accept the explicit `(λ vector, n̂)` instead of the YaRN formula.\\n\\nSources:\\n- [LongRoPE (arXiv HTML, Ding et al. 2024)](https://arxiv.org/html/2402.13753v1)\\n- [LongRoPE overview — EmergentMind](https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/longrope)\\n\\nWant me to write this up into `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md` (the file you have open) as a clean implementation spec — the genome, the GA loop, the `build_rope_cache` signature change, and the search-driver skeleton wired to `CP_EVAL_PPL`?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":58},"type":"attachment","uuid":"eb41bfbc-d04a-42d5-91b2-daa8e42f852c","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:46:08.899Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
