{"parentUuid":"c6a89e12-657a-4804-88ad-25eb1fde500e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda1SBY1vNhpEf2F6YVeP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017AZC7DUrY4z4mMJoW5Twmo","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Verify YARNOps cache internals","prompt":"I'm planning to add a LongRoPE cache builder alongside the existing YaRN one. I need EXACT details from these files (read-only, report precisely with line numbers and short code excerpts):\n\n1. /home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp — the full `build_rope_cache` implementation:\n   - Its exact signature.\n   - The cos/sin CACHE LAYOUT: for a [seq_len, head_dim] cache, which columns hold cos and which hold sin? (e.g. cos in [0,hd/2), sin in [hd/2,hd)?) Is it NeoX half-split or interleaved?\n   - The per-dimension frequency formula: how inv_freq / the NTK-by-parts (find_correction_dim / ramp) is computed. I need the exact math so I can port PI, NTK, and YaRN per-dimension lambda factors as Python seeds.\n   - The attention-temperature `m` (mscale): how is it computed and where is it multiplied into cos/sin? Confirm it scales ALL positions.\n   - How YARN_SCALE / YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS / YARN_BETA_FAST / YARN_BETA_SLOW env vars feed the formula.\n   - Whether the cache is built on CPU then moved to device.\n\n2. /home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp — how the RoPE cache is built in the GPT/model constructor and installed: find where build_rope_cache is called (around line 337), the `cream_full_cache_` member and the CREAM install path (install_cream_positions, set_rope_cache), and how CP_CREAM_MODE gating is done. I want to mirror that additive gating pattern for a new CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS env.\n\n3. The CP_EVAL_PPL output format: confirm the exact CSV columns written (pos,count,mean_nll,ppl?) and the file/env (CP_EVAL_OUT). Around lines 960-1045 of bluscriptCP.cpp.\n\nReport exact signatures, the layout convention, the frequency+m formula, the env plumbing, and the CREAM gating pattern. Do not propose changes; just extract the ground truth.","subagent_type":"Explore"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3124,"cache_read_input_tokens":465025,"output_tokens":2706,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3124,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2706,"cache_read_input_tokens":465025,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3124,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3124},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda1S5yPt46GB5QL5jei5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5905bb57-88c3-49fa-b1f1-f8cc917bdc93","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:52:28.689Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
