{"parentUuid":"7705d00e-7fc3-4183-ba57-c9d365071ab3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fc67f2a4-0b60-4391-b13e-a77cb3ee6dd7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B7qHrujAuyPyXi8begqS1H","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n2\t\n3\t## Context\n4\t\n5\tCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\n6\tmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\n7\tmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\n8\tsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\n9\tblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n10\t4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\n11\tvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\n12\trepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n13\t\n14\t**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\n15\tthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that"}]},"uuid":"b7e3bc5e-1a4f-41ef-b851-687bd97cffbd","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:52:28.962Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","content":"# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)\n\n## Context\n\nCREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a\nmodel's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding\nmanipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical\nsequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle\nblock from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays\n4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`\nvalues it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the\nrepo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).\n\n**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;\nthe fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that","numLines":15,"startLine":1,"totalLines":174}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"60126963-a386-4269-81ff-5ebf1b0d14e0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
