{"parentUuid":"b9a0ef6b-bf7e-4b73-aa7c-92966d2151b9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda1VLenDE9d6FtNnxWLD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cn2VWbry9dQPmeuPHNZnCs","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"LongRoPE's search is training-free; the full recipe adds a fine-tune. What scope do you want for this implementation?","header":"Scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Search-only first, then optional fine-tune","description":"Phase 2a: run the evolutionary search on the base checkpoint with NO fine-tune, eval it (matches LongRoPE's headline '8x without fine-tuning'). Phase 2b: optionally fine-tune with the found cache. Cheapest first result; recommended."},{"label":"Search + fine-tune together (single stage)","description":"Search for the target factor, then always fine-tune with the found cache (like your CREAM/YaRN arms). One combined pipeline, directly comparable to your existing arms."},{"label":"Full progressive (multi-stage)","description":"Search -> fine-tune to intermediate -> re-search -> extend further, as in the paper's 256k->2048k curriculum. Most faithful but most work; overkill for the 48M/32-64k scale."}]},{"question":"The GA fitness is perplexity. Over which positions should it be minimized?","header":"Fitness region","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Overall PPL (all positions)","description":"exp(sum nll*count / sum count) over the whole target-length sequence. Matches the paper (they eval full-length PPL). Recommended."},{"label":"Extended-region PPL only (>orig_ctx)","description":"Minimize PPL only for positions beyond the original 4k context. Focuses the search on the extension quality, ignores the in-distribution region."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3556,"cache_read_input_tokens":468149,"output_to