bel":"Extended-region PPL only (>orig_ctx)","description":"Minimize PPL only for positions beyond the original 4k context. Focuses the search on the extension quality, ignores the in-distribution region."}],"multiSelect":false}],"answers":{"LongRoPE's search is training-free; the full recipe adds a fine-tune. What scope do you want for this implementation?":"Full progressive (multi-stage)","The GA fitness is perplexity. Over which positions should it be minimized?":"Overall PPL (all positions)"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca35fcc2-6ecf-402d-a09d-118e057a9b4f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"e37be537-718f-42e1-9388-59399592ddd3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a40a89138b9ac0675</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_017AZC7DUrY4z4mMJoW5Twmo</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b/tasks/a40a89138b9ac0675.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify YARNOps cache internals\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have all the ground truth. Here is the complete extraction.\n\n## 1. `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp` — `build_rope_cache`\n\n### Exact signature (line 47)\n```cpp\nTensor build_rope_cache(int64_t seq_len, int64_t head_dim, float base, DeviceIndex device)\n```\n- Guards `head_dim % 2 != 0` -&gt; `std::invalid_argument` (lines 49-51).\n- `base` is the RoPE theta.\n\n### Cache layout — NeoX half-split (lines 62, 108-122)\nCache tensor is `[seq_len, head_dim]`, fp32. With `half = head_dim / 2`, the inner loop runs `i` over `[0, half)` and writes:\n- **cos** in columns `[0, half)`: `p[pos*head_dim + i] = cos(angle) * m`\n- **sin** in columns `[half, head_dim)`: `p[pos*head_dim + i + half] = sin(angle) * m`\n\nSo it is the **NeoX half-split** convention (cos in first half, sin in second half), NOT interleaved. Each cos/sin column `i` shares the same `inv_freq[i]`.\n\n### Per-dimension frequency formula (lines 108-119)\n```cpp\nexponent  = (2.0f * i) / head_dim;\nbase_freq = 1.0f / pow(base, exponent);           // pure RoPE / extrapolation freq\nramp      = (i - low) / denom;  clamped to [0,1]  // linear ramp over DIM INDEX i\ninv_freq  = (base_freq / s) * ramp + base_freq * (1 - ramp);\nangle     = pos * inv_freq;\n```\nInterpretation (comments lines 115-117):\n- `ramp = 0` (i &lt; low, high-freq end) -&gt; keep `base_freq` (extrapolate, PI-off).\n- `ramp = 1` (i &gt; high, low-freq end) -&gt; `base_freq / s` (interpolate = PI by scale `s`).\n- Linear blend in between = NTK-by-parts.\n\nFor your Python seeds: PI factor = `1/s` for all dims; NTK-by-parts / YaRN = the per-dim `ramp`-weighted blend above, i.e. `inv_freq[i] = base_freq[i] * ((ramp/s) + (1-ramp))`.\n\n### Correction range (find_correction_dim / find_correction_range) — lines 67-78\n```cpp\nfind_dim(num_rot) = head_dim * log( L / (num_rot * 2*PI) ) / (2 * log(base));\nlow  = floor(find_dim(b_fast));   // clamped to &gt;= 0\nhigh = ceil (find_dim(b_slow));   // clamped to &lt;= half-1  (deliberate deviation from HF head_dim-1)\ndenom = high - low;               // set to 1e-3 if &lt;= 0\n```\nNote the clamp to `half - 1` at line 75 is intentional (comment: \"do not fix\"). `denom` guards `low==high`.\n\n### Attention temperature `m` (mscale) — lines 59-60, 120-121\n```cpp\nconst float m = (s &gt; 1.0f) ? (0.1f * std::log(s) + 1.0f) : 1.0f;\n```\n- Computed once from `s = YARN_SCALE`. When `s &lt;= 1`, `m == 1` (no-op).\n- Multiplied into **both** cos and sin (`cos(angle)*m`, `sin(angle)*m`), for **every** position `pos` in the loop — so it scales ALL positions uniformly (it is position-independent; it depends only on `s`). Header comment (lines 28-30): RoPE hits both Q and K, so `m` appears twice per QK logit giving `m^2 = 1/t`; the fused kernel's `1/sqrt(hd)` scale is left untouched.\n\n### Env vars (lines 41-57, via `yarn_env_f`)\n- `YARN_SCALE` -&gt; `s` (default 1.0) = target_ctx/original_ctx. Drives both `inv_freq` interpolation and `m`.\n- `YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS` -&gt; `L` (default 1024.0) = original pretrain context; used in `find_dim`.\n- `YARN_BETA_FAST` -&gt; `b_fast` (default 32.0) = high-rotation bound -&gt; `low`.\n- `YARN_BETA_SLOW` -&gt; `b_slow` (default 1.0) = low-rotation bound -&gt; `high`.\n- `yarn_env_f` reads via `std::getenv` + `std::atof`; default when unset.\n- With `YARN_SCALE=1.0` the whole thing collapses to standard RoPE bit-identically (comment lines 32-34): `base_freq/s == base_freq` and `m==1`.\n- Guards: bad correction range throws (lines 81-86); `seq_len != s*L` warns only (lines 89-94); init log line at 98-100.\n\n### Device (lines 36-38, 102-131)\nAlways built on **CPU fp32** (`TensorOptions().with_dtype(Float32).with_device(CPU)`), filled, `set_requires_grad(false)`, then `cpu.to(device)` only if `device.device == Device::CUDA` (also grad-free). The CUDA kernel `rope_build_cache_cuda` is deliberately bypassed (no per-dim freq hook).\n\n## 2. `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp` — RoPE cache construction + CREAM install\n\n### Member (line 334)\n```cpp\nTensor cream_full_cache_;   // full YaRN-scaled cache, built ONLY when cream_mode != \"off\"\n```\nBase cache member `cos_sin_cache` at line 330.\n\n### build_rope_cache calls in GPT ctor\n- Base cache (initializer list, lines 353-354):\n```cpp\ncos_sin_cache(autograd::build_rope_cache(c.context_length, c.head_dim,\n                                         static_cast&lt;float&gt;(c.rope_theta), dev))\n```\n- CREAM gather-source cache (additive, lines 367-371) — only built when `cream_mode != \"off\"`:\n```cpp\nif (c.cream_mode != \"off\") {\n    cream_full_cache_ = autograd::build_rope_cache(\n        c.cream_scaled_max, c.head_dim, static_cast&lt;float&gt;(c.rope_theta), dev);\n}\n```\nNote: `build_rope_cache` reads `YARN_SCALE` from env, so `cream_full_cache_` row `pos` holds the YaRN-interpolated cos/sin for absolute position `pos`. The base `cos_sin_cache` is passed into each `CausalGQA` layer (line 374); `cream_full_cache_` is never passed to the kernel directly — only used as gather source.\n\n### CREAM install path — `install_cream_positions(uint64_t seed)` (lines 432-459)\n- No-op when `cream_mode == \"off\"` (line 433).\n- Generates position LABELS `L` (vector&lt;int64_t&gt;) via `generate_cream_positions` / `generate_pose_positions` / `generate_randpos_positions` depending on mode; unknown mode throws (lines 437-444).\n- Builds an `[T, hd]` Int64 gather-index tensor where row `i` = `L[i]` broadcast across all `hd` columns (lines 448-454), moves to device (455), then:\n```cpp\nTensor cream_cache = OwnTensor::gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, idx_dev);  // out[i][j]=full[L[i]][j]\nfor (auto&amp; a : attn) a-&gt;cp_-&gt;set_rope_cache(cream_cache);   // fan out to every layer\n```\nGather done ONCE, fanned to all layers.\n\n### `set_rope_cache` — `/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/ContextParallel.h` lines 324-332\n```cpp\nvoid set_rope_cache(const Tensor &amp;cos_sin_cache) {\n    if (cos_sin_cache.requires_grad()) throw std::runtime_error(\"... must be gradient-free ...\");\n    cos_sin_cache_ = cos_sin_cache;\n    if (use_ulysses_fused_) cos_sin_cache_f_ = cos_sin_cache;  // keep fused path in sync\n}\n```\nRequires grad-free cache. Overwrites `cos_sin_cache_`; if never called, the layer keeps exactly the base cache from `enable_rope()` (byte-identical default behavior).\n\n### CP_CREAM_MODE additive gating pattern (lines 627-655) — the pattern to mirror\n```cpp\nif (const char* e = std::getenv(\"CP_CREAM_MODE\"))  cfg.cream_mode = e;\nif (const char* e = std::getenv(\"CP_CREAM_SIGMA\")) cfg.cream_sigma = std::atof(e);\nif (const char* e = std::getenv(\"CP_CREAM_SEED\"))  cfg.cream_seed = strtoull(...);\nconst bool cream_on = (cfg.cream_mode != \"off\");\nif (cream_on) {\n    const double yarn_scale = std::getenv(\"YARN_SCALE\") ? std::atof(...) : 1.0;\n    cfg.cream_factor     = static_cast&lt;int&gt;(yarn_scale + 0.5);\n    cfg.cream_scaled_max = cfg.cream_factor * cfg.T;\n    // validation die()s: mode whitelist, cp_size==1, YARN_SCALE&gt;1, factor&gt;=2, scaled_max % T == 0, ...\n}\n```\nConfig member default at line 143: `std::string cream_mode = \"off\";  // CP_CREAM_MODE`. The gate is: env resolved into `cfg`, a `bool xxx_on` computed, all extra work guarded behind `if (xxx_on)`, default path untouched. `cream_on` also gates `install_cream_positions` calls at lines 1305 (eval) and 1438 (training loop).\n\n## 3. CP_EVAL_PPL output format (lines 1245-1398)\n\n- Gate: `eval_ppl_mode` = `CP_EVAL_PPL` set and non-zero (lines 575-576). Requires `cp_size == 1` else throws (1246-1249).\n- Output file env: `CP_EVAL_OUT`, default `\"ppl_vs_pos.csv\"` (lines 1252-1253).\n- Other env: `CP_EVAL_WINDOWS` (default 10, line 1251), `CP_EVAL_TOKENS_BIN` (optional int32 LE shared token stream, forces B=1, lines 1266-1290).\n- **CSV columns (exact, line 1385):**\n```\npos,count,mean_nll,ppl\n```\n- Written with `std::fixed &lt;&lt; std::setprecision(6)` (line 1386). Each row (lines 1387-1391):\n```cpp\nmean_nll = cnt[t] &gt; 0 ? sum_nll[t]/cnt[t] : 0.0;\nf &lt;&lt; t &lt;&lt; \",\" &lt;&lt; cnt[t] &lt;&lt; \",\" &lt;&lt; mean_nll &lt;&lt; \",\" &lt;&lt; std::exp(mean_nll) &lt;&lt; \"\\n\";\n```\nSo `ppl = exp(mean_nll)`, i.e. per-position `PPL(t) = exp(mean_nll(t))`. NLL per position = `logsumexp(logits) - logits[target]` (lines 1358-1376), summed over batch/windows into `sum_nll[t]` / `cnt[t]`. Only master rank writes; then `MPI_Finalize(); return 0;` (1396-1397). During eval, config/log files are opened to `/dev/null` (lines 971, 1013).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>36927</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>10</tool_uses><duration_ms>74837</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:53:43.537Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5d2d72a-42cd-4d2d-8064-5f09f3ae007a","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:53:43.537Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
