{"parentUuid":"25458e61-9f3a-4831-8c1a-dd22d7a6209f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda1dN4LT4VFSpX4puwjZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now have complete ground truth (NeoX half-split layout, the `inv_freq[i] = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` YaRN formula, the `m` temperature, the CREAM gating pattern, and the `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` CSV). Combined with your choices (full progressive + overall-PPL fitness), I can write the final plan. Let me record it."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6873,"cache_read_input_tokens":471705,"output_tokens":8187,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8187,"cache_read_input_tokens":471705,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda1dJjueWdN4uTd19qa6","type":"assistant","uuid":"6286574f-1531-4fb4-96c5-a7434e52d377","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:55:16.454Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6286574f-1531-4fb4-96c5-a7434e52d377","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda1dN4LT4VFSpX4puwjZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N29wnBFhLzZF4enywFNCv1","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","content":"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\n\n## Context\n\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\n\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\n```\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\n```\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\n\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\n\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\n\n## Non-destructive invariant\n\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\n\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\n\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\n\n## Approach\n\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\n   ```\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\n   ```\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\n\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \"\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\n\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\n\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\n\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\n\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\n\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\n  fine-tune → final.\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\n\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\n\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\n\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\n\n## Reuse\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6873,"cache_read_input_tokens":471705,"output_tokens":8187,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6873,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8187,"cache_read_input_tokens":471705,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6873},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda1dJjueWdN4uTd19qa6","type":"assistant","uuid":"baf659e3-1f33-4594-bb9a-3b3252e24e62","timestamp":"2026-07-31T10:56:08.707Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
