identical** to today.\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\n\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\n\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\n\n## Approach\n\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\n   ```\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\n   ```\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\n\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \"\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\n\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\n\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\n\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\n\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\n\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\n  fine-tune → final.\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\n\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\n\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\n\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\n\n## Reuse\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":173,"newStart":1,"newLines":137,"lines":["-# Plan: Implement CREAM position-manipulation in bluscriptCP (single-GPU first)","+# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP"," "," ## Context"," ","-CREAM (bigai-nlco/CREAM, \"Continuity-Relativity indexing with gAussianMiddle\") extends a","-model's usable context window by **fine-tuning at the pre-trained sequence length while feeding","-manipulated RoPE position labels** drawn from the larger target range. A 4K-token physical","-sequence is relabeled with positions like `[0..head)` ++ (a Gaussian-sampled contiguous middle","-block from the scaled range) ++ `[scaled_max-tail .. scaled_max)`. The attention matrix stays","-4K x 4K (memory cost unchanged) but the model is forced to compute rotations at large `m`","-values it would otherwise only see in a 32K sequence. Reference: `src/train.py::CREAM` in the","-repo (mirrored to `/tmp/cream_train.py`).","+We have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working","+in `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a","+*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale","+factors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the","+current SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another","+context-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM."," ","-**Why this is feasible here.** In `bluscriptCP.cpp` RoPE positions are never stored as data;","-the fused CP kernel computes `pos = local_idx + delta` and indexes the cos/sin cache at that","-row (`GQA_fused_fwd_sm103_cp.cu:94-97`, mirrored by `RopeDeltas.h::rope_global_pos`). At","-**CP_SIZE=1** every delta collapses to zero (`compute_deltas(rank=0,i=0,N=1)` -> `(0,0)`), so","-`pos == local_idx`. The wrapper derives `cache_seq_len` from the cache tensor's row count","-(`FusedRoPESDPA.h:114`). Therefore, if we feed a cache whose **row `j` already holds the cos/sin","-for CREAM label `L[j]`**, the unmodified kernel produces exactly CREAM's rotations — no CUDA","-changes for single GPU.","+Rescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:","+```","+angle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)","+angle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)","+```","+`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature."," ","-**Decisions taken with the user:** single-GPU (CP_SIZE=1) first, CP later; wire plumbing to","-serve **both** training fine-tune and the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` eval path. On \"which variant","-helps context extension\": all three in the repo do (PoSE is the seminal skip-wise method; CREAM","-adds the truncated-Gaussian middle to fight lost-in-the-middle; RandPos is a weaker random","-baseline). We implement **CREAM as primary** behind a small generator interface so PoSE/RandPos","-become ~10-line selectable modes sharing the same plumbing.","+**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions)."," ","-## Approach (single-GPU, no CUDA edits): cache-row gather","+The search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages."," ","-Per step: build the **full scaled** cos/sin cache once (length = `scaled_max`, via existing","-`build_rope_cache` + YaRN env), generate a length-`T` CREAM label vector `L`, gather","-`cream_cache = full_cache[L]` (shape `[T, hd]`), and install `cream_cache` on every CP layer","-before running the blocks. The kernel reads `pos = local_idx in [0,T)` and picks","-`cream_cache[local_idx]` = rotation at `L[local_idx]`. Correct because at CP_SIZE=1 the","-sub-chunk is `Full`, deltas are 0, and the causal mask uses **local indices** (independent of","-RoPE position — see the CONTRACT comment at `ContextParallel.h:751-758`), and CREAM labels are","-monotonic (head < middle < tail).","+## Non-destructive invariant"," ","-**Known simplification (acceptable for v1):** the cos/sin cache is shared across the batch, so","-one CREAM labeling applies to all `B` rows per step (the reference samples per-row). We resample","-fresh each step. True per-row labels would require an explicit per-token position array in the","-kernel — deferred to the CP phase. Likewise v1 relabels the natural contiguous token chunk","-(standard PoSE/CREAM position-only relabeling, sufficient for extension); the reference's","-optional middle-token re-gather is a later refinement.","+Everything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.","+New C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive","+gating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`."," ","-## Corrections from a line-by-line diff against the mirrored source (`/tmp/cream_train.py:188-223`, call site :256)","+## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)"," ","-These override the earlier prose and are the substance of the review:","+- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX","+  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)","+  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU","+  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).","+- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on","+  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer","+  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at","+  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).","+- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via","+  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source."," ","-- **`model_max` IS the physical sequence length.** The reference truncates each chunk to","-  `model_max_position_embeddings` (line 133), so `T == model_max` always. The generator's","-  `model_max` argument MUST be bound to `cfg.T`, not to any model pretrain constant. With that","-  binding, `head_len+tail_len = 2*T/3 < T` can never produce a degenerate middle — the","-  \"1365+1365 > T\" failure mode only appears if `model_max` is set independently of `T`, which we","-  forbid.","-- **Both segmentation branches are real** and chosen per batch by `random.randint(0,1)`:","-  branch 0 -> `head_len=tail_len=T/3`; branch 1 -> `head_len=tail_len=4*factor` (this is the","-  paper's small-`k` regime: `factor=8` gives `k=32`). Port BOTH faithfully; do not collapse to","-  one.","-- **`scaled_max` and the RoPE scale are locked, not independent.** Source: `scaled_max =","-  model_max * rope_scaling_factor` (line 256), and that same value is YaRN's","-  `max_position_embeddings` with `original_max_position_embeddings = model_max`. So we DERIVE","-  `factor = YARN_SCALE` (must be integer `>= 2`), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`. There is NO","-  independent `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX` env. Assert `factor >= 2` (the Gaussian samples","-  `rand_factor in [2, 2*factor]`) and `scaled_max % T == 0`.","-- **YaRN must be ON when CREAM is on.** The full cache is built at `scaled_max`; if `YARN_SCALE`","-  were left at 1.0 while `scaled_max` grows, CREAM would train against unmitigated high-freq","-  aliasing at the extreme labels — the exact regime YaRN exists to fix. Assert `YARN_SCALE > 1`","-  under CREAM; the two features compose by construction (`factor == YARN_SCALE`).","-- **Integration guard replacing the removed `T != context_length` check:** assert","-  `head_len + tail_len < T` and `len_chunk = T - head_len - tail_len >= 1` at the call site with a","-  real (possibly tiny bring-up) `T`, plus `scaled_max >= T`. Do not merely delete the old guard.","+## Approach"," ","-## Non-destructive / additive invariant (hard requirement)","+LongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that","+picks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we","+**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap."," ","-Every change is **purely additive and gated behind `CP_CREAM_MODE`**. No existing line's default","-behavior is altered or removed. With `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` (the default) the program must be","-**bit-for-bit identical to today** — same cache built the same way, same guard, same forward, same","-eval. New behavior lives in new files, new members, new methods, and `if (cream_on) { ... } else","-{ <existing code verbatim> }` branches. This mirrors the established additive-gating discipline","-already used in the CP stack (e.g. `-DCP_FUSED_ROPE` in `FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and the","-`use_rope_==false` default path in `ContextParallel.h:749`). Nothing existing is erased.","-"," ## Files to change"," ","-1. **New: `context_parallel/CreamPositions.h`** (header-only, immutable/value-returning). Split into","-   THREE layers so every cross-language hazard is isolated and unit-testable independent of RNG parity","-   (a **line-by-line** port of `CREAM()` `/tmp/cream_train.py:196-223`, with `model_max := T`,","-   `scaled_max := factor * T`):","+1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,","+   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.","+   ```","+   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):","+       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)","+       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq","+       ang       = n * base_freq / scale","+       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m","+       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)","+   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free","+   ```","+   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header."," ","-   - **(a) Pure math layer** — `std::vector<int64_t> cream_labels_from_draws(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor, int64_t end_id)`: given fully-resolved draws, assemble labels.","-     `head=tail = (branch==0 ? T/3 : 4*factor)`; `len_chunk = T - head - tail`;","-     `pos_ids_1=[0,head)`; `pos_ids_2=[end_id-(len_chunk-1), end_id]`; `pos_ids_3=[factor*T-tail, factor*T)`;","-     return the concat (length exactly `T`). No randomness — this is the deterministic transform.","-   - **(b) Range/CDF layer** — the two spots where language semantics bite:","-     - `int rand_factor_from_u(double u, int factor, double sigma)`: `mu=1+factor`;","-       `x=linspace(2, 2*factor, 1000)`; `cdf=0.5*(1+erf((x-mu)/(sigma*sqrt2)))`;","-       `rand_factor = round(np_interp(u, /*xp=*/cdf, /*fp=*/x))` clamped to `[2, 2*factor]`.","-       **`np_interp` argument order MUST be `(query=u, xp=cdf, fp=x)`** — look `u` up against the CDF","-       domain, return the `x` value (matches `np.interp(u, cdf, x)`); a swapped `xp/fp` silently","-       samples the wrong distribution. Use a dedicated `np_interp` helper, not a generic one whose","-       arg convention might differ.","-     - `std::pair<int64_t,int64_t> end_id_range(int T, int factor, int branch, int rand_factor)`:","-       `lo = head + (len_chunk-1) * (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0)`,","-       `hi = (static_cast<double>(rand_factor)/2.0) * T - tail - 1`, each floored to int.","-       **`rand_factor/2` MUST be true division** (`rand_factor` is odd ~half the time; integer","-       floor-division here biases `end_id` for half of all draws) — cast to `double` at BOTH sites.","-   - **(c) Sampling wrapper** — `generate_cream_positions(int T, int factor, double sigma, uint64_t seed)`:","-     draws `branch = randint(0,1)`, `u = U[0,1)`, then `[lo,hi]=end_id_range(...)`,","-     `end_id = randint(lo,hi)`, and returns `cream_labels_from_draws(...)`. Use","-     **`std::uniform_int_distribution<int64_t>(a,b)`** for every `randint` (inclusive on BOTH ends,","-     matching Python's `random.randint`) — never a hand-rolled `a + rng()%(b-a)` (excludes `b`).","-     Explicit `seed` (no hidden global state). No claim of RNG-stream parity with Python — that is","-     deliberately NOT relied on (see test 4).","-   - `generate_pose_positions(...)` / `generate_randpos_positions(...)` factored the same way","-     (faithful ports of `PoSE` :150-183 and `RandPos` :126-144).","-   - Guards: `factor >= 2`, `head+tail < T`, `len_chunk >= 1` — throw with a clear message rather than","-     emit a malformed (non-monotonic / negative-middle) vector.","+2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:","+   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \"\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on","+     = !longrope_factors.empty();`","+   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.","+   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.","+   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,","+     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —","+     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune","+     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.","+   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the","+     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs","+     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup."," ","-2. **`context_parallel/ContextParallel.h`** — ADD a per-step cache setter (new method only; no existing member/method changed):","-   - `void set_rope_cache(const Tensor& c) { cos_sin_cache_ = c; }` — points the resident cache at the caller's tensor. This is called ONLY when CREAM is on; when off it is never invoked and `cos_sin_cache_` keeps exactly the value `enable_rope()` gave it (existing behavior untouched). `cache_seq_len` already flows from the tensor shape, so no other code changes. No delta/mask logic touched. The passed tensor must be **gradient-free end to end** — built with `with_req_grad(false)`; assert `!c.requires_grad()` in the setter.","+3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode","+   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:","+   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.","+   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).","+   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with","+     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.","+   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.","+   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.","+   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`","+     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.","+   - Output `longrope_best.txt`."," ","-3. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — the main integration:","-   - **Config/env:** `CP_CREAM_MODE` (off|cream|pose|randpos), `CP_CREAM_SIGMA` (default 3.0), optional `CP_CREAM_SEED`. **No `CP_CREAM_SCALED_MAX`** — `factor = YARN_SCALE` (integer), `scaled_max = factor * cfg.T`, both derived. Add to `ModelConfig` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:104-111` region).","-   - **Startup asserts (CREAM on):** `YARN_SCALE > 1`, `factor >= 2`, `scaled_max % T == 0`, `scaled_max >= T`. Fail fast with a message naming the offending value.","-   - **Cache build (additive — existing cache untouched):** do NOT modify the constructor's `cos_sin_cache(build_rope_cache(c.context_length, ...))` member initializer (`bluscriptCP.cpp:337-338`) — it stays verbatim. ADD a separate member (e.g. `Tensor cream_full_cache_`) built in the constructor body **only when CREAM is on**, at `scaled_max` with YaRN active (same `build_rope_cache`, which already reads `YARN_SCALE`). When off, `cream_full_cache_` is never built and nothing else sees it. The per-step gather sources from `cream_full_cache_`, never from the base cache.","-   - **Guard (additive — existing die() preserved):** keep the existing `if (cfg.T != cfg.context_length) die(...)` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:552`) verbatim for the CREAM-off path. Wrap it: `if (cream_off) { <existing guard verbatim> } else { <new scaled_max==factor*T / factor>=2 / YARN_SCALE>1 asserts> }`. Nothing is removed or relaxed on the default path.","-   - **Per-step install (additive branch; gather once, fan out to all layers):** in `TransformerModel::forward` (`bluscriptCP.cpp:369`), the existing body runs unchanged; ADD an `if (cream_on)` block at the top: `auto L = generate_*_positions(cfg.T, factor, sigma, seed_for_step)` (guards enforced inside); `Tensor Lt = tensor(L)`; `Tensor cream_cache = gather(cream_full_cache_, /*dim=*/0, Lt)` (`ops/IndexingOps.h::gather`, non-autograd, grad-free). Compute ONCE, then loop layers calling `cp_->set_rope_cache(cream_cache)` — explicit comment that the gather stays OUTSIDE the layer loop (moving it in pays `n_layers`x for nothing). Expose each layer's `cp_` via a small accessor or a model-level `set_rope_cache` fan-out (new accessor, no existing member changed). When off, this block is skipped and the layers keep the base cache from `enable_rope()`.","-   - **Eval path:** in the `CP_EVAL_PPL` loop (`bluscriptCP.cpp:~960-1040`), the same install (a FIXED labeling, not resampled) so PPL-vs-position is measured under CREAM/extended labels vs the naive-extrapolation baseline. This path has its OWN install logic, so it gets its OWN off-mode regression check (below) — it does not inherit training's.","+4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:","+   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the","+   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold."," ","-4. **`Tests/`** — TDD:","-   - `Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp`: because RNG streams are NOT bit-identical across Python and C++,","-     the golden test targets the DETERMINISTIC layers with **injected draws** (not \"same seed\"):","-     - **Golden math** — feed `(branch, rand_factor, end_id)` tuples *captured by running the actual","-       Python reference once* into `cream_labels_from_draws(...)` and assert the exact label vector.","-       Capture-and-commit those tuples as fixtures (a tiny script noted in the test header).","-     - **Range/CDF** — assert `rand_factor_from_u(u,...)` and `end_id_range(...)` against values","-       hand-computed from `/tmp/cream_train.py:209-219`; specifically include an ODD `rand_factor`","-       case to catch integer-vs-true division, and an `interp` case that would differ if `xp/fp` were","-       swapped.","-     - **Structural** — monotonic head<middle<tail; exact block lengths for BOTH branches; middle","-       within `[head, scaled_max-tail)`; total length == `T`; guards throw on `factor<2` / `head+tail>=T`.","-     - **randint convention** — a direct assert that the wrapper's `randint(a,b)` can return `b`","-       (inclusive upper bound).","-     - PoSE/RandPos shape tests too. Style per `Tests/cp_rope_deltas_test.cpp`.","-   - `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`: (a) feeding `gather(full_cache, 0, L)` through `sdpa_fused_forward_rope` at CP_SIZE=1 equals applying RoPE directly at positions `L` (reuse `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`) — the core proof of the no-CUDA trick; (b) **YaRN spot-check**: a handful of `full_cache` rows at large labels match the expected NTK-by-parts YaRN-interpolated cos/sin (mirrors the original YaRN plan's spot-check), confirming the gathered cache is YaRN-scaled, not plain-extrapolated.","-   - Wire both into the `Makefile` alongside existing CP tests; run with `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1`.","+5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a","+   `longrope-search` convenience target."," ","-5. **`README.md`** — document the `CP_CREAM_*` env vars under the bluscriptCP section (mirrors the existing YaRN / re-warmup env tables), including the batch-shared-labeling caveat and the single-GPU-only scope for now.","+6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then","+   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow."," ","-## Reuse (do not hand-roll)","-- `build_rope_cache` + YaRN scaling via env — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`.","-- `gather(input, dim, index)` — `BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/include/ops/IndexingOps.h:16`.","-- Fused RoPE forward/backward wrappers (unchanged) — `context_parallel/FusedRoPESDPA.h`.","-- Delta/position source-of-truth (untouched at CP_SIZE=1) — `context_parallel/RopeDeltas.h`.","-- Reference algorithm — `src/train.py::CREAM/PoSE/RandPos` (mirror at `/tmp/cream_train.py`).","+## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)"," ","-## Verification (end-to-end)","-1. `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 <cream tests>` and run `cream_positions_test` + `cream_cache_gather_parity` — expect PASS (cos parity ~1.0 on the gather path; YaRN spot-check within tol).","-2. Single-GPU sanity: `CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 CP_SIZE=1 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream YARN_SCALE=<N>` short training run (tiny cfg, e.g. T=256, as in the 2026-07-10 log) — loss decreases, finite grad-norm, no NaNs. Because at tiny `T` the `4*factor` branch is the tightest, confirm the smoke run exercises both branches without hitting the `head+tail<T` guard.","-3. **Regression (both paths):** `CP_CREAM_MODE=off` reproduces the current baseline bit-for-bit in BOTH the training run AND the `CP_EVAL_PPL` path (the eval path has separate install logic — check it explicitly).","-4. **Distribution check (correctness of the truncated-Gaussian, not just \"no NaN\"):** log the sampled middle-block start (`end_id`) over a few hundred steps and confirm the histogram approximates the intended truncated-Gaussian shape. A subtly-wrong `erf`/inverse-CDF can still yield a healthy loss curve while defeating CREAM's \"focus the middle\" property — this is the check that catches it.","-5. `CP_EVAL_PPL` before/after: base ckpt + naive extrapolation (blows up past `orig_ctx`) vs a CREAM-fine-tuned ckpt at extended positions (flatter PPL-vs-position curve) — plotted via the existing notebook cell.","+- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**","+  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.","+- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light","+  fine-tune → final.","+- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL."," ","-## Deferred (Phase 2 — CP_SIZE>1)","-Multi-GPU needs an **explicit per-token position array** threaded into the kernel","-(`gqa_fused_rope_cp_forward/backward` gain `const int* q_pos/k_pos`; device `pos = q_pos[idx]`","-overriding the delta formula), fed from the sharder's already-computed-but-unused","-`ShardedInputs::pos_local` (`ContextParallel.h:81-85`). This composes CREAM labels with HeadTail","-shard geometry and also unlocks true per-row labeling. Touches the two `.cu` files,","-`FusedRoPESDPA.h`, and `ContextParallel.h`/`ContextParallelBackward.h`. Out of scope for now.","+**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —","+real `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in","+the CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with","+CREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k","+physical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is","+forward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`","+search under CP or cap `T` where it fits.","+","+## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)","+","+LongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒","+`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,","+`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.","+","+## Verification","+","+1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.","+2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to","+   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).","+3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best","+   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds","+   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.","+4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the","+   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect","+   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.","+","+## Reuse","+- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.","+- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.","+- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.","+- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.","+- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"52a8d368-6353-475c-8255-8045d539bb3b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
