{"parentUuid":"50a36f4b-3623-42e4-a6bc-beb933a6a493","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda2CvjHK83Gdtm2bJkuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a sharp critique — the CREAM-composition coupling is a real instance of the exact bug class this project hardened before, and the resident-evaluator feasibility point is important. Let me fold all of it into the plan."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2816,"cache_read_input_tokens":487957,"output_tokens":4011,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2816,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4011,"cache_read_input_tokens":487957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2816},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda2Cr3zbsY9bciqa9uAY","type":"assistant","uuid":"372a3fcc-47dc-474e-a383-66f5988d71b7","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:36.542Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"372a3fcc-47dc-474e-a383-66f5988d71b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda2CvjHK83Gdtm2bJkuz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","old_string":"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.","new_string":"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly.\n\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \"two values must agree\" bug).**\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\n\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \"continuity\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2816,"cache_read_input_tokens":487957,"output_tokens":4011,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2816,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4011,"cache_read_input_tokens":487957,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2816},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda2Cr3zbsY9bciqa9uAY","type":"assistant","uuid":"9291c170-5139-4dc6-9737-8058cee88d78","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:47.783Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9291c170-5139-4dc6-9737-8058cee88d78","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"f2335b7a-e598-4c2e-b23b-318ca681e56b","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:48.850Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.","newString":"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly.\n\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \"two values must agree\" bug).**\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\n\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \"continuity\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.","originalFile":"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\n\n## Context\n\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\n\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\n```\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\n```\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\n\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\n\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\n\n## Non-destructive invariant\n\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\n\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\n\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\n\n## Approach\n\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\n\n## Files to change\n\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\n   ```\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\n   ```\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\n\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \"\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\n\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\n\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\n\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\n\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\n\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\n  fine-tune → final.\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\n\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\n\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\n\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\n\n## Reuse\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":71,"oldLines":8,"newStart":71,"newLines":26,"lines":["      gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.","    - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the","      *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs","-     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.","+     the cache directly."," ","+   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \"two values must agree\" bug).**","+   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =","+   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at","+   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land","+   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix","+   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at","+   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have","+   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with","+   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and","+   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache","+   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-","+   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.","+","+   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length","+   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \"continuity\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region","+   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head","+   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.","+"," 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode","    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:","    - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5544d67a-7d38-4236-8f39-55765c75f52b","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"f2335b7a-e598-4c2e-b23b-318ca681e56b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"newString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":71,\"oldLines\":8,\"newStart\":71,\"newLines\":26,\"lines\":[\"      gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\",\"    - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\",\"      *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\",\"-     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"+     the cache directly.\",\" \",\"+   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\",\"+   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\",\"+   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\",\"+   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\",\"+   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\",\"+   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\",\"+   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\",\"+   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\",\"+   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\",\"+   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\",\"+   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\",\"+   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\",\"+\",\"+   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\",\"+   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\",\"+   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\",\"+   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"+\",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"    - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj\",\"duration_ms\":8}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":31},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cca10002-a7c1-4b0a-931a-4b20938710e0","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:47.878Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"cca10002-a7c1-4b0a-931a-4b20938710e0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"newString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":71,\"oldLines\":8,\"newStart\":71,\"newLines\":26,\"lines\":[\"      gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\",\"    - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\",\"      *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\",\"-     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"+     the cache directly.\",\" \",\"+   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\",\"+   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\",\"+   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\",\"+   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\",\"+   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\",\"+   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\",\"+   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\",\"+   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\",\"+   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\",\"+   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\",\"+   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\",\"+   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\",\"+\",\"+   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\",\"+   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\",\"+   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\",\"+   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"+\",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"    - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj\",\"duration_ms\":8}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":45},"type":"attachment","uuid":"801f0fc6-8852-44bc-912f-3dd9f33a7c4d","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:47.892Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"801f0fc6-8852-44bc-912f-3dd9f33a7c4d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"new_string\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"newString\":\"   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":71,\"oldLines\":8,\"newStart\":71,\"newLines\":26,\"lines\":[\"      gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\",\"    - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\",\"      *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\",\"-     the cache directly. Assert a sane combination at startup.\",\"+     the cache directly.\",\" \",\"+   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\",\"+   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\",\"+   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\",\"+   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\",\"+   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\",\"+   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\",\"+   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\",\"+   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\",\"+   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\",\"+   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\",\"+   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\",\"+   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\",\"+\",\"+   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\",\"+   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\",\"+   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\",\"+   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\",\"+\",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"    - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01G9RgDjNFA8huQ4spe2jHVj\",\"duration_ms\":8}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":49},"type":"attachment","uuid":"215157ed-b4d5-4ae2-9b51-51bdd9a52281","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:02:47.896Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"215157ed-b4d5-4ae2-9b51-51bdd9a52281","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda2H3beAWkxksk3s13NE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","old_string":"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.","new_string":"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4097,"cache_read_input_tokens":490773,"output_tokens":1382,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4097,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1382,"cache_read_input_tokens":490773,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4097,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4097},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda2GuJZwQt41Ps9PoUrG","type":"assistant","uuid":"f804b5c6-5dfc-4157-b04e-2736d2e3fe2c","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:07.714Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
