(monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":93,"oldLines":15,"newStart":93,"newLines":23,"lines":[" "," 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode","    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:","-   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.","+   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,","+     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.","    - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).","    - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with","-     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.","+     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where","+     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =","+     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and","+     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.","    - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.","    - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.","-   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`","-     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.","-   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.","+   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).","+     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor","+     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.","+   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.","+   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.","+     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.","+   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`)."," "," 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:","    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc46aed7-a242-442c-9657-1a650ab582b6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c4f6c5ad-9a8b-4635-b1ef-f6ff5084bd3d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"new_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"newString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":93,\"oldLines\":15,\"newStart\":93,\"newLines\":23,\"lines\":[\" \",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"-   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\",\"+   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\",\"+     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\",\"    - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\",\"    - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\",\"-     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"+     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\",\"+     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\",\"+     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\",\"+     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"    - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\",\"    - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\",\"-   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\",\"-     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\",\"-   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"+   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\",\"+     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\",\"+     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\",\"+   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\",\"+   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\",\"+     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"+   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":28},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b85a4756-644a-4904-b2aa-441ae97614b0","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:07.787Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b85a4756-644a-4904-b2aa-441ae97614b0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"new_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"newString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":93,\"oldLines\":15,\"newStart\":93,\"newLines\":23,\"lines\":[\" \",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"-   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\",\"+   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\",\"+     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\",\"    - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\",\"    - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\",\"-     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"+     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\",\"+     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\",\"+     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\",\"+     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"    - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\",\"    - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\",\"-   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\",\"-     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\",\"-   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"+   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\",\"+     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\",\"+     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\",\"+   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\",\"+   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\",\"+     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"+   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":37},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9ca1ca15-30a9-419b-89ef-01055ddacf1d","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:07.796Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9ca1ca15-30a9-419b-89ef-01055ddacf1d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"new_string\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"newString\":\"   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\\n     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":93,\"oldLines\":15,\"newStart\":93,\"newLines\":23,\"lines\":[\" \",\" 3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\",\"    already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\",\"-   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,…,256}.\",\"+   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\",\"+     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\",\"    - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\",\"    - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\",\"-     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; `λ_NTK` from the NTK base-scaled freqs. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"+     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\",\"+     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\",\"+     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\",\"+     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\",\"    - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\",\"    - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\",\"-   - **Fitness** = write `λ,n̂` file → run `CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=cand … CP_EVAL_OUT=cand.csv`\",\"-     → overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the CSV. Memoize identical genomes.\",\"-   - Output `longrope_best.txt`.\",\"+   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\",\"+     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\",\"+     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\",\"+   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\",\"+   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\",\"+     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"+   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01JLpij6NSB4rgKF1SZaMmDs\",\"duration_ms\":2}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b7467461-2e9a-4d80-a9be-ce74ed318802","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:07.806Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b7467461-2e9a-4d80-a9be-ce74ed318802","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda2JT2KdmkdjN3q8MeUf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1444,"cache_read_input_tokens":494870,"output_tokens":1166,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":494870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda2JNRkNaC4dCgFZfzXX","type":"assistant","uuid":"5676bcfa-8116-4408-865e-6c181858b931","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:18.528Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"5676bcfa-8116-4408-865e-6c181858b931","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cda2JT2KdmkdjN3q8MeUf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","old_string":"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**","new_string":"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\n\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1444,"cache_read_input_tokens":494870,"output_tokens":1166,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1166,"cache_read_input_tokens":494870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Cda2JNRkNaC4dCgFZfzXX","type":"assistant","uuid":"b61b079e-092e-40a4-bcfc-1c0fd9f12ca6","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:26.632Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b61b079e-092e-40a4-bcfc-1c0fd9f12ca6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"1695c3b5-acd1-49fb-be50-8c0bd1fd82ac","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:27.687Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md","oldString":"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**","newString":"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\n\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\n\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":111,"oldLines":6,"newStart":111,"newLines":19,"lines":["      Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.","    - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`)."," ","+   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness","+   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call","+   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the","+   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE","+   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval","+   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`","+   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the","+   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch","+   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that","+   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,","+   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at","+   full `P=64,iters=40`.","+"," 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:","    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the","    PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d2d01dfd-edd8-459f-b03a-dd5d552875c9","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"1695c3b5-acd1-49fb-be50-8c0bd1fd82ac","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"new_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"newString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":111,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":111,\"newLines\":19,\"lines\":[\"      Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"    - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\"+   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\",\"+   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\",\"+   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\",\"+   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\",\"+   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\",\"+   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\",\"+   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\",\"+   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\",\"+   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\",\"+   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\",\"+   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\",\"+   full `P=64,iters=40`.\",\"+\",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\",\"    PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB\",\"duration_ms\":4}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:format\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-format.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":20},"type":"attachment","uuid":"87eee613-fb54-46c2-a695-718a1cdd2925","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:26.704Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"87eee613-fb54-46c2-a695-718a1cdd2925","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"new_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"newString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":111,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":111,\"newLines\":19,\"lines\":[\"      Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"    - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\"+   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\",\"+   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\",\"+   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\",\"+   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\",\"+   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\",\"+   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\",\"+   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\",\"+   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\",\"+   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\",\"+   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\",\"+   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\",\"+   full `P=64,iters=40`.\",\"+\",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\",\"    PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB\",\"duration_ms\":4}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:console-warn\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-console-warn.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":35},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0055e767-1d89-495c-8db4-d3031297ce7e","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:26.719Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"0055e767-1d89-495c-8db4-d3031297ce7e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Edit","toolUseID":"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"350f98d5-0fdc-48d0-b9d0-afd0f61ec876\",\"permission_mode\":\"plan\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"PostToolUse\",\"tool_name\":\"Edit\",\"tool_input\":{\"file_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"old_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"new_string\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"replace_all\":false},\"tool_response\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/plans/polished-cuddling-graham.md\",\"oldString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"newString\":\"   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\\n   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\\n   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\\n   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\\n   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\\n   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\\n   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\\n   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\\n   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\\n   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\\n   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\\n   full `P=64,iters=40`.\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`**\",\"originalFile\":\"# Plan: Implement LongRoPE (searched non-uniform RoPE) in bluscriptCP\\n\\n## Context\\n\\nWe have YaRN (fixed-formula frequency interpolation) and CREAM (position-relabel training) working\\nin `bluscriptCP`. **LongRoPE** (Ding et al. 2024, arXiv:2402.13753) is the next rung: instead of a\\n*fixed* per-dimension interpolation formula, it **searches** for the best per-dimension rescale\\nfactors `λ_i` plus an initial-token threshold `n̂`, using perplexity as the objective. It's the\\ncurrent SOTA cache-only method (extended LLaMA/Mistral to 2M tokens). Goal: add it as another\\ncontext-extension arm on the existing PPL-vs-position rig, comparable to YaRN and CREAM.\\n\\nRescale formula (Eq. 3), position `n`, dim `i`, pure RoPE freq `base_freq_i = base^(-2i/d)`:\\n```\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i              if n <  n̂    (initial tokens: original RoPE)\\nangle(n,i) = n · base_freq_i / λ_i        if n >= n̂    (rescaled: λ_i divides the freq)\\n```\\n`λ_i ≥ 1` monotone non-decreasing across dims. LongRoPE does **not** use YaRN's `m` temperature.\\n\\n**User-chosen scope:** full **progressive** multi-stage recipe; fitness = **overall PPL** (all positions).\\n\\nThe search (`λ, n̂`) is **training-free** (forward-only PPL); the recipe adds fine-tuning stages.\\n\\n## Non-destructive invariant\\n\\nEverything gated behind a new env `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=<file>`. Unset ⇒ **byte-identical** to today.\\nNew C++ function is *separate* from `build_rope_cache` (YaRN untouched); mirror the exact additive\\ngating used for `CP_CREAM_MODE`.\\n\\n## Ground truth (verified — reuse, don't reinvent)\\n\\n- **`build_rope_cache`** — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp:47`. `[seq_len, head_dim]` fp32, **NeoX\\n  half-split**: cos in cols `[0, hd/2)`, sin in `[hd/2, hd)`; `inv_freq[i] = base_freq_i·((ramp_i/s)\\n  + (1−ramp_i))`; `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` multiplied into cos & sin at **all** positions. Built on CPU\\n  then `.to(device)`, grad-free. `ramp` from `find_correction_range` (lines 67–78).\\n- **CREAM install pattern** — `bluscriptCP.cpp`: `cream_full_cache_` member (334), built when on\\n  (367–371); `install_cream_positions` gathers rows and fans `set_rope_cache` to every layer\\n  (432–459); `set_rope_cache` in `ContextParallel.h:324` (grad-free assert). Gating pattern at\\n  627–655 (env→cfg→`bool xxx_on`→`if (xxx_on)`), install gated at train (1438) and eval (1305).\\n- **CP_EVAL_PPL** — CSV columns `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl` (`ppl = exp(mean_nll)`), file via\\n  `CP_EVAL_OUT`, requires `cp_size==1`. This is the search **fitness** source.\\n\\n## Approach\\n\\nLongRoPE cache is applied exactly where YaRN's is; the novelty is an offline **GA search** that\\npicks the cache, using the existing `CP_EVAL_PPL` binary as the fitness function. On a single GPU we\\n**compose LongRoPE with CREAM** for the fine-tune stages (see Memory note) so training stays cheap.\\n\\n## Files to change\\n\\n1. **`context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`** — ADD `build_rope_cache_longrope(seq_len, head_dim, base,\\n   const std::vector<float>& lambda, int64_t n_hat, device)`. Separate from `build_rope_cache`.\\n   ```\\n   for n in [0,seq_len): for i in [0,hd/2):\\n       base_freq = pow(base, -2i/hd)\\n       scale     = (n < n_hat) ? 1.0 : lambda[i]      // λ divides the freq\\n       ang       = n * base_freq / scale\\n       cache[n][i]        = cos(ang)                   // NeoX half-split, NO m\\n       cache[n][i+hd/2]   = sin(ang)\\n   return cache.to(device)   // grad-free\\n   ```\\n   Match the YaRN layout exactly. Declare in the corresponding header.\\n\\n2. **`Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp`** — additive gating mirroring CREAM:\\n   - Config: `std::string longrope_factors = \\\"\\\";` (`CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS`). `const bool longrope_on\\n     = !longrope_factors.empty();`\\n   - Parse the factors file → `std::vector<float> lambda` (len `head_dim/2`) + `int64_t n_hat`.\\n   - Startup asserts: file exists, `|lambda|==head_dim/2`, monotone non-decreasing, `λ_i≥1`.\\n   - When on, build the RoPE cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope(CP_T, head_dim, rope_theta,\\n     lambda, n_hat, dev)` and install it (either as the base `cos_sin_cache` passed to layers, or —\\n     preferred for cheap training — as `cream_full_cache_` so a CREAM short-physical fine-tune\\n     gathers from the LongRoPE cache). Default path untouched when off.\\n   - **v1 exclusivity:** if both `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` and `CP_CREAM_MODE≠off` are set, that's the\\n     *composition* path (LongRoPE cache as CREAM's gather source); otherwise LongRoPE alone installs\\n     the cache directly.\\n\\n   **CRITICAL — CREAM-composition coupling (fixes a recurring \\\"two values must agree\\\" bug).**\\n   CREAM's label generator places its tail block at `scaled_max = factor·T` with `factor =\\n   YARN_SCALE` (hardened invariant from the CREAM plan). If we gather from a LongRoPE cache built at\\n   some independent `T_stage`, CREAM's labels can index **past** the cache rows, or worse land\\n   in-bounds at rows the search never tuned for — a silent, plausible-loss wrong result. **Fix\\n   (reuse, don't decouple):** in the composition path the LongRoPE cache MUST be built at\\n   `seq_len = cfg.cream_scaled_max` (i.e. `factor·T`), and the search that produced `λ,n̂` MUST have\\n   targeted that same length. Add startup asserts: `build_rope_cache_longrope` is called with\\n   `seq_len == cream_scaled_max`; the factors file records the search target length `S_search` and\\n   we assert `S_search == cream_scaled_max` and the grid's `s == factor`. This ties LongRoPE's cache\\n   length to CREAM's already-derived `scaled_max` rather than introducing a second knob. LongRoPE-\\n   alone (no CREAM) builds at `CP_T` and installs directly — no coupling.\\n\\n   **Interaction note (intentional, not a bug):** when composing, if CREAM's head-block length\\n   exceeds LongRoPE's `n̂`, some CREAM \\\"continuity\\\" head tokens fall in LongRoPE's *rescaled* region\\n   instead of its preserved region. Document this; pick `n̂ ≥ cream_head_len` if you want the head\\n   fully preserved, or accept it deliberately.\\n\\n3. **NEW `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py`** — the GA driver (offline, no CUDA). Full pseudocode\\n   already in `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`; key points:\\n   - Genome = `λ` (len `head_dim/2`, grid `[1, s·1.25]` step 0.01 — bound **verified from Table 4**,\\n     not just the summary) + `n̂` ∈ {0,1,2,4,8,12,16,20,24,28,32,64,128,256}.\\n   - Params: `P=64, N₁=16, N₂=16, iters=40, top-k=32, p_mut=0.3` (halve P/N for >512k).\\n   - **Seeds** (port the YARNOps math): `λ_PI[i]=s`; `λ_YaRN[i]=1/((ramp_i/s)+(1−ramp_i))` with\\n     `ramp` from `find_correction_range`; **`λ_NTK[i] = base_freq_i / ntk_inv_freq_i`** where\\n     `ntk_inv_freq_i = (base·s^(d/(d−2)))^(−2i/d)` — closed form simplifies to `λ_NTK[i] =\\n     s^(2i/(d−2))` (monotone increasing, `λ_NTK[0]=1`); use the ratio form to avoid a sign slip and\\n     confirm gen-0 PPL matches a known NTK run. + `P−3` mutated.\\n   - **Mutation** = per-dim **resample from grid at p=0.3** (not a jitter), then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **Crossover** = per-dim pick from either parent, then `repair_monotone`.\\n   - **`repair_monotone` = forward running-max clamp** `λ_i ← max(λ_i, λ_{i−1})` (then grid-snap).\\n     **NEVER `sort(λ)`** — a sort is monotone but scrambles which frequency dim gets which factor\\n     (semantically wrong while passing every structural check). This must be explicit in the code.\\n   - **Fitness** = overall PPL `= exp(Σ mean_nll·count / Σ count)` from the `CP_EVAL_PPL` CSV.\\n   - **Memoize on discretized grid INDICES**, not raw floats: key = `(tuple(round((λ_i−1)/0.01)), n̂)`.\\n     Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\\n   - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\\n\\n4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\\n   `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\\n   PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\\n\\n5. **`Makefile`** — add `cream-cache-parity`-style targets: `cp-rope-longrope` (parity) and a\\n   `longrope-search` convenience target.\\n\\n6. **`README.md`** — `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` section + factors-file format (line 1 = `n_hat`, then\\n   `head_dim/2` floats), and the progressive workflow.\\n\\n## Progressive pipeline (multi-stage, adapted to the 48M / single-GPU scale)\\n\\n- **Stage A (intermediate):** search at `T1` (e.g. 16k) on the base ckpt → `λ1,n̂1`; **fine-tune**\\n  the base with that cache (reuse `CP_REWARMUP`/`CP_REWARMUP_PEAK`) → `ckpt_ext1`.\\n- **Stage B (target):** search at `T2` (e.g. 64k) on `ckpt_ext1` → `λ2,n̂2`; optionally a light\\n  fine-tune → final.\\n- **Stage C (recovery, optional):** 4k/8k search with reduced max-`λ` → restore short-ctx PPL.\\n\\n**Memory note (important):** LongRoPE's fine-tune (Stages A/B) is at the *long* physical length —\\nreal `T×T` attention, which single-GPU can't hold much past ~16–32k (the logits ceiling you hit in\\nthe CREAM eval). Two options: (a) run those fine-tunes under CP (multi-GPU), or (b) **compose with\\nCREAM** — build `cream_full_cache_` via `build_rope_cache_longrope` so the fine-tune runs at 4k\\nphysical while gathering the searched cache. (b) is recommended on the 3060. The *search* itself is\\nforward-only but still processes length-`T` sequences → same single-GPU ceiling; run the long-`T`\\nsearch under CP or cap `T` where it fits.\\n\\n## Seed math to port (YaRN→λ equivalence)\\n\\nLongRoPE `inv_freq = base_freq/λ_i`; YaRN `inv_freq = base_freq·((ramp/s)+(1−ramp))` ⇒\\n`λ_YaRN[i] = 1 / ((ramp_i/s) + (1−ramp_i))`. `λ_PI[i]=s` (ramp=1 everywhere). Compute `ramp_i`,\\n`low`, `high` exactly as `find_correction_range` in `YARNOps.cpp:67-78`.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n1. **Parity:** `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — `λ=1,n̂=0`≡plain RoPE; `λ=s`≡PI. PASS.\\n2. **Off-mode regression:** `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` unset ⇒ training + `CP_EVAL_PPL` byte-identical to\\n   current (compare a short run's loss/CSV before vs after).\\n3. **Search smoke:** tiny `P`/iters on the 48M base at a length that fits (e.g. 8k) — confirm best\\n   `λ` stays monotone, `n̂` in-set, and best PPL is **non-increasing** across generations; seeds\\n   (PI/YaRN) reproduce their known PPL as generation-0 baselines.\\n4. **End-to-end arm:** run Stage A search+fine-tune, then eval the LongRoPE arm at the target on the\\n   PPL-vs-position rig; overlay in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` with `{naive, YaRN-LCE, CREAM}`. Expect\\n   LongRoPE ≤ YaRN on the flat floor.\\n\\n## Reuse\\n- `build_rope_cache` + `find_correction_range` — `context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp`.\\n- `set_rope_cache` / `cream_full_cache_` gather-install — `ContextParallel.h`, `bluscriptCP.cpp`.\\n- `CP_EVAL_PPL` (fitness) + `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` (overlay) — existing.\\n- Parity harness — `Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`, `Tests/cp_rope_fused_parity.cpp`.\\n- Detailed algorithm + full pseudocode — `.mdfiles/LongRoPEexplanasion.md`.\\n\",\"structuredPatch\":[{\"oldStart\":111,\"oldLines\":6,\"newStart\":111,\"newLines\":19,\"lines\":[\"      Float-equality keys silently miss hits on genomes reached via different accumulation paths.\",\"    - Output `longrope_best.txt` (records `λ`, `n̂`, and the search target length `S_search`).\",\" \",\"+   **Search feasibility — MUST decide before writing the driver.** `P=64 × 40 iters ≈ 2560` fitness\",\"+   calls (minus memoized hits), each over a length-`T` sequence (up to 64k at Stage B). If each call\",\"+   is a fresh `CP_EVAL_PPL` subprocess that **reloads the checkpoint and re-inits the model**, the\",\"+   search dominates the whole project's cost. The model load is the expensive part; the LongRoPE\",\"+   cache rebuild is a cheap CPU loop. **Decision: add a resident search-evaluator mode** to the eval\",\"+   binary (`CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1`): load ckpt + model **once**, then loop — read a candidate `(λ,n̂)`\",\"+   file, rebuild ONLY the cache via `build_rope_cache_longrope` + `set_rope_cache`, run the\",\"+   forward-only PPL on the calibration windows, emit overall PPL, repeat (candidates fed via a watch\",\"+   dir / fifo / stdin). The Python GA becomes the controller; no per-candidate model reload. If that\",\"+   mode is out of scope for v1, explicitly cap the search (small `P`/iters, short calibration `T`,\",\"+   aggressive memoization) and log the cost tradeoff — do not silently ship subprocess-per-genome at\",\"+   full `P=64,iters=40`.\",\"+\",\" 4. **NEW `Tests/cp_rope_longrope_parity.cpp`** — mirror `cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp`:\",\"    `λ_i=1,n̂=0` ⇒ cache == plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ_i=s,n̂=0` ⇒ == PI (`build_rope_cache` with the\",\"    PI-equivalent). Confirms the divide-by-λ sign, the NeoX layout, and the `n̂` threshold.\"]}],\"userModified\":false,\"replaceAll\":false},\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01MRqrPB5JthvZJkTZJQVSXB\",\"duration_ms\":4}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"post:edit:typecheck\" \"scripts/hooks/post-edit-typecheck.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":46},"type":"attachment","uuid":"def9ee8f-d88d-456b-8287-3e1e35462ced","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:26.730Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"def9ee8f-d88d-456b-8287-3e1e35462ced","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"todo_reminder","content":[{"content":"Create context_parallel/CreamPositions.h (3-layer: math, range/CDF, sampling wrapper) + PoSE/RandPos","status":"completed","activeForm":"Creating CreamPositions.h"},{"content":"Write Tests/cream_positions_test.cpp (golden math, range/CDF, structural, randint, PoSE/RandPos) and run RED->GREEN","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing cream_positions_test.cpp"},{"content":"Add set_rope_cache setter to context_parallel/ContextParallel.h (additive, grad-free assert)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Adding set_rope_cache setter"},{"content":"Integrate into Scripts/Blutrain/bluscriptCP.cpp (config/env, asserts, cream_full_cache_, gated guard, per-step install, eval path)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Integrating CREAM into bluscriptCP.cpp"},{"content":"Write Tests/cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp (gather==direct RoPE + YaRN spot-check), wire Makefile","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing cream_cache_gather_parity.cpp"},{"content":"Document CP_CREAM_* env vars in README.md","status":"completed","activeForm":"Documenting in README.md"},{"content":"Build bluscript-cp with CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 (compile-verify integration)","status":"completed","activeForm":"Building bluscript-cp"},{"content":"Verification: parity test, off-mode regression, CREAM smoke run, distribution check","status":"completed","activeForm":"Running verification"},{"content":"Log work to Obsidian Logs.md + write session report","status":"completed","activeForm":"Logging work"}],"itemCount":9},"type":"attachment","uuid":"bcb09c03-b6d0-4527-b945-be35be75bf52","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:03:27.692Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
