{"parentUuid":"ba67f01c-3571-491d-ae3f-7c476006dda5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"5e2595fa-ad58-4dbd-9b87-ff4a7e3e30bb","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UsKrvqN8FhyPTHbYayg3Xg","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\n2\t#include \"autograd/operations/RoPEOps.h\"\n3\t#include \"autograd/backward/RoPEBackward.h\"\n4\t#include \"autograd/AutogradContext.h\"\n5\t#include \"autograd/Variable.h\"\n6\t#include \"autograd/GraphRecorder.h\"\n7\t#include \"checkpointing/GradMode.h\"\n8\t#include \"ops/helpers/RoPEKernels.h\"\n9\t#include \"autograd/ops_template.h\"\n10\t\n11\t#include <stdexcept>\n12\t#include <cmath>\n13\t#include <cstdlib>   // std::getenv, std::atof\n14\t#include <cstdio>    // std::fprintf\n15\t#include \"CPLog.h\"    // cplog::log_rank() — gate one-time notices to rank 0\n16\t#include <string>    // std::to_string\n17\t#include <algorithm> // std::max, std::min\n18\t\n19\tnamespace OwnTensor {\n20\tnamespace autograd {\n21\t\n22\t// ============================================================================\n23\t// build_rope_cache — YaRN (NTK-by-parts + attention temperature) cos/sin cache\n24\t//\n25\t// Canonical HF/Qwen3 YaRN. Extends context (e.g. 1024 -> 8192) by blending\n26\t// per-dimension inverse frequencies (extrapolate high-freq, interpolate low-freq\n27\t// via a dimension-index linear ramp between correction dims) and baking the\n28\t// attention temperature m = 0.1*ln(s)+1 into BOTH cos and sin. RoPE hits both Q\n29\t// and K, so m appears twice in each QK logit (m^2 = 1/t), matching YaRN's\n30\t// softmax temperature; the fused kernel's 1/sqrt(hd) scale is left untouched.\n31\t//\n32\t// Params are hardcoded defaults, each overridable by an env var. Default\n33\t// YARN_SCALE=1.0 reduces this to standard RoPE bit-identically (base_freq/s ==\n34\t// base_freq for all i, and m==1), preserving all existing callers.\n35\t//\n36\t// The cache is always built on CPU (fp32) then copied to the target device: the\n37\t// device kernel rope_build_cache_cuda has no per-dimension frequency hook, so we\n38\t// bypass it. Cost is negligible (built once at model init).\n39\t// ============================================================================\n40\tnamespace {\n41\tinline float yarn_env_f(const char* key, float dflt) {\n42\t    const char* v = std::getenv(key);\n43\t    return v ? static_cast<float>(std::atof(v)) : dflt;\n44\t}\n45\t} // anonymous namespace\n46\t\n47\tTensor build_rope_cache(int64_t seq_len, int64_t head_dim, float base, DeviceIndex device)\n48\t{\n49\t    if (head_dim % 2 != 0) {\n50\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"build_rope_cache: head_dim must be even\");\n51\t    }\n52\t\n53\t    // --- YaRN config (env-overridable; scale=1.0 => standard RoPE) ---\n54\t    const float s      = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_SCALE\",       1.0f);   // target_ctx / original_ctx\n55\t    const float L      = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS\", 1024.0f);// original pretrain context\n56\t    const float b_fast = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_BETA_FAST\",   32.0f);  // \"beta\"  (high-rotation bound)\n57\t    const float b_slow = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_BETA_SLOW\",   1.0f);   // \"alpha\" (low-rotation bound)\n58\t\n59\t    // Attention temperature m (s==1 -> m==1 -> no scaling).\n60\t    const float m = (s > 1.0f) ? (0.1f * std::log(s) + 1.0f) : 1.0f;\n61\t\n62\t    const int64_t half = head_dim / 2;\n63\t\n64\t    // Canonical correction range: linear ramp over dimension index between the\n65\t    // dims where the number of rotations equals b_fast (high-freq end) and\n66\t    // b_slow (low-freq end). Matches HF find_correction_dim/find_correction_range.\n67\t    auto find_dim = [&](float num_rot) {\n68\t        return (static_cast<float>(head_dim)\n69\t                * std::log(L / (num_rot * 2.0f * static_cast<float>(M_PI))))\n70\t               / (2.0f * std::log(base));\n71\t    };\n72\t    int64_t low  = static_cast<int64_t>(std::floor(find_dim(b_fast)));\n73\t    int64_t high = static_cast<int64_t>(std::ceil (find_dim(b_slow)));\n74\t    low  = std::max<int64_t>(low, 0);\n75\t    high = std::min<int64_t>(high, half - 1);   // clamp to half-1: loop indexes [0,half) only;\n76\t                                                // deliberate deviation from HF head_dim-1 -- do not \"fix\"\n77\t    float denom = static_cast<float>(high - low);\n78\t    if (denom <= 0.0f) denom = 1e-3f;           // avoid /0 when low==high\n79\t\n80\t    // (R5) Guard degenerate env input: L/(num_rot*2pi) <= 0 -> log(neg) = NaN.\n81\t    if (s > 1.0f && (!std::isfinite(find_dim(b_fast)) || !std::isfinite(find_dim(b_slow)) || low > high)) {\n82\t        throw std::runtime_error(\n83\t            \"build_rope_cache(YaRN): bad correction range -- check \"\n84\t            \"YARN_BETA_FAST/YARN_BETA_SLOW/YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS (got low=\"\n85\t            + std::to_string(low) + \" high=\" + std::to_string(high) + \")\");\n86\t    }\n87\t\n88\t    // (R2) scale <-> seq_len consistency (warn, don't hard-fail).\n89\t    if (s > 1.0f && std::abs(static_cast<float>(seq_len) - s * L) > 1.0f) {\n90\t        if (cplog::log_rank()) std::fprintf(stderr,\n91\t            \"[YaRN][warn] seq_len(%lld) != scale(%.3f)*orig_maxpos(%.1f)=%.1f \"\n92\t            \"-- cache scaled for a different context than it is sized for\\n\",\n93\t            (long long)seq_len, s, L, s * L);\n94\t    }\n95\t\n96\t    // (R3) Init log: makes the active config + the YARNOps-symbol-wins link\n97\t    // dependency visible. Missing line / scale=1 => silent revert to std RoPE.\n98\t    if (cplog::log_rank()) std::fprintf(stderr,\n99\t        \"[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=%lld hd=%lld scale=%.3f low=%lld high=%lld m=%.4f\\n\",\n100\t        (long long)seq_len, (long long)head_dim, s, (long long)low, (long long)high, m);\n101\t\n102\t    // --- Build on CPU, fill, then copy to device (bypass the CUDA kernel). ---\n103\t    TensorOptions cpu_opts = TensorOptions().with_dtype(Dtype::Float32)\n104\t                                            .with_device(DeviceIndex(Device::CPU));\n105\t    Tensor cpu(Shape{{seq_len, head_dim}}, cpu_opts);\n106\t    float* p = cpu.data<float>();\n107\t\n108\t    for (int64_t pos = 0; pos < seq_len; ++pos) {\n109\t        for (int64_t i = 0; i < half; ++i) {\n110\t            float exponent  = (2.0f * static_cast<float>(i)) / static_cast<float>(head_dim);\n111\t            float base_freq = 1.0f / std::pow(base, exponent);   // extrapolation freq\n112\t\n113\t            float ramp = (static_cast<float>(i) - static_cast<float>(low)) / denom;\n114\t            ramp = ramp < 0.0f ? 0.0f : (ramp > 1.0f ? 1.0f : ramp);\n115\t            // ramp=0 (i<low, high-freq) -> keep base_freq (extrapolate)\n116\t            // ramp=1 (i>high, low-freq) -> base_freq/s   (interpolate)\n117\t            float inv_freq = (base_freq / s) * ramp + base_freq * (1.0f - ramp);\n118\t\n119\t            float angle = static_cast<float>(pos) * inv_freq;\n120\t            p[pos * head_dim + i]        = std::cos(angle) * m;  // bake temperature m\n121\t            p[pos * head_dim + i + half] = std::sin(angle) * m;\n122\t        }\n123\t    }\n124\t\n125\t    cpu.set_requires_grad(false);\n126\t    if (device.device == Device::CUDA) {\n127\t        Tensor cache = cpu.to(device);\n128\t        cache.set_requires_grad(false);\n129\t        return cache;\n130\t    }\n131\t    return cpu;\n132\t}\n133\t\n134\t// ============================================================================\n135\t// rope — separate-tensor forward\n136\t// Operates on x of shape [B, T, H, D]; returns rotated tensor (out-of-place).\n137\t// ============================================================================\n138\tTensor rope(const Tensor& x,\n139\t            const Tensor& cos_sin_cache,\n140\t            bool interleaved,\n141\t            int64_t position_offset)\n142\t{\n143\t    GraphRecordMode::record_forward(\"ROPE: rope\");\n144\t\n145\t    if (x.ndim() != 4) {\n146\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: input must be 4-D [B, T, H, D]\");\n147\t    }\n148\t    if (x.dtype() != Dtype::Float32 || cos_sin_cache.dtype() != Dtype::Float32) {\n149\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: only fp32 is supported in v1\");\n150\t    }\n151\t\n152\t    int64_t B  = x.shape().dims[0];\n153\t    int64_t T  = x.shape().dims[1];\n154\t    int64_t H  = x.shape().dims[2];\n155\t    int64_t D  = x.shape().dims[3];\n156\t    if (D % 2 != 0) throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: head_dim must be even\");\n157\t\n158\t    // Cache is [seq_len, head_dim]; every token's pos = t + position_offset must\n159\t    // index a valid row. Validate before launch so we fail with a clear message\n160\t    // instead of an out-of-bounds device read.\n161\t    int64_t cache_seq_len = cos_sin_cache.shape().dims[0];\n162\t    if (T + position_offset > cache_seq_len) {\n163\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\n164\t            \"rope: T + position_offset (\" + std::to_string(T + position_offset) +\n165\t            \") exceeds cos_sin_cache seq_len (\" + std::to_string(cache_seq_len) +\n166\t            \"); rebuild cache with a larger seq_len\");\n167\t    }\n168\t\n169\t    // Out-of-place: clone input, rotate the clone in place. Clone is\n170\t    // contiguous so strides are simple.\n171\t    Tensor out = x.contiguous().clone();\n172\t\n173\t    int64_t token_stride = H * D;   // contiguous [B,T,H,D]\n174\t    int64_t head_stride  = D;\n175\t\n176\t    if (x.device().device == Device::CUDA) {\n177\t        cuda::rope_forward_cuda(\n178\t            out.data<float>(),\n179\t            /*k=*/nullptr,\n180\t            cos_sin_cache.data<float>(),\n181\t            B, T,\n182\t            cache_seq_len,\n183\t            /*nh_q=*/H, /*nh_k=*/0, D,\n184\t            token_stride, head_stride,\n185\t            /*k_token_stride=*/0, /*k_head_stride=*/0,\n186\t            position_offset,\n187\t            interleaved,\n188\t            /*inverse=*/false);\n189\t    } else {\n190\t        throw std::runtime_error(\"rope: CPU path not yet wired (see RoPE.cpp)\");\n191\t    }\n192\t\n193\t    if (GradMode::is_enabled() && x.requires_grad()) {\n194\t        auto grad_fn = std::make_shared<RoPEBackward>(\n195\t            cos_sin_cache, interleaved, position_offset);\n196\t        grad_fn->set_next_edge(0, get_grad_edge(x));\n197\t        out.set_grad_fn(grad_fn);\n198\t        out.set_requires_grad(true);\n199\t    }\n200\t\n201\t    if (autograd::g_shape_debug) GraphRecordMode::attach_forward_shape(out.shape(), out.dtype());\n202\t    return out;\n203\t}\n204\t\n205\t// ============================================================================\n206\t// rope_packed_qk — packed-QKV forward\n207\t// Rotates Q (heads [0..nh_q)) and K (heads [nh_q..nh_q+nh_k)) of a packed\n208\t// [B, T, (nh_q+nh_k+nh_v)*D] tensor. V slice is copied through untouched.\n209\t// ============================================================================\n210\tTensor rope_packed_qk(const Tensor& qkv,\n211\t                      int64_t nh_q, int64_t nh_k, int64_t nh_v,\n212\t                      int64_t head_dim,\n213\t                      const Tensor& cos_sin_cache,\n214\t                      bool interleaved,\n215\t                      int64_t position_offset)\n216\t{\n217\t    GraphRecordMode::record_forward(\"ROPE: rope_packed_qk\");\n218\t\n219\t    if (qkv.ndim() != 3) {\n220\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: qkv must be 3-D [B, T, C]\");\n221\t    }\n222\t    if (qkv.dtype() != Dtype::Float32 || cos_sin_cache.dtype() != Dtype::Float32) {\n223\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: only fp32 is supported in v1\");\n224\t    }\n225\t    if (head_dim % 2 != 0) throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: head_dim must be even\");\n226\t\n227\t    int64_t B = qkv.shape().dims[0];\n228\t    int64_t T = qkv.shape().dims[1];\n229\t    int64_t C = qkv.shape().dims[2];\n230\t    int64_t expected_C = (nh_q + nh_k + nh_v) * head_dim;\n231\t    if (C != expected_C) {\n232\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: last dim does not match (nh_q+nh_k+nh_v)*head_dim\");\n233\t    }\n234\t\n235\t    // Cache is [seq_len, head_dim]; pos = t + position_offset must index a valid\n236\t    // row. Validate before launch (clear error instead of an OOB device read).\n237\t    int64_t cache_seq_len = cos_sin_cache.shape().dims[0];\n238\t    if (T + position_offset > cache_seq_len) {\n239\t        throw std::invalid_argument(\n240\t            \"rope_packed_qk: T + position_offset (\" + std::to_string(T + position_offset) +\n241\t            \") exceeds cos_sin_cache seq_len (\" + std::to_string(cache_seq_len) +\n242\t            \"); rebuild cache with a larger seq_len\");\n243\t    }\n244\t\n245\t    Tensor out = qkv.contiguous().clone();\n246\t\n247\t    // In packed layout: token stride spans the full Q|K|V row; head stride is D.\n248\t    // Q starts at offset 0; K starts at offset nh_q * head_dim within each token.\n249\t    int64_t token_stride = (nh_q + nh_k + nh_v) * head_dim;\n250\t    int64_t head_stride  = head_dim;\n251\t\n252\t    if (qkv.device().device == Device::CUDA) {\n253\t        float* base = out.data<float>();\n254\t        float* q_ptr = base;\n255\t        float* k_ptr = base + nh_q * head_dim;\n256\t\n257\t        cuda::rope_forward_cuda(\n258\t            q_ptr, k_ptr,\n259\t            cos_sin_cache.data<float>(),\n260\t            B, T,\n261\t            cache_seq_len,\n262\t            nh_q, nh_k, head_dim,\n263\t            token_stride, head_stride,\n264\t            token_stride, head_stride,\n265\t            position_offset,\n266\t            interleaved,\n267\t            /*inverse=*/false);\n268\t    } else {\n269\t        throw std::runtime_error(\"rope_packed_qk: CPU path not yet wired (see RoPE.cpp)\");\n270\t    }\n271\t\n272\t    if (GradMode::is_enabled() && qkv.requires_grad()) {\n273\t        auto grad_fn = std::make_shared<RoPEPackedBackward>(\n274\t            cos_sin_cache, nh_q, nh_k, nh_v, head_dim, interleaved, position_offset);\n275\t        grad_fn->set_next_edge(0, get_grad_edge(qkv));\n276\t        out.set_grad_fn(grad_fn);\n277\t        out.set_requires_grad(true);\n278\t    }\n279\t\n280\t    if (autograd::g_shape_debug) GraphRecordMode::attach_forward_shape(out.shape(), out.dtype());\n281\t    return out;\n282\t}\n283\t\n284\t} // namespace autograd\n285\t} // namespace OwnTensor\n286\t"}]},"uuid":"7d65c5f7-a852-49bc-9811-4f9e00dc9ea0","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.764Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP/context_parallel/YARNOps.cpp","content":"\n#include \"autograd/operations/RoPEOps.h\"\n#include \"autograd/backward/RoPEBackward.h\"\n#include \"autograd/AutogradContext.h\"\n#include \"autograd/Variable.h\"\n#include \"autograd/GraphRecorder.h\"\n#include \"checkpointing/GradMode.h\"\n#include \"ops/helpers/RoPEKernels.h\"\n#include \"autograd/ops_template.h\"\n\n#include <stdexcept>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstdlib>   // std::getenv, std::atof\n#include <cstdio>    // std::fprintf\n#include \"CPLog.h\"    // cplog::log_rank() — gate one-time notices to rank 0\n#include <string>    // std::to_string\n#include <algorithm> // std::max, std::min\n\nnamespace OwnTensor {\nnamespace autograd {\n\n// ============================================================================\n// build_rope_cache — YaRN (NTK-by-parts + attention temperature) cos/sin cache\n//\n// Canonical HF/Qwen3 YaRN. Extends context (e.g. 1024 -> 8192) by blending\n// per-dimension inverse frequencies (extrapolate high-freq, interpolate low-freq\n// via a dimension-index linear ramp between correction dims) and baking the\n// attention temperature m = 0.1*ln(s)+1 into BOTH cos and sin. RoPE hits both Q\n// and K, so m appears twice in each QK logit (m^2 = 1/t), matching YaRN's\n// softmax temperature; the fused kernel's 1/sqrt(hd) scale is left untouched.\n//\n// Params are hardcoded defaults, each overridable by an env var. Default\n// YARN_SCALE=1.0 reduces this to standard RoPE bit-identically (base_freq/s ==\n// base_freq for all i, and m==1), preserving all existing callers.\n//\n// The cache is always built on CPU (fp32) then copied to the target device: the\n// device kernel rope_build_cache_cuda has no per-dimension frequency hook, so we\n// bypass it. Cost is negligible (built once at model init).\n// ============================================================================\nnamespace {\ninline float yarn_env_f(const char* key, float dflt) {\n    const char* v = std::getenv(key);\n    return v ? static_cast<float>(std::atof(v)) : dflt;\n}\n} // anonymous namespace\n\nTensor build_rope_cache(int64_t seq_len, int64_t head_dim, float base, DeviceIndex device)\n{\n    if (head_dim % 2 != 0) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"build_rope_cache: head_dim must be even\");\n    }\n\n    // --- YaRN config (env-overridable; scale=1.0 => standard RoPE) ---\n    const float s      = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_SCALE\",       1.0f);   // target_ctx / original_ctx\n    const float L      = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS\", 1024.0f);// original pretrain context\n    const float b_fast = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_BETA_FAST\",   32.0f);  // \"beta\"  (high-rotation bound)\n    const float b_slow = yarn_env_f(\"YARN_BETA_SLOW\",   1.0f);   // \"alpha\" (low-rotation bound)\n\n    // Attention temperature m (s==1 -> m==1 -> no scaling).\n    const float m = (s > 1.0f) ? (0.1f * std::log(s) + 1.0f) : 1.0f;\n\n    const int64_t half = head_dim / 2;\n\n    // Canonical correction range: linear ramp over dimension index between the\n    // dims where the number of rotations equals b_fast (high-freq end) and\n    // b_slow (low-freq end). Matches HF find_correction_dim/find_correction_range.\n    auto find_dim = [&](float num_rot) {\n        return (static_cast<float>(head_dim)\n                * std::log(L / (num_rot * 2.0f * static_cast<float>(M_PI))))\n               / (2.0f * std::log(base));\n    };\n    int64_t low  = static_cast<int64_t>(std::floor(find_dim(b_fast)));\n    int64_t high = static_cast<int64_t>(std::ceil (find_dim(b_slow)));\n    low  = std::max<int64_t>(low, 0);\n    high = std::min<int64_t>(high, half - 1);   // clamp to half-1: loop indexes [0,half) only;\n                                                // deliberate deviation from HF head_dim-1 -- do not \"fix\"\n    float denom = static_cast<float>(high - low);\n    if (denom <= 0.0f) denom = 1e-3f;           // avoid /0 when low==high\n\n    // (R5) Guard degenerate env input: L/(num_rot*2pi) <= 0 -> log(neg) = NaN.\n    if (s > 1.0f && (!std::isfinite(find_dim(b_fast)) || !std::isfinite(find_dim(b_slow)) || low > high)) {\n        throw std::runtime_error(\n            \"build_rope_cache(YaRN): bad correction range -- check \"\n            \"YARN_BETA_FAST/YARN_BETA_SLOW/YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS (got low=\"\n            + std::to_string(low) + \" high=\" + std::to_string(high) + \")\");\n    }\n\n    // (R2) scale <-> seq_len consistency (warn, don't hard-fail).\n    if (s > 1.0f && std::abs(static_cast<float>(seq_len) - s * L) > 1.0f) {\n        if (cplog::log_rank()) std::fprintf(stderr,\n            \"[YaRN][warn] seq_len(%lld) != scale(%.3f)*orig_maxpos(%.1f)=%.1f \"\n            \"-- cache scaled for a different context than it is sized for\\n\",\n            (long long)seq_len, s, L, s * L);\n    }\n\n    // (R3) Init log: makes the active config + the YARNOps-symbol-wins link\n    // dependency visible. Missing line / scale=1 => silent revert to std RoPE.\n    if (cplog::log_rank()) std::fprintf(stderr,\n        \"[YaRN] build_rope_cache: seq_len=%lld hd=%lld scale=%.3f low=%lld high=%lld m=%.4f\\n\",\n        (long long)seq_len, (long long)head_dim, s, (long long)low, (long long)high, m);\n\n    // --- Build on CPU, fill, then copy to device (bypass the CUDA kernel). ---\n    TensorOptions cpu_opts = TensorOptions().with_dtype(Dtype::Float32)\n                                            .with_device(DeviceIndex(Device::CPU));\n    Tensor cpu(Shape{{seq_len, head_dim}}, cpu_opts);\n    float* p = cpu.data<float>();\n\n    for (int64_t pos = 0; pos < seq_len; ++pos) {\n        for (int64_t i = 0; i < half; ++i) {\n            float exponent  = (2.0f * static_cast<float>(i)) / static_cast<float>(head_dim);\n            float base_freq = 1.0f / std::pow(base, exponent);   // extrapolation freq\n\n            float ramp = (static_cast<float>(i) - static_cast<float>(low)) / denom;\n            ramp = ramp < 0.0f ? 0.0f : (ramp > 1.0f ? 1.0f : ramp);\n            // ramp=0 (i<low, high-freq) -> keep base_freq (extrapolate)\n            // ramp=1 (i>high, low-freq) -> base_freq/s   (interpolate)\n            float inv_freq = (base_freq / s) * ramp + base_freq * (1.0f - ramp);\n\n            float angle = static_cast<float>(pos) * inv_freq;\n            p[pos * head_dim + i]        = std::cos(angle) * m;  // bake temperature m\n            p[pos * head_dim + i + half] = std::sin(angle) * m;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cpu.set_requires_grad(false);\n    if (device.device == Device::CUDA) {\n        Tensor cache = cpu.to(device);\n        cache.set_requires_grad(false);\n        return cache;\n    }\n    return cpu;\n}\n\n// ============================================================================\n// rope — separate-tensor forward\n// Operates on x of shape [B, T, H, D]; returns rotated tensor (out-of-place).\n// ============================================================================\nTensor rope(const Tensor& x,\n            const Tensor& cos_sin_cache,\n            bool interleaved,\n            int64_t position_offset)\n{\n    GraphRecordMode::record_forward(\"ROPE: rope\");\n\n    if (x.ndim() != 4) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: input must be 4-D [B, T, H, D]\");\n    }\n    if (x.dtype() != Dtype::Float32 || cos_sin_cache.dtype() != Dtype::Float32) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: only fp32 is supported in v1\");\n    }\n\n    int64_t B  = x.shape().dims[0];\n    int64_t T  = x.shape().dims[1];\n    int64_t H  = x.shape().dims[2];\n    int64_t D  = x.shape().dims[3];\n    if (D % 2 != 0) throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope: head_dim must be even\");\n\n    // Cache is [seq_len, head_dim]; every token's pos = t + position_offset must\n    // index a valid row. Validate before launch so we fail with a clear message\n    // instead of an out-of-bounds device read.\n    int64_t cache_seq_len = cos_sin_cache.shape().dims[0];\n    if (T + position_offset > cache_seq_len) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\n            \"rope: T + position_offset (\" + std::to_string(T + position_offset) +\n            \") exceeds cos_sin_cache seq_len (\" + std::to_string(cache_seq_len) +\n            \"); rebuild cache with a larger seq_len\");\n    }\n\n    // Out-of-place: clone input, rotate the clone in place. Clone is\n    // contiguous so strides are simple.\n    Tensor out = x.contiguous().clone();\n\n    int64_t token_stride = H * D;   // contiguous [B,T,H,D]\n    int64_t head_stride  = D;\n\n    if (x.device().device == Device::CUDA) {\n        cuda::rope_forward_cuda(\n            out.data<float>(),\n            /*k=*/nullptr,\n            cos_sin_cache.data<float>(),\n            B, T,\n            cache_seq_len,\n            /*nh_q=*/H, /*nh_k=*/0, D,\n            token_stride, head_stride,\n            /*k_token_stride=*/0, /*k_head_stride=*/0,\n            position_offset,\n            interleaved,\n            /*inverse=*/false);\n    } else {\n        throw std::runtime_error(\"rope: CPU path not yet wired (see RoPE.cpp)\");\n    }\n\n    if (GradMode::is_enabled() && x.requires_grad()) {\n        auto grad_fn = std::make_shared<RoPEBackward>(\n            cos_sin_cache, interleaved, position_offset);\n        grad_fn->set_next_edge(0, get_grad_edge(x));\n        out.set_grad_fn(grad_fn);\n        out.set_requires_grad(true);\n    }\n\n    if (autograd::g_shape_debug) GraphRecordMode::attach_forward_shape(out.shape(), out.dtype());\n    return out;\n}\n\n// ============================================================================\n// rope_packed_qk — packed-QKV forward\n// Rotates Q (heads [0..nh_q)) and K (heads [nh_q..nh_q+nh_k)) of a packed\n// [B, T, (nh_q+nh_k+nh_v)*D] tensor. V slice is copied through untouched.\n// ============================================================================\nTensor rope_packed_qk(const Tensor& qkv,\n                      int64_t nh_q, int64_t nh_k, int64_t nh_v,\n                      int64_t head_dim,\n                      const Tensor& cos_sin_cache,\n                      bool interleaved,\n                      int64_t position_offset)\n{\n    GraphRecordMode::record_forward(\"ROPE: rope_packed_qk\");\n\n    if (qkv.ndim() != 3) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: qkv must be 3-D [B, T, C]\");\n    }\n    if (qkv.dtype() != Dtype::Float32 || cos_sin_cache.dtype() != Dtype::Float32) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: only fp32 is supported in v1\");\n    }\n    if (head_dim % 2 != 0) throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: head_dim must be even\");\n\n    int64_t B = qkv.shape().dims[0];\n    int64_t T = qkv.shape().dims[1];\n    int64_t C = qkv.shape().dims[2];\n    int64_t expected_C = (nh_q + nh_k + nh_v) * head_dim;\n    if (C != expected_C) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\"rope_packed_qk: last dim does not match (nh_q+nh_k+nh_v)*head_dim\");\n    }\n\n    // Cache is [seq_len, head_dim]; pos = t + position_offset must index a valid\n    // row. Validate before launch (clear error instead of an OOB device read).\n    int64_t cache_seq_len = cos_sin_cache.shape().dims[0];\n    if (T + position_offset > cache_seq_len) {\n        throw std::invalid_argument(\n            \"rope_packed_qk: T + position_offset (\" + std::to_string(T + position_offset) +\n            \") exceeds cos_sin_cache seq_len (\" + std::to_string(cache_seq_len) +\n            \"); rebuild cache with a larger seq_len\");\n    }\n\n    Tensor out = qkv.contiguous().clone();\n\n    // In packed layout: token stride spans the full Q|K|V row; head stride is D.\n    // Q starts at offset 0; K starts at offset nh_q * head_dim within each token.\n    int64_t token_stride = (nh_q + nh_k + nh_v) * head_dim;\n    int64_t head_stride  = head_dim;\n\n    if (qkv.device().device == Device::CUDA) {\n        float* base = out.data<float>();\n        float* q_ptr = base;\n        float* k_ptr = base + nh_q * head_dim;\n\n        cuda::rope_forward_cuda(\n            q_ptr, k_ptr,\n            cos_sin_cache.data<float>(),\n            B, T,\n            cache_seq_len,\n            nh_q, nh_k, head_dim,\n            token_stride, head_stride,\n            token_stride, head_stride,\n            position_offset,\n            interleaved,\n            /*inverse=*/false);\n    } else {\n        throw std::runtime_error(\"rope_packed_qk: CPU path not yet wired (see RoPE.cpp)\");\n    }\n\n    if (GradMode::is_enabled() && qkv.requires_grad()) {\n        auto grad_fn = std::make_shared<RoPEPackedBackward>(\n            cos_sin_cache, nh_q, nh_k, nh_v, head_dim, interleaved, position_offset);\n        grad_fn->set_next_edge(0, get_grad_edge(qkv));\n        out.set_grad_fn(grad_fn);\n        out.set_requires_grad(true);\n    }\n\n    if (autograd::g_shape_debug) GraphRecordMode::attach_forward_shape(out.shape(), out.dtype());\n    return out;\n}\n\n} // namespace autograd\n} // namespace OwnTensor\n","numLines":286,"startLine":1,"totalLines":286}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b4edd323-3cf5-415a-8f31-f1c59fc14727","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"7d65c5f7-a852-49bc-9811-4f9e00dc9ea0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/security.md","content":{"path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/security.md","type":"User","content":"# C++ Security\n\n> This file extends [common/security.md](../common/security.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Memory Safety\n\n- Never use raw `new`/`delete` — use smart pointers\n- Never use C-style arrays — use `std::array` or `std::vector`\n- Never use `malloc`/`free` — use C++ allocation\n- Avoid `reinterpret_cast` unless absolutely necessary\n\n## Buffer Overflows\n\n- Use `std::string` over `char*`\n- Use `.at()` for bounds-checked access when safety matters\n- Never use `strcpy`, `strcat`, `sprintf` — use `std::string` or `fmt::format`\n\n## Undefined Behavior\n\n- Always initialize variables\n- Avoid signed integer overflow\n- Never dereference null or dangling pointers\n- Use sanitizers in CI:\n  ```bash\n  cmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address,undefined\" ..\n  ```\n\n## Static Analysis\n\n- Use **clang-tidy** for automated checks:\n  ```bash\n  clang-tidy --checks='*' src/*.cpp\n  ```\n- Use **cppcheck** for additional analysis:\n  ```bash\n  cppcheck --enable=all src/\n  ```\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for detailed security guidelines.\n","globs":["**/*.cpp","**/*.hpp","**/*.cc","**/*.hh","**/*.cxx","**/*.h","**/CMakeLists.txt"],"contentDiffersFromDisk":true,"rawContent":"---\npaths:\n  - \"**/*.cpp\"\n  - \"**/*.hpp\"\n  - \"**/*.cc\"\n  - \"**/*.hh\"\n  - \"**/*.cxx\"\n  - \"**/*.h\"\n  - \"**/CMakeLists.txt\"\n---\n# C++ Security\n\n> This file extends [common/security.md](../common/security.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Memory Safety\n\n- Never use raw `new`/`delete` — use smart pointers\n- Never use C-style arrays — use `std::array` or `std::vector`\n- Never use `malloc`/`free` — use C++ allocation\n- Avoid `reinterpret_cast` unless absolutely necessary\n\n## Buffer Overflows\n\n- Use `std::string` over `char*`\n- Use `.at()` for bounds-checked access when safety matters\n- Never use `strcpy`, `strcat`, `sprintf` — use `std::string` or `fmt::format`\n\n## Undefined Behavior\n\n- Always initialize variables\n- Avoid signed integer overflow\n- Never dereference null or dangling pointers\n- Use sanitizers in CI:\n  ```bash\n  cmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address,undefined\" ..\n  ```\n\n## Static Analysis\n\n- Use **clang-tidy** for automated checks:\n  ```bash\n  clang-tidy --checks='*' src/*.cpp\n  ```\n- Use **cppcheck** for additional analysis:\n  ```bash\n  cppcheck --enable=all src/\n  ```\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for detailed security guidelines.\n"},"displayPath":"../.claude/rules/cpp/security.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"487886bb-d908-4889-a6a1-7db0a93e418e","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.843Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"487886bb-d908-4889-a6a1-7db0a93e418e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/hooks.md","content":{"path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/hooks.md","type":"User","content":"# C++ Hooks\n\n> This file extends [common/hooks.md](../common/hooks.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Build Hooks\n\nRun these checks before committing C++ changes:\n\n```bash\n# Format check\nclang-format --dry-run --Werror src/*.cpp src/*.hpp\n\n# Static analysis\nclang-tidy src/*.cpp -- -std=c++17\n\n# Build\ncmake --build build\n\n# Tests\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n\n## Recommended CI Pipeline\n\n1. **clang-format** — formatting check\n2. **clang-tidy** — static analysis\n3. **cppcheck** — additional analysis\n4. **cmake build** — compilation\n5. **ctest** — test execution with sanitizers\n","globs":["**/*.cpp","**/*.hpp","**/*.cc","**/*.hh","**/*.cxx","**/*.h","**/CMakeLists.txt"],"contentDiffersFromDisk":true,"rawContent":"---\npaths:\n  - \"**/*.cpp\"\n  - \"**/*.hpp\"\n  - \"**/*.cc\"\n  - \"**/*.hh\"\n  - \"**/*.cxx\"\n  - \"**/*.h\"\n  - \"**/CMakeLists.txt\"\n---\n# C++ Hooks\n\n> This file extends [common/hooks.md](../common/hooks.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Build Hooks\n\nRun these checks before committing C++ changes:\n\n```bash\n# Format check\nclang-format --dry-run --Werror src/*.cpp src/*.hpp\n\n# Static analysis\nclang-tidy src/*.cpp -- -std=c++17\n\n# Build\ncmake --build build\n\n# Tests\nctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n\n## Recommended CI Pipeline\n\n1. **clang-format** — formatting check\n2. **clang-tidy** — static analysis\n3. **cppcheck** — additional analysis\n4. **cmake build** — compilation\n5. **ctest** — test execution with sanitizers\n"},"displayPath":"../.claude/rules/cpp/hooks.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"08ed3974-ea2a-454b-b260-e37c8890a0e0","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.843Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"08ed3974-ea2a-454b-b260-e37c8890a0e0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/coding-style.md","content":{"path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/coding-style.md","type":"User","content":"# C++ Coding Style\n\n> This file extends [common/coding-style.md](../common/coding-style.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Modern C++ (C++17/20/23)\n\n- Prefer **modern C++ features** over C-style constructs\n- Use `auto` when the type is obvious from context\n- Use `constexpr` for compile-time constants\n- Use structured bindings: `auto [key, value] = map_entry;`\n\n## Resource Management\n\n- **RAII everywhere** — no manual `new`/`delete`\n- Use `std::unique_ptr` for exclusive ownership\n- Use `std::shared_ptr` only when shared ownership is truly needed\n- Use `std::make_unique` / `std::make_shared` over raw `new`\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- Types/Classes: `PascalCase`\n- Functions/Methods: `snake_case` or `camelCase` (follow project convention)\n- Constants: `kPascalCase` or `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`\n- Namespaces: `lowercase`\n- Member variables: `snake_case_` (trailing underscore) or `m_` prefix\n\n## Formatting\n\n- Use **clang-format** — no style debates\n- Run `clang-format -i <file>` before committing\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for comprehensive C++ coding standards and guidelines.\n","globs":["**/*.cpp","**/*.hpp","**/*.cc","**/*.hh","**/*.cxx","**/*.h","**/CMakeLists.txt"],"contentDiffersFromDisk":true,"rawContent":"---\npaths:\n  - \"**/*.cpp\"\n  - \"**/*.hpp\"\n  - \"**/*.cc\"\n  - \"**/*.hh\"\n  - \"**/*.cxx\"\n  - \"**/*.h\"\n  - \"**/CMakeLists.txt\"\n---\n# C++ Coding Style\n\n> This file extends [common/coding-style.md](../common/coding-style.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Modern C++ (C++17/20/23)\n\n- Prefer **modern C++ features** over C-style constructs\n- Use `auto` when the type is obvious from context\n- Use `constexpr` for compile-time constants\n- Use structured bindings: `auto [key, value] = map_entry;`\n\n## Resource Management\n\n- **RAII everywhere** — no manual `new`/`delete`\n- Use `std::unique_ptr` for exclusive ownership\n- Use `std::shared_ptr` only when shared ownership is truly needed\n- Use `std::make_unique` / `std::make_shared` over raw `new`\n\n## Naming Conventions\n\n- Types/Classes: `PascalCase`\n- Functions/Methods: `snake_case` or `camelCase` (follow project convention)\n- Constants: `kPascalCase` or `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`\n- Namespaces: `lowercase`\n- Member variables: `snake_case_` (trailing underscore) or `m_` prefix\n\n## Formatting\n\n- Use **clang-format** — no style debates\n- Run `clang-format -i <file>` before committing\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for comprehensive C++ coding standards and guidelines.\n"},"displayPath":"../.claude/rules/cpp/coding-style.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ec6ec564-ba3d-4aa9-a5e1-b9b87740b43f","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.844Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ec6ec564-ba3d-4aa9-a5e1-b9b87740b43f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/testing.md","content":{"path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/testing.md","type":"User","content":"# C++ Testing\n\n> This file extends [common/testing.md](../common/testing.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Framework\n\nUse **GoogleTest** (gtest/gmock) with **CMake/CTest**.\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\ncmake --build build && ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n\n## Coverage\n\n```bash\ncmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"--coverage\" -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=\"--coverage\" ..\ncmake --build .\nctest --output-on-failure\nlcov --capture --directory . --output-file coverage.info\n```\n\n## Sanitizers\n\nAlways run tests with sanitizers in CI:\n\n```bash\ncmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address,undefined\" ..\n```\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-testing` for detailed C++ testing patterns, TDD workflow, and GoogleTest/GMock usage.\n","globs":["**/*.cpp","**/*.hpp","**/*.cc","**/*.hh","**/*.cxx","**/*.h","**/CMakeLists.txt"],"contentDiffersFromDisk":true,"rawContent":"---\npaths:\n  - \"**/*.cpp\"\n  - \"**/*.hpp\"\n  - \"**/*.cc\"\n  - \"**/*.hh\"\n  - \"**/*.cxx\"\n  - \"**/*.h\"\n  - \"**/CMakeLists.txt\"\n---\n# C++ Testing\n\n> This file extends [common/testing.md](../common/testing.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## Framework\n\nUse **GoogleTest** (gtest/gmock) with **CMake/CTest**.\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\ncmake --build build && ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure\n```\n\n## Coverage\n\n```bash\ncmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"--coverage\" -DCMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS=\"--coverage\" ..\ncmake --build .\nctest --output-on-failure\nlcov --capture --directory . --output-file coverage.info\n```\n\n## Sanitizers\n\nAlways run tests with sanitizers in CI:\n\n```bash\ncmake -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS=\"-fsanitize=address,undefined\" ..\n```\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-testing` for detailed C++ testing patterns, TDD workflow, and GoogleTest/GMock usage.\n"},"displayPath":"../.claude/rules/cpp/testing.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6bd09cff-1963-4a0a-bc3d-677fe14c5cd6","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.844Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6bd09cff-1963-4a0a-bc3d-677fe14c5cd6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/patterns.md","content":{"path":"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/rules/cpp/patterns.md","type":"User","content":"# C++ Patterns\n\n> This file extends [common/patterns.md](../common/patterns.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization)\n\nTie resource lifetime to object lifetime:\n\n```cpp\nclass FileHandle {\npublic:\n    explicit FileHandle(const std::string& path) : file_(std::fopen(path.c_str(), \"r\")) {}\n    ~FileHandle() { if (file_) std::fclose(file_); }\n    FileHandle(const FileHandle&) = delete;\n    FileHandle& operator=(const FileHandle&) = delete;\nprivate:\n    std::FILE* file_;\n};\n```\n\n## Rule of Five/Zero\n\n- **Rule of Zero**: Prefer classes that need no custom destructor, copy/move constructors, or assignments\n- **Rule of Five**: If you define any of destructor/copy-ctor/copy-assign/move-ctor/move-assign, define all five\n\n## Value Semantics\n\n- Pass small/trivial types by value\n- Pass large types by `const&`\n- Return by value (rely on RVO/NRVO)\n- Use move semantics for sink parameters\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Use exceptions for exceptional conditions\n- Use `std::optional` for values that may not exist\n- Use `std::expected` (C++23) or result types for expected failures\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for comprehensive C++ patterns and anti-patterns.\n","globs":["**/*.cpp","**/*.hpp","**/*.cc","**/*.hh","**/*.cxx","**/*.h","**/CMakeLists.txt"],"contentDiffersFromDisk":true,"rawContent":"---\npaths:\n  - \"**/*.cpp\"\n  - \"**/*.hpp\"\n  - \"**/*.cc\"\n  - \"**/*.hh\"\n  - \"**/*.cxx\"\n  - \"**/*.h\"\n  - \"**/CMakeLists.txt\"\n---\n# C++ Patterns\n\n> This file extends [common/patterns.md](../common/patterns.md) with C++ specific content.\n\n## RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization)\n\nTie resource lifetime to object lifetime:\n\n```cpp\nclass FileHandle {\npublic:\n    explicit FileHandle(const std::string& path) : file_(std::fopen(path.c_str(), \"r\")) {}\n    ~FileHandle() { if (file_) std::fclose(file_); }\n    FileHandle(const FileHandle&) = delete;\n    FileHandle& operator=(const FileHandle&) = delete;\nprivate:\n    std::FILE* file_;\n};\n```\n\n## Rule of Five/Zero\n\n- **Rule of Zero**: Prefer classes that need no custom destructor, copy/move constructors, or assignments\n- **Rule of Five**: If you define any of destructor/copy-ctor/copy-assign/move-ctor/move-assign, define all five\n\n## Value Semantics\n\n- Pass small/trivial types by value\n- Pass large types by `const&`\n- Return by value (rely on RVO/NRVO)\n- Use move semantics for sink parameters\n\n## Error Handling\n\n- Use exceptions for exceptional conditions\n- Use `std::optional` for values that may not exist\n- Use `std::expected` (C++23) or result types for expected failures\n\n## Reference\n\nSee skill: `cpp-coding-standards` for comprehensive C++ patterns and anti-patterns.\n"},"displayPath":"../.claude/rules/cpp/patterns.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d6bdaf20-0ca7-40dc-a12d-95152f947c2c","timestamp":"2026-07-31T11:10:40.844Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
