ython3 Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py \\\\\\n  --exec ./build/bluscriptCP_exec --ckpt-run <run> \\\\\\n  --target-t 16384 --s 4 --head-dim 64 --orig-maxpos 4096 \\\\\\n  --data-root $HOME/Downloads --cuda-devices 0 \\\\\\n  --arch \\\"$ARCH\\\" \\\\\\n  --pop 6 --iters 3 --calib-windows 2 \\\\\\n  --out longrope_best.txt\\n```\\nIt prints per-generation best PPL and writes `longrope_best.txt`. For a real search use `--pop 64 --iters 40 --calib-windows 5` (slow — one resident model load, then many cache swaps).\\n\\n## 3. Apply the searched factors\\n**Option A — LongRoPE alone** (extends directly; fine-tune is full-length, memory-heavy):\\n```bash\\nenv $ARCH CP_T=16384 CP_B=1 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=longrope_best.txt \\\\\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=<run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<+K> CP_REWARMUP=100 CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\\\\n    CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \\\\\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=... mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\\n```\\n**Option B — composed with CREAM** (recommended on the 3060: 4k-physical fine-tune, LongRoPE cache as gather source):\\n```bash\\nenv $ARCH CP_T=4096 CP_B=2 CP_CREAM_MODE=cream CP_CREAM_SIGMA=3.0 \\\\\\n    YARN_SCALE=4 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=longrope_best.txt \\\\\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=<run> CP_MAX_STEPS=<+K> CP_REWARMUP=100 CP_REWARMUP_PEAK=0.3 \\\\\\n    CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \\\\\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=... mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\\n```\\n(Here the startup coupling assert checks `S_search==16384==4·4096` and `s==4`; a mismatch dies with a clear message.)\\n\\n## 4. Eval the LongRoPE arm (PPL vs position)\\n```bash\\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_T=16384 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 \\\\\\n    CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=longrope_best.txt CP_CKPT_RESUME=<extended_run> \\\\\\n    CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_longrope_x4.csv CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \\\\\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=... mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\\n```\\nOverlay `ppl_longrope_x4.csv` with your CREAM/YaRN curves in `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb`.\\n\\nTwo reminders: the `--s`/`--target-t` you search with must match how you apply it, and every command needs `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES` pointed at a free GPU. Want me to bundle steps 2–4 into a single `run_longrope.sh` with the run number and factor as arguments?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b23c71d0-f4fa-4a60-bad3-44046e206326","timestamp":"2026-07-31T12:56:52.051Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
