{"parentUuid":"7dee56f2-a2e6-490c-b02c-9db8689378ae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdaBxC2mzJ3GEEjBM1GtZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I understood 1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8\n\nThen the first step is to **train a base checkpoint** — LongRoPE searches *against a trained model* (a random-init model's PPL barely responds to the RoPE cache, so the search would be meaningless). This is the same prerequisite as your CREAM experiments: base → search/extend.\n\n## Train a base (this produces the checkpoint the search needs)\n```bash\nARCH=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0\"\n\nenv $ARCH CP_T=4096 CP_B=2 CP_GLOBAL_BATCH=131072 \\\n    CP_MAX_STEPS=1000 CP_WARMUP=100 \\\n    CP_CKPT=1 CP_CKPT_FREQ=250 \\\n    CP_DATA_ROOT=$HOME/Downloads CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/lib:BluTrain/Profiler/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH \\\n    mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\n```\n\n- It prints a **run number** at startup (`… (run N)`) and writes `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run<N>_step_*.ckpt`. That `N` is what you pass as `--ckpt-run` to the search.\n- `CP_MAX_STEPS=1000` is a reasonable small base; more steps = better base = more meaningful search. Even ~200 steps gives a loadable ckpt if you just want to **smoke-test the pipeline** (not real results).\n\n## Two blockers right now\n1. **Free GPU** — both 3060s are still saturated by your other jobs (11.6/12 GB). Training needs one free; pin it with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`.\n2. That's it — once the base run finishes, plug its run number into the step-2 search command from before.\n\n## If you have CREAM checkpoints on the other box\nYour earlier CREAM runs (31/32/33/34) were on `/mnt/volgrp03/...`. If the architecture matches (`d384/L6/6-2/ffn1024/untied`, head_dim 64), you can **copy one of those base checkpoints here** into `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/` and skip retraining — the search only needs a trained model to score, not a specific one.\n\nSo the order is: **free a GPU → train a base (or copy one) → note its run number → run the search → apply/eval.** Want me to write a `run_longrope.sh` that takes `--base-run` and does search→apply→eval in sequence, so once you have the checkpoint it's one command?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3071,"cache_read_input_tokens":589651,"output_tokens":1910,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3071,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1910,"cache_read_input_tokens":589651,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3071,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3071},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdaBx6tDNbEeGJhVSG5Pa","type":"assistant","uuid":"2a257f39-ee99-4afe-8890-7ef7c8040fc2","timestamp":"2026-07-31T13:10:12.668Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
