 GB). Training needs one free; pin it with `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES`.\\n2. That's it — once the base run finishes, plug its run number into the step-2 search command from before.\\n\\n## If you have CREAM checkpoints on the other box\\nYour earlier CREAM runs (31/32/33/34) were on `/mnt/volgrp03/...`. If the architecture matches (`d384/L6/6-2/ffn1024/untied`, head_dim 64), you can **copy one of those base checkpoints here** into `checkpoints_bluscriptcp/` and skip retraining — the search only needs a trained model to score, not a specific one.\\n\\nSo the order is: **free a GPU → train a base (or copy one) → note its run number → run the search → apply/eval.** Want me to write a `run_longrope.sh` that takes `--base-run` and does search→apply→eval in sequence, so once you have the checkpoint it's one command?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8b33855c-adf8-4eaf-97d5-11d952c9716c","timestamp":"2026-07-31T13:10:12.765Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
