{"parentUuid":"6368f416-06a5-4402-9f75-9e7a15102214","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbRKbYFDs8kFneQkd5Av","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Ah — that changes my finding. Those OOMs were **GPU contention** (GPU 0 busy with your job), **not** a real memory limit. Let me retract the \"can't run 16k locally\" conclusion — I can't measure the true ceiling while the GPU is occupied. Sorry for the false alarm.\n\nHere's the honest picture:\n\n## 1. Single GPU — yes, as shipped\nThe pipeline is `CP_SIZE=1`. The **search** is parallelizable across GPUs (independent candidate evals), but the driver currently uses one — I'd need to extend it to shard candidates across N GPUs for an ~N× search speedup.\n\n## 2. Local vs server time — the key reframe\nBecause I made the search **wall-clock-bounded** (`SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC=8.5h`), the **total pipeline time is ~the same everywhere: ~10h** (8.5h search + ~1h fine-tune + ~1h eval). What differs between local and server is **not the time — it's how much of the search completes**:\n\n| | per-candidate eval | candidates in 8.5h | search quality |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **3060 (local)** | slower (est. ~60–120s @16k) | ~250–500 | partial search (gen0 + a few gens) |\n| **A100/H100 (server)** | ~3–5× faster (est. ~20–40s) | ~800–1500 | most/all of a full paper search |\n\nSo: **same ~10h wall clock, better result on the server** (more generations → lower PPL). The fine-tune (~50 min, 4k physical) and the final eval (~50 min) are fixed regardless.\n\nTwo caveats I *couldn't* verify because the GPU is busy:\n- **Whether 16k eval fits in the 3060's 12 GB when free** — the OOMs were contention; a free 3060 *might* fit 16k forward-only (logits ~3.3 GB + model + activations), but I can't confirm. If it doesn't fit even when free, that's the real reason to use the server.\n- **The actual per-eval time** — my numbers above are estimates.\n\nWant me to **measure both cleanly** (true 16k memory fit + per-candidate time) as soon as a GPU is free — pointed at GPU 1 if that one's idle? That would replace the estimates with real numbers and tell you exactly how many candidates each machine completes in the budget. Just say which GPU is free."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":667484,"output_tokens":2282,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2282,"cache_read_input_tokens":667484,"cache_creation_input_tokens":55,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":55},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbRKWUtavNNUKnYAACr2","type":"assistant","uuid":"92c3defe-a6ff-4ced-a58b-04ff875c0192","timestamp":"2026-08-01T04:46:12.655Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
