\"","durationMs":41},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b0bfa87a-d20b-4961-86d8-7b34f6ced53e","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:01:07.730Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b0bfa87a-d20b-4961-86d8-7b34f6ced53e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbSWC9kSfSp1zgrasoMZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":673032,"output_tokens":3644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3644,"cache_read_input_tokens":673032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbSW8mbVvB6tAewpic9P","type":"assistant","uuid":"809d8153-b738-4b35-9c48-4c0909b3aaca","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:01:47.833Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"809d8153-b738-4b35-9c48-4c0909b3aaca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbSWC9kSfSp1zgrasoMZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clean numbers now — and they **overturn my earlier worry**. Measured on the idle 3060:\n\n- **16k eval fits** (no OOM when the GPU is free — earlier OOMs were GPU-0 contention).\n- **Per-candidate eval @16k (CALIB=3): ~26s** (model load is one-time ~5s, thanks to the resident evaluator).\n\n## Local timing (RTX 3060) — measured\n\n| Stage | Cost |\n|---|---|\n| Full paper search (P=64, 40 iters ≈ ~1344 evals) | ~1344 × 26s ≈ **9.7h** |\n| — capped at `SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC=8.5h` → | ~1177 evals ≈ **~88% of a full search** (~35 generations) |\n| Fine-tune (300 steps @4k physical) | ~50 min |\n| Final eval (32 windows @16k) | ~5 min |\n| **Total** | **~9.4h** (fits your 12h) |\n\n**So the whole 4k→16k pipeline *does* run locally in ~9–10.5h** — I was wrong before; that was contention, not a real limit. If you want the *full* 40 generations locally, bump `SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC=34000` (9.4h) → total ~10.6h, still under 12h.\n\n## Server timing\nThe catch: per-eval isn't purely GPU-bound — a big chunk is the **CPU log-sum-exp NLL** over the 50k vocab for every position. So a faster server GPU speeds up the forward but not the CPU part. Realistic server gain (faster GPU **+** more CPU cores for the OMP NLL loop): **~2–3× per-eval → ~10–13s/candidate**:\n\n- **Full search in ~4–5h** → total pipeline **~5–6h**, or\n- Same 8.5h budget → a full search **with margin**, and you could raise `CALIB` (more windows → less-noisy fitness → better search) since you have headroom.\n\n## Bottom line\n- **Locally:** ~10h, ~88% of a full search — perfectly usable, fits 12h.\n- **Server:** ~half the time (or same time, better/deeper search).\n- Either way the wall-clock is **bounded by `SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC`**, so it can't overrun — the machine only changes *how much search* completes.\n\nSince 16k fits and the timing is measured, you're clear to launch locally now (point `GPU=1` while GPU 0 is busy):\n```bash\nGPU=1 nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > longrope_pipeline.log 2>&1 &\n```\nWant me to switch the fitness NLL to the GPU (a small kernel) so per-eval drops from ~26s toward the forward-only ~5–8s? That would roughly **3–4× the search throughput** on *both* local and server — the single biggest speedup available here."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_read_input_tokens":673032,"output_tokens":3644,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3644,"cache_read_input_tokens":673032,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1398,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1398},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbSW8mbVvB6tAewpic9P","type":"assistant","uuid":"174c5756-c2fa-4238-a74f-3c75e692e52b","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:02:00.722Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
