{"parentUuid":"0635b6a6-f4af-4bd5-9b8f-875253c4b7ce","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbT7m6sNfheRyyCT5r8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":683057,"output_tokens":1592,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":194,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":683057,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":194},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbT7g1XVbv67NFZDCxS5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c35798b3-2004-499e-a00c-ca4285ad1f8a","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:09:24.733Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c35798b3-2004-499e-a00c-ca4285ad1f8a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbT7m6sNfheRyyCT5r8C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both pass. The search is now **right-sized with early-stopping** — it runs only until it converges, then stops.\n\n## New defaults (tuned for your 48M, not the paper's 7B)\n`POP=16, N1=8, N2=8, ITERS=20, PATIENCE=4` — vs the paper's `64/16/16/40`. Rationale: you have **32 search dims** (not 64), a modest **4× extension**, and the **PI/NTK/YaRN seeds already start close**, so a small GA converges fast. `PATIENCE=4` stops when the best PPL hasn't improved for 4 generations; `SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC=8.5h` is just a backstop ceiling.\n\n## Expected time (using the measured 26s/eval)\n- **Per generation:** 16 children × 26s ≈ **7 min** (minus memoized duplicates).\n- **Convergence:** a 48M/4× search typically settles in ~5–10 generations → **search ≈ 45 min – 2h**, then early-stops (it won't burn the full 8.5h).\n- **Fine-tune** ~50 min + **eval** ~5 min.\n- **Total: ~2–3h locally** — nowhere near your 12h.\n\nSo \"the amount required for your model size\" is roughly **~150–350 evals**, not the ~1300 of a full paper search.\n\n## Launch (same command, now right-sized)\n```bash\nGPU=1 nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > longrope_pipeline.log 2>&1 &\ntail -f longrope_pipeline.log\n```\nWatch the `no_improve=` counter in the log — when it reaches `PATIENCE`, the search stops.\n\n## Two honest notes\n- The seeds include YaRN, so **LongRoPE can never do worse than YaRN** here — the search only squeezes improvement on top. For a small model + gentle 4× extension, that improvement may be **modest** (YaRN is already strong at 4×); the bigger LongRoPE wins show up at larger extension factors. If you want to see a clearer gap, run `S=8` (4k→32k) or `S=16` (64k).\n- If the fitness looks noisy (best PPL bouncing), raise `CALIB=5` (more windows → steadier ranking) — costs ~1.7× per eval but still well within budget.\n\nIf you want it even leaner: `POP=12 N1=6 N2=6 PATIENCE=3 GPU=1 nohup bash ... &` → search in ~30–60 min, total ~1.5h."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_read_input_tokens":683057,"output_tokens":1592,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":194,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1592,"cache_read_input_tokens":683057,"cache_creation_input_tokens":194,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":194},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbT7g1XVbv67NFZDCxS5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dbb09cf2-5d1d-419b-9c79-072bb211a5dd","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:09:36.058Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"dbb09cf2-5d1d-419b-9c79-072bb211a5dd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"765fa069-adc3-4c0c-937a-826945378118","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"1001b050-a5da-4e58-8161-6eb03d6c491e\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Both pass. The search is now **right-sized with early-stopping** — it runs only until it converges, then stops.\\n\\n## New defaults (tuned for your 48M, not the paper's 7B)\\n`POP=16, N1=8, N2=8, ITERS=20, PATIENCE=4` — vs the paper's `64/16/16/40`. Rationale: you have **32 search dims** (not 64), a modest **4× extension**, and the **PI/NTK/YaRN seeds already start close**, so a small GA converges fast. `PATIENCE=4` stops when the best PPL hasn't improved for 4 generations; `SEARCH_BUDGET_SEC=8.5h` is just a backstop ceiling.\\n\\n## Expected time (using the measured 26s/eval)\\n- **Per generation:** 16 children × 26s ≈ **7 min** (minus memoized duplicates).\\n- **Convergence:** a 48M/4× search typically settles in ~5–10 generations → **search ≈ 45 min – 2h**, then early-stops (it won't burn the full 8.5h).\\n- **Fine-tune** ~50 min + **eval** ~5 min.\\n- **Total: ~2–3h locally** — nowhere near your 12h.\\n\\nSo \\\"the amount required for your model size\\\" is roughly **~150–350 evals**, not the ~1300 of a full paper search.\\n\\n## Launch (same command, now right-sized)\\n```bash\\nGPU=1 nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > longrope_pipeline.log 2>&1 &\\ntail -f longrope_pipeline.log\\n```\\nWatch the `no_improve=` counter in the log — when it reaches `PATIENCE`, the search stops.\\n\\n## Two honest notes\\n- The seeds include YaRN, so **LongRoPE can never do worse than YaRN** here — the search only squeezes improvement on top. For a small model + gentle 4× extension, that improvement may be **modest** (YaRN is already strong at 4×); the bigger LongRoPE wins show up at larger extension factors. If you want to see a clearer gap, run `S=8` (4k→32k) or `S=16` (64k).\\n- If the fitness looks noisy (best PPL bouncing), raise `CALIB=5` (more windows → steadier ranking) — costs ~1.7× per eval but still well within budget.\\n\\nIf you want it even leaner: `POP=12 N1=6 N2=6 PATIENCE=3 GPU=1 nohup bash ... &` → search in ~30–60 min, total ~1.5h.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":51},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a5ceb041-bb68-4eb4-beac-4cc9312b0057","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:09:36.149Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
