{"parentUuid":"2a9723a2-1b7b-4fc1-aad7-1c2f862b65aa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_1374579","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 294 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ae40469f-260b-489f-b207-91106be6651e","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:13:26.137Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ae40469f-260b-489f-b207-91106be6651e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbTSdu4SH5jx26bTJmMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_read_input_tokens":684889,"output_tokens":2490,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2490,"cache_read_input_tokens":684889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbTSZkmmGUB57xsWB2by","type":"assistant","uuid":"4742186b-9435-4885-a4f0-19212b2bf795","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:13:49.794Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"4742186b-9435-4885-a4f0-19212b2bf795","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbTSdu4SH5jx26bTJmMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — **LongRoPE does not require CREAM.** They're orthogonal, and I only wired CREAM in as a **memory workaround for the fine-tune on your 12 GB 3060**. Let me be clear about why and what the alternatives are.\n\n## Why CREAM showed up here\nLongRoPE's own recipe is: **search the cache → fine-tune the model at the (long) target length** with that cache. That fine-tune is at the *full physical target length* (16k, 64k…) — real long-sequence training, which needs a big GPU. The 3060 can't fine-tune at 16k+ (barely even forwards it).\n\nSo to make the fine-tune fit the 3060, I **composed** LongRoPE's cache with CREAM: CREAM keeps the physical sequence at **4k** (cheap attention) while the LongRoPE cache supplies the extended-position rotations. The model gets trained against the searched cache **without ever allocating a 16k attention matrix**. It's purely an efficiency layer — not part of LongRoPE.\n\n## The three fine-tune options (you choose)\n\n| Mode | Fine-tune | Memory | Fidelity |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **LongRoPE-alone** | at the **full target length** (16k/64k physical) | heavy — needs a big GPU | **faithful to the paper** |\n| **LongRoPE + CREAM** (what I wired) | at **4k physical**, LongRoPE cache as gather source | cheap — fits the 3060 | pragmatic hybrid (extra approximation) |\n| **Search-only** | **no fine-tune** — apply the searched cache at inference | cheapest | the paper's \"8× without fine-tuning\" mode |\n\n## What this means for you\nSince you have **RTX 6000 Adas (48 GB)**, the memory constraint that motivated CREAM **disappears** — you can (and for a clean result, *should*) run **LongRoPE-alone**: fine-tune at the true target length, no CREAM. That's the faithful method, and it removes the CREAM approximation from the comparison (\"is LongRoPE better than YaRN?\" is cleaner without a second technique layered in).\n\nOn the 3060, CREAM composition is the only way to fine-tune at 16k without OOM — but you also have the **search-only** option, which needs no fine-tune at all and avoids CREAM entirely.\n\n## So, concretely\n- **Want the faithful LongRoPE result:** use a 6000 Ada, **LongRoPE-alone**, fine-tune at 16k/64k.\n- **Just want a cheap first result on the 3060:** either the CREAM-composed fine-tune (what's wired) or **search-only** (no fine-tune, no CREAM).\n\nThe pipeline currently hardcodes the CREAM-composed path. Want me to add a `COMPOSE={cream|alone|none}` toggle to `run_longrope_pipeline.sh` so you can pick — LongRoPE-alone on the 6000 Ada, or search-only to skip fine-tuning and CREAM completely?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_read_input_tokens":684889,"output_tokens":2490,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2490,"cache_read_input_tokens":684889,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3916},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbTSZkmmGUB57xsWB2by","type":"assistant","uuid":"6fdde37b-f584-48b5-9042-051b23c6b363","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:14:01.769Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6fdde37b-f584-48b5-9042-051b23c6b363","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"1d503080-c6e2-451e-acb4-43f90fd64010","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"0ee49353-7314-4a15-9e6e-c58ac0f809c2\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"No — **LongRoPE does not require CREAM.** They're orthogonal, and I only wired CREAM in as a **memory workaround for the fine-tune on your 12 GB 3060**. Let me be clear about why and what the alternatives are.\\n\\n## Why CREAM showed up here\\nLongRoPE's own recipe is: **search the cache → fine-tune the model at the (long) target length** with that cache. That fine-tune is at the *full physical target length* (16k, 64k…) — real long-sequence training, which needs a big GPU. The 3060 can't fine-tune at 16k+ (barely even forwards it).\\n\\nSo to make the fine-tune fit the 3060, I **composed** LongRoPE's cache with CREAM: CREAM keeps the physical sequence at **4k** (cheap attention) while the LongRoPE cache supplies the extended-position rotations. The model gets trained against the searched cache **without ever allocating a 16k attention matrix**. It's purely an efficiency layer — not part of LongRoPE.\\n\\n## The three fine-tune options (you choose)\\n\\n| Mode | Fine-tune | Memory | Fidelity |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| **LongRoPE-alone** | at the **full target length** (16k/64k physical) | heavy — needs a big GPU | **faithful to the paper** |\\n| **LongRoPE + CREAM** (what I wired) | at **4k physical**, LongRoPE cache as gather source | cheap — fits the 3060 | pragmatic hybrid (extra approximation) |\\n| **Search-only** | **no fine-tune** — apply the searched cache at inference | cheapest | the paper's \\\"8× without fine-tuning\\\" mode |\\n\\n## What this means for you\\nSince you have **RTX 6000 Adas (48 GB)**, the memory constraint that motivated CREAM **disappears** — you can (and for a clean result, *should*) run **LongRoPE-alone**: fine-tune at the true target length, no CREAM. That's the faithful method, and it removes the CREAM approximation from the comparison (\\\"is LongRoPE better than YaRN?\\\" is cleaner without a second technique layered in).\\n\\nOn the 3060, CREAM composition is the only way to fine-tune at 16k without OOM — but you also have the **search-only** option, which needs no fine-tune at all and avoids CREAM entirely.\\n\\n## So, concretely\\n- **Want the faithful LongRoPE result:** use a 6000 Ada, **LongRoPE-alone**, fine-tune at 16k/64k.\\n- **Just want a cheap first result on the 3060:** either the CREAM-composed fine-tune (what's wired) or **search-only** (no fine-tune, no CREAM).\\n\\nThe pipeline currently hardcodes the CREAM-composed path. Want me to add a `COMPOSE={cream|alone|none}` toggle to `run_longrope_pipeline.sh` so you can pick — LongRoPE-alone on the 6000 Ada, or search-only to skip fine-tuning and CREAM completely?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1b5d9561-b6ae-445a-bdc5-d680636c2678","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:14:01.863Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
