{"parentUuid":"8f8744c2-fb32-4904-ac7f-a70b5ac3c9a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbU953WmBbPiSzgL6zBH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`bash OK`. Here's how to launch with your checkpoint, plus the timing.\n\n## Launch (server, run 30)\n```bash\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 DATA_ROOT=<server data dir> \\\n  nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > longrope_pipeline.log 2>&1 &\n```\n(`ARCH` default already matches your config exactly; leave `CP_ATTN_MODE` unset → ring, the tested path.)\n\n## Time on the 6000 Ada — but first, the honest caveat about \"2 GPUs\"\n\n**As shipped the pipeline is single-GPU, so 2× 6000 Ada uses only ONE.** The 2nd GPU sits idle unless I add search-sharding (the parallelization I offered). So the numbers below are for **1× 6000 Ada** (≈2–3× faster per-eval than the 3060's measured 26s, though the CPU-NLL part caps the gain):\n\n| Config | Search (right-sized, early-stop) | Fine-tune | Eval | **Total (1 GPU)** |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **s=4 (16k)**, CREAM-composed | ~30–70 min | ~20 min (4k) | ~2 min | **~1–1.5h** |\n| **s=16 (64k)**, CREAM-composed | ~2–5h | ~20 min (still 4k!) | ~10 min | **~2.5–5.5h** |\n| **s=16 (64k)**, LongRoPE-**alone** (faithful) | ~2–5h | ~2.5–5h (64k training) | ~10 min | **~5–10h** |\n\nNotes:\n- **CREAM-composed keeps the fine-tune at 4k** regardless of `s` — that's why its total stays low even at 64k. The 48 GB only matters for the search/eval forward (which fit easily).\n- **LongRoPE-alone** at s=16 trains at **64k physical** — heavy, but the 48 GB handles it; that's the faithful-to-paper run and the one worth doing on this hardware.\n\n## Using both 6000 Adas\nTwo options to actually use the 2nd GPU:\n1. **Search-sharding** (I'd add it): one resident evaluator per GPU, candidates split round-robin → **search ~2× faster**. This is the clean win — the search is the dominant cost.\n2. **Manual split:** run two pipelines at once — e.g. `GPU=0 S=4` and `GPU=1 S=16` — to get both extension factors in parallel with zero code change.\n\n## My recommendation for your setup\nSince you have the memory: run **s=16 LongRoPE-alone** (faithful) on GPU 0, and in parallel **s=4** (quick sanity) on GPU 1 — both single-GPU, launched together, no code change:\n```bash\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 S=16 COMPOSE=alone DATA_ROOT=<dir> nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s16.log 2>&1 &\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=1 S=4  DATA_ROOT=<dir>              nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s4.log  2>&1 &\n```\n\nOne gap: the pipeline currently **hardcodes CREAM-composed** fine-tune — there's no `COMPOSE=alone` toggle yet. Want me to add `COMPOSE={cream|alone|none}` so you can run the faithful LongRoPE-alone path (and `none` = search-only, no fine-tune) on the 6000 Ada? That's the one change needed to do the faithful run."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_read_input_tokens":697724,"output_tokens":1851,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1851,"cache_read_input_tokens":697724,"cache_creation_input_tokens":148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":148},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbU91Qyenoe1Au8bnjkg","type":"assistant","uuid":"2d177132-d4a3-4f65-8254-ffab24f9b7c0","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:23:00.766Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"2d177132-d4a3-4f65-8254-ffab24f9b7c0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"b74dc76a-19fb-4a18-89d8-0b103b158993","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"eb0df96f-5a92-478a-aae3-9946c7945628\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"`bash OK`. Here's how to launch with your checkpoint, plus the timing.\\n\\n## Launch (server, run 30)\\n```bash\\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 DATA_ROOT=<server data dir> \\\\\\n  nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > longrope_pipeline.log 2>&1 &\\n```\\n(`ARCH` default already matches your config exactly; leave `CP_ATTN_MODE` unset → ring, the tested path.)\\n\\n## Time on the 6000 Ada — but first, the honest caveat about \\\"2 GPUs\\\"\\n\\n**As shipped the pipeline is single-GPU, so 2× 6000 Ada uses only ONE.** The 2nd GPU sits idle unless I add search-sharding (the parallelization I offered). So the numbers below are for **1× 6000 Ada** (≈2–3× faster per-eval than the 3060's measured 26s, though the CPU-NLL part caps the gain):\\n\\n| Config | Search (right-sized, early-stop) | Fine-tune | Eval | **Total (1 GPU)** |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| **s=4 (16k)**, CREAM-composed | ~30–70 min | ~20 min (4k) | ~2 min | **~1–1.5h** |\\n| **s=16 (64k)**, CREAM-composed | ~2–5h | ~20 min (still 4k!) | ~10 min | **~2.5–5.5h** |\\n| **s=16 (64k)**, LongRoPE-**alone** (faithful) | ~2–5h | ~2.5–5h (64k training) | ~10 min | **~5–10h** |\\n\\nNotes:\\n- **CREAM-composed keeps the fine-tune at 4k** regardless of `s` — that's why its total stays low even at 64k. The 48 GB only matters for the search/eval forward (which fit easily).\\n- **LongRoPE-alone** at s=16 trains at **64k physical** — heavy, but the 48 GB handles it; that's the faithful-to-paper run and the one worth doing on this hardware.\\n\\n## Using both 6000 Adas\\nTwo options to actually use the 2nd GPU:\\n1. **Search-sharding** (I'd add it): one resident evaluator per GPU, candidates split round-robin → **search ~2× faster**. This is the clean win — the search is the dominant cost.\\n2. **Manual split:** run two pipelines at once — e.g. `GPU=0 S=4` and `GPU=1 S=16` — to get both extension factors in parallel with zero code change.\\n\\n## My recommendation for your setup\\nSince you have the memory: run **s=16 LongRoPE-alone** (faithful) on GPU 0, and in parallel **s=4** (quick sanity) on GPU 1 — both single-GPU, launched together, no code change:\\n```bash\\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 S=16 COMPOSE=alone DATA_ROOT=<dir> nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s16.log 2>&1 &\\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=1 S=4  DATA_ROOT=<dir>              nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s4.log  2>&1 &\\n```\\n\\nOne gap: the pipeline currently **hardcodes CREAM-composed** fine-tune — there's no `COMPOSE=alone` toggle yet. Want me to add `COMPOSE={cream|alone|none}` so you can run the faithful LongRoPE-alone path (and `none` = search-only, no fine-tune) on the 6000 Ada? That's the one change needed to do the faithful run.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":52},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6d24251a-17df-4643-9d6c-3a218f63ab9a","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:23:00.857Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
