{"parentUuid":"07492b40-7914-4674-8d9b-6588233cf0b5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbUrEzwP8KK9XAbUZh3c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":149,"cache_read_input_tokens":715465,"output_tokens":2483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":149,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2483,"cache_read_input_tokens":715465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":149},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbUr6qoWyfi8ByHXpi4Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c0193c9-9c3c-4f66-98cd-5a35ad930ea3","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:32:17.181Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"6c0193c9-9c3c-4f66-98cd-5a35ad930ea3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbUrEzwP8KK9XAbUZh3c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`bash OK`. The pipeline now supports **`COMPOSE={alone|cream|none}`**, defaulting to `alone` (no CREAM). So your exact request — no CREAM, s=16, LongRoPE-alone — is one command:\n\n## Launch (server, run 30, no CREAM, s=16)\n```bash\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 S=16 COMPOSE=alone \\\n  DATA_ROOT=<server data dir> \\\n  nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s16_alone.log 2>&1 &\n```\n- `COMPOSE=alone` → fine-tune at the **full 64k physical length**, no CREAM (faithful LongRoPE).\n- Search + eval + fine-tune all at 64k, which **fits one 6000 Ada** (13 GB eval logits; ~30–40 GB fine-tune) — so no CP, no CREAM.\n\n## Timing (1× 6000 Ada)\n| Stage | ~time |\n|---|---|\n| Search (right-sized, early-stop) @64k | ~2–5h |\n| Fine-tune LongRoPE-alone @64k physical | ~2.5–5h |\n| Eval @64k | ~10 min |\n| **Total** | **~5–10h** |\n\n## Using the 2nd GPU\nThe pipeline is single-GPU, and s=16 doesn't *need* the 2nd. Two zero-code-change options:\n- **Run a parallel experiment on GPU 1** — e.g. a search-only baseline (`GPU=1 S=16 COMPOSE=none`) or a different factor (`GPU=1 S=8 COMPOSE=alone`), launched alongside.\n- If you want the 2nd GPU to actually *speed up the s=16 run*, that needs the **search-sharding** extension (candidates split across both GPUs, ~2× faster search).\n\n## One risk to watch\nThe **64k fine-tune (~30–40 GB) is the tight part**. If it OOMs on the 48 GB card:\n- lower `FT_B` (already 1) — can't go lower, so instead\n- use **CP=2 for the fine-tune** (LongRoPE-alone *is* CP-compatible for training — contiguous positions). That needs the fine-tune launched with `NP=2 CP_SIZE=2`, which the pipeline doesn't expose yet.\n\nSo: **s=16 is a solid, faithful target that fits one 6000 Ada with no CREAM and no CP.** Launch the command above. Want me to (a) add search-sharding to use both GPUs for the search, and/or (b) expose `NP/CP_SIZE` on the fine-tune step as a fallback in case 64k training OOMs?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":149,"cache_read_input_tokens":715465,"output_tokens":2483,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":149,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2483,"cache_read_input_tokens":715465,"cache_creation_input_tokens":149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":149},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbUr6qoWyfi8ByHXpi4Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8842440-8e39-418d-b9f7-032de4cb2107","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:32:28.234Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a8842440-8e39-418d-b9f7-032de4cb2107","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"87e2641d-697e-4842-985c-269118a5563f","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"1e868dda-25c7-4e5b-be2b-74d92205f6dd\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"`bash OK`. The pipeline now supports **`COMPOSE={alone|cream|none}`**, defaulting to `alone` (no CREAM). So your exact request — no CREAM, s=16, LongRoPE-alone — is one command:\\n\\n## Launch (server, run 30, no CREAM, s=16)\\n```bash\\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=0 S=16 COMPOSE=alone \\\\\\n  DATA_ROOT=<server data dir> \\\\\\n  nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s16_alone.log 2>&1 &\\n```\\n- `COMPOSE=alone` → fine-tune at the **full 64k physical length**, no CREAM (faithful LongRoPE).\\n- Search + eval + fine-tune all at 64k, which **fits one 6000 Ada** (13 GB eval logits; ~30–40 GB fine-tune) — so no CP, no CREAM.\\n\\n## Timing (1× 6000 Ada)\\n| Stage | ~time |\\n|---|---|\\n| Search (right-sized, early-stop) @64k | ~2–5h |\\n| Fine-tune LongRoPE-alone @64k physical | ~2.5–5h |\\n| Eval @64k | ~10 min |\\n| **Total** | **~5–10h** |\\n\\n## Using the 2nd GPU\\nThe pipeline is single-GPU, and s=16 doesn't *need* the 2nd. Two zero-code-change options:\\n- **Run a parallel experiment on GPU 1** — e.g. a search-only baseline (`GPU=1 S=16 COMPOSE=none`) or a different factor (`GPU=1 S=8 COMPOSE=alone`), launched alongside.\\n- If you want the 2nd GPU to actually *speed up the s=16 run*, that needs the **search-sharding** extension (candidates split across both GPUs, ~2× faster search).\\n\\n## One risk to watch\\nThe **64k fine-tune (~30–40 GB) is the tight part**. If it OOMs on the 48 GB card:\\n- lower `FT_B` (already 1) — can't go lower, so instead\\n- use **CP=2 for the fine-tune** (LongRoPE-alone *is* CP-compatible for training — contiguous positions). That needs the fine-tune launched with `NP=2 CP_SIZE=2`, which the pipeline doesn't expose yet.\\n\\nSo: **s=16 is a solid, faithful target that fits one 6000 Ada with no CREAM and no CP.** Launch the command above. Want me to (a) add search-sharding to use both GPUs for the search, and/or (b) expose `NP/CP_SIZE` on the fine-tune step as a fallback in case 64k training OOMs?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":50},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ca8b3405-2cf3-478b-91b4-fb1cd808fa62","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:32:28.332Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
