{"parentUuid":"2d8a95f0-c9cc-4a33-96bc-82c14accd7f4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbV3RVXd225N78DVTuE4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_read_input_tokens":715614,"output_tokens":1833,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1833,"cache_read_input_tokens":715614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbV3MyhBFgzbpLtbzYtn","type":"assistant","uuid":"9395e1cc-e891-4fea-b91c-1fff4a0338b4","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:34:45.622Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9395e1cc-e891-4fea-b91c-1fff4a0338b4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbV3RVXd225N78DVTuE4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Rough estimate on **one 6000 Ada**: **~5–8 hours**, best guess **~5–6h**.\n\nBreakdown:\n- **Search** (right-sized, early-stops): **~2–3h** — could be less if it converges in a few generations.\n- **Fine-tune** LongRoPE-alone @64k, 300 steps: **~1.5–3h** — the biggest swing factor (64k training is heavy).\n- **Eval** @64k: **~10–15 min**.\n\nCaveats on the number:\n- It's **extrapolated** — I measured 26s/eval at 16k on the 3060; scaling to 64k (~4×) and to the 6000 Ada (~2–3× faster, but partly CPU-NLL-bound) gives ~40s/eval. Real numbers could shift this ±30%.\n- The **early-stop** (`PATIENCE=4`) means the search often finishes well before its ceiling — so it leans toward the low end.\n- If the 64k fine-tune is tight/OOMs and you drop to fewer `FT_STEPS`, it's faster.\n\nIf you run **both GPUs** as two parallel experiments (e.g. `S=16` on GPU 0, `S=8` on GPU 1), you get two results in the same ~5–6h wall clock instead of one.\n\nWant me to just measure one real 64k eval on the server once it's up (like I did for 16k) so this becomes an exact number instead of an estimate?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_read_input_tokens":715614,"output_tokens":1833,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1833,"cache_read_input_tokens":715614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2488,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2488},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbV3MyhBFgzbpLtbzYtn","type":"assistant","uuid":"c7a5e7f6-7333-4d79-8707-ceac3e6eeb6d","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:34:52.463Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c7a5e7f6-7333-4d79-8707-ceac3e6eeb6d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"f1d49076-3ed8-478b-b5f1-c83c2081163e","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"202772d1-a8bf-4a82-9409-5a473793a7d3\",\"permission_mode\":\"acceptEdits\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Rough estimate on **one 6000 Ada**: **~5–8 hours**, best guess **~5–6h**.\\n\\nBreakdown:\\n- **Search** (right-sized, early-stops): **~2–3h** — could be less if it converges in a few generations.\\n- **Fine-tune** LongRoPE-alone @64k, 300 steps: **~1.5–3h** — the biggest swing factor (64k training is heavy).\\n- **Eval** @64k: **~10–15 min**.\\n\\nCaveats on the number:\\n- It's **extrapolated** — I measured 26s/eval at 16k on the 3060; scaling to 64k (~4×) and to the 6000 Ada (~2–3× faster, but partly CPU-NLL-bound) gives ~40s/eval. Real numbers could shift this ±30%.\\n- The **early-stop** (`PATIENCE=4`) means the search often finishes well before its ceiling — so it leans toward the low end.\\n- If the 64k fine-tune is tight/OOMs and you drop to fewer `FT_STEPS`, it's faster.\\n\\nIf you run **both GPUs** as two parallel experiments (e.g. `S=16` on GPU 0, `S=8` on GPU 1), you get two results in the same ~5–6h wall clock instead of one.\\n\\nWant me to just measure one real 64k eval on the server once it's up (like I did for 16k) so this becomes an exact number instead of an estimate?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":54