{"parentUuid":"3bec0738-30e9-4a47-8ee0-bb411348b1fa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_1402822","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[SessionEnd] Updated session file: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/sessions/2026-08-01-CP-session.tmp\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"599e060e-bab3-4706-88f0-a1afb1ace3e8","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:39:06.972Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"599e060e-bab3-4706-88f0-a1afb1ace3e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbVQEAj9q9Nmyn7zw6p7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_read_input_tokens":718102,"output_tokens":2027,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2027,"cache_read_input_tokens":718102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbVQ9f7P4ozwTLddoGV2","type":"assistant","uuid":"f68460a5-86d5-42d3-823b-83a5901a4125","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:39:27.826Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"f68460a5-86d5-42d3-823b-83a5901a4125","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbVQEAj9q9Nmyn7zw6p7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — not half, for a few concrete reasons.\n\n## Why it's not 2×\n1. **As shipped it's single-GPU.** A single `s=16` run uses **one** GPU; the 2nd sits idle. So without code changes, 2 GPUs = same time as 1.\n2. **Only 1 of the 3 stages is parallelizable.** The pipeline is sequential: **search → fine-tune → eval**. The *search* is embarrassingly parallel (independent candidates), but **fine-tune and eval are single-GPU and sequential** — a 2nd GPU can't speed them up. By Amdahl's law: if the search is ~40–50% of total, halving *just* the search cuts total time by only ~20–25%.\n3. **Even the search wouldn't cleanly double.** If I add search-sharding (candidates split across both GPUs), the **CPU log-sum-exp NLL** is shared across cores on one node → sub-linear, more like ~1.5–1.8× on that stage.\n\nSo realistically, **fully parallelized** (search-sharding + CP=2 fine-tune, both of which need wiring), you'd get maybe **~1.5–1.7× overall** — total ~5.5h → ~3.5–4h, not 2.75h.\n\n## The clean way to get 2× value from 2 GPUs\nRun **two independent experiments in parallel** — no code change, no contention:\n```bash\nGPU=0 S=16 COMPOSE=alone ... nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s16.log 2>&1 &\nGPU=1 S=8  COMPOSE=alone ... nohup bash ...run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s8.log  2>&1 &\n```\nSame ~5–6h wall clock, but you get **both s=16 and s=8** curves instead of one. That's the best bang for the 2nd GPU here — the s=16 run itself doesn't get faster, but you're not wasting the GPU.\n\n## If you specifically want the s=16 run *itself* faster\nThe single biggest lever isn't the 2nd GPU — it's **moving the NLL to the GPU** (~3–4× per-eval on *one* GPU, since much of the 40s/eval is CPU-bound). That would cut the search stage more than a 2nd GPU would. Want me to do that instead? It speeds up every eval on both local and server, single- or multi-GPU."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_read_input_tokens":718102,"output_tokens":2027,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2027,"cache_read_input_tokens":718102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1858},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbVQ9f7P4ozwTLddoGV2","type":"assistant","uuid":"86bdd805-a7ea-4c27-b719-f80baf3d0150","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:39:38.075Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
