get **both s=16 and s=8** curves instead of one. That's the best bang for the 2nd GPU here — the s=16 run itself doesn't get faster, but you're not wasting the GPU.\\n\\n## If you specifically want the s=16 run *itself* faster\\nThe single biggest lever isn't the 2nd GPU — it's **moving the NLL to the GPU** (~3–4× per-eval on *one* GPU, since much of the 40s/eval is CPU-bound). That would cut the search stage more than a 2nd GPU would. Want me to do that instead? It speeds up every eval on both local and server, single- or multi-GPU.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8202c4e2-9192-4b29-ae74-4ba55a3e6d11","timestamp":"2026-08-01T05:39:38.163Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
