{"parentUuid":"0d24ce60-0619-4041-a11f-719caadb3014","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbaFkctGKqTVRPr8UUGi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Driver OK. Since I can't run on your server, here's the fastest way to see the **real** error — run one candidate manually on the server and it prints the actual C++ failure:\n\n```bash\ncd /mnt/volgrp03/3rd_floor/Adhitya/CP/Context_Parallelism\nARCH=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0\"\nprintf 'n_hat 0\\ns 16\\nS_search 65536\\nlambda %s\\n' \"$(python3 -c \"print(' '.join(['1.00']*32))\")\" > /tmp/c.txt\nprintf '/tmp/c.txt\\n' | env $ARCH CP_LONGROPE_SEARCH=1 CP_T=65536 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=1 \\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=30 CP_DATA_ROOT=<your server data dir> CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/lib:BluTrain/Profiler/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH \\\n    mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec 2>&1 | tail -40\n```\nPaste the last ~40 lines and I'll pinpoint it.\n\n## My leading hypothesis: OOM at 65536\nThe evaluator died right after building the 64k cache (i.e., during model setup / first forward at 64k). Two things to check:\n1. **`nvidia-smi`** — confirm `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0` on the server is actually the **48 GB 6000 Ada and free** (if GPU 0 is a different/smaller/busy card, 64k OOMs).\n2. **Quick bisect** — run the same diagnostic with `CP_T=32768` (s=8, half the memory). If 32k works and 64k OOMs, it's pure memory scaling — and it may mean the attention isn't fully flash (materializing O(T²) at 64k), which would blow up fast.\n\n## Also: sync the updated driver\nI made the driver **capture and print the evaluator's stderr** on death, so future runs show the real cause automatically. Pull the updated `Tests/bluscriptcp/longrope_search.py` to the server (it's the same file, just re-synced).\n\n## If it's OOM, quick unblock options\n- **Use both GPUs via CP=2 for the search** — but that needs the CP-eval wiring I described (allreduce fitness). This is the *right* fix for 64k if one GPU can't hold it.\n- **Drop to s=8 (32k)** — fits comfortably on one 48 GB card, gives a real LongRoPE result now while we sort out 64k.\n- **Point `GPU` at the actual free 6000 Ada** if GPU 0 isn't it.\n\nRun the diagnostic and paste the tail — that tells us definitively whether it's OOM, a kernel constraint, or something else, and I'll fix the right thing."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_read_input_tokens":729087,"output_tokens":2182,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2182,"cache_read_input_tokens":729087,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2173},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbaFgHwCLu2ywCxtkUdS","type":"assistant","uuid":"d8290bfb-0c96-431a-8a65-628cc512598b","timestamp":"2026-08-01T06:43:15.450Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
