{"parentUuid":"401caadd-d15b-4f02-8d52-4c4c44386f0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbawJDW4d7XHYkwcH1KK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found the two root causes:\n\n1. **The notebook `merge=keep-local` driver isn't actually active on your machines.** `.gitattributes` says `graph_*.ipynb merge=keep-local`, but `keep-local` is a *custom driver* whose definition lives in each repo's **local** `.git/config` — which is **not committed**. So on the server (and any fresh clone) the driver is undefined → git falls back to a normal 3-way merge → conflict. That's why your notebooks keep colliding.\n\n2. **`.log` files and `.mdfiles/output.md` are tracked** — they were committed *before* the ignore rules, and `.gitignore` doesn't untrack already-tracked files. `.gitignore` also has **no `*.log` rule**, so all those `Tests/.../logs/*.log` diverge and conflict.\n\n## Fix — 3 steps (you run the git parts; I edit the ignore file)\n\n**Step 1 — activate the notebook driver on BOTH machines** (one-time, per machine):\n```bash\ngit config merge.keep-local.driver true\n```\nNow `git pull` auto-keeps your local notebook, no conflict.\n\n**Step 2 — I'll add the missing ignore patterns:**"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4007,"cache_read_input_tokens":744128,"output_tokens":3261,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4007,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3261,"cache_read_input_tokens":744128,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4007,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4007},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbawCKYgM8PWdpzGrprQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"14802660-c