s, `output.md`, and notebooks stop conflicting because git either ignores them (logs/outputs) or auto-keeps your local copy (notebooks).\\n\\n## One caveat to know\\n`keep-local` means **your local notebook always wins on pull** — the other machine's notebook changes are discarded. That's correct for your workflow (each machine plots its own local CSVs). If you ever need to actually share notebook *code* across machines, do it deliberately (copy the file, or switch to `nbstripout` which strips outputs so only code is versioned). Want me to set up `nbstripout` instead if you'd rather version the notebook code cleanly?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":50},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c92af9c3-1c79-4bc2-8c80-ab54a803b1f9","timestamp":"2026-08-01T06:53:19.979Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
