{"parentUuid":"137585a9-ace5-4c68-97c4-be47f3edeb8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cdbbkm5qedUPL3j9vypTw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82,"cache_read_input_tokens":771869,"output_tokens":3654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3654,"cache_read_input_tokens":771869,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbbkcHzsNPveqBHBizQS","type":"assistant","uuid":"a86c5e4e-3427-49de-8d03-4c21d181faa2","timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:03:13.577Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a86c5e4e-3427-49de-8d03-4c21d181faa2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cdbbkm5qedUPL3j9vypTw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Deep breath — **you can't lose committed work here.** \"Behind\" just means \"needs to pull,\" not \"lost.\" Pushing from the server updates the shared remote (origin); it never deletes local's commits. So there's no danger — you just need to funnel both sides through origin in the right order.\n\n## Your current state\n- **Local:** has your LongRoPE work (ahead of origin).\n- **Server:** just committed the cleanup (ahead of origin too, on a *different* commit).\n- They've **diverged** — each has a commit the other lacks. That's fine; git merges them.\n\n## The clean sequence (no force-push, no loss)\n\n**1. Server — push the cleanup:**\n```bash\ngit push\n# if REJECTED (\"non-fast-forward\"): someone updated origin first, so:\ngit pull --no-edit   # brings origin's changes in (notebooks auto-keep-local, logs ignored)\ngit push\n```\n\n**2. Local — get the cleanup, then send your work:**\n```bash\ngit status                      # if uncommitted changes: git add -A && git commit -m \"longrope work\"\ngit pull --no-edit              # merges the server's cleanup into local\ngit push                        # sends your LongRoPE work to origin\n```\n\n**3. Server — pull your work:**\n```bash\ngit pull --no-edit              # now the server has your local changes\n```\n\nAfter this, **origin, local, and server all match** — your local changes are on the server, and the cleanup is everywhere.\n\n## Why this is safe\n- Every `git pull` **merges** — it combines both histories, keeping all commits from both sides. Nothing is overwritten.\n- The only files that *could* conflict (notebooks, logs) are now handled: logs/pyc are ignored, and notebooks use `keep-local` (make sure `git config merge.keep-local.driver true` is set on **both** machines, or notebooks will conflict again).\n\n## Simplest rule going forward\nOn each machine, before you start work: **`git pull`**. When you finish: **`git commit -am \"...\"` then `git push`**. Since the machine-specific junk is now ignored, `pull`/`push` stay clean — no more stash dance.\n\nIf any `git pull` reports a conflict on a **real source file** (not a log/notebook), paste it and I'll tell you how to resolve it."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82,"cache_read_input_tokens":771869,"output_tokens":3654,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3654,"cache_read_input_tokens":771869,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbbkcHzsNPveqBHBizQS","type":"assistant","uuid":"009b5c69-6f73-42cf-ab64-4c3edb4e2079","timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:03:22.679Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
