n, local, and server all match** — your local changes are on the server, and the cleanup is everywhere.\\n\\n## Why this is safe\\n- Every `git pull` **merges** — it combines both histories, keeping all commits from both sides. Nothing is overwritten.\\n- The only files that *could* conflict (notebooks, logs) are now handled: logs/pyc are ignored, and notebooks use `keep-local` (make sure `git config merge.keep-local.driver true` is set on **both** machines, or notebooks will conflict again).\\n\\n## Simplest rule going forward\\nOn each machine, before you start work: **`git pull`**. When you finish: **`git commit -am \\\"...\\\"` then `git push`**. Since the machine-specific junk is now ignored, `pull`/`push` stay clean — no more stash dance.\\n\\nIf any `git pull` reports a conflict on a **real source file** (not a log/notebook), paste it and I'll tell you how to resolve it.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":50},"type":"attachment","uuid":"28955017-a43c-4af6-9952-2b486a9b94ac","timestamp":"2026-08-01T07:03:23.044Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
