{"parentUuid":"d182922a-8c57-4223-af23-ef20fd6cfb05","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbiiySFLCxjqhkoYwLRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2311,"cache_read_input_tokens":791452,"output_tokens":1285,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":791452,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbiisQbwMezLCWGTYG8S","type":"assistant","uuid":"346dcc1d-006d-41c7-b24f-27833044c38a","timestamp":"2026-08-01T08:34:03.299Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"346dcc1d-006d-41c7-b24f-27833044c38a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbiiySFLCxjqhkoYwLRp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That's the clue: `credential.helper` returned **nothing** — there's no credential helper, so an HTTPS push has to prompt for a username + token on the terminal, and when that prompt can't show (pasted commands / non-interactive), it just hangs.\n\n**Fastest fix — force the prompt and log in:**\n```bash\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push\n```\nWhen it asks:\n- **Username:** `adhityablubridge`\n- **Password:** a **Personal Access Token** (github.com → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → generate one with `repo` scope). Paste the token here — not your GitHub password.\n\n**So you don't retype the token every push**, save it once:\n```bash\ngit config credential.helper store\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push     # enter username + token once; it's cached in ~/.git-credentials\n```\n(`store` keeps it in plaintext in your home dir; use `cache` instead if you prefer it only held in memory for a while.)\n\n**Cleaner long-term — switch to SSH** (no tokens, no prompts) if the server has an SSH key on your GitHub account:\n```bash\ngit remote set-url origin git@github.com:adhityablubridge/Context_Parallelism.git\ngit push\n```\nIf you haven't added the server's key to GitHub yet: `cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` (or `id_rsa.pub`), add it at github.com → Settings → SSH keys, then push. If there's no key, `ssh-keygen -t ed25519` first.\n\nAny of these gets the push through. Once it succeeds, `git pull` on your local machine to converge — then you're finally back to the actual work (rebuild + s=16 run)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2311,"cache_read_input_tokens":791452,"output_tokens":1285,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2311,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1285,"cache_read_input_tokens":791452,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2311},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbiisQbwMezLCWGTYG8S","type":"assistant","uuid":"28596696-996b-4291-850f-ea006218e0b8","timestamp":"2026-08-01T08:34:10.364Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"28596696-996b-4291-850f-ea006218e0b8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"b46a09d5-e217-4fcc-8a31-404ffd021060","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"e215a682-a113-4088-add4-fe53399ca884\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"That's the clue: `credential.helper` returned **nothing** — there's no credential helper, so an HTTPS push has to prompt for a username + token on the terminal, and when that prompt can't show (pasted commands / non-interactive), it just hangs.\\n\\n**Fastest fix — force the prompt and log in:**\\n```bash\\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push\\n```\\nWhen it asks:\\n- **Username:** `adhityablubridge`\\n- **Password:** a **Personal Access Token** (github.com → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens → generate one with `repo` scope). Paste the token here — not your GitHub password.\\n\\n**So you don't retype the token every push**, save it once:\\n```bash\\ngit config credential.helper store\\nGIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push     # enter username + token once; it's cached in ~/.git-credentials\\n```\\n(`store` keeps it in plaintext in your home dir; use `cache` instead if you prefer it only held in memory for a while.)\\n\\n**Cleaner long-term — switch to SSH** (no tokens, no prompts) if the server has an SSH key on your GitHub account:\\n```bash\\ngit remote set-url origin git@github.com:adhityablubridge/Context_Parallelism.git\\ngit push\\n```\\nIf you haven't added the server's key to GitHub yet: `cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub` (or `id_rsa.pub`), add it at github.com → Settings → SSH keys, then push. If there's no key, `ssh-keygen -t ed25519` first.\\n\\nAny of these gets the push through. Once it succeeds, `git pull` on your local machine to converge — then you're finally back to the actual work (rebuild + s=16 run).\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":45},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dbf9f824-14aa-4c4a-8fdc-4c27f838e235","timestamp":"2026-08-01T08:34:10.561Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
