{"parentUuid":"91664d01-3596-44b8-9663-0b20cce79ad9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbinMUdqgyjvE6Hvtbdv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two possibilities for what you're looking at:\n\n**If you see `Username for 'https://github.com':`** — type:\n- Username: `adhityablubridge` → Enter\n- `Password for 'https://...':` → paste your **Personal Access Token** and press Enter. **The token won't show as you type/paste — that's normal.** It's not echoed for security; just paste and hit Enter.\n\n**If it's still sitting there with NO prompt after ~10 seconds** — it's hanging (not prompting). Ctrl+C and let's switch to SSH, which avoids this entirely:\n```bash\n# check for an existing key first\nls ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub ~/.ssh/id_rsa.pub 2>/dev/null\n```\n- **If a key exists:** print it (`cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub`), add it at github.com → Settings → SSH and GPG keys → New SSH key, then:\n  ```bash\n  git remote set-url origin git@github.com:adhityablubridge/Context_Parallelism.git\n  git push\n  ```\n- **If no key:** make one, then add the `.pub` to GitHub as above:\n  ```bash\n  ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"server\" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N \"\"\n  cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub\n  ```\n\nTell me which one you're seeing (a `Username:` prompt, or dead silence), and I'll take you the rest of the way."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1355,"cache_read_input_tokens":793763,"output_tokens":1255,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1355,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1255,"cache_read_input_tokens":793763,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1355,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1355},"type":"message"}],"sp