{"parentUuid":"c6815be0-fa9a-41b8-9398-319ea1a38e99","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cdbj7n8VTq3ibPVeg8819","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That explains the hang — you're in the **VS Code integrated terminal**, and its **GitHub Authentication extension** hijacked the git auth (that's the `GIT_ASKPASS` VS Code injects). It's waiting on you to complete a browser login.\n\n**Easiest path — click `Yes`** on that \"device code\" notification. VS Code will then show you a short code (like `ABCD-1234`) and offer to open **github.com/login/device**:\n1. Click through / copy the code.\n2. Open **https://github.com/login/device** (on the server browser, or even on your laptop — any browser).\n3. Enter the code, authorize the app.\n4. The stuck `git push` completes automatically, and VS Code caches it so future pushes just work — **no PAT needed.**\n\n(Ignore the \"Kubectl not found\" notification — unrelated.)\n\n**If browser/device auth is a hassle on the server**, cancel it (`No`) and force a plain-terminal token prompt instead, which bypasses VS Code's helper:\n```bash\nenv -u GIT_ASKPASS -u SSH_ASKPASS -u VSCODE_GIT_ASKPASS_NODE GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push\n```\n→ `Username:` = `adhityablubridge`, password = a Personal Access Token.\n\n**Or the permanent no-prompt fix — SSH:**\n```bash\ngit remote set-url origin git@github.com:adhityablubridge/Context_Parallelism.git\ngit push\n```\n\nClicking **Yes** and doing the device-code flow is the quickest right now. Once it's authorized, your push lands and you're finally through the git saga — back to rebuilding the binary and the s=16 run."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2666,"cache_read_input_tokens":796381,"output_tokens":1581,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_