{"parentUuid":"3319212c-3834-4b87-90da-9d7d65c43e9a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbjeJgrH8G3ji1gdoqHP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2577,"cache_read_input_tokens":800842,"output_tokens":1497,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2577,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1497,"cache_read_input_tokens":800842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2577,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2577},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbjeE2ZdbPH4h3akyP1c","type":"assistant","uuid":"2e3fb6c0-5893-4036-ac78-73bc5fe7047f","timestamp":"2026-08-01T08:46:08.267Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"2e3fb6c0-5893-4036-ac78-73bc5fe7047f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbjeJgrH8G3ji1gdoqHP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The push **succeeded** — look at line 12: `2615900..f8da71e main -> main`. The server's merge (cleanup + your local work) is now on origin. 🎉 The git saga is basically over.\n\nThe only hiccup: you then switched the remote to **SSH**, which failed with `Permission denied (publickey)` — the server has no SSH key registered with GitHub. So **revert the remote back to HTTPS** (which just worked):\n```bash\ngit remote set-url origin https://github.com/adhityablubridge/Context_Parallelism.git\n```\n\n**Cache the token so you stop getting prompted** (you used the bypass command, not the `store` one, so it wasn't saved):\n```bash\ngit config credential.helper store\nenv -u GIT_ASKPASS GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=1 git push    # nothing to push now; or on the next real push — enter token once, then cached\n```\nAfter one cached auth, plain `git push` works even in the VS Code terminal.\n\n**Finally, converge your local machine:**\n```bash\ngit config pull.rebase false\ngit pull\n```\nNow local, server, and origin all match.\n\nThat's it — everything's synced. If you want SSH later (no tokens ever), generate a key on the server and add it to GitHub:\n```bash\nssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C \"server\" -f ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -N \"\"\ncat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub   # add this at github.com -> Settings -> SSH keys\n```\n…then switch the remote back to the `git@github.com:` URL. But that's optional — HTTPS + stored token is fine.\n\nNow back to the actual work: on the server, **rebuild the binary** (`make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp`) so the LongRoPE resident evaluator is live, then launch the s=16 run."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2577,"cache_read_input_tokens":800842,"output_tokens":1497,"