{"parentUuid":"a86cc313-b017-44c7-8c08-7395848ecc93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbjppzXaNa1EVG4teXBo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Good news first: **the server's push worked and your local pull fetched it** (`2615900..f8da71e`). The only thing blocking the merge is **uncommitted `.gitignore` edits on your local machine** — git won't overwrite them. Easy to resolve, one time:\n\n```bash\ngit stash          # set aside your local .gitignore edit\ngit pull           # brings in f8da71e cleanly\ngit stash pop      # reapply your local .gitignore edit on top\n```\n\nThen one of two things:\n- **Applies cleanly** → done. If there's now a small change, `git add .gitignore && git commit -m \"local gitignore\" && git push`.\n- **Says `CONFLICT` in `.gitignore`** (both sides added ignore rules) → open it, delete the `<<<<<<<`/`=======`/`>>>>>>>` marker lines but **keep all the actual rules from both sides** (duplicate ignore lines are harmless), then:\n  ```bash\n  git add .gitignore\n  git commit --no-edit\n  git push\n  ```\n\nThis preserves every ignore rule and finishes the sync — local, server, origin all match.\n\nTwo side notes:\n- The `bash: .../snap/code/.../bin/env: No such file or directory` in your other terminal is an unrelated **VS Code snap PATH glitch**, not git — ignore it (or open a fresh terminal / `hash -r`).\n- After this, everything's clean. On the **server**, the real next step is still: `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp` (rebuild so the LongRoPE resident evaluator is live), then launch the s=16 run.\n\nIf `git stash pop` throws the conflict, paste the `.gitignore` conflict section and I'll tell you the exact final content to keep."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4753,"cache_read_input_tokens":804916,"output_tokens":4305,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_re