{"parentUuid":"7797f5d7-2abf-47e3-906d-2414fe052158","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbnWthcwmH9GxyoFytE7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Normal case now — someone (the server) pushed to origin after your local last synced, so your local is behind. Just **pull then push**:\n```bash\ngit pull\ngit push\n```\n\n`git pull` merges origin's newer commit with your `51370b0`. Two outcomes:\n- **Clean merge** → `git push` succeeds. Done.\n- **Conflict on `.gitignore`** (both machines edited it — likely) → keep **all** rules from both sides (delete the `<<<<`/`====`/`>>>>` markers, keep every ignore line), then:\n  ```bash\n  git add .gitignore\n  git commit --no-edit\n  git push\n  ```\n\nThis is just the normal \"integrate remote changes before pushing\" flow — not the old mess. With the ignores now in place, it'll be quick.\n\nIf the pull shows a conflict on anything other than `.gitignore`, paste it and I'll tell you which side to keep. Otherwise you're set — then get the server rebuilt (`make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 bluscript-cp`) and launch s=16."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_read_input_tokens":826536,"output_tokens":991,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":991,"cache_read_input_tokens":826536,"cache_creation_input_tokens":995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":995},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdbnWnJA3L6dVKx9rS3bb","type":"assistant","uuid":"6662573a-dbde-44ac-b16e-b69ff53a1173","timestamp":"2026-08-01T09:23:49.978Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/ho