{"parentUuid":"31dc22cb-7b19-4f79-bf65-e2c31612a7b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbnsDgBvLL1578wvbGok","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Added `*.ipynb` to `.gitignore` (and removed a duplicate block the merge left). Now untrack the notebooks — this keeps your local copy on disk but removes them from git/remote. Do it on **both machines** so neither loses its version.\n\n## On LOCAL (do this first)\n```bash\ngit rm --cached graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb graph_gpt2_cp.ipynb   # untrack; files STAY on disk\ngit add .gitignore\ngit commit -m \"stop tracking notebooks; keep per-machine, ignore *.ipynb\"\ngit push\n```\nAfter this, the notebooks are **gone from origin** (what you wanted), but still sitting in your local folder — now ignored.\n\n## On SERVER (after the local push)\n```bash\ngit pull\n```\n- If it merges clean → done.\n- If it says **`CONFLICT (modify/delete): graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb`** (origin deleted it, server modified it) → resolve by **keeping the file, dropping it from git**:\n  ```bash\n  git rm --cached graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb graph_gpt2_cp.ipynb   # file stays on disk, out of git\n  git commit --no-edit\n  git push\n  ```\n\n## Result\n- **Remote (origin):** no notebooks — clean.\n- **Each machine:** keeps its own `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb`, untracked and ignored → they never conflict again, and each plots its own local CSVs independently.\n\nNotes:\n- `git rm --cached` (with `--cached`) **only removes from git, never deletes the file** — your work is safe on both machines.\n- The old `merge=keep-local` lines in `.gitattributes` are now dead (notebooks aren't tracked), but harmless — you can leave them or delete those two lines later.\n- If you ever *do* want to share a notebook deliberately, `git add -f graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb` overrides the ignore for that one commit."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_c