{"parentUuid":"bf160749-5e35-4444-91f9-ddd7f22a97ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdboyN41LAgR7wMfYLXv7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's running correctly — everything's working:\n- Resident evaluator is **live** at T=65536 ✓\n- It's evaluating the **seed candidates**: `lam0=16, lam_last=16` is the **PI seed** (uniform λ=s), and `lam0=1, lam_last=16` is the **NTK/YaRN seed** (monotone ramp). Exactly as designed.\n\nSo the search is underway on the initial population (16 candidates). Next in the log you'll see `[gen 0] seeds -> best PPL …` once all 16 are scored (each 64k eval is ~30–60s, so gen 0 takes ~10–15 min), then per-generation lines.\n\nHarmless note: `tail: inotify resources exhausted … reverting to polling` is just a **system limit on file watches** (common on a busy server with VS Code) — it only affects `tail`, not your run. The `nohup` job (PID 1476132) runs independently; you can close the terminal and it keeps going. To re-attach later: `tail -f lr_s16_alone.log`.\n\nWhat to watch:\n- **`[gen 0] seeds -> best PPL X`** — X should be **well below the 305** you saw for λ=1 (the seeds are real interpolations, not plain extrapolation). That's your first sanity check.\n- **`[gen N] best PPL … no_improve=K`** — best PPL trending down; when `no_improve` hits `4`, it early-stops.\n- Then `BEST PPL … -> longrope_best.txt`, followed by the 64k fine-tune (run 80) and eval.\n\nLet it run. Paste the `[gen 0] seeds` line when it appears and I'll confirm the seed PPLs look right (they should be a big drop from 305). If GPU 5 memory is tight during the fine-tune stage later, that's the one place it could OOM — but the search/eval clearly fit."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2137,"cache_read_input_tokens":841860,"output_tokens":1377,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests"