{"parentUuid":"b6df5d31-f273-429d-91e3-5e6d69528689","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdbzwKd8VsooC29VcziSy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The **search finished fine** (~2.4h) — but two things happened:\n\n## 1. The search converged flat at the NTK seed\n```\ngen 0 seeds: PI=337.8, NTK=267.2, YaRN=280.0  → best 267.2\ngen 1–4: best stayed 267.2 (no_improve → 4) → early-stopped\n```\nThe GA found **nothing better than the NTK seed**, and PPL **267 at 64k is poor** (your base is ~180 PPL at 4k). This confirms what I flagged: **64× extension is too aggressive for a 48M model** — the interpolation search can't rescue it because the model simply can't represent 64k context well, regardless of `λ`.\n\n## 2. The fine-tune OOM'd at 64k\n```\n[ALLOCATOR] cudaMallocAsync(size=13186891776) failed: out of memory  → CUDA OOM\n```\nThat 13.2 GB alloc is the 64k logits tensor. The **search (forward-only) fit**, but the **fine-tune (forward + backward + gradients)** doesn't fit even the 48 GB card at 64k physical. This is exactly the memory-heavy stage I warned about for `COMPOSE=alone`.\n\n## What to do — I strongly recommend dropping to s=8 (32k)\n`s=16` is both too big for the fine-tune memory **and** too aggressive for quality. **`s=8` (4k→32k)** is the sweet spot:\n- 32k fine-tune (~13 GB logits fwd+grad) **fits** the 48 GB card.\n- 32× extension is far more reasonable for a 48M model → the search will likely find real improvement.\n\n```bash\nBASE_RUN=30 BASE_MAX_STEPS=917 GPU=5 S=8 COMPOSE=alone \\\n  DATA_ROOT=/mnt/volgrp03/3rd_floor/Adhitya/CP/Context_Parallelism/Data_Loader/Data \\\n  nohup bash Tests/bluscriptcp/run_longrope_pipeline.sh > lr_s8_alone.log 2>&1 &\n```\n(Or `S=4` for 16k — guaranteed to fit and even better quality.)\n\n## Alternatives if you specifically want s=16 (64k)\n- **Salvage a result now (no fine-tune, no OOM):** eval the base with the cache you already searched — this is the legitimate \"LongRoPE without fine-tuning\" curve:\n  ```bash\n  ARCH=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0\"\n  env $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_T=65536 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 \\\n      CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS=longrope_best.txt CP_CKPT_RESUME=30 \\\n      CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_longrope_x16_searchonly.csv CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=5 \\\n      CP_DATA_ROOT=/mnt/volgrp03/3rd_floor/Adhitya/CP/Context_Parallelism/Data_Loader/Data \\\n      LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/lib:BluTrain/Profiler/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH \\\n      mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\n  ```\n- **CP=2 for the 64k fine-tune** — split the 64k sequence across your 2 GPUs. LongRoPE-alone *is* CP-compatible for training (contiguous positions), but the pipeline runs `NP=1` — I'd need to add an `NP`/`CP_SIZE` option to the fine-tune step. Say the word and I'll wire it.\n\nMy call: **run `S=8` now** (best result-per-effort, fits memory), and separately do the search-only 64k eval above if you want an `s=16` data point for the curve. Nothing was lost — `longrope_best.txt` for s=16 is on disk, and run 30 is untouched (the OOM was on run 200, which just won't have valid steps)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834934,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"output_tokens":6547,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":834934,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6547,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":834934,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":834934},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdbzwCRHskzW1UiD9Dojq","type":"assistant","uuid":"b