{"parentUuid":"503d5dcd-8163-457a-9b07-7a940a311704","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdcDtZN4CkRyBLR7QxZRb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Just the **search stage** — nothing else finishes in 10 min. At that point you'll see:\n```\n[gen 4] converged: no PPL improvement > 0.05 for 4 gens -- stopping\nBEST PPL 202.63  n_hat=0  -> longrope_best.txt\n```\ni.e. `longrope_best.txt` (the searched λ/n̂) gets written, and the pipeline **immediately moves to the fine-tune stage** — you'll see the config banner and `Starting training...`.\n\nSo the ~10-min mark is exactly the moment to **watch for OOM**: right after `Starting training...` at 32k. If it prints step lines (`step 918 | loss …`), the fine-tune fits and it'll run ~2h. If it prints `cudaMallocAsync … out of memory` like the 64k run did, the fine-tune needs CP=2 or a drop to `s=4`.\n\nStill ahead after that 10 min: **fine-tune (~2h) + eval (~5 min)**. So the *whole* `s=8` pipeline (with a usable `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv`) is ~2–3h out. Keep `tail -f lr_s8_alone.log` on it through the `Starting training...` line to catch the OOM early if it happens."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":871112,"output_tokens":847,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":847,"cache_read_input_tokens":871112,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2481,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2481},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdcDtRCRAM9t9gC19eUwb","type":"assistant","uuid":"daaa1691-01f4-43cd-b005-1b0a45575b3a","timestamp":"2026-08-01T14:56:31.963Z","effort"