{"parentUuid":"1bf16f36-d728-45f5-b579-f64bf6955457","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdcDyQ6puAcBwBjyvkGRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":873593,"output_tokens":983,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":873593,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdcDyH5ABg2u9DAYN294v","type":"assistant","uuid":"ffc5a975-a0b7-428a-a8eb-4aa547a7db13","timestamp":"2026-08-01T14:57:33.877Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ffc5a975-a0b7-428a-a8eb-4aa547a7db13","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdcDyQ6puAcBwBjyvkGRA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Correct — the **pipeline outputs a CSV, not a graph.** The final step (eval) writes `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv` (per-position PPL). You make the graph yourself in the **notebook** — exactly like you did for the x16 curve you showed me.\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. Pipeline finishes (search → fine-tune → eval) → writes `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv`.\n2. In `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb`, add that file to the `CURVES` dict and run the cell → you get the plot.\n\nTiming on the CSV: it's written by the **eval stage**, which is the **last** step — so **not in 10 min**. In 10 min only the *search* finishes (writes `longrope_best.txt`, an intermediate). The CSV comes after the full chain (~2–3h): search → 32k fine-tune → eval.\n\nSo:\n- **~10 min:** search done (`longrope_best.txt`), fine-tune starts.\n- **~2–3h:** eval done → `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv` written → **then** you plot it in the notebook.\n\n(The x16 graph you already have is the search-only CSV you generated separately — you can overlay the x8 curve on the same plot once its CSV lands, plus the plain-RoPE/YaRN baselines if you ran those.)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_read_input_tokens":873593,"output_tokens":983,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":983,"cache_read_input_tokens":873593,"cache_creation_input_tokens":861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":861},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdcDyH5ABg2u9DAYN294v","type":"assistant","uuid":"c2a9c7d1-74e7-4304-9e0c-80890225e804","timestamp":"2026-08-01T14:57:39.551Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"c2a9c7d1-74e7-4304-9e0c-80890225e804","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"d95eb227-40b1-4201-b885-7bd353e124e1","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"abde2bf3-5a37-42f0-9eea-65ad17b5df9b\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Correct — the **pipeline outputs a CSV, not a graph.** The final step (eval) writes `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv` (per-position PPL). You make the graph yourself in the **notebook** — exactly like you did for the x16 curve you showed me.\\n\\nSo the flow is:\\n1. Pipeline finishes (search → fine-tune → eval) → writes `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv`.\\n2. In `graph_bluscript_cp.ipynb`, add that file to the `CURVES` dict and run the cell → you get the plot.\\n\\nTiming on the CSV: it's written by the **eval stage**, which is the **last** step — so **not in 10 min**. In 10 min only the *search* finishes (writes `longrope_best.txt`, an intermediate). The CSV comes after the full chain (~2–3h): search → 32k fine-tune → eval.\\n\\nSo:\\n- **~10 min:** search done (`longrope_best.txt`), fine-tune starts.\\n- **~2–3h:** eval done → `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv` written → **then** you plot it in the notebook.\\n\\n(The x16 graph you already have is the search-only CSV you generated separately — you can overlay the x8 curve on the same plot once its CSV lands, plus the plain-RoPE/YaRN baselines if you ran those.)\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs