{"parentUuid":"9fbd749d-f20d-4312-b728-4f3d9939dc1b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_341508","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 370 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f227572e-b728-4308-90f6-9db95be28f91","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:14:04.099Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"f227572e-b728-4308-90f6-9db95be28f91","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdfZQmapg5FECwtQRtCpY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":886989,"output_tokens":3869,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3869,"cache_read_input_tokens":886989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1758},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdfZQgdv6tkS1r6QWRMR6","type":"assistant","uuid":"04b8b608-8a7c-4f29-a74c-0d81fe7d1204","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:14:48.140Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"04b8b608-8a7c-4f29-a74c-0d81fe7d1204","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdfZQmapg5FECwtQRtCpY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The clean way to tell **what a run is** and **whether it was overwritten** is its two artifacts: the **config** (what it was) and the **checkpoint step range** (whether anything trained over it).\n\n## 1. Identify which log is the \"naive\"/base run\nThe base is **run 30** (your `BASE_RUN`). Check its config to confirm it's the plain 4k base (no LongRoPE, no YaRN):\n```bash\ncat CP_BluScreipt_Training_logs/CP_Training_log30_config.txt | grep -iE \"context_length|T:|YARN|LONGROPE|max_steps|resumed\"\n```\n- Base/naive → `context_length: 4096`, no `LongRoPE`, `YARN_SCALE` absent/1, `max_steps: 917`.\n\n## 2. Check it wasn't overwritten (trained over)\n```bash\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run30_step_*.ckpt\n```\n- **Top step = 917** → untouched base. ✓ Not overwritten.\n- **Any step > 917** → something resumed run 30 and trained on top of it (overwritten/extended).\n\n## The rule (so you know what's safe)\n- A run is **only overwritten** if you launch with **`CP_CKPT_RESUME=<that number>` + `CP_CKPT=1` + `CP_MAX_STEPS` past its last step**. That resumes and appends new checkpoints.\n- **Eval runs never overwrite anything** — `CP_EVAL_PPL=1` writes its log/config to `/dev/null` and only produces the `CP_EVAL_OUT` CSV. So all your search-only/baseline evals left run 30 (and its log) **untouched**.\n- Each run number has its **own** `CP_Training_log<N>.csv` — a new run number can't clobber a different one's log.\n\n## Your run map (from what we did)\n- **run 30** = base (naive) — the reference, should still top out at step 917.\n- **run 81** = LongRoPE x8 fine-tuned (your manual fine-tune, steps 917→1217).\n- **run 200** = the failed s=16 OOM — just a *copy* of run 30's step_917 (no real training; safe to delete).\n\nSo: `grep` the config + `ls` the checkpoint steps of run 30. If its config says 4k/no-LongRoPE and its top checkpoint is step 917, the naive base is intact and never overwritten.\n\nOne separate thing to watch — the **eval CSVs** (`ppl_*.csv`): those *do* overwrite if you reuse the same `CP_EVAL_OUT` filename. `ls -la ppl_*.csv` and check each has a distinct name (e.g. `ppl_base_noyarn_64k.csv`, `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv`) so no baseline curve clobbered another.\n\nIf you tell me which specific run number you mean by \"naive,\" I'll confirm exactly whether it's intact."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache_read_input_tokens":886989,"output_tokens":3869,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1758,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3869,"cache_read_input_tokens":886989,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1758,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1758},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdfZQgdv6tkS1r6QWRMR6","type":"assistant","uuid":"facad8c3-b52f-4a4f-a2b6-4864a9414ce8","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:15:00.624Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"facad8c3-b52f-4a4f-a2b6-4864a9414ce8","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"5d680c53-415c-42a6-be44-3dace96ff1e8","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"35284d16-c1ae-40c6-8ecf-446242c88498\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"The clean way to tell **what a run is** and **whether it was overwritten** is its two artifacts: the **config** (what it was) and the **checkpoint step range** (whether anything trained over it).\\n\\n## 1. Identify which log is the \\\"naive\\\"/base run\\nThe base is **run 30** (your `BASE_RUN`). Check its config to confirm it's the plain 4k base (no LongRoPE, no YaRN):\\n```bash\\ncat CP_BluScreipt_Training_logs/CP_Training_log30_config.txt | grep -iE \\\"context_length|T:|YARN|LONGROPE|max_steps|resumed\\\"\\n```\\n- Base/naive → `context_length: 4096`, no `LongRoPE`, `YARN_SCALE` absent/1, `max_steps: 917`.\\n\\n## 2. Check it wasn't overwritten (trained over)\\n```bash\\nls checkpoints_bluscriptcp/blumodelcp_run30_step_*.ckpt\\n```\\n- **Top step = 917** → untouched base. ✓ Not overwritten.\\n- **Any step > 917** → something resumed run 30 and trained on top of it (overwritten/extended).\\n\\n## The rule (so you know what's safe)\\n- A run is **only overwritten** if you launch with **`CP_CKPT_RESUME=<that number>` + `CP_CKPT=1` + `CP_MAX_STEPS` past its last step**. That resumes and appends new checkpoints.\\n- **Eval runs never overwrite anything** — `CP_EVAL_PPL=1` writes its log/config to `/dev/null` and only produces the `CP_EVAL_OUT` CSV. So all your search-only/baseline evals left run 30 (and its log) **untouched**.\\n- Each run number has its **own** `CP_Training_log<N>.csv` — a new run number can't clobber a different one's log.\\n\\n## Your run map (from what we did)\\n- **run 30** = base (naive) — the reference, should still top out at step 917.\\n- **run 81** = LongRoPE x8 fine-tuned (your manual fine-tune, steps 917→1217).\\n- **run 200** = the failed s=16 OOM — just a *copy* of run 30's step_917 (no real training; safe to delete).\\n\\nSo: `grep` the config + `ls` the checkpoint steps of run 30. If its config says 4k/no-LongRoPE and its top checkpoint is step 917, the naive base is intact and never overwritten.\\n\\nOne separate thing to watch — the **eval CSVs** (`ppl_*.csv`): those *do* overwrite if you reuse the same `CP_EVAL_OUT` filename. `ls -la ppl_*.csv` and check each has a distinct name (e.g. `ppl_base_noyarn_64k.csv`, `ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv`) so no baseline curve clobbered another.\\n\\nIf you tell me which specific run number you mean by \\\"naive,\\\" I'll confirm exactly whether it's intact.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":38},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cf05d224-7127-4d64-9b1d-e8a049d4ce91","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:15:00.716Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
