{"parentUuid":"572f83ea-b69b-4335-9734-c94515254f5c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_372104","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 371 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ca6440e3-244e-43aa-a1fd-ceb06bf20233","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:27:24.261Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"ca6440e3-244e-43aa-a1fd-ceb06bf20233","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdfaRmKbKtpT8pQsVtVdC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4316,"cache_read_input_tokens":888747,"output_tokens":3951,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4316,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3951,"cache_read_input_tokens":888747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4316,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4316},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdfaRfcJ5hTU67X1cRLoX","type":"assistant","uuid":"b2f6ea1a-aae5-48d9-a5c4-c608d57cfdd1","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:28:00.536Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"b2f6ea1a-aae5-48d9-a5c4-c608d57cfdd1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdfaRmKbKtpT8pQsVtVdC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You **can't tell a CSV's origin from its contents** — the eval file is just `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl`, with no record of which config wrote it. So the only ways to know if `ppl_naive_x8.csv` is the real naive run or got clobbered by a LongRoPE eval are **filename + timestamp + magnitude**.\n\n## 1. Check the timestamp (on the server)\n```bash\nls -la --time-style=full-iso ppl_naive_x8.csv ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv\n```\n- If `ppl_naive_x8.csv`'s modified time matches when you ran a **LongRoPE** eval → it was overwritten.\n- If it's from the earlier naive-baseline sweep → it's intact.\n\n## 2. Sanity-check the magnitude\n```bash\nawk -F, 'NR>1 && $2>0 {s+=$4; n++} END{print \"mean PPL =\", s/n}' ppl_naive_x8.csv\n```\n- **Naive-with-YaRN** at 32k should be **elevated but flattish** (higher than fine-tuned).\n- **Naive-no-YaRN** would **blow up** (very high tail).\n- If it looks like a **LongRoPE** profile instead, it was overwritten.\n\n## The reliable fix: just regenerate it with an unambiguous name\nNaive baselines are cheap (~5 min at 32k) and deterministic — don't agonize, re-run:\n```bash\nARCH=\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0\"\n# naive = base run 30, NO LongRoPE. YaRN baseline (scale=8) at 32k:\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_T=32768 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=8 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=30 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_naive_yarn_x8_32k.csv CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=5 \\\n    CP_DATA_ROOT=/mnt/volgrp03/3rd_floor/Adhitya/CP/Context_Parallelism/Data_Loader/Data \\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/lib:BluTrain/Profiler/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH \\\n    mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\n```\n(no `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` = naive. Use `YARN_SCALE=1` instead for the *no-YaRN* naive that blows up.)\n\n## Going forward — stop the collisions\nYour folder has lots of ambiguous `ppl_*_x8.csv` from different rounds. Adopt one scheme so nothing overwrites, e.g.:\n```\nppl_<method>_x<S>_<T>.csv    →  ppl_naive_yarn_x8_32k.csv, ppl_longrope_alone_x8_32k.csv, ...\n```\nEach eval → a unique `CP_EVAL_OUT`. Since `*.csv` is gitignored, these stay local per machine and never conflict in git either.\n\nSo: check the timestamp to confirm the overwrite, but the fastest path is just to **regenerate the naive baseline into a fresh filename** — 5 minutes, and then you know exactly what it is. If you want, tell me the timestamps of `ppl_naive_x8.csv` vs your LongRoPE runs and I'll confirm whether it was clobbered."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4316,"cache_read_input_tokens":888747,"output_tokens":3951,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4316,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3951,"cache_read_input_tokens":888747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4316,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4316},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdfaRfcJ5hTU67X1cRLoX","type":"assistant","uuid":"9533a8a1-7d0c-48e6-ac00-cc3282f09f1b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:28:16.393Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"9533a8a1-7d0c-48e6-ac00-cc3282f09f1b","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"172e1601-bf11-412d-a9a0-7ae6208e1ce8","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"cd21e383-e288-4db0-ab0a-7fa300a44dbb\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"You **can't tell a CSV's origin from its contents** — the eval file is just `pos,count,mean_nll,ppl`, with no record of which config wrote it. So the only ways to know if `ppl_naive_x8.csv` is the real naive run or got clobbered by a LongRoPE eval are **filename + timestamp + magnitude**.\\n\\n## 1. Check the timestamp (on the server)\\n```bash\\nls -la --time-style=full-iso ppl_naive_x8.csv ppl_longrope_x8_alone.csv\\n```\\n- If `ppl_naive_x8.csv`'s modified time matches when you ran a **LongRoPE** eval → it was overwritten.\\n- If it's from the earlier naive-baseline sweep → it's intact.\\n\\n## 2. Sanity-check the magnitude\\n```bash\\nawk -F, 'NR>1 && $2>0 {s+=$4; n++} END{print \\\"mean PPL =\\\", s/n}' ppl_naive_x8.csv\\n```\\n- **Naive-with-YaRN** at 32k should be **elevated but flattish** (higher than fine-tuned).\\n- **Naive-no-YaRN** would **blow up** (very high tail).\\n- If it looks like a **LongRoPE** profile instead, it was overwritten.\\n\\n## The reliable fix: just regenerate it with an unambiguous name\\nNaive baselines are cheap (~5 min at 32k) and deterministic — don't agonize, re-run:\\n```bash\\nARCH=\\\"CP_SIZE=1 CP_N_EMBD=384 CP_N_LAYER=6 CP_N_HEAD=6 CP_N_KVHEAD=2 CP_FFN=1024 CP_WEIGHT_TYING=0\\\"\\n# naive = base run 30, NO LongRoPE. YaRN baseline (scale=8) at 32k:\\nenv $ARCH CP_EVAL_PPL=1 CP_T=32768 CP_B=1 CP_EVAL_WINDOWS=32 YARN_SCALE=8 YARN_ORIG_MAXPOS=4096 \\\\\\n    CP_CKPT_RESUME=30 CP_EVAL_OUT=ppl_naive_yarn_x8_32k.csv CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=5 \\\\\\n    CP_DATA_ROOT=/mnt/volgrp03/3rd_floor/Adhitya/CP/Context_Parallelism/Data_Loader/Data \\\\\\n    LD_LIBRARY_PATH=BluTrain/Tensor-Implementations/lib:BluTrain/Profiler/lib:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH \\\\\\n    mpirun -np 1 ./build/bluscriptCP_exec\\n```\\n(no `CP_LONGROPE_FACTORS` = naive. Use `YARN_SCALE=1` instead for the *no-YaRN* naive that blows up.)\\n\\n## Going forward — stop the collisions\\nYour folder has lots of ambiguous `ppl_*_x8.csv` from different rounds. Adopt one scheme so nothing overwrites, e.g.:\\n```\\nppl_<method>_x<S>_<T>.csv    →  ppl_naive_yarn_x8_32k.csv, ppl_longrope_alone_x8_32k.csv, ...\\n```\\nEach eval → a unique `CP_EVAL_OUT`. Since `*.csv` is gitignored, these stay local per machine and never conflict in git either.\\n\\nSo: check the timestamp to confirm the overwrite, but the fastest path is just to **regenerate the naive baseline into a fresh filename** — 5 minutes, and then you know exactly what it is. If you want, tell me the timestamps of `ppl_naive_x8.csv` vs your LongRoPE runs and I'll confirm whether it was clobbered.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":48},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4f7600de-c8d3-4f33-877c-696e03022d9b","timestamp":"2026-08-03T09:28:16.502Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
