{"parentUuid":"5dce58a4-3605-4e00-9923-7570ac9e9b0d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cdfxkeo2Zv8eg4zPMPD7w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Same as the run-81 fine-tune you just finished — because **YaRN has no search stage** (it's a fixed formula), so it's just **fine-tune + eval**, no ~1h GA on top.\n\n- **Fine-tune @32k (300 steps):** identical compute to run 81 → **whatever run 81's training took** (my estimate was ~1.5–2.5h; you saw the actual time).\n- **Eval @32k (32 windows):** ~5–10 min.\n\nSo **≈ run-81's fine-tune time + ~10 min**, and it skips the search entirely — so overall *faster* than the LongRoPE pipeline was.\n\nTo get the exact number, check how long run 81 trained:\n```bash\nhead -1 CP_BluScreipt_Training_logs/CP_Training_log81.csv   # or eyeball first/last step timestamps\n```\nor look at the `dt:` per-step time in the run-81 log × 300 steps. That's your YaRN-LCE fine-tune duration.\n\nSince it's a single fine-tune + eval (no search), you can just launch both back-to-back (the two commands I gave) with `nohup` and it'll be done in roughly that window."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4177,"cache_read_input_tokens":899244,"output_tokens":1183,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4177,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1183,"cache_read_input_tokens":899244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4177,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4177},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdfxkY8vycfZbyonwiXj1","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3261ee4-0b5b-4fe4-9c0a-315d1fb9020e","timestamp":"2026-08-03T14:20:30.420Z","effort":"low","userType":"externa