{"parentUuid":"a3261ee4-0b5b-4fe4-9c0a-315d1fb9020e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"7de0535d-aef6-45be-8051-532d62f6168d","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"a14d9774-cf8c-4ce2-9fa7-8cf2bab58ac7\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Same as the run-81 fine-tune you just finished — because **YaRN has no search stage** (it's a fixed formula), so it's just **fine-tune + eval**, no ~1h GA on top.\\n\\n- **Fine-tune @32k (300 steps):** identical compute to run 81 → **whatever run 81's training took** (my estimate was ~1.5–2.5h; you saw the actual time).\\n- **Eval @32k (32 windows):** ~5–10 min.\\n\\nSo **≈ run-81's fine-tune time + ~10 min**, and it skips the search entirely — so overall *faster* than the LongRoPE pipeline was.\\n\\nTo get the exact number, check how long run 81 trained:\\n```bash\\nhead -1 CP_BluScreipt_Training_logs/CP_Training_log81.csv   # or eyeball first/last step timestamps\\n```\\nor look at the `dt:` per-step time in the run-81 log × 300 steps. That's your YaRN-LCE fine-tune duration.\\n\\nSince it's a single fine-tune + eval (no search), you can just launch both back-to-back (the two commands I gave) with `nohup` and it'll be done in roughly that window.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":47},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a2e8a8da-7282-4901-8728-e0dda646b587","timestamp":"2026-08-03T14:20:30.550Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cla