{"parentUuid":"24bceb20-cb96-4d73-a0fc-fcad61c66a0e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"async_hook_response","processId":"async_hook_1588827","hookName":"Stop","hookEvent":"Stop","response":{},"stdout":"","stderr":"[ContinuousLearning] Session has 381 messages - evaluate for extractable patterns\n[ContinuousLearning] Save learned skills to: /home/blu-bridge25/.claude/skills/learned/\n","exitCode":0},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0ed93a81-f7cd-44ab-9d20-4cd5874dc419","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:02:42.462Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"0ed93a81-f7cd-44ab-9d20-4cd5874dc419","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhSMSdup1hSM19E7Yzx8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888922,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"output_tokens":4004,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4004,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdhSMMKvewAH8DCF7DNZc","type":"assistant","uuid":"35f09252-6d49-482f-913f-c92992c6e7e1","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:03:37.390Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"35f09252-6d49-482f-913f-c92992c6e7e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhSMSdup1hSM19E7Yzx8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"First, look closely: the gap is **tiny** — LongRoPE (blue) and YaRN-fine-tuned (green) nearly overlap, and both **clearly beat** the naive YaRN (orange). So LongRoPE isn't broken; it's just a hair behind YaRN. The ordering is exactly sensible: **YaRN-FT ≤ LongRoPE-FT ≪ naive-YaRN**.\n\nTwo concrete reasons it's slightly behind, both of which we can see in your run:\n\n## 1. The search found nothing better than the seeds\nYour s=8 search **converged flat at 202.63 from gen 0** (`no_improve` climbed straight to 4). The GA never beat the NTK/YaRN seed. For a **48M model at 8×**, the model is **capacity-limited, not interpolation-limited** — no choice of `λ` meaningfully helps, so the search just returns ~the seed. (It was also a deliberately small search with `CALIB=3`, i.e. noisy fitness.) So \"LongRoPE\" here is essentially **the NTK-seed cache**, not something the search improved.\n\n## 2. LongRoPE's cache omits YaRN's attention-temperature `m` — by design\nThis is the real reason it lands *below* YaRN specifically. My `build_rope_cache_longrope` follows the paper's formula, which has **no attention-temperature `m`**. But YaRN's cache bakes in `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` (you saw `m=1.2773` in the logs), which gives it a small but real edge. Critically, **even the YaRN *seed* inside the search is YaRN-minus-`m`** (the seed only ports the frequencies, not `m`), so the search *couldn't* reproduce true YaRN. YaRN-with-`m` therefore wins.\n\nSo: LongRoPE ≈ NTK-without-`m`, and YaRN = NTK-by-parts-**with**-`m` + (in principle) a search that didn't find anything. YaRN's `m` + refined ramp give it the slight edge.\n\n## Is this the \"wrong\" result?\nNo — it's the **expected** result at this scale. LongRoPE's published wins are on **7B+ models, 256k–2M extension, with a large search (P=64, 40 iters) + progressive extension**. On a **48M model at 8×**, there's no headroom for the search to exploit, so formula-YaRN ≥ searched-LongRoPE. Your experiment faithfully reproduced that.\n\n## If you want a truly fair cache-vs-cache fight\nTwo options:\n- **Add `m` to `build_rope_cache_longrope`** (multiply cos/sin by `m` like YaRN does). Then the YaRN seed *is* real YaRN, and the search can match or beat it. This makes it \"searched interpolation vs formula interpolation\" with `m` held constant — the honest comparison. I can make that one-line change.\n- Or accept the finding as-is: *at 48M/8×, LongRoPE's searched cache doesn't beat YaRN's formula* — which is itself a legitimate, publishable observation (the method needs scale to pay off).\n\nWant me to add the `m` temperature to the LongRoPE builder so you can re-run a fair comparison? It's a small, gated change (and I'd re-verify the parity test)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888922,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"output_tokens":4004,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888922,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":4004,"cache_read_input_tokens":21078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":888922,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":888922},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CdhSMMKvewAH8DCF7DNZc","type":"assistant","uuid":"21a2633a-ea61-4ee3-a7bf-c668e43fcc0e","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:03:51.736Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"21a2633a-ea61-4ee3-a7bf-c668e43fcc0e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"d128d214-688c-4f00-8ad8-32bd6ac2b0f8","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"75a802e6-f666-4311-902f-8c4373c933c3\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"First, look closely: the gap is **tiny** — LongRoPE (blue) and YaRN-fine-tuned (green) nearly overlap, and both **clearly beat** the naive YaRN (orange). So LongRoPE isn't broken; it's just a hair behind YaRN. The ordering is exactly sensible: **YaRN-FT ≤ LongRoPE-FT ≪ naive-YaRN**.\\n\\nTwo concrete reasons it's slightly behind, both of which we can see in your run:\\n\\n## 1. The search found nothing better than the seeds\\nYour s=8 search **converged flat at 202.63 from gen 0** (`no_improve` climbed straight to 4). The GA never beat the NTK/YaRN seed. For a **48M model at 8×**, the model is **capacity-limited, not interpolation-limited** — no choice of `λ` meaningfully helps, so the search just returns ~the seed. (It was also a deliberately small search with `CALIB=3`, i.e. noisy fitness.) So \\\"LongRoPE\\\" here is essentially **the NTK-seed cache**, not something the search improved.\\n\\n## 2. LongRoPE's cache omits YaRN's attention-temperature `m` — by design\\nThis is the real reason it lands *below* YaRN specifically. My `build_rope_cache_longrope` follows the paper's formula, which has **no attention-temperature `m`**. But YaRN's cache bakes in `m = 0.1·ln(s)+1` (you saw `m=1.2773` in the logs), which gives it a small but real edge. Critically, **even the YaRN *seed* inside the search is YaRN-minus-`m`** (the seed only ports the frequencies, not `m`), so the search *couldn't* reproduce true YaRN. YaRN-with-`m` therefore wins.\\n\\nSo: LongRoPE ≈ NTK-without-`m`, and YaRN = NTK-by-parts-**with**-`m` + (in principle) a search that didn't find anything. YaRN's `m` + refined ramp give it the slight edge.\\n\\n## Is this the \\\"wrong\\\" result?\\nNo — it's the **expected** result at this scale. LongRoPE's published wins are on **7B+ models, 256k–2M extension, with a large search (P=64, 40 iters) + progressive extension**. On a **48M model at 8×**, there's no headroom for the search to exploit, so formula-YaRN ≥ searched-LongRoPE. Your experiment faithfully reproduced that.\\n\\n## If you want a truly fair cache-vs-cache fight\\nTwo options:\\n- **Add `m` to `build_rope_cache_longrope`** (multiply cos/sin by `m` like YaRN does). Then the YaRN seed *is* real YaRN, and the search can match or beat it. This makes it \\\"searched interpolation vs formula interpolation\\\" with `m` held constant — the honest comparison. I can make that one-line change.\\n- Or accept the finding as-is: *at 48M/8×, LongRoPE's searched cache doesn't beat YaRN's formula* — which is itself a legitimate, publishable observation (the method needs scale to pay off).\\n\\nWant me to add the `m` temperature to the LongRoPE builder so you can re-run a fair comparison? It's a small, gated change (and I'd re-verify the parity test).\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":53},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b6a1d7a2-eab7-4740-9287-7be18c5febfe","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:03:51.919Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
