{"parentUuid":"ef055b4c-ebce-4742-9cea-7a24d0f0b633","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhTddBj2b8cThEUmzNqF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4044,"cache_read_input_tokens":910000,"output_tokens":2338,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":910000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4044},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdhTdTgj3vEEkGXm8bZCh","type":"assistant","uuid":"fc696422-2399-4cc8-b53e-0c6f374f5a68","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:19:52.083Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"fc696422-2399-4cc8-b53e-0c6f374f5a68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhTddBj2b8cThEUmzNqF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — the implementation is **not wrong**. It's a **faithful** port of the LongRoPE paper, and it's verified:\n- The formula matches Eq. 3 exactly (`angle = n·base_freq / λᵢ`, with the `n̂` threshold) — confirmed against the actual paper in two review rounds.\n- The parity tests pass (`λ=1,n̂=0` → plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ=s` → PI; `n̂` threshold straddle).\n\n**LongRoPE genuinely does not use an attention-temperature `m`.** That's a **YaRN-specific ingredient**, not part of LongRoPE. So \"no `m`\" is correct — it's not a missing feature, it's a real difference between the two methods:\n\n- **YaRN** = a *fixed* per-dim interpolation formula **+ attention temperature `m`**.\n- **LongRoPE** = a *searched* per-dim interpolation, **no `m`**.\n\nLongRoPE is *supposed* to win via the **search** finding better per-dim factors than any formula. In the paper that advantage (at 7B / 256k+ with a big search) outweighs not having `m`. On your **48M / 8×** model, the search finds nothing better than the seed (the model is capacity-limited), so LongRoPE has no search advantage to offset YaRN's `m` — and lands a hair behind. **That's a genuine result, not a bug.**\n\nSo to be precise about the three possibilities:\n1. **Implementation wrong?** No — faithful and parity-verified.\n2. **Result wrong?** No — it's the expected outcome when the search finds no gain at small scale.\n3. **Comparison perfectly apples-to-apples?** Not quite — YaRN has `m`, LongRoPE doesn't. That's fair as \"YaRN-the-method vs LongRoPE-the-method,\" but if you specifically want to isolate *searched-cache vs formula-cache*, the `m` difference is a confound.\n\n## If you want to remove that confound\nAdding `m` to `build_rope_cache_longrope` would make it a **LongRoPE+m hybrid** — **not** paper-LongRoPE, but it would put both caches on equal footing so the comparison isolates the interpolation itself. That's an *optional experiment*, not a correctness fix. If you did it and LongRoPE *still* didn't beat YaRN, that would firmly confirm \"no search headroom at 48M/8×.\"\n\nBottom line: **your implementation is correct and your result is real** — LongRoPE just doesn't pay off at this small scale, which is exactly what the literature predicts. If you want the fairer cache-vs-cache variant (add `m`), say the word and I'll make the gated one-line change + re-verify parity."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4044,"cache_read_input_tokens":910000,"output_tokens":2338,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2338,"cache_read_input_tokens":910000,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4044,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4044},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdhTdTgj3vEEkGXm8bZCh","type":"assistant","uuid":"a3b0bd4a-e692-4b86-afea-021569a1f220","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:20:03.652Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"a3b0bd4a-e692-4b86-afea-021569a1f220","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"3a308e3c-d593-4b0c-9aef-b463a0a511ff","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"78c2c217-f46b-4309-bb71-339df248c469\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"No — the implementation is **not wrong**. It's a **faithful** port of the LongRoPE paper, and it's verified:\\n- The formula matches Eq. 3 exactly (`angle = n·base_freq / λᵢ`, with the `n̂` threshold) — confirmed against the actual paper in two review rounds.\\n- The parity tests pass (`λ=1,n̂=0` → plain RoPE bit-for-bit; `λ=s` → PI; `n̂` threshold straddle).\\n\\n**LongRoPE genuinely does not use an attention-temperature `m`.** That's a **YaRN-specific ingredient**, not part of LongRoPE. So \\\"no `m`\\\" is correct — it's not a missing feature, it's a real difference between the two methods:\\n\\n- **YaRN** = a *fixed* per-dim interpolation formula **+ attention temperature `m`**.\\n- **LongRoPE** = a *searched* per-dim interpolation, **no `m`**.\\n\\nLongRoPE is *supposed* to win via the **search** finding better per-dim factors than any formula. In the paper that advantage (at 7B / 256k+ with a big search) outweighs not having `m`. On your **48M / 8×** model, the search finds nothing better than the seed (the model is capacity-limited), so LongRoPE has no search advantage to offset YaRN's `m` — and lands a hair behind. **That's a genuine result, not a bug.**\\n\\nSo to be precise about the three possibilities:\\n1. **Implementation wrong?** No — faithful and parity-verified.\\n2. **Result wrong?** No — it's the expected outcome when the search finds no gain at small scale.\\n3. **Comparison perfectly apples-to-apples?** Not quite — YaRN has `m`, LongRoPE doesn't. That's fair as \\\"YaRN-the-method vs LongRoPE-the-method,\\\" but if you specifically want to isolate *searched-cache vs formula-cache*, the `m` difference is a confound.\\n\\n## If you want to remove that confound\\nAdding `m` to `build_rope_cache_longrope` would make it a **LongRoPE+m hybrid** — **not** paper-LongRoPE, but it would put both caches on equal footing so the comparison isolates the interpolation itself. That's an *optional experiment*, not a correctness fix. If you did it and LongRoPE *still* didn't beat YaRN, that would firmly confirm \\\"no search headroom at 48M/8×.\\\"\\n\\nBottom line: **your implementation is correct and your result is real** — LongRoPE just doesn't pay off at this small scale, which is exactly what the literature predicts. If you want the fairer cache-vs-cache variant (add `m`), say the word and I'll make the gated one-line change + re-verify parity.\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":54},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5760bb81-ad6a-447b-a1d7-1a843c091108","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:20:03.842Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
