{"parentUuid":"d1e2de2b-6245-4591-945a-468051d1e2c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhUysd4dhmE447ZFyb3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_read_input_tokens":914044,"output_tokens":2022,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2022,"cache_read_input_tokens":914044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdhUyktVz3gNYzfjCV7H6","type":"assistant","uuid":"8cff8056-6a34-4648-adb5-405de5716c4d","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:37:32.151Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"8cff8056-6a34-4648-adb5-405de5716c4d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdhUysd4dhmE447ZFyb3G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two different \"re-verifies\" — let me separate them:\n\n**1. Re-verify the parity test** (what I meant by \"re-verify parity\"): that's just the **CPU unit test** on the cache builder — `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — **no fine-tune, no eval, no GPU**. It just confirms the m-included builder still reduces correctly (λ=1→plain RoPE, etc.). Takes seconds. This is just to make sure adding `m` didn't break the math.\n\n**2. To actually get a fair LongRoPE+m *result* curve** — that's the full experiment, and it needs **both fine-tune and eval** (and the search), because the cache change propagates:\n- The cache feeds the **search** (fitness would change — the seeds now include real YaRN-with-m).\n- The **fine-tune** must be redone — run 81's weights adapted to the *no-m* cache. If you add `m` and just re-eval run 81, the weights won't match the new cache → a train/eval mismatch → misleading (the same effect that inflates the \"naive\" curve).\n- Then **eval** the newly fine-tuned checkpoint.\n\nSo: **you can't just re-eval.** A valid LongRoPE+m comparison = re-run search → fine-tune (~2h at 32k) → eval (~10 min). Roughly the same ~2–3h as the s=8 run you just did.\n\nSummary:\n| What | Fine-tune? | Eval? | Time |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Re-verify parity (builder correctness) | no | no | seconds |\n| Get the LongRoPE+m curve (fair comparison) | **yes** | **yes** (+ search) | ~2–3h |\n\nSo if you just want to confirm the code is right after adding `m`, it's the quick unit test. If you want to *see whether LongRoPE+m beats YaRN*, it's a full re-run (fine-tune + eval), because the model has to be trained against the new cache.\n\nWant me to make the `m` change + run the parity test now (quick), so it's ready — then you decide whether to spend the ~2–3h on the full re-run?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_read_input_tokens":914044,"output_tokens":2022,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2022,"cache_read_input_tokens":914044,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2426,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2426},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdhUyktVz3gNYzfjCV7H6","type":"assistant","uuid":"279c1883-8f37-47ca-9a03-6a770274e5d0","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:37:41.317Z","effort":"low","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
{"parentUuid":"279c1883-8f37-47ca-9a03-6a770274e5d0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"4e819526-5858-44b8-a179-6c10149967fe","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"session_id\":\"3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b\",\"transcript_path\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/.claude/projects/-home-blu-bridge25-CP/3d0a11bb-de89-4095-8132-fc46c7f9936b.jsonl\",\"cwd\":\"/home/blu-bridge25/CP\",\"prompt_id\":\"57937663-36fc-4158-911d-2bc1c0572d40\",\"permission_mode\":\"default\",\"effort\":{\"level\":\"low\"},\"hook_event_name\":\"Stop\",\"stop_hook_active\":false,\"last_assistant_message\":\"Two different \\\"re-verifies\\\" — let me separate them:\\n\\n**1. Re-verify the parity test** (what I meant by \\\"re-verify parity\\\"): that's just the **CPU unit test** on the cache builder — `make CP_FUSED_ROPE=1 cp-rope-longrope` — **no fine-tune, no eval, no GPU**. It just confirms the m-included builder still reduces correctly (λ=1→plain RoPE, etc.). Takes seconds. This is just to make sure adding `m` didn't break the math.\\n\\n**2. To actually get a fair LongRoPE+m *result* curve** — that's the full experiment, and it needs **both fine-tune and eval** (and the search), because the cache change propagates:\\n- The cache feeds the **search** (fitness would change — the seeds now include real YaRN-with-m).\\n- The **fine-tune** must be redone — run 81's weights adapted to the *no-m* cache. If you add `m` and just re-eval run 81, the weights won't match the new cache → a train/eval mismatch → misleading (the same effect that inflates the \\\"naive\\\" curve).\\n- Then **eval** the newly fine-tuned checkpoint.\\n\\nSo: **you can't just re-eval.** A valid LongRoPE+m comparison = re-run search → fine-tune (~2h at 32k) → eval (~10 min). Roughly the same ~2–3h as the s=8 run you just did.\\n\\nSummary:\\n| What | Fine-tune? | Eval? | Time |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Re-verify parity (builder correctness) | no | no | seconds |\\n| Get the LongRoPE+m curve (fair comparison) | **yes** | **yes** (+ search) | ~2–3h |\\n\\nSo if you just want to confirm the code is right after adding `m`, it's the quick unit test. If you want to *see whether LongRoPE+m beats YaRN*, it's a full re-run (fine-tune + eval), because the model has to be trained against the new cache.\\n\\nWant me to make the `m` change + run the parity test now (quick), so it's ready — then you decide whether to spend the ~2–3h on the full re-run?\",\"background_tasks\":[],\"session_crons\":[]}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/hooks/run-with-flags.js\" \"stop:check-console-log\" \"scripts/hooks/check-console-log.js\" \"standard,strict\"","durationMs":43},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8d1221d8-db92-4f03-a012-8ef46324a215","timestamp":"2026-08-04T09:37:41.413Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/blu-bridge25/CP","sessionId":"3d913bc2-47ed-4031-b9d2-02eae46f0296","version":"2.1.220","gitBranch":"main","slug":"polished-cuddling-graham"}
